{"columns":["comment_id","issue_key","issue_project_key","comment_author_email","comment_author_name","comment_body","comment_created_at_ts"],"row_count":10000,"rows":[["3829655","WD-22616","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","[~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82] any decision on this?","2026-01-22T09:45:39.880Z"],["3829657","LSS-61783","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^Bolt Operations UK Ltd - annual report 31.12.24 - fully signed.pdf]\n[^Bolt Operations UK Ltd - filing copy 31.12.24 - fully signed.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T09:46:00.674Z"],["3829658","LSS-61982","LSS","elisabeth.gunnarsson@bolt.eu","Elisabeth Gunnarsson","[~accountid:712020:7f47c2af-14e1-4206-a795-ac87cb906276] no I am not. I seem to have lost my admin properties. ","2026-01-22T09:46:00.212Z"],["3829659","LSS-61599","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] hi, feel free to add any necessary address, thanks.","2026-01-22T09:46:05.960Z"],["3829660","LSS-61984","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-22T09:46:07.838Z"],["3829661","LSS-61982","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-22T09:46:07.917Z"],["3829663","SCM-1074","SCM","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] [~accountid:712020:82bad36a-3f0b-4609-8bbe-b4ba65e1094e] \n\n{color:#36B37E}*[ DECISION ]*{color} \n\nBased on Kevin’s latest information this morning we made a decision that we will move on with our improved design and ask supplier to open the mould. We can accept the unit cost increase 1RMB. Supplier will cover the new mould cost.\n\nThe only question is that can we actually put our logo onto the handle or not. I would like to do it but in some cases maybe it is not allowed and we should have “BOLT app”. So what do you think [~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] should we skip the logo (in that case supplier can sell our design to everybody. On the same time we do not have to pay for the mould - so maybe not that big deal. Or we want to have the logo on the handle?","2026-01-22T09:46:26.340Z"],["3829665","BRE-1064","BRE","uladzislau.klimiankou@bolt.eu","Vlad Klimenkov","The remaining ones should be the ones, which have already refunds applied. So should be processed 1-by-1 manually carefully checking the amounts","2026-01-22T09:46:40.304Z"],["3829667","LSS-60107","LSS","karoli.kesner@bolt.eu","Karoli Kesner","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] no updates yet. Thank you for the follow up, i will remind the auditors and let you know. Best wishes, Karoli","2026-01-22T09:47:08.630Z"],["3829668","LSS-59742","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","[~accountid:712020:ca818823-efac-45fe-ba7d-a6686a5e08b5] sorry for the confusion. If the partner agrees and we only need the signatures, then I’m happy to help to collect them 🙂 \n\nHowever, if you still have to align the agreement conditions with the partner, then please share the agreement draft with the partner (consultant) for their review and after that please share their amendments in the ticket. \n\nHope that clears the situation a bit, thanks! ","2026-01-22T09:47:09.505Z"],["3829669","WFM-10082","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","done [~accountid:61ea6e9084311c0069465f61]","2026-01-22T09:47:29.750Z"],["3829670","LSS-61713","LSS","nicoleta.pandelea@bolt.eu","Nicoleta-Steluta Pandelea","Hi [~accountid:712020:3d4c87bb-37b3-4ce8-a9b9-7232af464c95] \n\nThank you very much for sharing the contract.  😃 \n\nI have forwarded it to the provider and received some feedback, which I’ve outlined below. Could you please help me review these points?\n\n\n\n# *Article 2.2.6 – Food preparation*\nArticle 2.2.6 states that all food consumed at the event must be freshly prepared. It would be helpful to clarify that while lunch will indeed be prepared fresh on site, we will also provide snacks (such as cookies, coffee, and tea) that will be purchased from a store and consumed within their expiration dates.\n# *Article 2.2.4 – Professional feedback and freedom of expression*\nThe current wording of Article 2.2.4 raises legitimate concerns regarding my ability to provide honest, professional, and constructive feedback, both during and after the training.\n\nAs a trainer and expert in canine behavior and animal welfare, my role is not to formally endorse or “praise” situations where genuine issues exist, but rather to contribute actively to identifying, correcting, and improving them. Recent experience, including numerous negative public comments on Bolt Pet–related videos, highlights the importance of an open and transparent approach to these matters.\n\nIf such issues persist over time, I cannot be contractually required to express only positive opinions or to omit relevant critical observations. For clarity, I would like to specify that:\n\n* professional feedback, including critical feedback provided in good faith and aimed at service improvement, does not constitute damage to image;\n* expressing a public opinion is permissible in serious cases involving animal welfare, safety, or professional ethics;\n* the shared objective is to address and improve problems collaboratively, not to conceal them.\n\nI therefore kindly request that Article 2.2.4 be reworded or supplemented to ensure it does not oblige me to silence or artificial validation in problematic situations.\n\n# *Intellectual property rights – use and editing of materials*\nI agree that Bolt may use the materials delivered during the training, subject to the following essential clarifications:\n\n* the materials are developed by me and my team and reflect my professional methodology;\n* their use must include appropriate attribution to the author;\n* any editing, fragmentation, or use out of context must require my prior written consent, in order to avoid misrepresentation or harm to my professional reputation.\n\nGiven that the training covers sensitive topics (canine behavior, safety, animal welfare), uncontrolled partial or modified use could lead to unintended negative consequences.\n\n# *Right of the trainer to reuse materials*\nI request explicit confirmation of my right to reuse the materials, concepts, and experience gained through this training in:\n\n* my professional portfolio;\n* future trainings;\n* educational materials and internal products.\n\nThese materials do not include Bolt confidential information and represent my professional know-how, which should not be restricted.\n\n# *Diplomas and educational materials*\nParticipation diplomas, stickers, patches, and other educational materials are developed by the partner as part of the training methodology. I propose the following process:\n\n* materials will be submitted to Bolt for approval in principle;\n* it will be clearly stated that these materials are developed by the trainer;\n* upon Bolt’s request, the Bolt logo can be removed without impacting the delivery of the training.\n\nThese items are educational tools, not commercial deliverables of Bolt.\n\n# *Dog training demonstration and participant involvement*\nThe training includes a practical dog training demonstration, which is essential for a genuine understanding of behavior and safety. The current contract does not clarify whether participants may be actively involved, which significantly reduces the training’s value.\n\nI propose that participant involvement be permitted under the following conditions:\n\n* participation is strictly voluntary;\n* protective equipment is used exclusively;\n* continuous professional supervision is ensured;\n* participants sign a consent and assumption-of-risk agreement.\n\nThank you in advance for your support! \n\n","2026-01-22T09:47:32.701Z"],["3829674","PFI-835316","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! We will be looking into this","2026-01-22T09:48:02.575Z"],["3829675","LSS-61599","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","[~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5], please use Vana-Lõuna 15, Tallinn, 10134, Estonia for Anna as a witness.","2026-01-22T09:48:04.076Z"],["3829676","C2-457","C2","janeli.takk@bolt.eu","Janeli Takk","[~accountid:5f7722e1a2909600750e0434] TWS batteries report cell voltages, but in 0.1V units. Techsum reports in 0.01V units. \n\nDoes this affect triggering the error?\n\n!image-20260122-094720.png|width=585,alt=\"image-20260122-094720.png\"!","2026-01-22T09:48:10.092Z"],["3829680","ROPSC-347","ROPSC","riin@bolt.eu","Riin Kotsalainen","Reported data validated in 98% \nLooker dashboard per country stats can be found [HERE|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/28186?Country+Name=&Entity+Type=driver%2Cfleet]","2026-01-22T09:48:44.984Z"],["3829681","LSS-61322","LSS","domantas.dabrukas@bolt.eu","Domantas Dabrukas","Hey [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc],\n\nThis procurement is being organised as a low-value tender, below EUR 15,000 per year.\n\nThe procurement section that requires your approval is the second section below. They have included provisions from the procurement law regarding price changes. Although this is not strictly necessary, it would be preferable to leave it as is in order to minimize friction and proceed with signing more quickly.\n\n","2026-01-22T09:49:04.092Z"],["3829682","ROPSC-452","ROPSC","riin@bolt.eu","Riin Kotsalainen","Research finished for natural person and UBO’s \n\nOngoing for Legal entities and Sole traders","2026-01-22T09:49:18.992Z"],["3829685","LSS-61892","LSS","kristine.bezerrakjerulfa@bolt.eu","Kristīne Bezerra-Kjerulfa","Sorry [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] , it was my advice to tag you here, because the issue is delicate and media keeps us under magnifying glass. This reply really needs extra love and attention. \n\nNo need to check WIP, but we would definitely ask your final read. ","2026-01-22T09:50:11.799Z"],["3829686","PAW-15085","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-22T09:50:21.449Z"],["3829688","LSS-61599","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","Thank you!","2026-01-22T09:50:24.997Z"],["3829690","LSS-61955","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] assigned to you as you’re already in communication with stakeholders:)","2026-01-22T09:51:50.616Z"],["3829692","WFM-10058","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Thanks [~accountid:6294d703e76a9c00705d0785] . \n[~accountid:5f1a9692b385da00156b98be] queue has been created [07 BU_Saudi Arabia_Business_Partner|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/queues/assign/2970009?filter=%7B%7D&pagination=%7B%22currentPage%22%3A0%2C%22rowsPerPage%22%3A25%7D&search=Ali%20Abdu]\nCould you please tell me the specific Bolt email of the agent? Couldn’t find it by his name.","2026-01-22T09:52:51.701Z"],["3829693","LSS-61302","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Looping [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] from product legal in the ticket. [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] could you please advise why the general T&C accepted by the Customer while registering of the account won’t apply if the MSA is concluded? I cannot get it and I didn’t work on the Global MSA template. Perhaps you do know? If the general T&C do not apply, are there any T&C applying to the Customer then?\n\n8.6. _The Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the parties relating to its subject matter and supersedes all prior communications, drafts, agreements, representations, warranties, stipulations and undertakings of whatsoever nature, whether oral or written between the parties._ *_For sake of clarity, the General Terms and Conditions for Bolt Business the Customer accepts when signing up for a Business account won’t be applicable to the arrangements under this Agreement._*\n\nWill appreciate your support! 🙏 ❤️ ","2026-01-22T09:53:14.861Z"],["3829698","BEE-3491","BEE","anton.lapin@bolt.eu","Anton Lapin","Any updates here? Agents sometimes experience problems with it - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1769013434670029|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1769013434670029|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T09:54:04.465Z"],["3829701","PFI-835302","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, I can’t give an answer without having an invoice link/invoice number. If there’s any help need e still from Billing side, please, provide the invoices to reissue","2026-01-22T09:54:38.326Z"],["3829702","LSS-61586","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hi [~accountid:712020:78fc81c0-7482-443a-bf90-aacc3d89384a], just to clarify: are we discussing a specific fleet owner that went bankrupt, or a general process?\n\n# If this concerns a specific fleet, is the goal now to properly pay out the deposit to the fleet owner (or, in this case, to the bankruptcy curator/administrator who has taken over the company’s legal representation)?\n# Given that communication with the fleet is lost, but we are still willing to make the payout, the most efficient approach would be to contact the bankruptcy administrator directly and express our intention to return the deposit, since the cooperation agreement with the fleet has been terminated and we have an obligation to do so (assuming the equipment was returned to us - was it?).\n# The bankruptcy administrator should then provide the instructions we need to follow. They are best placed to guide us here, as collecting such payments is also directly in the interest of the bankruptcy estate.","2026-01-22T09:55:01.256Z"],["3829703","CAMLE-9894","CAMLE","uladzislau.tolkach@bolt.eu","Uladzislau Tolkach","so, I've checked on prelive, and yes — there I cannot approve a test that starts in the past.\nOn live we're using RnA, and I've actually managed to send to review [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/campaign-targeting/tests/rides_and_rental/4821624|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/campaign-targeting/tests/rides_and_rental/4821624] test, id didn't run validation on test period. -Still need to confirm how it'll look after it gets approved in RnA-, *yup, it gets approved.* but looks like we should enforce same level of validation for ready for review / approved state transitions, not just the latter one","2026-01-22T09:55:09.542Z"],["3829704","WFM-10076","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","Closing the request as per comment from [~accountid:712020:d1c62e3c-349c-4497-abae-15cc1ab532be]","2026-01-22T09:55:09.911Z"],["3829705","CAMLE-9894","CAMLE",null,"Slack","[Uladzislau Tolkach|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6305dd67cf3340e8737f8f66] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CDQN2UG9X/p1768988332008799?thread_ts=1768910349.907189&cid=CDQN2UG9X|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CDQN2UG9X/p1768988332008799?thread_ts=1768910349.907189&cid=CDQN2UG9X|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-22T09:55:10.920Z"],["3829707","DSR-3943","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T09:56:06.836Z"],["3829708","CNT-461","CNT","anton.sljussarev@bolt.eu","Anton Sljussarev","[~accountid:6163ec849cdb930072d02e8e] Previous copies for LCM: \n- [Sofia launch|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1AVDVmpMU1ZY0fWphOFV3CyeuJY62xytbJAU_rKNS2WQ/edit?gid=2097314132#gid=2097314132&range=A44]\n- [Palanga launch|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vG8D804tupn1BVOFZUluOPnypK1zwEx0P8MmufjcUko/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.sq16m2vxcufj]\n- [Sigulda launch|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1z8slWHGZJ51hvOwGKbqIUHw_GgPiBftjzZVX2Ttr_co/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-22T09:56:13.595Z"],["3829709","DRX-28246","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","❌  Tested on DA.127.0 (1512) Firebase build on Samsung A12, OS:13 and Google Pixel 8 Pro, OS:16\n\nThe issue is still present on the landscape mode\n\n||✅  *Portrait*||❌ *Landscape*||\n|!Screenshot_20260122-114923.png|width=235,alt=\"Screenshot_20260122-114923.png\"!|!Screenshot_20260122-114447.png|width=516,alt=\"Screenshot_20260122-114447.png\"!|","2026-01-22T09:56:40.697Z"],["3829712","LSS-61985","LSS","axel.olsson@bolt.eu","Axel Olsson","[^BPT_559267-4591 (1).pdf] _(350 kB)_\n\n[^Carler .pdf] _(179 kB)_\n\n[^MasterloanandsubsidyagreementBol tOperationsOUArienAB03.10.24 1 (1).pdf] _(198 kB)_","2026-01-22T09:57:28.049Z"],["3829715","LSS-61892","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:63d10e64c565900ff4057c9d] thank you for the context 🙂 \n\n[~accountid:61150a517ab143006e967b15] , please let me know once the answer is finalised from the Ops side, I will review. Still kind request to tag me where you are especially unsure about the answer provided.  ","2026-01-22T09:57:36.773Z"],["3829716","LSS-61982","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] this should’ve been a Legal ops ticket instead, should I push business to create such or would this one suffice for you? Thanks!","2026-01-22T09:57:44.510Z"],["3829717","PFI-834038","PFI","aisma.austruma@bolt.eu","Aisma Austruma","Hello! \nWhile oficially from them we have not gotten back, the asumption is that they cannot pay the invoice - as the Invoice data seams to be brought from the CSV Doc - and the VAT and Whole amounts are incorrect. \n\nWaiting for the fix here, as the main invoice is incorrect, and we need for it to be corrected. And that should come together with the fixed CSV doc - as it is needed for accounting.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-22T09:57:44.804Z"],["3829718","PFI-837125","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","\n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T09:57:47.416Z"],["3829719","LSS-61821","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:712020:3628e8e4-2c88-4d47-8c51-14aa1e98735c] , thanks for the clarifications. \n\nCan you please ask them to replace *Article 6. Mutual Non-Recruitment Clause* with the wording we agreed in Clyde’s contract? When this is done we can move forward with the signing.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-22T09:58:40.997Z"],["3829722","GN-106","GN","vlad.foamete@bolt.eu","Vlad Foamete","[~accountid:712020:ab1787cc-8432-4ebc-b628-abe39d0d6320] when you have time could you please have a look? Not sure why there is a different instruction for that particular roundabout.","2026-01-22T09:59:08.983Z"],["3829723","RISK2-2366","RISK2","kristi.loit@bolt.eu","Kristi Loit","[~accountid:63622ea17d4645af4f03bd18] Access given.","2026-01-22T09:59:13.038Z"],["3829724","PFI-835621","PFI","alexandru.stavarache@bolt.eu","Alexandru Stavarache","Thank you very much for the help. \nMy client is going to need the previous invoice reissued as well, number RO1525-47951 of 174.15 lei. \nPlease assist with this one as well. \n\nI appreciate it. Have a great day.","2026-01-22T09:59:21.618Z"],["3829725","LSS-61985","LSS","axel.olsson@bolt.eu","Axel Olsson","[^Loan_and_Subsidy_Agreement_Bolt_Operations_OÜ_Arien_AB_02.04.2024 (5) (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T09:59:28.447Z"],["3829726","FPD-1445","FPD","kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu","Kateryna Kolomiiets","created a PR [https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/814|https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/814]","2026-01-22T09:59:36.600Z"],["3829727","DSR-3943","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","New download from [Balance history |https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/balanceHistory?balanceHistoryFilterSearch=%7B%22external_id%22%3A8403207%2C%22type%22%3A%22Driver%22%2C%22month%22%3A%7B%22year%22%3A2026%2C%22month%22%3A1%7D%2C%22viewType%22%3Anull%2C%22week%22%3A%7B%22start%22%3A1768773600000%2C%22end%22%3A1769378399999%7D%7D]","2026-01-22T09:59:56.187Z"],["3829728","LSS-60779","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:11ff4938-2eb6-4197-95c0-34077455863e] , I am closing the ticket due to inactivity. Please let me know how we can help.","2026-01-22T10:00:12.994Z"],["3829730","CEBF-1835","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","Testing is completed. Please find details [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1f4Bku8sel7jXxFpM7-0YWjyquXYBtLMMziw0RiFmT90/edit?usp=sharing].","2026-01-22T10:00:26.982Z"],["3829731","BB-2284","BB","yeshwant.kumar@bolt.eu","Yeshwant Kumar","Hello [~accountid:557058:b2aaf2b9-4465-40fe-b31b-1711dbe61946], all the credit notes are issued.","2026-01-22T10:00:36.127Z"],["3829732","ROPSC-491","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","[Summary of the project.|https://docs.google.com/document/d/19GVx7Tf45qobzAMopHcWX8UjAYikalUfKY9JDuP5N6s/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.aw1cvr21jfh2]","2026-01-22T10:00:41.706Z"],["3829738","PRIV-545","PRIV","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09D2AVUE58/p1767973080553479|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09D2AVUE58/p1767973080553479|smart-link] \n\nh2. Proposal\n\nBolt Drive would store user-level flags indicating that a third-party rental partner has blocked or denied a rental to a specific user, for any reason.\n\n✅ We already receive this information today, however, there’s no User impact\n\n🆕 Storage at user-level\n\nh2. Personal Data\n\n:yes: – DL number, DL issue country, personal code or name, DoB, reason for ban, issue data, expiry date\n\nh2. Set up\n\nUsers create an account in Bolt, so all personal data is already stored in our database. The main change is the following:\n\n# We will store at the order level the fact that an order cannot be created\n# If a partner returns an error during order creation, we will store this fact together with the reason.\n# Based on this data, we plan to prohibit some users from starting a ride. e.g. manually issue ban.\n\nh2. User impact\n\nBooking denial\n\nh2. User comms\n\nPrivacy & Legal recommendation → generic reason","2026-01-22T10:01:05.316Z"],["3829739","SREDESK-7454","SREDESK","adam.kudybinski@bolt.eu","Adam Kudybiński","approved","2026-01-22T10:01:09.340Z"],["3829740","LSS-61985","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-22T10:01:09.925Z"],["3829742","LSS-61757","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/345650|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/345650|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T10:01:30.672Z"],["3829743","DRX-27736","DRX","taxifyqa@bolt.eu","QA Testing","PR comment for QA:\nPlease test landscape mode as per ticket.","2026-01-22T10:01:36.229Z"],["3829744","HS-29186","HS","weronika.michalska@bolt.eu","Weronika Michalska-Chrabańska","hey, sure\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 11.01.28.png|width=425,height=635,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 11.01.28.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-22T10:01:37.252Z"],["3829746","LSS-61757","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:61addb80b0b630006a695081] - sent out for Ahto’s signature 🙂 ","2026-01-22T10:01:48.348Z"],["3829752","LSS-61941","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:712020:7a0eb594-fb3b-4988-9715-b614bae4a6fb], thanks for raising this! \n\nCould you please share this response with the rider: \n\n_Dear [Name],_\n_Thank you for your inquiry. Please note that your complaint will be reviewed in accordance with Bolt's Internal Complaint-Handling System Rules, available at:_\n\n[https://bolt.eu/lt-lt/legal/tnc-internal-rules/?category=other|https://bolt.eu/lt-lt/legal/tnc-internal-rules/?category=other|smart-link] \n\n_You can expect a response within 30 days from the date we receive a complete complaint. If you have any questions in the meantime, feel free to contact us at [email]._\n\n_Best regards,_\n_The Bolt Team_\n\n\nThanks! \n","2026-01-22T10:03:30.565Z"],["3829753","PFI-837129","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-22T10:03:32.192Z"],["3829754","PFI-837129","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:6108e65ceb7aef0069e5ba05] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-22T10:03:33.750Z"],["3829755","LSS-61682","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hey [~accountid:712020:9bc1ca8e-c2f1-41a2-9476-90ce966c2205] [~accountid:712020:3d4c87bb-37b3-4ce8-a9b9-7232af464c95] - agreed to *reject* the clause 👌 \n\nWe are not exchanging any personal data, so there is also no point to have this clause at this stage - it only takes up space 🙂 Aligned and thanks!","2026-01-22T10:03:36.445Z"],["3829756","LSS-58932","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:712020:d77c5e6c-f92f-4d79-955d-9f88e6d0a883] !\n\nAny news here?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-22T10:03:39.854Z"],["3829757","FX-3399","FX","katharina.skolimowski@bolt.eu","Katharina Skolimowski","Design\n\n\n\n[https://www.figma.com/design/kR6WsMBwsBQqaTWAK0eX40/Driver-performance-and-activity?node-id=11008-383&t=FI8VHKO3vsRPIjX5-1|https://www.figma.com/design/kR6WsMBwsBQqaTWAK0eX40/Driver-performance-and-activity?node-id=11008-383&t=FI8VHKO3vsRPIjX5-1|smart-card]","2026-01-22T10:03:46.489Z"],["3829759","WEB-9864","WEB","samuel.oyekeye@bolt.eu","Samuel Oluseyi Oyekeye","Hi [~accountid:64009ca94307e46ad144aee7] \nI wrapped the icon request in a try-catch and an added icon fallback to reduce the noise.\n[~accountid:63c11ab62a526608c5506c05] would using this [icon|https://kalep.uip.boltint.net/@bolteu/kalep-icons-svg/index.html?icon=HelpCircleOutlined] work for cases of unresolved flags?","2026-01-22T10:05:36.697Z"],["3829760","GRWA-1524","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","here is the detailed [post|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C1JQJKT5/p1769075516057599] in growth_tools","2026-01-22T10:06:07.795Z"],["3829761","PFI-837131","PFI","darina.vozgrina@bolt-outsource.eu","Darina Vozgrina","[^Изображение в PDF_1767619761007 (3).pdf]","2026-01-22T10:06:14.075Z"],["3829762","WFM-10058","WFM","david.tomes@bolt.eu","David Tomeš","It’s [+ali.alomari@bolt.eu+|mailto:ali.alomari@bolt.eu].\n\nThank you","2026-01-22T10:06:22.862Z"],["3829763","LSS-57846","LSS","bianca.medrea@bolt.eu","Bianca Medrea","Hey, I synced with [~accountid:712020:3d4c87bb-37b3-4ce8-a9b9-7232af464c95] on the floor last week.\n\nQuick update is that Difereat is now open to re-activating the tablet. We still need to align internally and then with him on the exact next steps. I’ll keep you posted.","2026-01-22T10:06:31.147Z"],["3829764","LSS-61322","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey team,\n[~accountid:618d20acfba4d0006ae30dd3] thanks for clarifying this so quickly!\nIf the terms regarding price change is suitable for you from business perspective, then I see no major risks to sign this agreement as suggested. \n\nIf you have any additional questions, please let me know 😉 ","2026-01-22T10:06:42.924Z"],["3829765","LSS-54429","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] \nFrom a data protection and privacy perspective, the existing [Global Privacy Notice|https://bolt.eu/en-my/privacy/privacy-for-drivers/?category=rides] sufficiently covers the personal data processing involved in the Bad Rider Management system. The system relies on existing categories of personal data and falls within the already-notified purposes of service provision, platform integrity, and safety. Malaysian PDPA does not require additional disclosures regarding automated decision-making or behavioural scoring, and no privacy-driven updates to the Privacy Policy are required.\n\nIf anything - please tag me.\nThank you!\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a]  ","2026-01-22T10:07:55.243Z"],["3829772","WD-22575","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","-Nothing to be found in Telema Prelive under PL003.- \n\nInvoice is here - IN-PL003-26-000037","2026-01-22T10:09:04.458Z"],["3829776","BDB-1494","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:628e5c9d8026a10068b1e457] \nCan I close the ticket, please?\nThank you ","2026-01-22T10:10:49.313Z"],["3829777","DSR-3945","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T10:11:07.856Z"],["3829778","SUPX-2337","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Should we show CSAT for proactive (trip anomaly cases), as they are also outbound safety cases?","2026-01-22T10:11:12.389Z"],["3829780","PFI-837134","PFI","mahu.teymurova@bolt-outsource.eu","Mahu Teymurova","!5578F13E-04C1-49A3-B845-974947C619CB.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!5EF38820-46BD-457B-9F2E-E871FE18339D.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T10:11:26.237Z"],["3829781","BEE-3659","BEE","maksym.shuldiner@bolt.eu","Maksym Shuldiner","Hi. This was done and deployed to live :white_check_mark:\n\nBased on the metrics, it looks like the change was successfully propagated, and cases with a {{resolution_reason}} state are excluded from FRT.","2026-01-22T10:11:33.989Z"],["3829785","PFI-837135","PFI","juri.zuravljov@bolt.eu","Juri Žuravljov","!image0.png.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T10:12:17.287Z"],["3829787","LSS-61898","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hi [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] \nFYI, Liivika meant a review of Global Privacy Notice on our website - [Link|https://bolt.eu/en-my/privacy/privacy-for-drivers/?category=rides].\nI’ve reviewed the notice against the Bad Rider Management setup and left a confirmation comment in the main ticket :done: ","2026-01-22T10:12:45.766Z"],["3829788","WEB-9864","WEB","conor.mclaughlin@bolt.eu","Conor McLaughlin","[~accountid:712020:2bb94136-b4e4-463e-a0f6-8be773ff520f] [~accountid:64009ca94307e46ad144aee7] can we just add a fill colour instead?\n\nMore important is getting those locations filled in correctly 😄","2026-01-22T10:13:04.032Z"],["3829789","PFI-834038","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Got it, thanks. It has been escalated to the engineering team, seems that work is being done; I will provide an update once the invoice and Rides csv are fixed.","2026-01-22T10:13:20.173Z"],["3829790","PAW-14164","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-product-async-communication-libraries, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-22T10:13:32.466Z"],["3829792","PFI-834038","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BB-2282?issueKey=BB-2282&subProduct=jira-software|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BB-2282?issueKey=BB-2282&subProduct=jira-software|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T10:13:43.907Z"],["3829794","PFI-837136","PFI","babajide.bamidele@bolt-outsource.eu","Babajide Bamidele","!Screenshot_20260120-095624.jpg.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T10:14:27.133Z"],["3829795","DRX-28267","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-28207 has been resolved","2026-01-22T10:14:27.884Z"],["3829796","DRX-28205","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-28207 has been resolved","2026-01-22T10:14:27.891Z"],["3829797","DRX-28246","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-28207 has been resolved","2026-01-22T10:14:27.978Z"],["3829798","PFI-837137","PFI","tyler.ison@bolt.eu","Tyler Hamilton Ison","[^Rahalise_nõude_arestimisest_GREEN_PAK_S.R.O._(Bolt_Operations_OÜ-le).pdf]","2026-01-22T10:14:34.235Z"],["3829799","BDB-1513","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:5d5a47614aeeb80c2cc0d00a] \nCan we proceed to close this ticket?\nThank you!","2026-01-22T10:14:53.868Z"],["3829800","BDB-1500","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] \nCan we proceed to close this ticket?\nThank you!","2026-01-22T10:15:12.077Z"],["3829803","WD-22615","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22424|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22424|smart-link]  I also have this ticket [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] . Not sure if something was done while I was on the sabbatical.\n\nDo we just add it to this Custom Validation? - *Activity must be Empty for this Spend Category*","2026-01-22T10:15:25.051Z"],["3829804","BDB-1482","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:6358f0a501c2ff842c182ef2] \nCan we proceed to close this ticket?\nThank you!","2026-01-22T10:15:27.789Z"],["3829805","MKP-9899","MKP","jan.stoltman@bolt.eu","Jan Stoltman","Seems that expire is 2x - 10x faster than set\nPrelive:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 12.14.05.png|width=353,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 12.14.05.png\"!","2026-01-22T10:15:53.428Z"],["3829806","BDB-1482","BDB","agata.bieniek@bolt.eu","Agata Bieniek","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] yes. Thank you!","2026-01-22T10:15:59.779Z"],["3829808","DSR-3947","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T10:16:07.605Z"],["3829809","LSS-58970","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hey team [~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] [~accountid:619cad8cb43d5b006af304cc] , a privacy sub-ticket was created for me for this one so jumping in 🙏 \n\n(/) No issues with this from a *privacy* *POV*, we already checked this project from a central privacy POV, and there are no local law issues as well.\n\nAs we’re not using/sharing any personal data or otherwise engaging in anything that could fall under the scope of privacy laws, we can proceed provided that [~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] is happy with that 😉 ","2026-01-22T10:16:51.424Z"],["3829811","WFM-10091","WFM","papawarin.khamsangthong@bolt-outsource.eu","Papawarin Khamsangthong","!image (2).png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T10:17:20.038Z"],["3829815","PFI-837143","PFI","eleanora.maruma@bolt.eu","Eleanora Maruma","!image001 (1).jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T10:17:49.524Z"],["3829817","PFI-835621","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Sure, reissued too","2026-01-22T10:18:22.092Z"],["3829818","LSS-61920","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* Emma’s responses via Slack.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 10.18.41 AM.png|width=1021,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 10.18.41 AM.png\"!","2026-01-22T10:18:50.498Z"],["3829820","MKP-9901","MKP","artjom.brehhunov@bolt.eu","Artjom Brehhunov","Hi team,\n\nI am looking into categories where the state is shown as {{busy}} in app and had a few questions:\n• What are the factors that come into play for a category to be busy? \n• How does this interact with FIFO area dispatching?\n• Currently an exclusion [FF|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/featureflags/edit/7626] applies to London city wide allowing orders to be placed on {{busy}} categories, could this potentially be set on a regional/category level?","2026-01-22T10:19:06.299Z"],["3829821","MKP-9901","MKP",null,"Slack","[Artjom Brehhunov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:987e0719-a08b-4a9e-9349-ae881aeaf688] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02LWCMELDD/p1769077114183119?thread_ts=1757941507.644529&cid=C02LWCMELDD|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02LWCMELDD/p1769077114183119?thread_ts=1757941507.644529&cid=C02LWCMELDD|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-22T10:19:07.263Z"],["3829822","MKP-9901","MKP","jan.stoltman@bolt.eu","Jan Stoltman","• If any drivers are available for orders in this category & region\n• We get drivers from the FIFO queue first\n• This FF is not used anymore from what I can see. There's a remote config for it, but also not exposed/used anywhere except for hardcoded London","2026-01-22T10:19:07.868Z"],["3829824","MKP-9901","MKP","nicholas.p.smith@bolt.eu","Nick Smith","Thanks [@jan.stoltman|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5fca4c37cbead5006998a665], on the last point are you saying this FF in essence doesn’t do anything or that it is only configured for London somewhere else? :sweat_smile: ","2026-01-22T10:19:09.086Z"],["3829825","MKP-9901","MKP","jan.stoltman@bolt.eu","Jan Stoltman","The flag itself doesn't do anything and could be disabled (let's double-check first :smile:) - London city id is hardcoded in code","2026-01-22T10:19:09.789Z"],["3829826","MKP-9901","MKP","jan.stoltman@bolt.eu","Jan Stoltman","{quote}could this potentially be set on a regional/category level?{quote}\n\nPotentially yes, but would require some development","2026-01-22T10:19:10.394Z"],["3829827","MKP-9901","MKP","nicholas.p.smith@bolt.eu","Nick Smith","Ahh okay I get what you mean now, if you could double check there would be no impact in disabling it please as well as finding out how difficult it would be to remove that hardcoded value that would be great :pray::skin-tone-2:","2026-01-22T10:19:10.949Z"],["3829828","MKP-9901","MKP","jan.stoltman@bolt.eu","Jan Stoltman","Do we want to get rid of this feature for London?","2026-01-22T10:19:11.559Z"],["3829829","MKP-9901","MKP","nicholas.p.smith@bolt.eu","Nick Smith","Potentially yes","2026-01-22T10:19:12.404Z"],["3829830","MKP-9901","MKP","jan.stoltman@bolt.eu","Jan Stoltman","What does the decision depend on?","2026-01-22T10:19:12.999Z"],["3829831","MKP-9901","MKP","jan.stoltman@bolt.eu","Jan Stoltman","Yeah, the FF is unused, it was removed in [this commit|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/commit/91aa0fb1be955630318db4382593c76d8dd191be] (just for posterity)","2026-01-22T10:19:13.939Z"],["3829832","MKP-9901","MKP","nicholas.p.smith@bolt.eu","Nick Smith","Hi [@jan.stoltman|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5fca4c37cbead5006998a665] - Coming back to this thread, can we go ahead and remove the exception for London and enable {{BUSY}} categories please :pray::skin-tone-2:\n\nCC: [@mariacaterina.cucu|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/620e4df5a713ab0068139e4a]","2026-01-22T10:19:14.944Z"],["3829833","MKP-9901","MKP","jan.stoltman@bolt.eu","Jan Stoltman","cc: *group-S05BGTJ2K6Z* ptal","2026-01-22T10:19:15.544Z"],["3829834","MKP-9901","MKP","artjom.brehhunov@bolt.eu","Artjom Brehhunov","Created a task for it: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MKP-9901|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MKP-9901|smart-link]","2026-01-22T10:19:16.672Z"],["3829835","LSS-61407","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:cb6fc720-3c42-4171-99dd-eaefef0e51eb], the email is good - it puts in writing the request to stop and highlights the breach of contractual obligation. \n\nIf they push back and ask where in the contract, we have specified the articles for you in the previous comment. If they continue to use the driver’s data to promote their fleet, please let me know we can draft a cease and desist letter for you.\n\nThank you for the update on the photo verification and the booking tool.","2026-01-22T10:19:21.336Z"],["3829837","MKP-9901","MKP","nicholas.p.smith@bolt.eu","Nick Smith","Hey [@artjom.brehhunov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:987e0719-a08b-4a9e-9349-ae881aeaf688] - Do you know when this change would be actioned","2026-01-22T10:19:59.529Z"],["3829840","MKP-9901","MKP","artjom.brehhunov@bolt.eu","Artjom Brehhunov","[@iaroslav.melnichuk|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:d88f5976-1e33-47f5-acb2-a9c422493f69] - to review the priority","2026-01-22T10:20:29.056Z"],["3829841","MKP-9906","MKP","albert.tumanov@bolt.eu","Albert Tumanov","We have discussed this feature:\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4612030480/Marketplace+Hackathon+23+Prices+are+about+to+go+high|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4612030480/Marketplace+Hackathon+23+Prices+are+about+to+go+high|smart-link]\n\nWhat I see is that the feature is abandoned (Experiment halted due to the negative results).\nBut we still have some code related to that, let's remove it?","2026-01-22T10:20:34.551Z"],["3829842","MKP-9906","MKP",null,"Slack","[Albert Tumanov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5d8df26bf2f0670dcb6dacbb] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02K3SSMCN4/p1769074087432969|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02K3SSMCN4/p1769074087432969|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-22T10:20:35.656Z"],["3829843","BDB-1551","BDB","olga.kulitska@bolt.eu","Olha Khmelenko","OOH required formats and resolutions:\n\n* EE [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1cLmH04GdbQaqJTgriI2qzm-iAU4ZVHNs/edit?gid=1838225169#gid=1838225169].\n* LV [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1YTIujSZrTLNEfgLp9XLaDHhv4cjZSN3N/edit?gid=1260042937#gid=1260042937].\n* LT [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1JhRRI-LUF7z3e-M8A3sFWOAsfRKS6tuK/edit?gid=1150216001#gid=1150216001].\n\nDeadline {{2026-01-26}}","2026-01-22T10:20:53.499Z"],["3829844","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] Hey! Can we still get the file for the last OOH placement. The 16 x 4?","2026-01-22T10:20:57.085Z"],["3829845","LSS-61928","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:e04282ea-9d2c-4f81-8507-cea4db4cd1b9] , thank you for escalating this! We also received it via our email [privacy@bolt.eu|mailto:privacy@bolt.eu], and our team will handle the case. Please don’t send any responses to the regulator, as we will be reviewing the case/preparing response strategy 🙏 \n\nThanks and have a good day! ☀️ ","2026-01-22T10:21:12.373Z"],["3829846","DO-5796","DO","volha.anishchanka@bolt.eu","Volha Anishchanka","I’ll Slack to you with the instructions, we can connect to Databricks","2026-01-22T10:21:22.656Z"],["3829848","LSS-61986","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^Bank confirmation letter Unibank (Bolt Services AZ LLC).pdf] _(45 kB)_","2026-01-22T10:21:45.323Z"],["3829849","SCM-1116","SCM","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","# [~accountid:712020:16f9a1bd-630a-44fc-acfd-57a270c13c42] what is the ETA of the components needed for the repair?\n# [~accountid:712020:199c869c-84be-4d6f-9d2d-2a504d806ff1] what is the ETA of receiving the broken IoTs?","2026-01-22T10:21:56.762Z"],["3829851","LSS-61987","LSS","jens.zarelius@bolt.eu","Jens Zarelius","!IMG_0103.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T10:22:00.337Z"],["3829854","LSS-58367","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] ,\n\nThanks a lot! \n\nMay you please help to initiate the signature?\n\nThe agreement will be signed from their side by our CEO, Wen Tzu-Wei ([jasonwen@wenk-media.com|mailto:jasonwen@wenk-media.com]).\nWhen sending the agreement for signature, please kindly CC the following email addresses:\n\n> [annechen@wenk-media.com|mailto:annechen@wenk-media.com]、[lewischen@wenk-media.com|mailto:lewischen@wenk-media.com]\n\nThank you!","2026-01-22T10:22:51.540Z"],["3829863","DSR-3949","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T10:26:07.528Z"],["3829868","URRIK-2824","URRIK","akram.yacob@bolt.eu","Akram Yacob","fyi [~accountid:712020:79c5e5df-c60a-423b-9b4d-50f3ab308f4e] and [~accountid:6336e2f5f568615bdc7f135d] please give Reops a heads up since we are ready to schedule a campaign int these countries, to avoid multiple research campaigns being sent at the same time","2026-01-22T10:27:59.001Z"],["3829869","RS-1951","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] ,\n\nLaw Enforcement requests are under the Risk team’s scope, and Privacy is always in the loop. The issue is that we don’t want to share the employee data, but instead want to offer support as an organization. The request came from the court, that’s why we are trying to be attentive with the way we respond ","2026-01-22T10:28:22.296Z"],["3829870","PFI-837120","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","!image-20260122-102757.png|width=657,alt=\"image-20260122-102757.png\"!\n\nIt’s part of the payments for the Service Fee.","2026-01-22T10:28:27.795Z"],["3829871","PRV-941","PRV","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","Submitted request for Slack channels 19 Jan - Pending response\n\n[https://www.google.com/url?q=https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KBGUkEB12qGeKoEfs_dWPOBe7NfR2EgtQa_7ETPwkso/edit?tab%3Dt.0%23heading%3Dh.p2z4crprb0d&sa=D&source=docs&ust=1769081260671932&usg=AOvVaw0pKnlLgVblNwI80_3QHDqI|https://www.google.com/url?q=https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KBGUkEB12qGeKoEfs_dWPOBe7NfR2EgtQa_7ETPwkso/edit?tab%3Dt.0%23heading%3Dh.p2z4crprb0d&sa=D&source=docs&ust=1769081260671932&usg=AOvVaw0pKnlLgVblNwI80_3QHDqI]","2026-01-22T10:28:40.599Z"],["3829872","PFI-836822","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Please, provide invoice links","2026-01-22T10:28:43.534Z"],["3829874","WEBSD-1503","WEBSD","bettina@bolt.eu","Bettina Szilagyi","[^Bolt Business Privacy Notice_1.0_HU_2026.01.22..pdf]\n\n[^Bolt Business Privacy Notice_1.0_HU_2026.01.22.docx]","2026-01-22T10:29:43.237Z"],["3829877","WEBSD-1503","WEBSD","bettina@bolt.eu","Bettina Szilagyi","Could anyone pls add *Kostiantyn Ponomarov* and *Gabrielė Kaveckytė* to this ticket for visibility? Thank you","2026-01-22T10:30:34.783Z"],["3829880","LSS-61989","LSS","elisabeth.gunnarsson@bolt.eu","Elisabeth Gunnarsson","[^1-anbudsformular.pdf] _(122 kB)_","2026-01-22T10:31:02.076Z"],["3829881","SREDESK-7450","SREDESK","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","Purged at 11:31 CET","2026-01-22T10:31:23.871Z"],["3829884","PFI-833568","PFI","monika.jurcik@bolt-outsource.eu","Monika Jurčík","hello any update?? ","2026-01-22T10:31:31.307Z"],["3829885","WEB-9954","WEB","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hey, \n\nTitle: *Global Sustainability Commitments* \n\nThis is the same as for United Nations Global Compact and Science Based Targets initiative. \n\nSubtitle: EcoVadis\n\nWhile updating would you also be able to:\n\n# Remove South Pole at the very bottom of the page as we don’t partner with them anymore.\n# Resize the Rohetiiger logo as it’s a bit off now that the website’s been updated. \n\nThank you! 🙏 ","2026-01-22T10:31:54.912Z"],["3829886","HS-29148","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-22T10:32:32.014Z"],["3829887","PFI-837149","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-22T10:32:46.468Z"],["3829888","PFI-837149","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:641c083a67102fc717c1538e] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-22T10:32:48.258Z"],["3829889","LSS-61989","LSS","elisabeth.gunnarsson@bolt.eu","Elisabeth Gunnarsson","THIS is the correct document.\n\n[^Bolt Services EE OÜ - Åberopande av kapacitet, referensuppdrag.docx]","2026-01-22T10:32:53.583Z"],["3829890","DO-5821","DO","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","Hey Oliver, I see you are already using the [unified auth setup.|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/compute/clusters/0121-133810-atfluwi4?o=3598988355446810] Is there any reason why you want access to legacy approach now?","2026-01-22T10:33:13.965Z"],["3829891","PRV-851","PRV","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (22.01)*+\n\n* See [+LSS-58344+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-58344]\n* Tapbox has reverted with comments on the Global Agreement ([LINK|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nm8KMG-AuZPCHNiOoqGmf_H8llMUlfLs/edit])\n** Schedule 3 (DSA) and its Annexes are for now unchanged ✅ \n** However, there have been some edits to clause 7 (data protection) of the main agreement. Key points are:\n*** *Processing Roles*: \n**** Tapbox inserted “_The Parties shall determine and document the applicable data protection roles (controller/processor and, where relevant, joint controllers and the terms of) for each processing activity in Schedule 3_”. This is not in principle an issue, but we should check with Tapbox whether they anticipate any activities to be outside of C2C (if so, edits will be needed) ⚠️ \n***** Similarly, at Clause 7.4, Tapbox inserted “_To the extent that Tapbox processes personal data as a processor on behalf of Bolt, the Parties shall ensure that an appropriate data processing agreement (or processor terms within Schedule 3) is in place prior to such processing and complies with applicable law. Tapbox shall not process personal data as a processor on Bolt’s behalf until such agreement/terms are in place_”. I have clarified as an internal comment that there are no explicit processor terms in Schedule 3, and that Tapbox should flag if they see the need for a DPA (i) \n**** Tapbox inserted that it is an IC with respect to payment / settlement data and Bolt is an IC with respect to ride-hailing personal data. This is fine ✅ \n*** Provisions re transparency and data minimisation - these are fine ✅ \n*** Counterparty is in Dubai - This is fine for now. We have international transfer provisions, Bolt currently has a presence in Dubai, and the parties are acting as ICs ✅ \n* Virtua has also reverted with comments on the Global Agreement ([LINK|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1eocLhItupdFOLGaIh2u0qJ4iiG-QjM-S-PixjTmue1Q/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.6zeyohruldjb])\n** No changes to data protection terms ✅ ","2026-01-22T10:33:29.188Z"],["3829892","BDB-1500","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] I’ve already deleted the file since you mentioned you won’t need one, but I can recreate it if necessary. Please let me know if there’s any chance we might need any file in the future.\n\nAlso, we’ll need a third category for this asset, could you please provide one? (see screenshot)\nComfort is now a placeholder.\n\nThank you!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 12.32.53.png|width=263,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 12.32.53.png\"!","2026-01-22T10:33:31.557Z"],["3829893","SOBB-1030","SOBB","lucas.santossilva@bolt.eu","Lucas Oliveira dos Santos Silva","(flagoff) Flag removed \n\nAble to connect Slack to Staging and Dev sandboxes.","2026-01-22T10:33:44.456Z"],["3829894","LSS-61818","LSS","pedro.alecrim@bolt.eu","Pedro Alecrim","Thank you, I’ve replied to the Authority [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/728026802] (/) ","2026-01-22T10:34:01.858Z"],["3829895","LSS-61989","LSS","elisabeth.gunnarsson@bolt.eu","Elisabeth Gunnarsson","Wrong document initially added, can’t remove it so I add here for clarification: “1-anbudsformular” is NOT correct.","2026-01-22T10:34:02.515Z"],["3829896","CSDT-901","CSDT","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Missing refund & comp metrics are to be added within the task [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CSDT-978|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CSDT-978|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T10:34:32.103Z"],["3829898","LSS-61978","LSS","martin.tomberg@bolt.eu","Martin Tomberg","Thank you for feedback.\nFor my knowledge we have also insurance - so deductible should be covered.\nFrom my experience if we wish to have higher G4S liability then price will increase or even they wish extra services like manned guard if it will be really high target.\nOur system is build that way it detects if connection with G4S is lost and they will receive signal for that.\nOnly device from G4S is communicator. \nWill you organize sign from our side?","2026-01-22T10:35:04.582Z"],["3829899","LSS-58352","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","Novitus signatories - \nKrzysztof Morawski – vice President of the Board, e-mail: [krzysztof.morawski@comp.com.pl|mailto:krzysztof.morawski@comp.com.pl]\n\nJaroslaw Wilk – vice Presiedent of the Board, e-mail: [jaroslaw.wilk@novitus.pl|mailto:jaroslaw.wilk@novitus.pl]\n\n ","2026-01-22T10:35:09.205Z"],["3829900","LSS-58344","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Hi [~accountid:712020:240e5e60-baab-4e72-a388-591f4f4ec6a2] I have taken a quick look at Tapbox’s comments on the Global Agreement from a privacy POV and have inserted one minor clarifying comment (Clause 7.4), otherwise I have nothing else to add for now. Similarly, Virtua does not appear to have changed any of the data protection terms, and so I similarly have nothing to add for now from the privacy side 🙂 ","2026-01-22T10:35:11.163Z"],["3829901","SREDESK-7458","SREDESK","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","on it","2026-01-22T10:35:13.357Z"],["3829902","WEBSD-1362","WEBSD","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:712020:42b2886c-722b-4c93-b02e-ff673b990b6e] \n\nThanks for the clarification, and sorry for the delayed reply.\n\nAs we’re currently redesigning the main Courier landing page and are also considering moving the sign-up flow to the landing page, similar to what we have for Drivers, we could:\n\n* Add a dedicated section to the Courier landing page highlighting Courier Fleet value propositions\n* Extract the Courier Fleet sign-up from the main flow and add a clear CTA linking directly to the courier fleet signuo (this would need to be aligned with the Couriers team)\n\nLet me know what you think of the suggested approach, and feel free to join the redesign discussion in Slack [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C09TEMXS4CT|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C09TEMXS4CT|smart-link]\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:f0f7cc2d-5968-45e9-91ec-ea445d725066]  ","2026-01-22T10:35:50.164Z"],["3829903","WEB-8406","WEB","burak.ozdemir@bolt.eu","Burak Özdemir","[~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] Hi, shared the issue with you.","2026-01-22T10:35:54.123Z"],["3829904","PFI-835480","PFI","anastacia.njunge@bolt.eu","Anastacia Njunge","Hi Team, Any updates concerning this client’s issue? ","2026-01-22T10:36:07.476Z"],["3829905","DMP-714","DMP","ionut.danila@bolt.eu","Ionuț Dănilă","* The first proposal was generated for an unbatched order, while the second was generated for a batched order containing the original order (280116468) and an additional order (280118179). \n* Both proposals were created at {{2026-01-03T21:20:21.000}}, which should not be possible. Also, according to the [+Admin Panel+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280116468?showUserTz=false], courier 470297 received a proposal that we DID NOT create. We have no logs for that proposal and no records.\n* Opened a [+support request+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C015U4MEKL3/p1769063538532029] in the {{#dev-logistics-efficiency-support}} channel to gather further context and support root cause analysis. The analysis performed on Logistics Efficiency showed that there were no requests with one order, only batches.\n* Going one step further, I opened another [+support request+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02SWJK1ADU/p1769069836202799] on {{#dev-eater-grox-support}}, since GROX is the owner team of {{delivery-order-courier-internal}} cron, that is calling our {{createCourierEarningProposal}} endpoint. I am working closely with the GROX team to understand the root cause.","2026-01-22T10:36:32.012Z"],["3829906","RDS-651","RDS","shreya.bhandari@bolt.eu","Shreya Bhandari","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] there are multiple requests bundled under the same main topic \n- Include Home city notification ( welcome back) is one of them \n","2026-01-22T10:36:33.189Z"],["3829907","LSS-58367","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Dear Legal Ops,\n\nPlease collect signatures the the 3 attached documents via SpotDraft:\n\nBolt - Ahto\nCounterparty - Wen Tzu-Wei ([+jasonwen@wenk-media.com+|mailto:jasonwen@wenk-media.com])\n\nPlease cc to the signature request also: [+annechen@wenk-media.com+|mailto:annechen@wenk-media.com]、[+lewischen@wenk-media.com+|mailto:lewischen@wenk-media.com]\n\nThank you in advance!\n\n\n\n[^WENK MEDIA x BOLT Taiwan｜媒體契約書(開帳戶)｜20260122 （英文版) (a12b6211-85b2-494d-8379-6bf01a308f97).pdf]\n[^WENK MEDIA x BOLT Taiwan｜媒體契約書(開帳戶)｜20260122 （中文版） (65ae6f83-88ae-45fb-a366-1c5ace68bcd2).pdf]\n[^WENK MEDIA x BOLT Taiwan｜LAP 2026Q1｜20260122 (1bf22120-8067-4ef3-80f6-9ed4eda1df53).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T10:37:07.699Z"],["3829908","LSS-61991","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","[^bodacc-RCS-B-949330807-20251014-09301MYG1371899-4859.pdf] _(99 kB)_","2026-01-22T10:37:23.290Z"],["3829909","DELIVERY-1230","DELIVERY","ionut.danila@bolt.eu","Ionuț Dănilă","26W3: *In Progress* - Backend: Implement Unified Distance-Based Ranges for City, Zone, and Merchant Layers:\n\n* Ongoing analysis of existing JSON schemas across all pricing layers to understand differences and constraints.\n* Actively working on defining an approach for migrating distance-based surcharges toward a unified distance-based range model (that currently exists only on our Experimentation platform), with the goal of improving consistency and feature parity across layers.","2026-01-22T10:37:25.027Z"],["3829912","PFI-837150","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","\n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T10:38:03.319Z"],["3829913","LSS-61668","LSS","pedro.alecrim@bolt.eu","Pedro Alecrim","That’s correct [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac], all good (/) ","2026-01-22T10:38:07.115Z"],["3829918","LSS-61982","LSS","elisabeth.gunnarsson@bolt.eu","Elisabeth Gunnarsson","I stand corrected: [~accountid:712020:7f47c2af-14e1-4206-a795-ac87cb906276] is correct in her observation. You can mark this ticket as closed and I’ll create a new one.","2026-01-22T10:38:50.793Z"],["3829919","LSS-54429","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Thank you [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] \n\n[~accountid:712020:f1cea5d5-ecbb-422c-b79c-3378c160b57c] Feel free to proceed with this initiative! ","2026-01-22T10:39:26.126Z"],["3829920","MKP-9901","MKP","artjom.brehhunov@bolt.eu","Artjom Brehhunov","There is a PR which might be related: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161333|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161333|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T10:39:41.266Z"],["3829922","PFI-836424","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, please, note invoice are issued for the services provided. All of the monthly invoices are available in the Invoices tab, if there’s a need for proof of payments, etc. Please, create a ticket to the Payments Tab.","2026-01-22T10:40:11.897Z"],["3829923","XP-3090","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","Just created this test and the required days duration is tooo long. This is Bucharest city and one of the highest order volume for Delivery and usually the days are less for this city.\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/tests/edit/14818|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/tests/edit/14818]\n\n_--_ *_@user-U02R5SFKWHW_*","2026-01-22T10:40:16.027Z"],["3829924","XP-3090","XP",null,"Slack","[Garret O'Connell|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6268ef8e429789006946b1ac] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CMET7BK2S/p1769073827038279?thread_ts=1769073824.076659&cid=CMET7BK2S|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CMET7BK2S/p1769073827038279?thread_ts=1769073824.076659&cid=CMET7BK2S|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-22T10:40:17.556Z"],["3829925","PFI-836424","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Partner Payments] Business made payment, but didn't reflect: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/306\n- [Customer Payments] Business had issues with their credit card: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/303\n\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/304\n\n[Billing] - Business invoicing and balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/305\n\n[Billing/Tax Tech]- Business invoice has not been reported (Fiscalized) : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-22T10:40:20.368Z"],["3829927","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] Kindly recreate it.\nMy assumption was that you were going to leave it on the working file. We will still flight our OOH after the other company takes theirs down.\nLast category would be named:\nBoda - It’s a two wheeler category(Motorbike in this case) In app the name is Boda\nPricing TZS 1,000\n","2026-01-22T10:40:49.146Z"],["3829930","PFI-836424","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Partner Payments] Business made payment, but didn't reflect: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/306\n- [Customer Payments] Business had issues with their credit card: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/303\n\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/304\n\n[Billing] - Business invoicing and balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/305\n\n[Billing/Tax Tech]- Business invoice has not been reported (Fiscalized) : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-22T10:41:24.857Z"],["3829931","LSS-61977","LSS","paula.pihelgas@bolt.eu","Paula Joanna Pihelgas","Law Firm onboarded ","2026-01-22T10:41:47.389Z"],["3829932","PFI-837153","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-22T10:41:48.404Z"],["3829933","LSS-61992","LSS","elisabeth.gunnarsson@bolt.eu","Elisabeth Gunnarsson","[^Bolt Operations OÜ - Åberopande av kapacitet.docx]\n\n","2026-01-22T10:42:11.049Z"],["3829935","HS-29095","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-22T10:43:01.845Z"],["3829937","LSS-61942","LSS","dovile.ligeikaite@bolt.eu","Dovile Ligeikaite","Hi [~accountid:5f0436f3b545e20015573888] there is a system issue thus I couldn’t. \nI did send the contract to [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-22T10:43:47.010Z"],["3829940","PFI-836431","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Tsotne, I’ve blocked 276932201’s cards and devices, since it seems to link with most other suspicious accounts as well - should provide sufficient friction for now.\nThanks for reporting.","2026-01-22T10:44:04.208Z"],["3829943","LSS-61993","LSS","elisabeth.gunnarsson@bolt.eu","Elisabeth Gunnarsson","[^Stockholm EventsCo Services AB - Åberopande av kapacitet.docx]\n[^Soomro Services AB - Åberopande av kapacitet.docx]\n[^Stockholm Svea Sverige Transport AB - Åberopande av kapacitet.docx]\n\n","2026-01-22T10:44:44.317Z"],["3829944","LSS-61928","LSS","reinis.levanovics@bolt.eu","Reinis Levanovičs","Hiii [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] 🌻 \n\nOki doki, understood 🤗 I only provided to them standard response, that we have received their document 😉 \n\n","2026-01-22T10:44:52.361Z"],["3829945","WEBSD-1498","WEBSD","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi! \n\nThanks for reaching out! Do I understand correct that you’re looking to update the information in the Support portal?\n\nIf so, please note Web team does not manage the support portal so please create a ticket in CS Knowledge Management Service Desk instead:\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2479|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2479|smart-link] \n\n_Please also note that due to capacity limits, CS Knowledge Management team will be focusing exclusively on the requests related to legal issues or content that is outdated. In all other cases, they will not be able to proceed with requests._","2026-01-22T10:45:05.391Z"],["3829948","LSS-60580","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nRegarding your questions, the current estimate is *$204,000 annually*.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-22T10:45:27.032Z"],["3829949","WD-22575","WD","lysette.ranne@bolt.eu","Lysette Ranne","Hi [~accountid:623c7881562ab90069f8f044] \n\nCan you please comment on what is currently missing in WD. ","2026-01-22T10:45:53.785Z"],["3829950","LSS-61994","LSS","elisabeth.gunnarsson@bolt.eu","Elisabeth Gunnarsson","[^Original Bilvård AB - Åberopande av kapacitet.docx]\n\n","2026-01-22T10:46:06.070Z"],["3829951","LSS-61991","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-22T10:46:07.320Z"],["3829952","MKP-9906","MKP","vivaksha.singh@bolt.eu","Vivaksha Singh","Possibly hand it over to riderX? It sounds like a good idea for them.","2026-01-22T10:47:05.185Z"],["3829953","PRF-1860","PRF","ash.syme@bolt.eu","Ash Syme","Hey [~accountid:5c2f512d36647b5b91017d0c]  - I’ve made a new column for Ireland in the docs *“Crowdin export visuals” sheet* and highlighted some text which will need to be updated in {color:#ff5630}*red*{color} (swapping the classic “ride” & “rider” to “trip” & “passenger”).\n\n*Just to reiterate which ones need updating:*\n\n* *Cell AD18:* update to “Offer more seats. Earn more per trip.”\n* *Cell AD21:* update to “Pick up more passengers with the same great taste.”\n* *Cell AD32:* update to “Earn more between trips.”\n* *Cell AD38:* update to “Fun trips for them.”\n\nLet me know if I perhaps need to mark these up somewhere else in the doc (unsure on if I’ve done this correctly as I can’t see any other highlighted red text in the doc).\n\nThank you so much!\nAsh\n","2026-01-22T10:47:26.516Z"],["3829954","RDS-1397","RDS","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/1622645185/Cancellation+Fee+Summary#Checks-by-Pricing|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/1622645185/Cancellation+Fee+Summary#Checks-by-Pricing|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T10:47:29.382Z"],["3829957","LSS-61925","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] , I have taken a look at the questionnaire/requirements and I see that these questions are technical and better answered by the Information Security team rather than the privacy team.\n\nCan you please reach out to [~accountid:5c987f2c0cf73c3215ff6aa7] and requet support?","2026-01-22T10:47:38.115Z"],["3829959","SUPX-2316","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Whoever picks it up can discuss within the team on which approach to take: \n* Time based (case close - X units of time)\n* Expire on case closing ","2026-01-22T10:47:45.245Z"],["3829961","LSS-61920","LSS","georgia.heathman@bolt.eu","Georgia Heathman","Hi [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] Just jumping in here. \n\n1. We do not need an electric scooter / bike charging rack in place. These will be a geo-fenced parking bay on site and can be moved on site as needed in agreement with the airport should any issues be identified during operation. Simply, yes it is a place where e-scooters and e-bikes can be parked safely on site for staff and visitors to the airport. Currently there is one agreed location, Others can be added at the airports guidance/discretion. \n\n2. That is what I think the airport will expect - that we will cover any damage to property caused by our vehicles while on site / airport land. \n\nThank you for picking this up for Liverpool 🙂 ","2026-01-22T10:47:56.765Z"],["3829964","PFI-836705","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Done, thanks!","2026-01-22T10:48:23.306Z"],["3829965","G3IOT-1214","G3IOT","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","If the main battery is present IOT can only enter low power mode if VSYS is above 4.4V. IOT does so to protect the modem. And indeed in this case IOT reports Vsys=4.395V volts making it very likely to be the reason for entering LPM. I double check bq25798 configuration","2026-01-22T10:48:25.184Z"],["3829966","PFI-836814","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Done, thanks!","2026-01-22T10:48:26.258Z"],["3829967","PFI-836844","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Done, thanks!","2026-01-22T10:48:29.002Z"],["3829970","MKP-9899","MKP","jan.stoltman@bolt.eu","Jan Stoltman","Pods using expire also seem to be using less CPU, but that might be a coincidence - to be verified\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 12.49.06.png|width=353,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 12.49.06.png\"!","2026-01-22T10:49:33.447Z"],["3829971","FPD-1002","FPD","matteo.casolari@bolt.eu","Matteo Casolari","RFC [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/fIBBuwE]","2026-01-22T10:49:51.251Z"],["3829972","SUPX-2313","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","[~accountid:631f27278738d3ca32254937] once you are back, can you provide some expected UX for reminders? 🙏 ","2026-01-22T10:49:52.010Z"],["3829976","LSS-59597","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:712020:e81c1984-54f1-46ce-bc81-864b3748de94] \nThank you for clarifying!\nI understand the urgency, so I’ll review the proposed clause shortly. Could you please grant me access to the document?","2026-01-22T10:50:59.762Z"],["3829978","DSR-3951","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T10:51:06.111Z"],["3829979","LSS-33345","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n# After aligning with Partner Payments and the business, I contacted Cellulant and included procurement in the discussion to encourage them to sign the DPA.\n# Cellulant promptly provided feedback on the DPA.\n# I reviewed the DPA and sent it back to Cellulant with updates. A few critical issues remain, particularly regarding the inclusion of SCCs in the DSA.\n\nStatus: Waiting for Cellulant's response.","2026-01-22T10:51:18.865Z"],["3829981","HS-28062","HS","alice.gorobets@bolt.eu","Alice Gorobets","the signed versions are in box","2026-01-22T10:51:37.440Z"],["3829982","HS-28164","HS","alice.gorobets@bolt.eu","Alice Gorobets","the signed versions are in box","2026-01-22T10:51:43.184Z"],["3829983","LSS-33345","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","[^Bolt_DPA_Cellulant_SCCs_Bolt_reviewed_22.01.2026.docx]\n[^Bolt_DPA (C-P)_Cellulant_SCCs-4.docx]\n\n","2026-01-22T10:51:55.753Z"],["3829984","PFI-836546","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","reissued the statement","2026-01-22T10:52:27.481Z"],["3829985","DSR-3871","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Driver is suspended due to someone else using his account, reported in [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1509108728/18?orderTryId=2898064788] and [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1439265034/18?orderTryId=2548075589].\nAppealing process in France [+here on this KB+|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/60855?country=global&language=en]\nIf the suspension was triggered by a rider report for ‘driver was not the same as app', inform the Driver that they may request reactivation using the [following link|https://bolt.eu/fr-fr/support/articles/26895/] 6 months after being blocked\"\nFor appeal: The rule is they can only ask to be reactivated +once+ after being terminated — even if they had multiple reports we might reactivate him. However, if they were terminated post-reactivation and asks to come back, the request will be rejected.\n*So even though the suspension is permanent and correct, he can appeal*","2026-01-22T10:52:42.082Z"],["3829986","WFM-10092","WFM","daniela.capatana@bolt-outsource.eu","Daniela Căpățână","they can’t access the order for a safety ticket because some of them only had the ‘'04 MM_Romania_Safety_Significant '’ assigned","2026-01-22T10:52:51.470Z"],["3829988","PFI-829363","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, is it still needs any help?","2026-01-22T10:53:25.425Z"],["3829989","RCE-372","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Alisher Matkurbanov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769079246110159]*{color}:\nHi <@U02JSL0KCQY>\nI've released the frequency changes\n{quote}","2026-01-22T10:54:20.038Z"],["3829991","LSS-61986","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[^Bank confirmation letter Unibank (Bolt Services AZ LLC) (f3f724be-4f92-43e1-8ee4-499f78735e5d).pdf]\n\n[~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] , hei! Please find the signed document(s) attached.","2026-01-22T10:54:39.490Z"],["3829995","LSS-61994","LSS","elisabeth.gunnarsson@bolt.eu","Elisabeth Gunnarsson","Found a wrong wording, sending new document to be signed.\n\n[^Original Bilvård AB - Åberopande av kapacitet (cf9e8af0-13b6-4ad7-bd9c-8c0a225edca0).docx]\n\n","2026-01-22T10:55:30.488Z"],["3829996","LSS-61997","LSS","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","[^initupload_220120261131.xml] _(2 kB)_","2026-01-22T10:55:30.169Z"],["3829998","PFI-836424","PFI","taechapart.intarasomwang@bolt.eu","Taechapart Intarasomwang","For your information, I know what I should do here. I've created this ticket to Payments not Billing, but Payments team said they won’t support this issue and forwarded the ticket to your team ([Slack|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01994U9SCB/p1768991661517659])\n\nThere's been back-and-forth many times between these two teams.\nCould you please help align on this issue and update me?","2026-01-22T10:55:54.533Z"],["3829999","PFI-836424","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-22T10:55:58.290Z"],["3830001","RCE-372","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769079372682069]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-372 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-22T10:56:26.019Z"],["3830004","PFI-836424","PFI","taechapart.intarasomwang@bolt.eu","Taechapart Intarasomwang","[~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] ","2026-01-22T10:56:39.660Z"],["3830005","LSS-61997","LSS","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","fyi for the other document I will submit separate ticket, as it concerns other company","2026-01-22T10:56:55.746Z"],["3830007","LSS-61993","LSS","elisabeth.gunnarsson@bolt.eu","Elisabeth Gunnarsson","Found a wrong wording, sending new document to be signed.\n\n[^Stockholm EventsCo Services AB - Åberopande av kapacitet (52613a9d-bbc2-4795-8f45-9900dea38dc9).docx]\n[^Soomro Services AB - Åberopande av kapacitet (470bc010-2cbb-4a44-a84f-e87fd4c9d052).docx]\n[^Stockholm Svea Sverige Transport AB - Åberopande av kapacitet (ef8a1a6e-f3c2-401a-ad9f-85873c1cdb09).docx]\n\n","2026-01-22T10:57:00.814Z"],["3830008","FPD-1558","FPD","matteo.casolari@bolt.eu","Matteo Casolari","PR has been merged to master. \n\nCurrently running backtest for current (v0.5.0 → {{s3://bolt-datascience-financial-modeling/LIVE/financial-planning-input-based-model/cycle=test_special_events/backtest_outputs/label=new_special_events_current/}}). Challenger will be run when this is over (v0.8.0).","2026-01-22T10:57:00.665Z"],["3830015","PFI-836546","PFI","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Thank you [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] ","2026-01-22T10:57:54.082Z"],["3830016","PFI-836546","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-22T10:57:57.602Z"],["3830017","LSS-61925","LSS","elisabeth.gunnarsson@bolt.eu","Elisabeth Gunnarsson","Thank you [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] ","2026-01-22T10:58:01.431Z"],["3830018","PAW-15087","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-22T10:58:09.026Z"],["3830021","WD-22626","WD","mihut.arsene@bolt.eu","Mihuț-Andrei Arsene","Closing this one as it is a duplicate of [+WD-22610+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22610]","2026-01-22T10:58:29.377Z"],["3830023","SUPX-2337","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","What about outbound cases that are created by the system. Eq. trip anomaly. Should CSAT be excluded for those cases as well?","2026-01-22T10:58:48.981Z"],["3830024","LSS-61987","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] , can you look into this? It seems to me that this is a DSR with a threat to escalate. We just need to undertand what has happened, and then handle the DSR as per our process. If you need any details of what we might have shared or need context about the driver - I added you to [#uk-privacy|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C04RBMX5B24] channel (it’s a bit dormant but the UK Ops and Legal teams are there)","2026-01-22T10:58:50.626Z"],["3830026","LSS-61998","LSS","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","[^Nicchiano Sp. z o.o. - Voluntary Disclosure_NIP-8_update.pdf] _(35 kB)_","2026-01-22T10:58:56.516Z"],["3830027","LSS-61734","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","1st - address the individual drivers - for those we can safely say that the T&Cs apply and I understand that on top of those there is an email sent to the individual drivers that confirm the incentives. \n\nHow they communicate the incentive to indiidual drivers?\n\nif they want to change - hopefully we dont need to ammend the T&Cs, but only the communication.\n\nIf it is a central initiative, Malta is not hight risk.\n\nFor fleet:\n\nThey have fleet branding agreements.\n\nThe vehicle belongs to the fleet, right? (confirm). Withing the fleets do we only have drivers who don’t own the car, being the car owned by the fleet?\n\nAssuming the fleet owns the car, is not that risky. KPI’s will need to be per car.\n\nShow them the document and ask how they currently fill it in.\n\nIf they want to add KPIs, this template need to be amended.\n\nBut if they say that this is central level, ask Luke how this central project is being tacklet? are there templates?","2026-01-22T10:59:08.304Z"],["3830028","PFI-836435","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Tsotne, this case seems to have been already handled on April last year. In cases when there’s suspicious relations, but no real activity, no need to raise these.\nIf you’ve gotten explicit reports regarding this (CS escalations, payment problems), then please ping me in this ticket again, and I’ll have a look.\nThank you!","2026-01-22T10:59:13.237Z"],["3830029","LSS-61999","LSS","karen.mwarari@bolt.eu","Karen Mwarari","[^Signed_SOP_25 (1).pdf] _(861 kB)_\n\n[^Bolt Mail - Fwd_ Pizza Inn _ Pizza Inn Delivery SOPs for Sign-off.pdf] _(595 kB)_","2026-01-22T11:00:01.711Z"],["3830031","MKP-9899","MKP","jan.stoltman@bolt.eu","Jan Stoltman","In general, Expire seems to bring some benefit. Seems like it’s worth investigating further.\n\nAverage across all pods with and without Expire over the same time period:\n\nWith Expire:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 12.58.13.png|width=991,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 12.58.13.png\"!\n\nWithout Expire:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 12.57.53.png|width=998,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 12.57.53.png\"!","2026-01-22T11:00:16.936Z"],["3830037","LSS-61999","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-22T11:01:42.143Z"],["3830038","WFM-10092","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","Users have all the necessary roles","2026-01-22T11:01:58.009Z"],["3830040","WFM-10087","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:620507bdff9289006eec9b3a]!\r\n\r\nPlay mode enabled for the agent mentioned above.\r\n\r\nHave a great day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-22T11:03:01.362Z"],["3830041","WFM-10088","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:620507bdff9289006eec9b3a]!\r\n\r\nPlay mode enabled for the agent mentioned above.\r\n\r\nHave a great day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-22T11:03:10.175Z"],["3830042","WFM-10089","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:620507bdff9289006eec9b3a]!\r\n\r\nPlay mode enabled for the agent mentioned above.\r\n\r\nHave a great day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-22T11:03:24.101Z"],["3830043","SUPX-2337","SUPX","teele.raudik@bolt.eu","Teele Raudik","That is a bit of different situation since Trip Anomaly and Emergency Assist tickets do have a high false positive rate. However, I think it can remain as is. But, can leave final judgement to [@thomas.schwalm|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:9cbaca4a-0e28-45d2-ae46-36c858f4d829] and others","2026-01-22T11:03:25.434Z"],["3830045","LSS-61774","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:db41f6cc-b777-4b3f-961b-09bab7b9da50] in addition to the feedback shared by Elisabetta and Gabriele, as discussed, please find hereafter a ticker from Etienne which relates to the same question and can help for inspiration to draft the email: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-53684|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-53684|smart-link] (not exactly the same, but relevant).\n\nThank you","2026-01-22T11:03:28.699Z"],["3830046","SUPX-2337","SUPX","pranav.dineshkumar@bolt.eu","Pranav Dinesh Kumar","[@fred.gehrke|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63b84562082abdd71bb7757c] I think we can stop asking CSAT for all outbound cases (not limited to safety). What say?","2026-01-22T11:03:42.816Z"],["3830047","RISK2-3127","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","*Guidance:*\n\n* Privacy team + our team has access to edit documents and add docs to RCMS drive and to RCMS. Otherwise the access is limited to our team *only* to limit unapproved documents from being uploaded to the public space. \n* Doc versions need to be added to RCMS drive for version control and for the ability to edit documents between multiple stakeholders:[https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/16lz5n7yPGt_1eRiEd0KZfqpwJuLT_r4v|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/16lz5n7yPGt_1eRiEd0KZfqpwJuLT_r4v|smart-link] \n** If a new document needs to be created, *the user must first make a copy of the document,* so we preserve the earlier version. The old version must be moved to *Archived* docs folder in the drive.\n* Docs need to be uploaded to Cognito for record-keeping:\n** [https://www.cognitoforms.com/bolttechnologyoü/governancedocumentmanagementdatabase/1-all-entries|https://www.cognitoforms.com/bolttechnologyo%C3%BC/governancedocumentmanagementdatabase/1-all-entries]\n* Correct *labels* need to be added to each RCMS Confluence page, for example 1. Policy labels are {{ims}} and {{policy}}, and 2. Compliance Management labels are {{compliance-management}} and {{ims}}.\n* Each page needs to have *Page Properties* section, so it shows up to[ +Document Control Registry+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IMS/pages/5730828769/Document+Control+Register+-+1.+Policy] automatically and shows next review/last update dates\n* Generally for updating documents, we follow the [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IMS/pages/4860871096/Risk+and+Compliance+Document+Management+Procedure+-+RCMS-PRO-03.01|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IMS/pages/4860871096/Risk+and+Compliance+Document+Management+Procedure+-+RCMS-PRO-03.01|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T11:03:51.892Z"],["3830049","RISK2-3127","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","cc [~accountid:712020:b0d06119-b7c8-4491-85a9-a5cb1e609b96] ","2026-01-22T11:03:58.663Z"],["3830050","CCM-22295","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey Gabija 👋 \n\nInstructor access given. 🌷 \n\nBest,\n\nIrena","2026-01-22T11:04:28.907Z"],["3830051","SUPX-2337","SUPX","pranav.dineshkumar@bolt.eu","Pranav Dinesh Kumar","{quote}What about outbound cases that are created by the system. Eq. trip anomaly. Should CSAT be excluded for those cases as well?{quote}\n\nI reckon we should. I dont see a merit in asking about quality of support experience when someone is being asked for a case that we had created.","2026-01-22T11:04:37.329Z"],["3830054","CSDA-304","CSDA","ramin.karimov@bolt.eu","Ramin Karimov","Worked now, thanks a lot!","2026-01-22T11:05:03.563Z"],["3830056","MKP-9910","MKP","daniil.popov@bolt.eu","Daniil Popov","*@user-U01ADCL71QQ* can you check and replicate it if needed?","2026-01-22T11:05:30.534Z"],["3830058","MKP-9910","MKP",null,"Slack","[Daniil Popov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f4905b29aa9650046196c33] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04SLV3GT5K/p1769078064226259?thread_ts=1769001640.256639&cid=C04SLV3GT5K|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04SLV3GT5K/p1769078064226259?thread_ts=1769001640.256639&cid=C04SLV3GT5K|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-22T11:05:31.583Z"],["3830059","DSR-3953","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T11:06:07.111Z"],["3830060","PFI-835963","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! I’m not sure why the payout for 22.12 was bigger - I know that Partner Payments have a system that prevents the balance from turning negative due to payouts, but this shouldn’t cause the payment to be bigger. I see that this payment is processed significantly later than usually. I recommend to ask Partner Payments to reopen the ticket and check from their side (as it seems like the answer was given by AI, so may not be a 100% accurate). Right now I don’t really have any reason to believe the issue is with the balance. ","2026-01-22T11:06:07.213Z"],["3830063","PFI-836588","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Valeria, due to elevated risk associated with this card, additional verification is required.\n\nTo add and use a new card on a Family account, the payment method needs to be verified via 3DS. We recommend the user configure their card with their bank to always “require confirmation” or “always enforce SCA”, and then complete a transaction in-app or attempt to add the card again. This allows us to confirm a legitimate card addition and/or payment attempt.\nThank you!","2026-01-22T11:07:04.486Z"],["3830064","L10N-29500","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29499](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29499)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T11:07:09.568Z"],["3830065","L10N-29501","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29499](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29499)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T11:07:10.607Z"],["3830066","L10N-29504","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks upd