 of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29499](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29499)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T11:07:57.722Z"],["3830083","WEBSD-1492","WEBSD","loi.nguyen@bolt.eu","Loi Nguyen","Please have this one done ideally by the end of this week Fri 24 Jan thank you.","2026-01-22T11:08:13.184Z"],["3830084","WD-22481","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Created Security Group - Bolt Inventory Analyst Org Group - by default gives membership to:\n\n* Bolt Micromobility (Tomas Veloso)\n* Micromobility Business Analytics (Dmitri Pivovarov (Inherited))\n* Rentals Hardware (Ardo Reinsalu)\n\nand all subordinates under them.\n\nCreated Security Group - Bolt Aggregated Inventory Analyst and copied all of the Inventory Analyst domain security policies to it. It’s an intersection between role Inventory Analyst and org Bolt Inventory Analyst Org Group groups. \nIt’s meant to be assigned as security group in all of the custom reports. \n\nIn future Inventory Analyst will become a group where we assign people outside of these organisation like Bolt Food, Finance Controlling, Procurement, etc. \n\nNext week in SBX, I will try to remove the domain security policies of Inventory Analyst to confirm that Bolt Aggregated one are working. \n\n[~accountid:627aae199311100068a00836] I’ll reach out to you in Slack DM to test out the solution. ","2026-01-22T11:08:15.293Z"],["3830085","CCM-22296","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey Gabija 👋 \n\nEnrolled this as well. I gave learner access. Let me know if Alexandra needs instructor one.\n\nBest,\nIrena","2026-01-22T11:08:28.633Z"],["3830088","PFI-823286","PFI","tiberiu.dosescu@bolt.eu","Tiberiu-Valeriu Dosescu","Hello, \n\nThe fleet claims the transfer was not returned. Could you please provide the proof of payment to send to him? \n\nThank you! ","2026-01-22T11:08:49.870Z"],["3830090","GRWA-1533","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","[fleet|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0682D79LQG/p1769070232758279?thread_ts=1762948773.578879&cid=C0682D79LQG] has been added","2026-01-22T11:09:11.718Z"],["3830091","CSDA-304","CSDA","roman.trohhalev@bolt.eu","Roman Trohhalev","Glad I was able to help, have a nice day!","2026-01-22T11:10:05.743Z"],["3830093","DRX-28267","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DA.127.0 (1512) Firebase build on Samsung A12, OS:13 and Google Pixel 8 Pro, OS:16\n\n||Samsung A12||Pixel 8 Pro||\n|!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 12.59.57.png|width=516,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 12.59.57.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 13.08.57.png|width=516,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 13.08.57.png\"!|","2026-01-22T11:10:10.779Z"],["3830094","PFI-837173","PFI","surachet.chaiwongkhajorn@bolt-outsource.eu","Surachet Chaiwongkhajorn","!image-20260122-110742.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260122-110753.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T11:10:11.359Z"],["3830095","DPM-2313","DPM","hanno.narvik@bolt.eu","Hanno Narvik","[~accountid:62b2cf2c99eafa602d88ec9e] Please review if this is something like you were interested in? [^daily_failure_reasons_with_success_failure_totals.xlsx] ","2026-01-22T11:10:13.630Z"],["3830096","DRX-28207","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-28267 has been resolved","2026-01-22T11:10:17.706Z"],["3830100","LSS-58409","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:793bd952-a372-4264-98c5-05f34ecedce8],\n\nPlease find below the link to the *Special Conditions reflecting the deviations agreed with the client*. Feel free to share the document with the client.\n\nMany thanks!\n\n[Special Conditions|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NvgBj18ysO0ObExBzqqAlz_z08C9NIcz/edit]","2026-01-22T11:11:10.049Z"],["3830102","G3IOT-1214","G3IOT","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","Vsys overshoot occurs when IOT tries to charge BB","2026-01-22T11:11:13.454Z"],["3830103","WEB-9954","WEB","samuel.oyekeye@bolt.eu","Samuel Oluseyi Oyekeye","[~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] thanks for the update\nFor no.2 can you maybe add a SS of the logo youre referring to?","2026-01-22T11:11:18.907Z"],["3830108","WD-22598","WD","andreea.moisoi@bolt.eu","Andreea Moisoi","Hey, it works for both of them, they were able to access it from Okta. Thank you1","2026-01-22T11:12:51.794Z"],["3830113","GRWA-1534","GRWA","andrea.santonastaso@bolt.eu","Andrea Santonastaso","[https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/3795267621853438?o=2472566184436351|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/3795267621853438?o=2472566184436351]","2026-01-22T11:14:39.791Z"],["3830115","CCM-22297","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey Gustav 👋 \n\nCan you please send the template that was advised, from the Supplier Handbook? It needs to be sent in CSV or XLSX form.\n\nWe need more information about new joiners, from which vertical they are supporting to which exact onboarding they need (correct name of the course) and their correct email address.\n\nWe cannot work with a picture you sent. Also, these are transcom emails, and we need their login emails that end with @bolt-outsource.eu\n\nDo let me know if you need help with finding the template in the Supplier Handbook. 🙌 \n\n\nBest,\nIrena","2026-01-22T11:15:43.547Z"],["3830116","LSS-61638","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","The council has notified us that a physical office is not needed and we can source a virtual one instead therefore the agreement does not need to be signed.","2026-01-22T11:15:58.794Z"],["3830118","PFI-832747","PFI","yusif.mehdiyev@bolt-outsource.eu","Yusif Mehdiyev","the driver account is hidden now","2026-01-22T11:16:26.350Z"],["3830124","PFI-835421","PFI","izabela.adamiec@bolt.eu","Izabela Rosińska","Hi [~accountid:5f896b8ee357dd006e937d7b] \n\nI reached out to the Billing team  ([PFI-835963|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-835963]) and from their side there is no reason to suspect this is issue with the balance. \n\nCould you please check on your side these payouts, so that I can reply to the Partner? 🙏 \n\n\n\nThanks, Iza ","2026-01-22T11:18:10.749Z"],["3830125","WD-22598","WD","mihut.arsene@bolt.eu","Mihuț-Andrei Arsene","HeyyAndreea,\n\nGreat news! In this case, I’ll proceed to close the ticket. Feel free to reach out for any questions or issues!\n\nMany thanks,\n\nMihut","2026-01-22T11:18:14.551Z"],["3830126","PFI-825654","PFI","marvellous.paul@bolt-outsource.eu","Marvellous Paul","Hi Team,\n\nWe are still expecting a feedback from you. ","2026-01-22T11:18:16.251Z"],["3830127","SREDESK-7420","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Hi Wisutta,\n\nIT applied the Okta change and I granted your Zero Trust permission for Live and Prelive CMS.","2026-01-22T11:18:16.705Z"],["3830129","CCM-22299","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey Nattawoot 👋 \n\nOnboarding assigned. 🌷 \n\nBest,\nIrena","2026-01-22T11:18:20.772Z"],["3830130","FPD-1505","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","Had a first try at adding tests for adjustments with Claudio’s help, but I did not work quite well. Will try again, but if a proper testing functionality is not able to be added to the library, I’ll test it outside of the codebase and share the results - my only concern is if adjustments will keep on working nicely for partner activations / churns (in a first test they did, but I’ll have to double check that).","2026-01-22T11:18:22.308Z"],["3830132","IDC-2251","IDC","adil.ansar@bolt.eu","Mohammad Adil Ansar","Why is it a bug though? [~accountid:633d44459b32cfef93291595] ","2026-01-22T11:19:25.258Z"],["3830136","GRWA-1537","GRWA","andrea.santonastaso@bolt.eu","Andrea Santonastaso","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1zHBKpsJnXz0TfLBpEmTSEeMzpWcmzXOdvZh_xV7omkc/edit?gid=56263213#gid=56263213|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1zHBKpsJnXz0TfLBpEmTSEeMzpWcmzXOdvZh_xV7omkc/edit?gid=56263213#gid=56263213]","2026-01-22T11:19:52.426Z"],["3830137","BDB-1562","BDB","eva.dieudonne@bolt.eu","Eva Dieudonné","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Fb12k8Aw4HkYYs01Ogca87JmTs-uikAwO5xP1-ibyBM/edit?gid=327468177#gid=327468177|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Fb12k8Aw4HkYYs01Ogca87JmTs-uikAwO5xP1-ibyBM/edit?gid=327468177#gid=327468177|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T11:20:03.894Z"],["3830138","CAMLE-9892","CAMLE","uladzislau.tolkach@bolt.eu","Uladzislau Tolkach","Increased it again, now properly :crossed_fingers:","2026-01-22T11:20:16.554Z"],["3830140","GRWA-1536","GRWA","andrea.santonastaso@bolt.eu","Andrea Santonastaso","[https://gs-gpt-3598988355446810.aws.databricksapps.com/|https://gs-gpt-3598988355446810.aws.databricksapps.com/]","2026-01-22T11:20:25.688Z"],["3830142","DSR-3577","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","[~accountid:712020:50057dc7-d3c1-4f13-9a33-a34da3415c60] This is outside my scope. I am not familiar with this field 🙂 ","2026-01-22T11:20:50.509Z"],["3830146","CAMLE-9892","CAMLE","roland.gheorghe@bolt.eu","Roland Gheorghe","user confirmed that the issue is fixed. Thank you!!","2026-01-22T11:22:13.696Z"],["3830147","CAMLE-9892","CAMLE","uladzislau.tolkach@bolt.eu","Uladzislau Tolkach","woah, it was quick!","2026-01-22T11:22:23.997Z"],["3830148","MVRT-1516","MVRT","kyrylo.matiupatenko@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Matiupatenko","Sorry for stepping in, it’s an offline thingy 😅 \n\nI’d suggest:\n\n*Delivery hours extended* ⏰\nFrom now on, Bolt Food in Sofia delivers from 9:30 to 1 a.m.","2026-01-22T11:22:35.101Z"],["3830150","L10N-29537","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29499](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29499)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T11:22:41.394Z"],["3830151","CAMLE-9892","CAMLE","roland.gheorghe@bolt.eu","Roland Gheorghe","it was one of our colleagues :smile: :fastparrot:","2026-01-22T11:22:50.827Z"],["3830152","PFI-837182","PFI","emmanuella.jecteyasare@bolt.eu","Emmanuella Jectey-Asare","!165397D1-056B-4E87-8AB0-678EB33E55B7.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T11:23:15.410Z"],["3830153","LSS-61757","LSS","liam.wentworth@bolt.eu","Liam Wentworth","@loi looks good on my side. ","2026-01-22T11:23:25.505Z"],["3830154","PAW-15088","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @xenJ\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161547\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-22 11:23:30 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-22T11:23:30.788Z"],["3830158","DPM-2313","DPM","pawel.dabrowski@bolt.eu","Paweł Dąbrowski","So majority is unknown error as well as for the incorrect doc can we also have more granularity what is wrong?\n\nfyi: [~accountid:712020:a8e993c7-e089-4c7f-96d3-8d2e1ee4caa6] ","2026-01-22T11:24:06.313Z"],["3830159","SREDESK-7453","SREDESK","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","Hey! I’ve created a group for your team in AWS and granted you access to the bucket. I had to truncate the team name a bit because of the group name length limit.\n\nChanges are applied, you should have the AWS IAM Identity Center application available in Okta (might need to manually open [bolt.okta.com|http://bolt.okta.com] the first time)\n\nPR for context: [https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15503/changes|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15503/changes] ","2026-01-22T11:24:42.114Z"],["3830162","LSS-61982","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Thanks [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] will close this one! ","2026-01-22T11:25:09.546Z"],["3830163","PFI-826328","PFI","aleksandr.maslov@bolt-outsource.eu","Aleksandr Maslov","Dear, Commerce team, could you please check if we can assist the customer. Driver claims to have not received pay after price review for [this order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2310354718/1?orderTryId=2957530205]. I cannot find this order in the [driver's rides for the day|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start_timestamp%22%3A1766354400%2C%22end_timestamp%22%3A1766440800%2C%22all_order_try_states%22%3Atrue%2C%22price_review_start_ts%22%3A1766354400%2C%22price_review_end_ts%22%3A1766440800%2C%22driver_id%22%3A7092033%2C%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22city_id%22%3A1%7D%7D] and it is unclear why the compensation was not added to his balance. Could you please check and advice?","2026-01-22T11:25:23.736Z"],["3830164","LSS-61984","LSS","stanislaw.staniszewski@bolt.eu","Stanisław Staniszewski","[^Umowa Aleco -  Bolt .pdf]\n[^Umowa Aleco - Bolt .docx]\n\nSharing the agreement here with completed details. The counterparty is ok with electronic signature. \n\nThank you! ","2026-01-22T11:25:25.519Z"],["3830165","L10N-29542","L10N","anna.cherentcova@bolt.eu","Anna Cherentcova","I've noticed again that Brand/Creative teams are super focused on alignment with local teams and keep considering their review as part of Localisation flow. [Leaving it here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0AA0BGJ6EN/p1768994913362539] as well for our call, or for the future.","2026-01-22T11:25:25.430Z"],["3830166","L10N-29542","L10N",null,"Slack","[Anna Cherentcova|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/638713eb8fd2d2d5f130908e] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07USTR52JG/p1768997149737829?thread_ts=1768997149.737829&cid=C07USTR52JG|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07USTR52JG/p1768997149737829?thread_ts=1768997149.737829&cid=C07USTR52JG|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-22T11:25:26.435Z"],["3830167","L10N-29542","L10N","oksana.naidjonova@bolt.eu","Oksana Naidjonova","Important topic for sure. We should park it somewhere for the future when we have capacity to start solving this","2026-01-22T11:25:26.986Z"],["3830168","L10N-29542","L10N","anna.cherentcova@bolt.eu","Anna Cherentcova","I'll start marking such items in the channel with :todo1: emoji, so we could search for them later (there seems to be a search by emoji tool somewhere on Slack)","2026-01-22T11:25:27.656Z"],["3830169","L10N-29542","L10N","oksana.naidjonova@bolt.eu","Oksana Naidjonova","We can also use Jira integration","2026-01-22T11:25:28.526Z"],["3830170","L10N-29542","L10N","oksana.naidjonova@bolt.eu","Oksana Naidjonova","To park it in our L10n software project","2026-01-22T11:25:29.088Z"],["3830171","L10N-29542","L10N","anna.cherentcova@bolt.eu","Anna Cherentcova","Hmm I haven't tried that... Maybe I can create a task/project in LS Operations","2026-01-22T11:25:29.673Z"],["3830172","L10N-29542","L10N","oksana.naidjonova@bolt.eu","Oksana Naidjonova","Try it out! :slightly_smiling_face: This (below) + Create issue from (Jira..)\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AAN865ALR/screenshot_2026-01-22_at_11.21.02.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AAN865ALR/screenshot_2026-01-22_at_11.21.02.png|smart-link]","2026-01-22T11:25:30.621Z"],["3830173","L10N-29542","L10N","oksana.naidjonova@bolt.eu","Oksana Naidjonova","pls tag with \"l10n-ops\"","2026-01-22T11:25:31.510Z"],["3830174","L10N-29542","L10N","anna.cherentcova@bolt.eu","Anna Cherentcova","Create Jira issue gets skipped for me, maybe I should somehow configure it on Jira first? Or are you using another option, like Jira Clowd :jira-1:?\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AAD0AKPS8/screenshot_2026-01-22_at_11.29.45___am.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AAD0AKPS8/screenshot_2026-01-22_at_11.29.45___am.png|smart-link]\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9TUVATP1/screenshot_2026-01-22_at_11.32.04___am.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9TUVATP1/screenshot_2026-01-22_at_11.32.04___am.png|smart-link]","2026-01-22T11:25:32.391Z"],["3830175","L10N-29542","L10N","oksana.naidjonova@bolt.eu","Oksana Naidjonova","Yup, that's the one. Here's my earlier announcement:\n\n{quote}To turn a thread into a Jira ticket: click :three-dots: on the support request, ={quote}\n\n> :jira-1:{{Create issue from Jira cloud}} => create a ticket. Localisation's Jira board is {{L10N}}.","2026-01-22T11:25:33.295Z"],["3830176","L10N-29542","L10N","oksana.naidjonova@bolt.eu","Oksana Naidjonova","Btw, headsup: I would like ALL of localisation team soon start using our own Jira SP for our ops tasks + managing your todo list.\n\nI don't know how you guys stay on top of your todo's, but mine are a MESS - -hundred- thousand pages long by now, and it's impossible to stay on top of priorities, as new ones fly in from left and right every day.\nHowever, if I took the effort to move all my todos into Jira, I'd be able to show my boss the queue, -scare him shitless- and ask for input on what do I drop or keep. Or reassign - as each of us is just one person and cannot bear the responsibility of feeling inadequate on a daily basis, due to a severely understaffed team","2026-01-22T11:25:33.927Z"],["3830177","L10N-29542","L10N","oksana.naidjonova@bolt.eu","Oksana Naidjonova","Not pushing this onto you (or me) yet, but we need to get there :awkward_monkey_look: for our own sanity's sake","2026-01-22T11:25:34.579Z"],["3830178","L10N-29542","L10N","gabriele.vlasova@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Vlasova","I agree 100%! I've been trying to make myself do it for a long time, but there's just no muscle memory for that. But it's my goal for this Q!","2026-01-22T11:25:35.392Z"],["3830179","L10N-29542","L10N","oksana.naidjonova@bolt.eu","Oksana Naidjonova","I'll arrange a session with [@vincenzo.rinella|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:d4126fc0-85ff-45d4-af88-bc851d5b32bc] for us, for best practise tips and some hands-on support","2026-01-22T11:25:36.270Z"],["3830180","L10N-29542","L10N","anna.cherentcova@bolt.eu","Anna Cherentcova","Yeah, fact! I wake up at 4am remembering the stuff I forgot to get to last night, and it's not helping..","2026-01-22T11:25:36.914Z"],["3830181","LSS-56592","LSS","andy.effiong@bolt.eu","Andy Effiong","[~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] Hi Elina, this has now been sent for signature","2026-01-22T11:26:02.515Z"],["3830183","LSS-62002","LSS","gayanjalie.dissanayake@bolt.eu","Gayanjalie Dissanayake","[^Bolt_Proposal for PCI DSS Certification_06.11.2025_2026 V1.pdf] _(1.10 MB)_","2026-01-22T11:26:32.029Z"],["3830184","LSS-62002","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nGayanjalie Dissanayake has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-22T11:26:33.409Z"],["3830185","IDC-2932","IDC","sergei.mironenko@bolt.eu","Sergei Mironenko","Discussed with Delivery Logistics team. [~accountid:615d633864ff010071607828] is ready to provide us with an event triggered at upper bound of originally estimated ETA.\n\n[~accountid:63d0ecc2f386bda5dcab9d6e] Delivery Logistics needs to know when we will start working on this.","2026-01-22T11:27:07.105Z"],["3830186","PFI-837185","PFI","lerato.kekana@bolt.eu","Lerato Mahlako Kekana","[^bolt payment 2.pdf]","2026-01-22T11:27:22.105Z"],["3830187","HS-29273","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Employee cancelled.","2026-01-22T11:27:30.496Z"],["3830189","DPM-2313","DPM","hanno.narvik@bolt.eu","Hanno Narvik","[~accountid:621f66f84160640069c66ff4] biggest majority is {{IVALID_ARGUMENT (9005)}} which from what I noticed from the logs is most often just due to some non-gdrive menu link, one example:\n\n{noformat}{\n  \"error\": \"BoltError: INVALID_ARGUMENT(9005)\",\n  \"menuUrl\": \"https://glovoapp.com/uk/ua/khmelnytskyi/stores/elbas-khm\",\n  \"providerId\": 187156,\n  \"s3FolderUri\": null,\n  \"vendorId\": 139416{noformat}\n\nJust noticed that Jira does terrible job showing xlsx preview, it is better to download the file.","2026-01-22T11:28:23.987Z"],["3830190","LSS-58970","LSS","sandra.bergstrom@bolt.eu","Sandra Bergström","Thanks for the additional review, [~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3]!\n\n{quote}I saw that you wrote that Legal should check “the use of average benchmarks”, could you clarify a bit on which benchmarks? {quote}\n\nWhere is this stated, sorry?\n\n\n{quote}I see that the script for the UGC creators says “*Note:* To get the most out of these videos, we recommend including a driver where possible.” Could you expand a bit more on why this is beneficial? If this is necessary, we might need some extra guidelines to ensure that the drivers don’t make any statements making it seem like they represent Bolt or Bolt’s opinions.{quote}\n\nSure. The idea is to make the videos feel more natural/authentic. In addition, we always aim to include both the rider and driver perspectives to promote both demand and supply.\n\nJust as a quick heads-up: the drivers will most likely not be speaking, they’ll simply be visible for a few seconds. If we were to include any spoken lines from drivers, we would of course provide clear guidance on do’s and don’ts.\n\n{quote}Do we have any contracts we enter into with the UGC creators, or do we only send them the script?{quote}\n\nIn the past, we’ve used the global creator agreement template, which I’d suggest we use for this campaign as well.\n\n{quote}Will we be pre-approving the videos before the creators post them online?{quote}\n\nYes, this is part of our standard process 😊\n\n{quote}Added the privacy team to the ticket as I’m not sure how consent is handled when these UGC creators involve other persons in their videos - do we have a form we send to them for them to use? Do we collect this form from them afterwards?{quote}\n\nIn general, the creators have been responsible for handling those consents. For example, in previous vox-pop formats, we provided them with agreements, which they then had participants sign before appearing in the videos.\n\n","2026-01-22T11:28:26.734Z"],["3830191","PFI-837187","PFI","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 14.28.14.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T11:28:44.779Z"],["3830194","SREDESK-7440","SREDESK","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","Hello! You should have now access to the Blog CMS ([cms.bolt.eu|http://cms.bolt.eu]), like the rest of your team.","2026-01-22T11:29:24.925Z"],["3830195","DSR-3057","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Letter and report has been sent (/) ","2026-01-22T11:29:45.515Z"],["3830199","DPM-2313","DPM","pawel.dabrowski@bolt.eu","Paweł Dąbrowski","[~accountid:60950a25539c14006ae92e40] ok so in this case menu link is competitor not a file > competition links OCR should be triggered when we can it ready 🙂 ","2026-01-22T11:30:45.859Z"],["3830202","PFI-837188","PFI","lerato.kekana@bolt.eu","Lerato Mahlako Kekana","[^bolt payment 1 (a9ea8eab-cd0c-41d2-983a-7ec04793c0c2).pdf]","2026-01-22T11:31:31.049Z"],["3830203","BDB-1561","BDB","mario.kartezi@bolt.eu","Mario Kartezi","[~accountid:5d289a7c3e09b40c262cfaa9] Here’s the slide: [https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1M_XZbw7mdXgCGtZNDCAuSoEog16CM8tlaSb7QNSAsHE/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1M_XZbw7mdXgCGtZNDCAuSoEog16CM8tlaSb7QNSAsHE/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T11:32:53.750Z"],["3830204","GRWA-1541","GRWA","andrea.santonastaso@bolt.eu","Andrea Santonastaso","W3: first iteration fails due to model training time constraints and lack of variability in past performance data.","2026-01-22T11:33:13.809Z"],["3830205","CNT-474","CNT","kristjan.konsap@bolt.eu","Kristjan-Johannes Konsap","[~accountid:610a6c97ec92ab0070d4d852] Please check: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1n0-13PdKqFaVRL4J9E4aWsS_U1OHA2oKIvAly8DFTuQ/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1n0-13PdKqFaVRL4J9E4aWsS_U1OHA2oKIvAly8DFTuQ/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] It should be 2610 characters at the moment\n\n\nI'm guessing you’d like to publish it next week? Then our editors could also take a look. I’m thinking Tuesday should be doable.","2026-01-22T11:33:31.600Z"],["3830206","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","[@shubham.singh|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/623194c0442e0e0069ed229c] PingCAP support is asking us to try bumping up TTL rate limiting temporarily to test. WDYT? Is it ok?\n\n{quote} Do you think it’s okay to temporarily increase these parameters tonight to improve TTL efficiency? Observe overnight to see if the problem resolves?\n```| tidb_ttl_delete_batch_size              | 100         --{quote}\n\n>   200\n\n{quote}| tidb_ttl_delete_worker_count            | 4           --{quote}\n\n>   8\n\n{quote}| tidb_ttl_scan_batch_size                | 500         --{quote}\n\n>   1020\n\n{quote}| tidb_ttl_scan_worker_count              | 4           --{quote}\n\n>   8```\n\n[https://tidb.support.pingcap.com/servicedesk/customer/portal/5/EMID-10067|https://tidb.support.pingcap.com/servicedesk/customer/portal/5/EMID-10067]","2026-01-22T11:33:31.652Z"],["3830208","MVRT-1514","MVRT","anton.sljussarev@bolt.eu","Anton Sljussarev","[~accountid:623de187d32a94006a658c4a] When it was increased? In Jan?","2026-01-22T11:33:36.464Z"],["3830209","LSS-61723","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:1d0a34aa-e1ae-4c55-bae7-010cdaef89e3] !\n\n[^RO, Bolt x Adrian Butușină, Christmas campaign, Dec 2025 .docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-22T11:33:58.744Z"],["3830210","DO-5824","DO","mikhail.kliasheu@bolt.eu","Mikhail Kliasheu","Hi! Could you pls provide a link to the notebook/sql-editor you are using to query it?","2026-01-22T11:34:09.660Z"],["3830211","PFI-837195","PFI","aviansarah.abraham@bolt.eu","Avian Abraham","!WhatsApp Image 2026-01-16 at 17.13.29.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T11:34:11.777Z"],["3830216","RS-1976","RS","karolina.jedrzejczak@bolt.eu","Karolina Jędrzejczak","[^Bolt BLS-AED 4h 01-2026 KG.pdf]\n\n[^Oferta Medykszkolenia.pdf]","2026-01-22T11:34:32.148Z"],["3830217","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","Yeah , please go ahead, just keep an eye on the CDC lag if it goes up then rate limit . ","2026-01-22T11:35:21.653Z"],["3830219","DRX-28237","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DA.127.0 (1512) Firebase build on Samsung A12, OS:13 and Google Pixel 8 Pro, OS:16\n\n|!20260122_132053.jpg|width=338,alt=\"20260122_132053.jpg\"!|!20260122_132101.jpg|width=338,alt=\"20260122_132101.jpg\"!|!20260122_132113.jpg|width=338,alt=\"20260122_132113.jpg\"!|","2026-01-22T11:36:13.442Z"],["3830221","DRX-28247","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-28237 has been resolved","2026-01-22T11:37:21.974Z"],["3830222","LSS-61920","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:712020:1d4eb168-65d8-4fe2-9240-3537fd827409] and [~accountid:712020:7bfaad56-f8bf-45b0-b951-dfd37b5ed5c2], thank you for the confirmations.\n\nHere is my current draft agreement: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/15hdIsbyII0hpvuQ4mAfeIhbpkq4r2bA9Fe2SBQNgtmI/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/document/d/15hdIsbyII0hpvuQ4mAfeIhbpkq4r2bA9Fe2SBQNgtmI/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link]  - please can you have a quick scan through and let me know if this covers the operational / commercial terms you’d expect?\n\nI note that [~accountid:712020:7bfaad56-f8bf-45b0-b951-dfd37b5ed5c2] said she is checking with the insurance team re our cover outside of trips. However, *please can you confirm you are comfortable with accepting the risk and liability for damage to private property outside of an active order (clause 9)*.\n\nSince this is a new template that I have had to draft, we need to run this past our external counsel for a high level review. I will push for this to be done by the end of tomorrow, however I cannot guarantee it will be finalised - I will keep you updated.\n\nThanks both!","2026-01-22T11:38:10.525Z"],["3830224","RDXENG-4452","RDXENG","denis.komissarov@bolt.eu","Denis Komissarov","{{Choose Payment method}} has been also changes to {{How would you like to pay?}} for the consistency in the 2nd PR","2026-01-22T11:38:15.849Z"],["3830226","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Thanks, done. Waiting to observe changes\n\n{noformat}root@ti-payments-dba.sqldb:(none)>SET GLOBAL tidb_ttl_delete_batch_size = 200; SET GLOBAL tidb_ttl_delete_worker_count = 8; SET GLOBAL tidb_ttl\n                              ->  _scan_batch_size = 1020 ; SET GLOBAL tidb_ttl_scan_worker_count = 8;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.014s\n\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.017s\n\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.018s\n\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.014s{noformat}","2026-01-22T11:38:23.520Z"],["3830229","PFI-835362","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Credit notes available in admin :) ","2026-01-22T11:39:53.408Z"],["3830230","PFI-835362","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-22T11:39:57.412Z"],["3830231","TAXP-1998","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filing and payment completed on time.\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1sIut80oBbmifDjTpFlbUyUT87GHeGjOG|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1sIut80oBbmifDjTpFlbUyUT87GHeGjOG]","2026-01-22T11:40:10.620Z"],["3830232","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","Rate limit is still 10\n\n{noformat}| tidb_ttl_delete_rate_limit              | 10          |{noformat}","2026-01-22T11:40:25.359Z"],["3830234","WD-22481","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","!image-20260122-114109.png|width=342,alt=\"image-20260122-114109.png\"!\n\nTesting successful!","2026-01-22T11:41:17.298Z"],["3830235","TAXP-1999","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filing and payment completed on time\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1TjBsHm4EsURfu-pc-zEn-T4FKDyRO1OF|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1TjBsHm4EsURfu-pc-zEn-T4FKDyRO1OF|smart-card]","2026-01-22T11:41:23.446Z"],["3830236","DSR-3955","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T11:41:26.857Z"],["3830237","PFI-835496","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Please escalate to customer payments team, billing cannot assist with payment related topics.","2026-01-22T11:41:39.851Z"],["3830238","PFI-835496","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-22T11:41:44.082Z"],["3830239","DRX-28247","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DA.127.0 (1512) Firebase build on Samsung A12, OS:13 \n\n||*Wait Here*||*Pickup adjusted*||\n|!20260122_133913.jpg|width=228,alt=\"20260122_133913.jpg\"!|!20260122_133550.jpg|width=234,alt=\"20260122_133550.jpg\"!|","2026-01-22T11:41:52.163Z"],["3830241","DRX-28237","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-28247 has been resolved","2026-01-22T11:42:07.123Z"],["3830243","PFI-837197","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-22T11:43:03.399Z"],["3830245","CSXRT-120","CSXRT","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","*RE: Rental* cases are misrouted between *Ride-Hailing* and other verticals./Translation queue does not always route consistently to local queues in fully translated markets.\n\n\n\nSpoke with Pranav as we’re still being overbilled in multi-supplier markets, September tests were not very successful as there was a misconfiguration. They started running new tests for Rider - RH in Jan, and will check if they can start running the test for MM already as well.\n\n*RE:* False safety positives are being incorrectly routed to *Tier 1 or Safety*, increasing manual triage effort.\n\nSafety false positive analysis completed by Tamara & Sven, the conclusion was to wait for the product solution here on natural context model as we’re unable to remove any actual safety keywords as of now. Safety false negative reviews are planned during Q1’26.","2026-01-22T11:43:19.933Z"],["3830249","BDB-1500","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] \nHere you are: [https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/7i3n82nfd1h7dza3j2aew/TZ_OOH_14000x6000_1-10.pdf?rlkey=zkiflg8819m8gcse5dnt0ra5b&dl=0|https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/7i3n82nfd1h7dza3j2aew/TZ_OOH_14000x6000_1-10.pdf?rlkey=zkiflg8819m8gcse5dnt0ra5b&dl=0|smart-link]\nPlease let me know if everything works for you and I can proceed to close the ticket?\nThank you! ","2026-01-22T11:44:12.668Z"],["3830252","TAXP-2001","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filing and payment completed on time\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Oynz6USYcNsFxRh9jrTZqX6hEryB9fDv|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Oynz6USYcNsFxRh9jrTZqX6hEryB9fDv|smart-card]","2026-01-22T11:44:36.381Z"],["3830256","TAXP-2000","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filing and payment completed on time\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Q4pmBoNxjfZNLRTQZKd28aTI_jcVJQ6v|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Q4pmBoNxjfZNLRTQZKd28aTI_jcVJQ6v|smart-card]","2026-01-22T11:46:09.182Z"],["3830264","LSS-61680","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] I see that CS / Ops cancelled the fine. I see they are alleging violation of Article 22 GDPR and threatens escalation to authorities. There is, however no request for clarification of ADM processes or access to their personal data. I’d recommend not addressing this, especially since the fine was cancelled – which was the request of the User.","2026-01-22T11:47:35.995Z"],["3830265","PFI-837202","PFI","michael.agwanda@bolt-outsource.eu","Michael Agwanda","[^Notification of Fraud-BOLT.pdf]","2026-01-22T11:47:42.766Z"],["3830266","WFM-10073","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, assigned you for Safety queues. What is the reason behind Tier2 request? Tier2 is restricted for IH agents only","2026-01-22T11:47:45.653Z"],["3830269","LSS-61713","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","hi [~accountid:712020:1d0a34aa-e1ae-4c55-bae7-010cdaef89e3] , please note that I have incorporated in the reviewed [service agreement|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MiwnQosb2ntKUUyiT2CLDpeYVfa3_z0kQrjXrBC6PlI/edit?tab=t.0], the following point outlined below: 1 - 4, and 6.\nIn what concers point 5 below, outlined by the counter-party, please feel free to incorporate such aspects in the agreement, if needed.\n\nAlso, having in mind that per your above description it results that the training will be offered to Bolt partner drivers, my question is, do we provide to the Supplier any personal data pertaining to such partner drivers? In case answer is yes, please seek involvement of Data Privacy team as well.\n\nBest,\n\nAlex","2026-01-22T11:47:59.813Z"],["3830271","PFI-833151","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:712020:51155f35-611f-4ae4-8802-edf2381a5aaa] \n\nYou have provided a screenshot of the booking. \nUnfortunately, I would not be able to to explain the booking logic. \n\nI would suggest referring to the payment page for the payment information. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3948532555|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3948532555]\n\nHowever, here is the proof of the refund we issued to the customer. \n\n[^Proof of Refund 16-12-2025 (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T11:48:04.353Z"],["3830274","CRC-2248","CRC","romet.varts@bolt.eu","Romet Varts","Business card project is closed","2026-01-22T11:48:16.459Z"],["3830275","LSS-53566","LSS","gayanjalie.dissanayake@bolt.eu","Gayanjalie Dissanayake","Hello,\n\nHave we included the “[https://bolt.eu/en/security/supplier-requirements/|https://bolt.eu/en/security/supplier-requirements/]” in the contract as this is standard practice? If so have they made any pushbacks?\n\n\n\nKind Regards,\n\nGaya","2026-01-22T11:48:20.350Z"],["3830276","PFI-837204","PFI","kosisochukwu.ochuaka@bolt-outsource.eu","Kosisochukwu Ochuaka","!image-20260122-114729.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T11:48:36.155Z"],["3830277","LSS-61952","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Advice provided in the main ticket.","2026-01-22T11:48:37.184Z"],["3830279","DO-5824","DO","kristo.sarnets@bolt.eu","Kristo Sarnets","[SQL Editor in Databricks Common|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/sql/editor/04903f78-c9bb-4971-bf08-13a989792caa?o=3598988355446810]\n\n[Personal Notebook in Databricks|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/3461116750424975?o=3598988355446810]","2026-01-22T11:48:41.186Z"],["3830280","DRX-27951","DRX","niyazi.gasimov@bolt.eu","Niyazi Gasimov","Note for the testing: Smoke suit execution during the Release is enough","2026-01-22T11:48:51.868Z"],["3830282","DSR-3393","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Send message to the user to address the remaining points, concerning privacy side.","2026-01-22T11:49:19.477Z"],["3830284","LSS-60580","LSS","anastassia.tsarenko@bolt.eu","Anastassia Tsarenko","hey ,[~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] - confirming that the user ID is not hashed. ","2026-01-22T11:49:37.760Z"],["3830286","PAW-15089","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @hekan\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17264\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-22 11:49:59 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-22T11:50:00.092Z"],["3830287","LSS-59827","LSS","margarita.karamysheva@bolt.eu","Margarita Karamysheva","Hi [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5] yes, in this context I mean Bolt take rate 🙂 ","2026-01-22T11:50:28.139Z"],["3830289","LSS-62005","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","[^Reigate Virtual Office Agreement.pdf] _(424 kB)_","2026-01-22T11:50:45.697Z"],["3830290","LSS-62005","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","Hey [~accountid:62ff8d58b582d07a14a96588] can you please confirm if you are happy to proceed","2026-01-22T11:50:49.140Z"],["3830292","CNT-441","CNT","aliis.topssalulaid@bolt.eu","Aliis Tops-Salulaid","[~accountid:712020:bca00e26-f5bd-4a5b-9a82-68a8ff2fc37e] Hey! Which posts and ads do you mean? \nJust to do a selection of what we have done (all verticals?), to highlight what we have done, and what are the possibilities in design and in copy? \n\nOr strictly only EB? \n\ncc: [~accountid:610a6c97ec92ab0070d4d852] ","2026-01-22T11:51:07.030Z"],["3830293","WEBSD-1484","WEBSD","tom.gander@bolt.eu","Tom Gander","Here is the report for traffic and device stats.\n[https://lookerstudio.google.com/reporting/70aca0ea-4624-43cd-907c-d10c9546107d|https://lookerstudio.google.com/reporting/70aca0ea-4624-43cd-907c-d10c9546107d]","2026-01-22T11:51:17.251Z"],["3830294","TAXP-2243","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filing and payment completed on time\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1zNooMzQ9kJrwpECQ_bgHXaWy6cmhTCll|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1zNooMzQ9kJrwpECQ_bgHXaWy6cmhTCll|smart-card]","2026-01-22T11:51:35.445Z"],["3830295","LSS-61667","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:b91275f1-415a-4b3c-8490-974f09f14a0d] ! Am I right that you need an extract for Poslovne vožnje d.o.o. entity from estonian business register?","2026-01-22T11:51:46.316Z"],["3830299","LSS-61920","LSS","georgia.heathman@bolt.eu","Georgia Heathman","Thanks [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] for your work on this. I made one minor change as we now have agreement for one parking bay so just removed the second. \n\nAdding [~accountid:628b3e951a437e0070414307] and [~accountid:62a3287576c0360069f59b72] too regarding the liability point.\n\n","2026-01-22T11:52:35.950Z"],["3830306","PFI-833185","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records?recordFilter={\"order_id\"%3A2280140806%2C\"city_id\"%3A3}&page={\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"limit\"%3A100}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records?recordFilter=%7B%22order_id%22%3A2280140806%2C%22city_id%22%3A3%7D&page=%7B%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22limit%22%3A100%7D]\n\nthis were the records for the Ride, seems 34.20 is used ","2026-01-22T11:54:03.310Z"],["3830307","PRODSEC-580","PRODSEC","pavel.kargin@bolt.eu","Pavel Kargin","Scheduled but currently under my account, need to share permissions","2026-01-22T11:54:09.027Z"],["3830308","DPX-3540","DPX","mihai.burlaciuc@bolt.eu","Mihai Burlăciuc","Thanks [~accountid:712020:66bb9418-0d92-46e7-811e-6ba68a304999] \n\nRegarding point 2 - infinite scroll, should be doable, not sure yet about the effort, but I’ll come back in case it’s needed.\n\nFollow up question about new Overall rating section on the [Ratings and feedback]. This value is not always available, meaning that IIRC it is available only after the provider has received 10 order ratings.\n\nWhat should be the behavior in this case should we use a placeholder like a dash or should we hide the section completely?\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 13.51.42.png|width=638,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 13.51.42.png\"!\n\ncc [~accountid:60f2a71a2f97d5006920d5de] Mentioned today in the sync that we may need to have the Overall Provider Rating and as the page is using the {{/deliveryProviderPortal/getOrderHistoryWithFeedbackPaginated}} thought that it may be related to the MP - Order history redesign project - however, I think I’ll create a dedicated endpoint for the ProviderOverallRating so that we don’t need to include it there.\n","2026-01-22T11:54:42.303Z"],["3830309","CCM-22297","CCM","gustav.borjesson@bolt-outsource.eu","Gustav Eric Alexander Borjesson","[^New TalentLMS Training Request Form all.xlsx]\n\nSorry about that. I believe this should be the correct form","2026-01-22T11:54:42.671Z"],["3830310","IDC-2932","IDC","ivan.koscheev@bolt.eu","Ivan Koshcheev","Two cents from my side. Before starting development, please ask your PM to align with the Logistics PM. As far as I know, there were some concerns about the direction.","2026-01-22T11:54:54.267Z"],["3830311","CNT-476","CNT","piers.mcewan@bolt.eu","Piers McEwan","Hey, added some comments. Will close here, but please Slack if any questions. ","2026-01-22T11:55:11.361Z"],["3830312","DMC-735","DMC","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 13.52.59.png|width=392,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 13.52.59.png\"!\n\n[~accountid:62b2cf2c99eafa602d88ec9e] this is just an early draft, but do we want to display city/store something like on this image above?\n","2026-01-22T11:55:22.338Z"],["3830314","CCM-22297","CCM","gustav.borjesson@bolt-outsource.eu","Gustav Eric Alexander Borjesson","Correct course name is: [Ride-Hailing Onboarding|https://transcom-boltcs.talentlms.com/reports/courseinfo/id:1723]\n\n","2026-01-22T11:56:15.699Z"],["3830315","LSS-59597","LSS","ann.koljalg@bolt.eu","Ann Kõljalg","Thank you everyone!\n[~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] I tagged you in a comment where your input is needed.\n[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] I reviewed all the comments and made couple of changes in my comments but noticed there on of your comment not in english - 1.12 clause.\n","2026-01-22T11:56:21.846Z"],["3830316","RDS-1015","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] agree, many thanks!","2026-01-22T11:56:26.773Z"],["3830318","DSR-3917","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Invoice link provided to user","2026-01-22T11:56:42.303Z"],["3830319","PFI-808451","PFI","agata.knapinska@bolt.eu","Agata Knapińska","Hi, [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] any updates?","2026-01-22T11:56:42.930Z"],["3830320","DPX-3540","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","[~accountid:61cc1c8d326554006ca9925c] yes, if it's not something that is needed in a specific order history row, then it makes sense to have it separately ","2026-01-22T11:56:50.100Z"],["3830321","SRED-1095","SRED","artem.timchenko@bolt.eu","Artem Timchenko","Issue in terraform-kafka repo happened due to Karpenter kill worker while the workflow was running.\r\nMaking runners non-disruptable to prevent from happening. Workers in case of that repo are short-living, so won't affect pretty much anything.","2026-01-22T11:57:08.791Z"],["3830322","PFI-834234","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Where did you look for the invoices? Can you send me the one invoice? ","2026-01-22T11:57:10.816Z"],["3830327","CLIENTAPP-38777","CLIENTAPP","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","UI tests execution has been completed. Test cycle created: \"https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/CLIENTAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin%3Acom.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/testPlayer/CLIENTAPP-R3009\"","2026-01-22T11:57:55.102Z"],["3830330","PFI-835572","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","👋 Hey there,\n\nPlease try:\n\n* Open the [Client page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D] in Admin \n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open  {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ - The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see another _error_ → let us know.\n* if you see _to_execute →_ it means that the invoice still needs to be generated. You either look at the invoice for the current month (which does not have an invoice yet because month is still going). If you see that to_execute is for the invoice for multiple months → it means that in the past months it was not generated and will be generated in the end of the month.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the tab (or under {{Partner Invoices}})\n\nBest regards\n\nKetlin Peldes ","2026-01-22T11:57:57.922Z"],["3830332","CLIENTAPP-38777","CLIENTAPP","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","UI tests execution has been completed. Test cycle created: \"https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/CLIENTAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin%3Acom.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/testPlayer/CLIENTAPP-R3010\"","2026-01-22T11:58:06.991Z"],["3830333","WFM-10068","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","please confirm if all needed access is there","2026-01-22T11:58:32.014Z"],["3830334","LSS-61667","LSS","victor.stratan@bolt.eu","Victor Stratan","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] thank you. Unfortunately, no. Poslovne vožnje d.o.o. is our HR3 entity based in Croatia. Thus, we would need an excerpt from business registry in Croatia, officially translate it to English and get it notarized and apostilled. The same is related to company’s articles of association as the bank requested it today. Could you please check it and let me know if we could proceed with it? ","2026-01-22T11:58:42.283Z"],["3830335","RDS-651","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:61386b11a4f86e0069546dff] Thx! Any idea who would be the best person to better describe and/or split this ticket?","2026-01-22T11:58:46.226Z"],["3830337","TAXP-2244","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filing and payment completed in time\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1A-PA748kn0ogX2zYcWvRP9TQcyxr8Pgr|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1A-PA748kn0ogX2zYcWvRP9TQcyxr8Pgr|smart-card]","2026-01-22T11:59:44.645Z"],["3830338","CCM-22297","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Excellent, this is the one. ☀️  Thank you!\n\nAll have been assigned. \n\nFeel free to reach out if anything else is needed.\n\nWishing you a lovely day ahead. 🌷 \n\nIrena","2026-01-22T12:00:03.519Z"],["3830339","WD-22664","WD","paula.noulik@bolt.eu","Paula Nõulik","C-EE002-26-000032\n\n","2026-01-22T12:00:08.096Z"],["3830344","RDS-651","RDS","shreya.bhandari@bolt.eu","Shreya Bhandari","[~accountid:5b7bea0e99f5015905382d6f] do you want to help us split this so we know what things we need for this please","2026-01-22T12:00:48.225Z"],["3830347","LSS-60379","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hi [~accountid:712020:199c869c-84be-4d6f-9d2d-2a504d806ff1],  thank you for the detailed summary of the case.\n\nI understand that we have collected all the goods and have paid all invoices issued by the partners. Accordingly, from Bolt’s side, we do not owe 3B OÜ anything.\n\nAre there any specific written demands or claims from 3B OÜ that remain unanswered and require legal input?\n\nFrom the description above, I understand that all previously received communications from 3B OÜ have already been replied to by Bolt.\n\nBased on the above, could you please clarify what specific input is currently expected from the legal team, i.e. how the legal team can assist at this particular stage?","2026-01-22T12:01:24.187Z"],["3830352","PRV-940","PRV","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","‘ODPO logins’ vault created on 1password - wider access pending team logins (22 Jan)","2026-01-22T12:01:42.300Z"],["3830353","PFI-835715","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! We do not provide earning reports on demand, please reach out to privacy team via BH for downloading the individual ride invoices. ","2026-01-22T12:01:43.221Z"],["3830354","LSS-62005","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-22T12:01:43.636Z"],["3830360","LSS-61593","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hey [~accountid:712020:6fe32059-7a68-4aa8-ba31-68f6c2731793] , please let me know if there are any unanswered questions still pending? If not, I will close the ticket 🙂 ","2026-01-22T12:02:31.346Z"],["3830364","LSS-61318","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","The document was sent for translation. ","2026-01-22T12:03:08.328Z"],["3830368","PFI-837216","PFI","nara.aiamlaoo@bolt-outsource.eu","Nara Aiamlaoo","!image-20260122-120221.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260122-120234.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T12:03:19.201Z"],["3830371","GRWA-1420","GRWA","andrea.santonastaso@bolt.eu","Andrea Santonastaso","W3: final analysis\nGMV: down\n\nspend: down\nuc: up\n[source|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/2869975772979139?o=2472566184436351#command/5887121051882826]","2026-01-22T12:03:32.592Z"],["3830372","BD-1965","BD","ave.tarend@bolt.eu","Ave Tarend","Released on {{2026-01-22}}\n\n\n\nBefore and after screenshots:\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 10.53.06.png|width=608,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 10.53.06.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 10.49.22.png|width=608,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 10.49.22.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 10.52.43.png|width=608,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 10.52.43.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 10.49.09.png|width=608,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 10.49.09.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 10.49.17.png|width=608,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 10.49.17.png\"!\n\n\n\n","2026-01-22T12:03:35.444Z"],["3830375","ROPSC-174","ROPSC","riin@bolt.eu","Riin Kotsalainen","Guide done! \nConfu link - [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PLBK/pages/6036423000/Nigeria+Document+Guide|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PLBK/pages/6036423000/Nigeria+Document+Guide|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T12:03:51.679Z"],["3830376","LSS-61919","LSS","alex.kalotheou@bolt.eu","Alex Kalotheou","Looks good, lets proceed with signing it.","2026-01-22T12:04:02.479Z"],["3830378","PFI-837217","PFI","ana.pelivanu@bolt-outsource.eu","Ana Pelivanu","[^49459350-c0d4-4fa0-95c6-3e442161a9ac.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-22T12:04:12.872Z"],["3830379","WFM-10092","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-22T12:04:13.387Z"],["3830380","TAXP-2017","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filing and payment completed on time\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Qa60gQaWhf5hr6912IEFGF4uPmWGPkp0|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Qa60gQaWhf5hr6912IEFGF4uPmWGPkp0|smart-card]","2026-01-22T12:04:22.263Z"],["3830384","PFI-837208","PFI","demetre.kanchaveli@bolt.eu","Demetre Kanchaveli","UPDATE: Customer just texted us that their balance Is “fixed” now and Is 0 \n\n","2026-01-22T12:05:37.869Z"],["3830385","GRWA-1542","GRWA","andrea.santonastaso@bolt.eu","Andrea Santonastaso","column J [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1VOK1-VqCfB-KsiaQRotlp4Jhx-I7ECYv-fuSXeMOxyo/edit?gid=840277763#gid=840277763]","2026-01-22T12:05:47.954Z"],["3830391","PFI-837218","PFI","glory.ogbuewu@bolt-outsource.eu","Glory Ogbuewu","[^PaymentNotification-2.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-22T12:07:00.345Z"],["3830392","TAXP-2017","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filing and payment completed on time\n\n\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Qa60gQaWhf5hr6912IEFGF4uPmWGPkp0|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Qa60gQaWhf5hr6912IEFGF4uPmWGPkp0|smart-card]","2026-01-22T12:07:11.808Z"],["3830397","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","hmm.. pingcap support didn’t ask to increase that :meow_shrug:","2026-01-22T12:08:12.918Z"],["3830398","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","I lower that only :wink:","2026-01-22T12:08:45.678Z"],["3830400","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","I don’t think it’s rate limit at all.. I think the scan phase is being aborted because it runs for too long:\n\n{noformat}{\"total_rows\":0,\"success_rows\":0,\"error_rows\":0,\"total_scan_task\":0,\"scheduled_scan_task\":0,\"finished_scan_task\":0,\"scan_task_err\":\"job is timeout\"}{noformat}\n\nLet’s see what they say","2026-01-22T12:08:59.462Z"],["3830407","PFI-835937","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi [~accountid:60af7f5f12b3b10069b80c10]  \n\nWe do not reissue rider invoices. This is  because we need to be compliant with tax rules. \n\nPlease ask the user to make sure that their Personal Profile has the correct information before the ride. \n\nIt is as essential as picking the right payment method before the ride.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,\n\nKetlin Peldes  ","2026-01-22T12:09:45.194Z"],["3830408","PFI-837219","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-22T12:09:48.859Z"],["3830409","PFI-835937","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-22T12:09:51.640Z"],["3830412","LSS-61798","LSS","freek.engel@bolt.eu","Freek van den Engel","THere are two more documents needed:\n\nCertified copy of the Certificate of Incorporation\nDirectors registry document\n\n","2026-01-22T12:11:02.288Z"],["3830413","RS-1976","RS","kristi.loit@bolt.eu","Kristi Loit","Hello [~accountid:712020:590a0677-fdbb-4c13-9916-d32af1588d3e] \n\nI am happy to confirm the request for the first aid training. If you enter the invoice then please mark it for Privacy, Risk, Compliance (HQ) cost centre and add there also that this is first aid training and bring out the details about the participants and office for what this is meant for. \n\nBest regards\n\nKristi Loit","2026-01-22T12:11:12.037Z"],["3830414","PRIV-545","PRIV","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","✅ Contractual coverage: [Bolt x Traficar|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/180207?blocked=true&returnTo=%2Fcontracts%2Fv2%3FreturnTo%3D%252Finbox%26CONTRACTSV3_SEARCH%3DeyJxdWVyeSI6W3siZmllbGROYW1lIjoicXVlcnkiLCJ2YWx1ZSI6InRyYWZpIiwib3BlcmF0b3IiOiJlcSJ9XX0%253D%26clusterId%3DEU%26workspaceId%3D31839&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839] 🇵🇱 –> DSA already covers – moreover, this data set was already exchanged between Bolt & Partner.","2026-01-22T12:11:32.331Z"],["3830415","RS-1976","RS","kristi.loit@bolt.eu","Kristi Loit","Budget confirmed for the first aid training. ","2026-01-22T12:11:37.303Z"],["3830418","DMC-735","DMC","kirill.krechetnikov@bolt.eu","Kirill Krechetnikov","[~accountid:712020:ddfe83d1-e2c1-4238-8459-1dfffb836745] This looks great!","2026-01-22T12:12:19.954Z"],["3830419","TAXP-2018","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filing and payment completed on time\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1p72ztPKgyN6_BfWXUu7GA74qxD3Dw_Zh|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1p72ztPKgyN6_BfWXUu7GA74qxD3Dw_Zh|smart-card]","2026-01-22T12:12:26.666Z"],["3830420","LSS-61978","LSS","airi.ilves@bolt.eu","Airi Ilves","Hi! \n\nIn your case I noticed that it was already sent in the envelope of Estonian e-signature signed by counter party. If this is true, then we will manage signing on our side this time: we will mark this ticket as to be signed and our legal ops will support the signing process.\n\nFYI only, in general the guidance is the following: Supplier can  initiate signing and send the agreement to [ahto.kink@bolt.eu|mailto:ahto.kink@bolt.eu] and cc [signing@bolt.eu|mailto:signing@bolt.eu] (we will not be able to find the request without putting this email in cc). Or Bolt can sign the document and share signed pdf with supplier. Please share email, name, title of signing person from supplier's side. \n\nBr, Airi","2026-01-22T12:12:52.027Z"],["3830423","LSS-57632","LSS","nafiu.raheem@bolt.eu","Nafiu Raheem","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] , I hope you are well. The Bastion team has shared the clean version of the partnership agreement [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lqRgbIhwHQtp3GoH68SaTASu0Pr1AuMo/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lqRgbIhwHQtp3GoH68SaTASu0Pr1AuMo/edit|smart-link] . Kindly advise on the next steps ","2026-01-22T12:13:19.019Z"],["3830426","HS-29279","HS","thomas.wagner@bolt.eu","Thomas Wagner","[^Arbeitgeberbescheinigung_Thomas.pdf]","2026-01-22T12:15:22.232Z"],["3830427","LSS-61874","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3], could you please share written request from the Norwegian Road Administration covering:\n\n* *Exact data fields* requested (GPS traces, timestamps, speed, distance, vehicle type, order/ride ID, price)\n* *Geographic scope* (cities, regions)\n* *Time range* (historical vs ongoing)\n* *Frequency & format* Live feed vs batch and MDS version\n* *Intended use*\n\n[~accountid:60e01bce7fcd82007303f981] FYI.\n\nWe also need to clarify some privacy specific points:\n\n* Are riders/users directly or indirectly identifiable? Is GPS data aggregated?\n* For how long will they hold the data, what are deletion obligations? Raw GPS + timestamps + order numbers is usually considered high risk unless strongly anonymised or aggregated.\n\nGenerally, MDS data is not considered personal data when it does not relate to an identified or identifiable individual and cannot reasonably be linked, directly or indirectly, to a natural person. In such cases, the data falls outside the scope of personal data protection requirements. This means we don’t need to sign Data Sharing Agreements and NDA is enough. Please provide the requested info so that we better understand the use case.","2026-01-22T12:16:24.647Z"],["3830432","LSS-61856","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] ! Tracking Code: 7031601721","2026-01-22T12:17:34.578Z"],["3830434","LSS-61459","LSS","mauricio.oropeza@bolt.eu","Mauricio Oropeza","Hi [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a]!\n\nI’m adding the SOW for the campaign here.\n\nAlso, apple share feedback that the wording of the 14 days window in T&Cs is confusing, I suggest changing it to:\n “50% off 2 car rides, valid within 14 days after activation and during the campaign period\".\n\n\n[^2026 Bolt FR & DE- Apple Pay Statement of Work_Marketing_.docx]\n\n","2026-01-22T12:17:48.066Z"],["3830435","DRAG101-405","DRAG101","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","I finished reviewing the ABE. \nI found an issue with the backup battery part numbers. The BOM P/N, spec sheet P/N and product label are all different. \n\nI asked [~accountid:6215e9f275803500683497d5] to help me figure out the correct P/N and correct the documentation. ","2026-01-22T12:18:08.447Z"],["3830436","LSS-62006","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nMihai Lățăianu has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-22T12:18:12.081Z"],["3830437","IDC-2251","IDC","sandeep.jaiswal@bolt.eu","Sandeep Prasad Jaiswal","[~accountid:63d0ecc2f386bda5dcab9d6e] a mistake. updated","2026-01-22T12:18:18.874Z"],["3830438","LSS-61978","LSS","airi.ilves@bolt.eu","Airi Ilves","Hi Legal Ops, please support signing this document. Here is now attached the downloaded envelope from the e-mail. \n\nBr, Airi\n\n[^Täisteenuse leping (507-11.3)_PR-21074_15.01.26281536 (4).asice] ","2026-01-22T12:18:50.631Z"],["3830439","LSS-61874","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:712020:7f47c2af-14e1-4206-a795-ac87cb906276], could you please open a sub-ticket for me? Let me clarify the scope of data sharing with the stakeholder. If personal data is not involved, then you can draft NDA and DSA is not needed. If not, I am happy to assist with the DSA 👍 ","2026-01-22T12:19:02.217Z"],["3830442","DPM-2313","DPM","kirill.krechetnikov@bolt.eu","Kirill Krechetnikov","[~accountid:60950a25539c14006ae92e40] thanks a lot, this is a great step towards clarity! Next, we’ll need an analysis of root causes for each column to make the data actionable. For example, is url not pointing to a G-drive always a reason for a failure marked as {{IVALID_ARGUMENT (9005)}} or are there any other reasons why we can see this error? What triggers {{INCORRECT_DOC_TYPE (2361)}} , {{NON_BINARY_FILE_DOWNLOAD}}, and {{UNKNOWN_CODE_2365(2365)}}? When would a file not be found? If a folder is completely empty in this case? \ncc [~accountid:712020:a5a9bde0-6d51-468a-85a6-ee3e42b31f73] [~accountid:712020:ddfe83d1-e2c1-4238-8459-1dfffb836745] ","2026-01-22T12:20:00.461Z"],["3830443","CSP-454","CSP","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","More context on the existing issues here: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1767366357447089|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1767366357447089|smart-link] \nand here: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768308504508939|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768308504508939|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T12:20:03.889Z"],["3830446","PFI-835421","PFI","izabela.adamiec@bolt.eu","Izabela Rosińska","Hi, quick update: I think I may have found the answer on the channel #*commerce-poland-rh*. On 22.12.2025 there was an issue raised about missing payouts for several partners and this is João’s message from that day:\n\n“_Please note: Due to the circunstances, we are not able to bulk track and provide the payouts in the same amount as they suppose to receive in the morning. Instead, we are processing the payouts for the whole balance amount available, which means partners with activity today will receive more funds._”\n\nThanks and regards, \n\nIza","2026-01-22T12:20:46.672Z"],["3830447","PFI-835640","PFI","caroline.kruberg@bolt.eu","Caroline Kruberg","Hi,\n\nThe driver got the email cause one of his orders had major GPS issues which resulted in us logging 100x the amount of kilometres driven from reality. Hence we excluded that order from the NLW calculation. This is not fraud and the driver was still paid the right amount of NLW for his worked hours and correct distance driven. We just had to adjust our calculation because of the data issue. \n\nHope this explains!\n\nBest,\nCaroline","2026-01-22T12:20:51.562Z"],["3830448","LSS-62005","LSS","lucca.carney@bolt.eu","Lucca Carney","All good!","2026-01-22T12:21:18.671Z"],["3830449","FPD-1447","FPD","kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu","Kateryna Kolomiiets","PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/816|https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/816|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T12:21:35.282Z"],["3830450","LSS-55901","LSS","migle.zuvelyte@bolt.eu","Miglė Žuvelytė","Thank you!\n\n[~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] Yes, Im sharing documents in docx, Ames was an exception as it was their requirement from the beginning (they had some difficulties with receiving documents / seeing comments). And yes, the rules / process applied for collab is the same with all schools, so the data shared will be the same. Thank you for such rapid review!\n\n[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] Thank you for review and for the provision of possible position. I will formulate the communication to drivers including these conditions you’ve mentioned and discussed. \n\nPlease keep this ticket open for a moment till the process of preparation ends, as I may need more assistance from you here in upcoming days/week. Apologies for this never-ending process establishment - we’re almost there! 😅 ","2026-01-22T12:21:42.794Z"],["3830451","PFI-835963","PFI","izabela.adamiec@bolt.eu","Izabela Rosińska","Hi Ketlin, thank you for your update. I think I may have found the answer on the channel #*commerce-poland-rh*. On 22.12.2025 there was an issue raised about missing payouts for several partners and this is João’s message from that day:\n\n“_Please note: Due to the circunstances, we are not able to bulk track and provide the payouts in the same amount as they suppose to receive in the morning. Instead, we are processing the payouts for the whole balance amount available, which means partners with activity today will receive more funds._”\n\nThanks and regards,\n\nIza","2026-01-22T12:21:54.564Z"],["3830452","CNT-377","CNT","aleksandra.onutsina@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Onutšina","[~accountid:712020:f172cd28-e81b-4011-8942-5ec6b2912f37] hey, the copy has been proofread. The final version is here: [https://www.figma.com/design/U7wnv1Gz61rZREc4SMWg4c/LCM-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Storytelling-Emails?node-id=5422-44775&p=f&t=ig8RMYnEqDM0Zzvn-0|https://www.figma.com/design/U7wnv1Gz61rZREc4SMWg4c/LCM-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Storytelling-Emails?node-id=5422-44775&p=f&t=ig8RMYnEqDM0Zzvn-0|smart-link] \n\nWould you like me to move the copy to a GoogleDoc ? ","2026-01-22T12:22:07.748Z"],["3830453","DBRE-8603","DBRE","akhmad.islami@bolt.eu","Akhmad Mukhson Islami","*[current -> downscale]*\ninstance type : i3en.6xlarge -> i3en.3xlarge\nDisk usage: ~20% -> ~36%\nCPU \n\n* avg: ~4.46% -> ~9%\n* peak: ~11.69% -> ~24%\n\ninnodb_buffer_pool_size: 126G -> 67G","2026-01-22T12:22:20.106Z"],["3830457","LSS-61998","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:33a1a5e8-52cb-4605-9ef3-0b89d57fe7b8] ![^Nicchiano Sp. z o.o. - Voluntary Disclosure_NIP-8_update (b1e89997-9f83-47c1-ba5c-213eeb6ff3dc).pdf] ","2026-01-22T12:23:40.283Z"],["3830460","LSS-61997","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:33a1a5e8-52cb-4605-9ef3-0b89d57fe7b8] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^initupload_220120261131 (2085da79-e8a2-4862-a1ea-c0265105f451).xml] ","2026-01-22T12:24:11.168Z"],["3830462","LSS-61668","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Thank you [~accountid:712020:b63b62e9-e039-44cb-8feb-1a5c42b0eb41] , the email was sent. ","2026-01-22T12:24:18.244Z"],["3830466","LSS-61242","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Clarified with Liivika and Nathadon if the personal data involved in fleet partnerships in Thailand is accessed or handled outside Thailand - the answer is *yes*, as fleet partnership are also managed on a global and HQ level.","2026-01-22T12:25:16.045Z"],["3830468","FRAUDOPS-1127","FRAUDOPS","nigar.alizada@bolt.eu","Nigar Alizada","{code:sql}WITH rider_changes AS (\n  SELECT \n    a.created,\n    a.meta.city_id AS city_id,\n    a.meta.user_id AS user_id,\n    CAST(get_json_object(a.input, '$.data.order_id') AS VARCHAR(255)) AS order_id,\n    a.meta.country AS country_code,\n    get_json_object(\n      a.input,\n      '$.query.corresponding_calculations.user_order_request.input.business_details.payment_type'\n    ) AS business_type,\n    CAST(\n  get_json_object(\n    a.input,\n    '$.query.corresponding_calculations.user_order_request.input.business_details.company_created_age_in_days'\n  ) AS INT\n) AS company_age_days,\n    CAST(\n      get_json_object(\n        a.input,\n        '$.query.corresponding_calculations.user_order_request.input.business_payments.company_captured_payments.months_3.amount_in_eur'\n      ) AS DECIMAL(18,2)\n    ) AS amount_in_eur\n  FROM sel_fraud_checks_pii_spark.user_destination_update a\n  WHERE a.created_date >= DATEADD(month, -2, current_date)\n    AND a.decision.decision IN ('pass','adjust_auth')\n),\n\nprice_prediction AS (\n  SELECT\n    p.order_id,\n    p.city_id,\n    p.predicted_price,\n    row_number() OVER (\n      PARTITION BY p.order_id, p.city_id\n      ORDER BY p.created\n    ) AS rn_asc,\n    row_number() OVER (\n      PARTITION BY p.order_id, p.city_id\n      ORDER BY p.created DESC\n    ) AS rn_desc\n  FROM ng_public_spark.pricing_order_prediction p\n  WHERE p.created_date >= DATEADD(month, -2, current_date)\n),\n\ndestination_changes AS (\n  SELECT\n    od.order_id,\n    od.city_id,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT od.id) AS count_of_destinations_changes\n  FROM (\n    SELECT\n      id,\n      order_id,\n      city_id,\n      destination_lat,\n      destination_lng,\n      LAG(destination_lat) OVER (PARTITION BY order_id, city_id ORDER BY created) AS prev_lat,\n      LAG(destination_lng) OVER (PARTITION BY order_id, city_id ORDER BY created) AS prev_lng\n    FROM ng_public_spark.company_order_destination\n    WHERE created_date >= DATEADD(month, -2, current_date)\n  ) od\n  WHERE prev_lat IS NOT NULL\n    AND (destination_lat <> prev_lat OR destination_lng <> prev_lng)\n  GROUP BY 1,2\n),\n\nfinal_dataset AS (\n  SELECT\n    etl.created,\n    etl.order_id,\n    etl.city_id,\n    etl.user_id,\n    etl.country_code,\n    rc.country_code AS rc_country_code,\n    rc.business_type,\n    rc.amount_in_eur,\n    rc.company_age_days,\n    pp_first.predicted_price AS first_predicted_price,\n    pp_last.predicted_price  AS last_predicted_price,\n    pp_last.predicted_price / NULLIF(pp_first.predicted_price, 0) AS predicted_price_ratio,\n    dc.count_of_destinations_changes,\n    etl.user_price,\n    etl.partner_price,\n    ROUND(pp_first.predicted_price / etl.eur_currency_rate, 2) AS first_price_eur,\n    ROUND(pp_last.predicted_price  / etl.eur_currency_rate, 2) AS last_price_eur,\n    CASE\n      WHEN\n        pp_first.predicted_price IS NOT NULL\n        AND pp_last.predicted_price IS NOT NULL\n        AND pp_first.predicted_price > 0\n      THEN\n        pp_last.predicted_price / pp_first.predicted_price\n      ELSE NULL\n    END AS ratio_predictions,\n    CONCAT(\n      'https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/',\n      CAST(etl.order_id AS VARCHAR(255)),\n      '/',\n      CAST(etl.city_id AS VARCHAR(255))\n    ) AS order_link,\n\n    CONCAT(\n      'https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/user_destination_update/',\n      CAST(etl.order_id AS VARCHAR(255))\n    ) AS destination_change_link\n\n  FROM ng_public_spark.etl_denormalized_commerce_orders etl\n  JOIN rider_changes rc\n    ON rc.order_id = etl.order_id\n   AND rc.city_id  = etl.city_id\n   AND rc.user_id  = etl.user_id\n  JOIN price_prediction pp_first\n    ON pp_first.order_id = etl.order_id\n   AND pp_first.city_id  = etl.city_id\n   AND pp_first.rn_asc = 1\n  JOIN price_prediction pp_last\n    ON pp_last.order_id = etl.order_id\n   AND pp_last.city_id  = etl.city_id\n   AND pp_last.rn_desc = 1\n  JOIN destination_changes dc\n    ON dc.order_id = etl.order_id\n   AND dc.city_id  = etl.city_id\n  WHERE etl.created_date >= DATEADD(month, -2, current_date)\n)\nSELECT *\nFROM final_dataset\nWHERE\n  business_type = 'credit_card'\n  --AND company_age_days < 90\n  AND amount_in_eur < 300\n  AND predicted_price_ratio > 5;{code}","2026-01-22T12:25:27.302Z"],["3830469","LSS-58495","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update based on the call with* [~accountid:61d554bb68926d00685d5727] *today:*\n\nSecured a decision to *use the existing eDMA consent solution to* ensure compliance and mitigate any risk to the 2026 roadmap and commercial goals.\n\n*The Win:*\n\n* Minimal Ads Effort: Implementation focuses on backend logic, sparing Ads Engineering or Product Roadmap resources.\n* Risk Mitigation: Solves the regulatory gap immediately without slowing down core monetisation features.\n\n*Next Steps:*\n\n* *Commercial Check:* Aligning with Martech on the impact of data visibility.\n* *Resourcing:* Locking in the timeline, effort allocation with Platform & Identity.\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nAds team ([~accountid:61d554bb68926d00685d5727] ) to drive the next steps - privacy team to be involved for visibility & to advise on risks.\n{panel}","2026-01-22T12:26:25.237Z"],["3830473","LSS-61296","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE*+\n\n* Response sent to AKI today ✅ ","2026-01-22T12:26:39.903Z"],["3830474","PFI-837202","PFI","caroline.kruberg@bolt.eu","Caroline Kruberg","route changes not logged [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/610043213/25?orderTryId=1520514093|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/610043213/25?orderTryId=1520514093]","2026-01-22T12:26:42.715Z"],["3830476","LSS-61713","LSS","nicoleta.pandelea@bolt.eu","Nicoleta-Steluta Pandelea","Hey [~accountid:712020:3d4c87bb-37b3-4ce8-a9b9-7232af464c95] \n\nThank you for your prompt response. 😄 \nTo answer your question, the only information we share is the names of the participating drivers—no additional data is communicated.\nRegarding the partner drivers, we already have an Image Rights Authorization form in place, which we sign with them to ensure their consent to appear in photos and videos. ","2026-01-22T12:27:04.776Z"],["3830477","SREDESK-7438","SREDESK","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","Hello! The access has been granted now. It might take a few moments to update, but you should have same access as Sonia now.","2026-01-22T12:27:25.349Z"],["3830478","FRAUDOPS-1127","FRAUDOPS","nigar.alizada@bolt.eu","Nigar Alizada","Both global cap rules are one. \n\n\n\n# for the user_destination_update  - [DESTINATION_CHANGE_BUSINESS_GLOBAL|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/user_destination_update/DESTINATION_CHANGE_BUSINESS_GLOBAL?tab=approval_requests&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]\n# for the driver_destination_update - [DESTINATION_CHANGE_BUSINESS_GLOBAL_DRIVER|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/driver_destination_update/DESTINATION_CHANGE_BUSINESS_GLOBAL_DRIVER?tab=approval_requests&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]\n\nNext step will be monitoring to make sure they work okay - DONE","2026-01-22T12:27:26.502Z"],["3830479","DSR-3577","DSR","juan.sanchez@bolt.eu","Juan Martin Sanchez","[~accountid:712020:714baa0e-ddd0-4776-8064-c5a5d3ae37aa] maybe?\n\nThis is important to be able to move fwd the ticket.","2026-01-22T12:27:41.941Z"],["3830480","CEBF-1769","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","[~accountid:712020:bcd1b76c-7935-49eb-a9ce-d0998dbc8d43] we still have 47k+acc\n\n!image-20260122-122703.png|width=580,alt=\"image-20260122-122703.png\"!","2026-01-22T12:27:44.827Z"],["3830484","PFI-836646","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Martyna, the new account has some mildly suspicious details that can be associated with a fake account → no prior activity on the platform, seemingly random email with an unknown domain.\nPlease advise the user to order at least one in-app ride without the promo, after which, they should be able to use the code again.\nThank you!","2026-01-22T12:28:36.239Z"],["3830485","HS-29254","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hello [~accountid:712020:ca243e6e-5caf-49e7-b44a-b87e19c22516] \n\nCan you please inform me about these two, what is meant here?\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 20.28.04.png|width=529,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 20.28.04.png\"!","2026-01-22T12:28:41.475Z"],["3830486","WFM-10094","WFM","aurelija.jovani@bolt-outsource.eu","Aurelija Jovani","!2026.01.19.png|thumbnail!\n\n!2026.01.20.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T12:28:59.032Z"],["3830487","LSS-61818","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:b63b62e9-e039-44cb-8feb-1a5c42b0eb41] .\n\nHaving in consideration the nature of the request, I believe there wont be additional communications, so I will close this ticket.\n\nHowever, if something else comes up please write here and I will reopen it.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-22T12:28:59.437Z"],["3830489","LSS-62008","LSS","elena-roxana.iordachel@bolt.eu","Elena-Roxana Iordăchel","[^Registreringsbevis - 559339-2169.pdf] _(63 kB)_","2026-01-22T12:29:17.339Z"],["3830491","PAW-15123","PAW","mihai.casandra@bolt.eu","Mihai Casandra","PintSec will not take responsibility for protecting employees' computers, we only want to protect the production environments. Each employee is responsible for the software it runs in his computer, that includes making sure that node.js packages don’t have any malware included in their install scripts.","2026-01-22T12:29:32.573Z"],["3830495","LSS-62006","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-22T12:31:06.728Z"],["3830496","RDXENG-4736","RDXENG","taras.sgibnev@bolt.eu","Taras Sgibnev","From a UX point of view, it would be better to block the flow earlier and show a clear message right after pickup or destination selection, explaining that scheduled rides are not supported for this area, and why. Showing this message instead of the time picker sounds reasonable.\n\nThis scenario is very similar to the existing “unsupported route” flow. However that case is also not handled well at the moment, so I think it makes sense to improve all of them in a consistent way instead of solving this one in isolation. Please note, we should be able to handle “unsupported destination” and “unsupported route” as different cases.\n\n[https://www.figma.com/design/2NcBATQxS2oFhws1Vljamo/Pre-order?node-id=77492-61455&t=rZWoT8tlWyuXnkZJ-11|https://www.figma.com/design/2NcBATQxS2oFhws1Vljamo/Pre-order?node-id=77492-61455&t=rZWoT8tlWyuXnkZJ-11|smart-link] \n\n[~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] , could you please review the copy when you have time?","2026-01-22T12:32:29.481Z"],["3830497","MICRO-290","MICRO","hannalore.taal@bolt.eu","Hannalore Taal","[~accountid:5d8df2708189fd0dc3ea6a85] let’s consider here an experiment, please, to not expose speed-limited areas to new riders during the first 3 rides. Understand, that in order to support this technically, we’d need to take care of the following things:\n\n# In case of rider on their 1st, 2nd, or 3rd Bolt ride, don’t apply speed limits while in speed-limited zone;\n# Turn off onboard geofencing. \n\nLet’s discuss and prioritise this!","2026-01-22T12:32:48.450Z"],["3830500","LSS-62006","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","hi [~accountid:61e144f79ee70a0068ec7efd] this seems to be our internal draft template for such agreements. Do you need anything specific from legal support?\n\nThanks,\nAlex","2026-01-22T12:33:39.286Z"],["3830505","PFI-837226","PFI","lotanna.nnaji@bolt-outsource.eu","Lotanna Nnaji","!Screenshot_20260122-125458.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T12:34:04.034Z"],["3830506","XP-3037","XP","yaroslav.morozevych@bolt.eu","Yaroslav Morozevych","h2. Results [[PR|https://github.com/bolteu/data-experimentation/pull/1128]]\n\nh3. Endpoints & Schema changes:\n\n* Implemented a set of time series endpoints for plotting:\n** {{/api/v2/timeseries/metric}} – Get time series plot data for a specific metric of an A/B test.\n** {{/api/v2/timeseries/dashboard/enrollments}} – Get time series plot data for dashboard enrollments of an A/B test.\n** {{/api/v2/timeseries/dashboard/randomization-pvalue}} – Get time series plot data for dashboard randomization p-value of an A/B test.\n** All the endpoints follow a *unified schema* that can be checked in the {{Timeseries}} Postman collection along with the examples.\n* Updated response schema of the {{/api/v2/dashboards/metadata}} endpoint by adding a new {{randomization_pvalue}} property.\n* Updated response schema of the {{/api/v2/dashboards/table}} endpoint by adding a new {{target_mde}} property in {{metrics[x]hypothesis.target_mde}}.\n\nh3. Pre-release requests [[doc|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kCaqGNfjexI6dRR-6enId80odbcjfLFs-9AZL3xm8qs/edit?tab=t.0]]:\n\n* Removed the alert for sample size not being reached – it conflicts with sequential testing.\n* De-duplicated metrics across dashboards – necessary for sequential testing. Now, if the same metric is selected as Primary, Guardrail, and Exploratory metric, it will be only shown in the Hypothesis tab as Primary metric.\n** The order of priority matters: {{Primary > Secondary > Guardrail > Exploratory}}.\n** This will also affect the alpha correction as if a metric is removed from the Guardrails tab and is shown in Hypothesis, the total number of metrics in Guardrails tab decreases increasing alpha.\n\nh3. Bug fixes:\n\n* Fixed control selection only expecting control group as an input (same for treatment). From now on, treatment groups can used as an input for control selection and vice versa. Inputing non-existing groups will throw an error.\n* Fixed a bug (only in v2) when capped and CUPED metrics where taken into alpha correction calculation.\n** If you had 3 base metrics all with capping and CUPED enabled, then you had 9 variants all of which were used in the alpha correction calculation, which was wrong as the correct number is 3.","2026-01-22T12:34:06.972Z"],["3830508","PFI-836688","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Vanessa, thanks for reporting. This is already under discussion in the fraud-kenya channel → [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GK9LUAWKX/p1768996873150509|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GK9LUAWKX/p1768996873150509|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T12:34:18.056Z"],["3830509","SREDESK-7443","SREDESK","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","Agreed with Orkhan in DMs that the ticket can be considered as done now.","2026-01-22T12:34:22.441Z"],["3830510","PFI-837228","PFI","folashade.akinsola@bolt.eu","Folashade Dolapo Akinsola","!image-20260122-123445.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T12:34:57.589Z"],["3830514","DPM-2313","DPM","hanno.narvik@bolt.eu","Hanno Narvik","\n\nAdded the Kibana logs to the ticket description for more in-depth look","2026-01-22T12:35:50.550Z"],["3830515","LSS-61242","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hey [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] \nPlease find the link to the DSA template for Bolt Holdings (Thailand) Limited - [^Bolt Holdings (Thailand) Limited Controller-Controller DSA Template.docx] \n\nIf anything - feel free to tag me.\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] ","2026-01-22T12:36:05.098Z"],["3830516","DCPAE-528","DCPAE","yashika.sharma@bolt.eu","Yashika Sharma","Currently Bolt Plus users are missing from this table, they should be added based on the start and end date, for example if for a given week they are enrolled in the subscription for only half a week for a week long campaign it should reflect that. \n\nTo talk with [~accountid:712020:9ffd93c0-be69-492c-af42-0a03b1e54cba] to see the state of tables with bolt plus subscription data","2026-01-22T12:36:04.201Z"],["3830517","BD-2002","BD","ave.tarend@bolt.eu","Ave Tarend","PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161574|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161574|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T12:36:30.799Z"],["3830520","CSDT-971","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Another issue with following metrics: \n\n* {{tier_transfer_rate_tier_1_to_tier_2_post_escalation_utc}}\n* {{tier_transfer_rate_tier_1_to_local_ops_pam_bqs_post_escalation_utc}}\n* {{tier_transfer_rate_global_to_tier_1_post_escalation_utc}}\n\nDenominator has escalated tier filter, while numerator doesn’t. This leads to inconsistencies where numerator can be bigger than denominator. \n\n\n\nThis will be fixed by adding escalated tier to dim_support_case_tier_history and then adding it to filters in the semantic of the dim_support_case_tier_history. \n\nPR with fix: [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15488|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15488]","2026-01-22T12:37:03.040Z"],["3830522","PAW-15123","PAW","artur.luik@bolt.eu","Artur Luik","How kalep solves -> [https://github.com/bolteu/kalep/blob/main/pnpm-workspace.yaml|https://github.com/bolteu/kalep/blob/main/pnpm-workspace.yaml]","2026-01-22T12:37:13.205Z"],["3830523","LSS-61869","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:62567ec6a872710069210b83] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^loa Bolt Support Services NL B.V (ab801e05-9de6-43c1-bfe9-d6dafa5e4d25).pdf] [^loa Bolt Support CH Sarl (a7079b9a-038a-491e-a2b3-d30c3d27161c).pdf] ","2026-01-22T12:37:27.782Z"],["3830527","PFI-837230","PFI","patryk.flakowski@bolt.eu","Patryk Flakowski","[^POTWIERDZENIE_TRANSAKCJI_20260122090925.pdf]","2026-01-22T12:38:17.084Z"],["3830528","PFI-837230","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-22T12:38:19.275Z"],["3830530","DCPAE-530","DCPAE","yashika.sharma@bolt.eu","Yashika Sharma","To be clarified further, to do when other sub tasks from the main task are addressed.","2026-01-22T12:38:23.805Z"],["3830533","DCPAE-533","DCPAE","yashika.sharma@bolt.eu","Yashika Sharma","Fix filtering logic to include aborted enrollments as well.","2026-01-22T12:39:33.085Z"],["3830536","DCPAE-553","DCPAE","yashika.sharma@bolt.eu","Yashika Sharma","To check after fixing missing Bolt plus and aborted enrollments issue","2026-01-22T12:40:17.381Z"],["3830539","LSS-62009","LSS","anja.smrek@bolt.eu","Anja Smrek","[^Decision on Position Abolishment.docx] _(637 kB)_","2026-01-22T12:40:46.968Z"],["3830540","DSR-3957","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T12:41:24.768Z"],["3830542","LSS-61593","LSS","ansis.ansbergs@bolt.eu","Ansis Ansbergs","All good.","2026-01-22T12:41:27.860Z"],["3830543","SUPX-2337","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","True, but in theory they started it.\n\nEq. a rider rates a driver 1 star and leaves a comment. Which triggers in some situations an outbound case","2026-01-22T12:41:38.276Z"],["3830546","LSS-61938","LSS","david.vysoky@bolt.eu","Dávid Vysoký","Payment was executed this morning.","2026-01-22T12:44:32.080Z"],["3830551","MVRT-1514","MVRT","teele.vallimae@bolt.eu","Teele Vallimäe","[~accountid:632d4729fedc6169aed5c944] Yes, in Jan from 30€ -> 88€.","2026-01-22T12:45:04.381Z"],["3830552","WEBSD-1493","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:712020:c5112ace-7ce1-4dda-ac10-3e11946d098c] 👋 \n\nHere are the changes:\n\n[https://bolt.eu/en-lt/driver/guide/categories/|https://bolt.eu/en-lt/driver/guide/categories/|smart-link] \n\n[https://bolt.eu/lt-lt/driver/guide/categories/|https://bolt.eu/lt-lt/driver/guide/categories/|smart-link] \n\nRegards,","2026-01-22T12:45:25.855Z"],["3830554","PFI-837232","PFI","jane.dike@bolt-outsource.eu","Jane Dike","[^10.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-22T12:45:28.528Z"],["3830556","PAW-15090","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @olshak\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161558\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-22 12:46:16 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-22T12:46:16.262Z"],["3830559","DPM-2313","DPM","artur.spunei@bolt.eu","Artur Spunei","[~accountid:62b2cf2c99eafa602d88ec9e] [~accountid:621f66f84160640069c66ff4] I will make an audit for each column this evening and I will come back with all my findings documented. ","2026-01-22T12:46:38.630Z"],["3830563","LSS-60921","LSS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hey [~accountid:712020:d8161849-388c-4312-84ee-638c0b0ece4f] ,\n\nUnfortunately, the student has informed me that the original signatory is not available. \n\nThey have requested the signatory for the third party be changed to:\n\n* Name: Priit Tannik\n* Title: Study Centre Manager (Tartu)\n* Email: priit@eek.ee\n* No telephone number, unfortunately, hope that is ok \n\nWould you be able to make this change and reissue? 🙏 \n\nThanks,\n\nKadi","2026-01-22T12:47:32.543Z"],["3830565","PFI-836758","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Sumaila, thanks for reaching out, and for the thorough summary.\nI’ve pulled some numbers on these orders, and aside from possible driver bonus abuse and rating manipulation, we’re not experiencing a lot of financial loss. We will reinstate the driver, given the likely impact of the FO. \nHowever, going forward, lack of awareness won’t be considered a valid justification for him. Additionally i can see the registration was created on 23 Feb 2025, driver was likely aware of this, and continued behaviour may result in a permanent suspension.\nI’ve unblocked the driver.\nBest,\nKarl\n","2026-01-22T12:47:43.024Z"],["3830569","CEBF-1709","CEBF","pradeep.yadav@bolt.eu","Pradeep Kumar Yadav","[~accountid:6218cbe4468c2e007170c08b] Instead of creating two button, can we go with single button like we have on parent opportunity “Create Growth Opportunities“?","2026-01-22T12:48:06.498Z"],["3830571","PFI-837235","PFI","szymon.barabasz@bolt.eu","Szymon Barabasz","[^PL1525-31739 (1).pdf]","2026-01-22T12:48:20.373Z"],["3830572","PFI-837235","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-22T12:48:22.839Z"],["3830579","DO-5815","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","PR Created https://github.com/bolteu/airflow-main/pull/9768\r\n\r\nConnection Tested https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A2JCLG9UL/p1769085678292419","2026-01-22T12:49:49.144Z"],["3830582","PFI-837236","PFI","somruethai.wanwong@bolt-outsource.eu","Somruethai Wanwong","!image-20260122-124812.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T12:50:10.794Z"],["3830584","TA-157","TA","paulo.morna@bolt.eu","Paulo Morna","h4. Progress & Setbacks Summary\n\n_(as of Jan 22, 2026)_\n\nh4. Progress\n\n* Pilot scope and countries aligned: Agreement reached to pilot offer automation in Portugal, Estonia, and Germany, covering both white-collar and selected blue-collar use cases, ensuring relevance for high-hiring and complex markets.\n* Reworked offer templates delivered: A newly branded offer template was presented, with core offer data successfully pulling from Greenhouse and Workday, including role details, compensation, probation period, and contract information.\n* Clear improvements to offer clarity and candidate experience identified: Feedback was incorporated to simplify the offer letter structure (e.g. moving detailed equity explanations to the end or an attachment, repositioning the personal questionnaire link, removing tax-sensitive benefits), with changes committed for immediate implementation.\n* Country-specific requirements actively addressed: Local needs such as meal allowances (Portugal), fixed-term vs. permanent contracts, working student roles, and blue-collar variations are being built into templates, demonstrating strong cross-functional collaboration.\n* Known data ownership and system dependencies clarified: Alignment achieved on which data points should come from Workday vs. Greenhouse, with transparency around limitations and manual overrides.\n* Strong momentum toward pilot go-live: Despite complexity, the team expressed confidence and motivation to proceed with a pilot launch next week, pending final template readiness.\n\n----\n\nh4. Setbacks / Challenges\n\n* Full offer automation no longer feasible due to equity calculator complexity: The new 2026 stock calculator is significantly more complex, making integration with Greenhouse impractical at this stage. As a result, stock numbers and values must now be manually entered by recruiters, reducing the intended automation benefits.\n* Original automation assumptions invalidated by compensation changes: Updates to job grades and compensation ranges meant previously built automation logic became inaccurate, requiring scope reduction and rework.\n* Partial automation reduces efficiency gains: While most offer elements remain automated, losing automated stock calculation introduces additional manual steps, impacting the original goal of end-to-end offer automation.\n* Integration risk with Workday remains: Any modification to the Workday–Greenhouse integration report (e.g. adding fields) carries a risk of temporary data issues or overrides, limiting flexibility and requiring careful coordination.\n* Template complexity increasing with variations: Supporting multiple countries, contract types, and role categories (e.g. blue-collar, working students) increases delivery risk and may affect readiness for all scenarios at pilot launch.\n\n----\n\nh3. Overall Assessment\n\n* The project is progressing with tangible outputs and strong cross-functional alignment, particularly on templates, pilot scope, and candidate experience improvements.\n* The main setback is technical, not strategic: equity automation limitations and upstream compensation changes constrained full automation.\n* Short-term value will still be delivered via partial automation, while longer-term solutions (e.g. embedding the stock calculator in Greenhouse) remain under exploration.\n* The pilot approach allows the team to validate impact, surface risks early, and iterate, rather than blocking progress on a perfect solution.","2026-01-22T12:50:47.065Z"],["3830585","G3IOT-1214","G3IOT","kaarel.vandler@bolt.eu","Kaarel Vandler","{quote}4.4V) and enters LPM to protect the modem. Here for example the <https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/rentals-micromobility/vehicles/iot/view/1164104?tab=logs&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A0%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22lines%22%3A100%7D%7D|IOT{quote}\n\nThere are cases [reported |https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/G3IOT-1214]when ebike IOT is entering LPM on full battery. According to IOT logic this is only possible if IOT FW detects Vsys overshoot (Vsys > is reporting Vsys 3.395 voltage. High Vsys is measured when BB charging is active. *@user-U01FV9KJ58U* can you tell if any of bq25798 registers are configured incorrectly causing Vsys overshoot:\n\n{noformat}\"adcControl\": 136,\n\"control0\": 162,\n\"control1\": 133,\n\"control2\": 64,\n\"control3\": 48,\n\"control4\": 64,\n\"control5\": 150,\n\"ibus\": 65,\n\"status0\": 15,\n\"status1\": 234,\n\"status2\": 1,\n\"status3\": 192,\n\"status4\": 4,\n\"tdie\": 31,\n\"ts\": 14,\n\"vac1\": 24135,\n\"vac2\": 7580,\n\"vbat\": 4154,\n\"vbus\": 24125,\n\"vsys\": 4395,{noformat}","2026-01-22T12:50:47.087Z"],["3830586","G3IOT-1214","G3IOT",null,"Slack","[Kaarel Vandler|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5fc10e1e2730d80076c1d3a4] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02PC32P35F/p1769083908465779?thread_ts=1769083908.465779&cid=C02PC32P35F|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02PC32P35F/p1769083908465779?thread_ts=1769083908.465779&cid=C02PC32P35F|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-22T12:50:48.651Z"],["3830587","G3IOT-1214","G3IOT","kaarel.vandler@bolt.eu","Kaarel Vandler","the max voltage must be capped. i dont remember what the register was but i can look it up","2026-01-22T12:50:48.920Z"],["3830592","PFI-837240","PFI","somruethai.wanwong@bolt-outsource.eu","Somruethai Wanwong","!image-20260122-125117.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260122-125132.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T12:52:16.080Z"],["3830594","CEBF-1709","CEBF","oleg.demkiv@bolt.eu","Oleh Demkiv","[~accountid:712020:7621878e-e68d-4cea-9df5-171c95c4c62d] yes, makes sense","2026-01-22T12:52:20.265Z"],["3830595","BDB-1461","BDB","amal.bahar@bolt.eu","Amal Bahar","[~accountid:60ab71565dc18500701cae80] thanks for sharing the link. I’ve added my comments. Wanted to clarify few things:\n\n1) Does the Hopp Plus launch assets cover assets for Ads (static/motion) as well- couldn’t find them? \n2) We also launched [vertical banners + 1 story slide|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/6366625878/New+Vertical+Banners+Setup+Guide+-+Home+Screen+and+Active+order?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiYjkzYzBkODk3MDAyNGYxMGJmZmQyNzJkM2IzNDY4NDMiLCJwIjoiY29uZmx1ZW5jZS1jaGF0cy1pbnQifQ] now. [~accountid:5fb225a6f2df6c00762b994d] was kind enough to help with the ratios: {{Visuals}}\n\n* Vertical Banner ratio: 9:20 ratio\n* Story slide ratio: 9:20 ratio\nLmk if we can design assets for these real estates as well. \n--\n\n{quote}PS! Let’s not gather LCM assets into a Figma page that is dedicated to emails only. {quote}\n\nNo clue about this.[~accountid:61cac1b0326554006c9b5945] maybe relevant to your workstream 🙏 ","2026-01-22T12:52:26.816Z"],["3830596","MVRT-1514","MVRT","anton.sljussarev@bolt.eu","Anton Sljussarev","[~accountid:623de187d32a94006a658c4a] ok,\n\nThen lets do like this (new budgets)\n\n|Algarve|€108|\n|Aveiro|€80|\n|Leiria|€70|\n|Viseu|€70|","2026-01-22T12:52:29.909Z"],["3830599","G3IOT-1214","G3IOT","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","it is capped to 4.2V using REG01. Or should it be capped to 4V given 200mV margin?","2026-01-22T12:53:27.159Z"],["3830608","DO-5821","DO","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","unified auth setup is preferred. Refer to [this document|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/4639785404/Setting+up+the+tooling+and+configuration]","2026-01-22T12:54:55.410Z"],["3830611","DO-5816","DO","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","Please use [unified auth|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/4639785404/Setting+up+the+tooling+and+configuration], the document has been updated with instructions.","2026-01-22T12:55:27.871Z"],["3830613","LSS-52184","LSS","gayanjalie.dissanayake@bolt.eu","Gayanjalie Dissanayake","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] provided a comment on 12th of December.  Adding 1 month more is ok by me, but till then make sure that they are complying with our standards. thanks cc [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ","2026-01-22T12:55:36.609Z"],["3830615","PFI-837241","PFI","victoria.akinfenwa@bolt-outsource.eu","Victoria Akinfenwa","!Screenshot_20260121_085313_OPay me.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T12:55:51.754Z"],["3830616","TAXP-1787","TAXP","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","done and saved [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1EZvQ_APGlgdWp_Sfnp997dYsMOiUyQZG?usp=drive_link]","2026-01-22T12:55:55.723Z"],["3830619","LSS-61783","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","[~accountid:712020:1d5390cd-af56-43c8-9d12-f431b20183ba] see [~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] response below","2026-01-22T12:56:10.705Z"],["3830620","LSS-61412","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hi [~accountid:712020:aa9604d8-cd49-4f98-bc6e-9c46af871b6b]! \nPlease see answers to clients' requests:\n\n# *Purpose of personal data use*\nThe use of personal data by Bolt cannot be limited solely to contract performance. All lawful bases for the processing of personal data by Bolt are set out in Section 4 of the Global Privacy Notice for Bolt Business: [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/global-privacy-notice-for-bolt-business/?category=boltBusiness|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/global-privacy-notice-for-bolt-business/?category=boltBusiness|smart-link] .\nThese include, among others, legitimate interests, legal obligations and vital interests, which may apply independently of contract performance. Please familiarise yourself with the referenced Privacy Notice, which governs data processing under the agreement.\n# *Contract term*\nAgreed. A fixed term of 3 years is added to [the Special Terms.|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XWurINlXdk4vqu9R8Gj7I7NKuD6vgXnak5u4FcVe9Jk/edit?tab=t.0]\n# *Unilateral changes -Clause 8.2*\nClause 8.2 applies only to the General Terms and Conditions and not to the Special Terms; that is, unilateral changes could be made only to the General T&Cs.\nGiven that Bolt provides services to a large number of customers, negotiation of the General T&Cs is not practically feasible, and this approach reflects standard industry practice. Any changes to the General T&C are subject to prior notice to all the Customers of at least 15 days. If the Customer does not accept the changes, the agreement may be terminated with 7 days’ notice (see clause 7.2 of [the General T&C)|https://bolt.eu/lv-lv/legal/terms-for-bolt-business-new/?category=boltBusiness]. Accordingly, clause 8.2 cannot be removed.\n# *Assignment (cession) rights – clause 8.5*\nThis clause reflects Bolt’s standard risk and operational framework and cannot be amended. Restricting the Customer’s ability to assign without Bolt’s prior consent ensures contractual clarity and control over who accesses the services, including from a sanctions-compliance perspective. Bolt’s limited right to assign supports potential corporate restructuring, financing, or group-level changes, which should not be subject to client approval. Any assignee must assume all obligations under the agreement and must not be a direct competitor of the Customer, which provides appropriate protection to the Customer.\n\nThe code of conduct added to [the Special terms|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XWurINlXdk4vqu9R8Gj7I7NKuD6vgXnak5u4FcVe9Jk/edit?tab=t.0] is approved, but the change to clause 2.5 is not - I have added the comment. \n\nIf in the future other clients ask the same questions, feel free to provide the same answer as shared here without double-checking with the legal team 🙂 ","2026-01-22T12:56:17.095Z"],["3830621","CNT-377","CNT","amal.bahar@bolt.eu","Amal Bahar","[~accountid:61cac1b0326554006c9b5945] Google docs would be perfect for collaborating with other teams. Thank you! ","2026-01-22T12:56:19.073Z"],["3830622","PFI-837243","PFI","tia.anderton@bolt.eu","Tia Anderton","!IMG_4728.PNG|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_4735.PNG|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T12:56:25.706Z"],["3830624","LSS-61998","LSS","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","thank you!","2026-01-22T12:56:40.153Z"],["3830625","LSS-61997","LSS","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","thank you!","2026-01-22T12:56:47.923Z"],["3830626","HS-29255","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hello!\n\nThe Employer confirmation letter has been sent for a signature and once signed you will receive it to your personal email.\n\n\n\nRegards,\nKadri","2026-01-22T12:57:02.487Z"],["3830627","HS-29276","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Even! Yes, of course - the confirmation letter about your previous employment was sent to your personal email via BoxSign.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina","2026-01-22T12:57:21.871Z"],["3830629","PFI-836772","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Patrycja, this typically happens when the driver does a double input by swiping twice. If a status change is made right after “Driving with client“, we translate this to a driver rejection (cases where rider doesn’t show up, driver doesn’t accept the rider etc etc). I can see they matched with the same rider right after that, and roughly in the same location, therefore no offline trip took place, and no one was incorrectly charged.\nIf the driver insists they did not accidentally swipe twice, then I’d recommend you reach out to tech-support, this might’ve been an app issue, and they might have more insight into this.\nThanks!\n","2026-01-22T12:57:46.052Z"],["3830631","LSS-58717","LSS","mauricio.oropeza@bolt.eu","Mauricio Oropeza","Hi [~accountid:712020:209f6e12-e421-4fbf-9a9f-60d100117bab], \n\nI asked the partner to update the contract to include both entities and receive the following comment/suggestion from their legal team. Can you please help me clarify and advice on best way to advance:\n\n\"Separately – I do not understand the request to add both entities. The contract needs to be entered into by one company, what is the purpose of the second company? If it’s for invoicing purposes we can factor that into the payment terms, but having two separate Bolt entities creates confusion over who is receiving the services, who is responsible for payment, who is providing us with the relevant licences, and who has the legal obligations under the agreement. Please find out the purpose behind the request so I can understand what we’re trying to do here.\"\n\n","2026-01-22T12:58:00.403Z"],["3830637","DO-5822","DO","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","Please check the updated document, we suggest [using unified auth|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/4639785404/Setting+up+the+tooling+and+configuration] now.","2026-01-22T12:58:58.639Z"],["3830638","RDXENG-4791","RDXENG","goutham.perugu@bolt.eu","Goutham Perugu","Fixed in scope of [this|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDXENG-4663] ticket","2026-01-22T12:59:03.126Z"],["3830639","PFI-837245","PFI","arfeef.abdulsata@bolt-outsource.eu","Arfeef Abdulsata","!1768894735671.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T12:59:08.242Z"],["3830645","BD-2002","BD","ave.tarend@bolt.eu","Ave Tarend","Released on {{2026-01-22}}","2026-01-22T13:00:09.034Z"],["3830650","LSS-61311","LSS","kaija.riismaa@bolt.eu","Kaija Riismaa","Hi Kristi\n\nPlease submit a new ticket regarding Deniss and Kristi and please also add final versions of the POA-s to the ticket (incl. full names, identification codes, correct dates etc.). \n\nBest regards, \nKaija","2026-01-22T13:01:16.646Z"],["3830655","PFI-837249","PFI","ana.pelivanu@bolt-outsource.eu","Ana Pelivanu","[^1830144457 22-12-2025.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-22T13:03:06.138Z"],["3830656","CMO-12981","CMO","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Remove Bolt Cards from the user persona list - Nigel confirmed it will be remove from Business","2026-01-22T13:03:30.068Z"],["3830658","LSS-59597","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:626c24971a4eb30069d28197], it might be the case that the agreement signed years ago had not been properly reviewed by Legal at the time (which [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] and I cannot comment on since we were not involved), resulting in us committing to unbalanced and non-client-friendly terms. Therefore, this time we would prefer to review it carefully to mitigate any risks and avoid the need to spend time on a review again if we decide to sign the same agreement in the future 🙏 ","2026-01-22T13:03:49.538Z"],["3830661","LSS-61821","LSS","mo.salama@bolt.eu","Mo Salama","Hi Raivis,\n\nthey have sent an updated version to address your concerns.\n\nplease let me know if this works.\n\nSincerely,\n\nMo","2026-01-22T13:04:24.363Z"],["3830662","TAX2-598","TAX2","victor.garces@bolt.eu","Víctor Garcés","+Update re new FI B2G entity+\n\n- Most efficient way is an off-the-shelf company;\n\n-VAT registration, the entity´s new board could initiate the registration immediately after the transfer (once the resolution for new board appointment is executed);\n\n- Object of the company (“_The company shall provide administrative services and business support to its parent company and provision of intermediary services for taxi and passenger transportation services, as well as other related activities._”)\n\n- Same address as the current FI existing entity (PL 279, 00101 Helsinki, Finland)","2026-01-22T13:04:27.635Z"],["3830663","LSS-61307","LSS","ksenia.korolkova@bolt.eu","Ksenia Korolkova","Hi [~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] , \n\nPlease find updated Related Party [IAS 24 disclosure form here (as of 31.12.2025)|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_zk_pTQyr4oQ-E-8fFtudJQ93lPsqR3V5a78jnczoGc/edit?tab=t.0].\n\nPlease also find attached the updated forms for Ahto and Martin. \n\nJust in case also copying here previous explanations provided in Slack:\n\n# *Jevgeni Kabanov / Bondora Finance AS and Bondora Group AS*\nAs per our disclosure approach, which is in line with IAS 24, we disclose only the entities being \"controlled\" by our key management personnel (i.e entities in which they hold direct or indirect ownership of at least 25% of the shares or have the ability to exercise control through other means, such as granted voting rights). Jevgeni Kabanov is a member of the supervisory board of Bondora Finance AS/ Bondora Group AS, however, these entities do not meet the definition of “controlled entities” and therefore have not been included in the list of related parties.\nFor reference, information regarding membership on supervisory boards of other entities (i.e broader disclosure) is provided only for Markus Villig, as he is considered the person controlling Bolt.\nPlease also note that Jevgeni Kabanov has held the supervisory board position since 2023, and this disclosure approach has been consistently accepted by the auditors in prior years without any questions raised.\nCould you please confirm whether there has been any change in interpretation or disclosure logic this year? If so, we would appreciate your clarification on the reasoning and basis for such change.\n# *Pavel Karagjaur / TextMagic AS*\nThe same principle applies to Pavel Karagjaur as a member of the supervisory board of TextMagic AS, which does not meet the definition of \"controlled entity\". He has held this position since 2022, and the same disclosure approach has been applied consistently without questions from auditors in previous years.\n\n[^Ahto Kink - related parties form - MB members - 31.12.2025.xlsx]\n[^Martin Villig - related parties form - SB members - 31.12.2025.xlsx]\n\n","2026-01-22T13:04:29.002Z"],["3830664","LSS-61821","LSS","mo.salama@bolt.eu","Mo Salama","[^Bolt x Tilstra_Service Agreement Michel.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T13:05:16.686Z"],["3830665","PFI-837250","PFI","ana.pelivanu@bolt-outsource.eu","Ana Pelivanu","[^1844820074 19-01-2026.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-22T13:05:17.164Z"],["3830667","CSDT-949","CSDT","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","{{2026-01-22}} \n\nprice review reports are built and added to the board - [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/boards/1760|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/boards/1760]\n\n* [Price Review Deep Dive|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/47115?toggle=fil,pik]\n* [Price Reviews|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/29745]","2026-01-22T13:05:57.409Z"],["3830668","G3IOT-1214","G3IOT","kaarel.vandler@bolt.eu","Kaarel Vandler","cap to 4V","2026-01-22T13:05:59.909Z"],["3830670","DSR-2883","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Hi [~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] ! [Here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1RcbdKpHdbr9bYulKR98TvJMDiPMqVTn9] would be the data and [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_yi3T685IuFxHXjew_Fccy6aZeIVPWA6vAnz8fO0p20/edit?tab=t.0] would be the response. Please let me know if I should request the GDrive link rather outside of the Jira ticket 🙏 ","2026-01-22T13:06:12.748Z"],["3830673","L10N-29545","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29543](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29543)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T13:07:12.609Z"],["3830674","L10N-29546","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29543](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29543)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T13:07:14.198Z"],["3830675","L10N-29549","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists worki