s for collaborating!","2026-01-22T13:08:07.362Z"],["3830683","L10N-29578","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29543](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29543)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T13:08:07.559Z"],["3830686","WFM-10068","WFM","fidan.kamilova@bolt.eu","Fidan Kamilova","Confirmed","2026-01-22T13:08:23.412Z"],["3830687","LSS-61924","LSS","artiemi.jewsiejenko@bolt.eu","Artiemi Pawlak-Jewsiejenko","[^BOLT_FOOD___Umowa_marketingowa__Sushi_Szop___Hawaiian_Poke_Bowl_-km.mroczkowski_gmail.com.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T13:08:29.130Z"],["3830688","CCM-22300","CCM","peter.vrba@bolt-outsource.eu","Peter Vrba","[^New TalentLMS Training Request Form.xlsx]","2026-01-22T13:08:44.363Z"],["3830690","MM-943","MM","kartikeya.sharma@bolt.eu","Kartikeya Sharma","{{s3://bolt-campaign-bulk-import/PRELIVE/rh-demand-session-discounting/}}\nhere you can see the structure, same for {{LIVE}}.\n\n{{metadata.json}} contains the latest file name and [budget-manager-targets/|https://eu-central-1.console.aws.amazon.com/s3/buckets/bolt-campaign-bulk-import?region=eu-central-1&prefix=PRELIVE/rh-demand-session-discounting/budget-manager-targets/&showversions=false] will contain a file with that name.\nfile contains {{{\"campaign_id\": 2.3, \"campaign_id_2\": 5.6, ...}}}\nIt only has entries for the campaigns that are running. Once the campaign finishes there is no entry in the file for that campaign. So If you plan to use redis lets set a timeout of 1 day for keys.\nIn case no entry exists for a campaign_id please send {{null}} in the request.","2026-01-22T13:09:03.028Z"],["3830692","WFM-10068","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","done","2026-01-22T13:09:20.498Z"],["3830695","WD-22665","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:637f4716de5cdaba3a67c532] , \nthis is because with the Integration we assign the due date from Telema information and we ignore the payment terms in Workday. \nFor the credit notes we actually ignore the due date set in Telema and we take the payment terms in Workday. \n\nI’m already working with [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] to update the Credit Note Due Date field in Workday with the date from Telema.","2026-01-22T13:09:50.307Z"],["3830697","PRIV-520","PRIV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Latest status update:*\n\n#  Legal shared Bolt’s follow-up questions with the Partner and requested a meeting with their legal counsel and compliance manager to discuss the proposed set-ups.\n# Waiting for the updates from the partner.","2026-01-22T13:10:10.656Z"],["3830699","FRAUDOPS-1120","FRAUDOPS","mark@bolt.eu","Mark-Erik Valge","Analysis notebook: [https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/212286361697760?o=3598988355446810#command/6996872918542377|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/212286361697760?o=3598988355446810#command/6996872918542377]","2026-01-22T13:10:35.743Z"],["3830701","TAXP-1150","TAXP","wenjing.zhang@bolt.eu","Grace Wenjing Zhang","A few views have been designed, due to data availability:\n\n* “net VAT” on entity level\n* “Total tax paid” on entity level\n* “Tax type summary“ yearly ","2026-01-22T13:11:19.674Z"],["3830704","COP-1971","COP","kartikeya.sharma@bolt.eu","Kartikeya Sharma","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MM-943|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MM-943|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T13:12:15.479Z"],["3830710","TS-4658","TS","laura.kaselaid@bolt.eu","Laura Kaselaid","Anna has asked about lunches in general - do we want to have 3x Fork (they can arrange like some card type system) or do we want just for seminar day and let sub-team later figure it out?","2026-01-22T13:13:25.319Z"],["3830711","PFI-837255","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 10.11.00 AM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T13:13:39.184Z"],["3830712","LSS-52184","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:5f896ba356eec000768527be] \n\nCould you please confirm if we can get the clean version of the documents from City Legal for final review? CC [~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c] \n\nFrom data protection side, there appears to be no outstanding matters apart from the security measures, which seems to be resolved with [~accountid:6061907490e3950069a3a5d3] .","2026-01-22T13:13:39.577Z"],["3830716","CCM-22300","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey Peter 👋 \n\nThey have all been assigned. ☀️ \n\nBest,\n\nIrena","2026-01-22T13:14:02.485Z"],["3830717","LSS-61841","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:61374989bba6c7006a2616ba] please find the risk analysis below:\n\n\n\nh1. Courier data uploaded to Meta\n\n*Proposal:* Share personal data of ~70,000 Bolt couriers to Meta. Meta would try to match couriers to existing profiles to exclude those from certain campaigns. \n\n*Business goal:* reduce ad spend & improve campaign efficiency\n\n*Personal data shared:* first name, last name, DoB, phone number, email address\n\n\n\nh2. Privacy risk\n\nh3. 1. Out of ordinary marketing data sharing\n\nUploading identifiable courier data to a social media platform for profile matching is considered risky processing, especially when:\n\n* it happens at large scale\n* concerns Data Subjects who are economically dependent on the Controller (Bolt)\n* the data is used for matching identities, not just analytics\n\n{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}\n*Risk 1:* This type of use attracts much more regulatory attention than standard ad tracking or pixel-based marketing.\n{panel}\n\nh3. 2. The amount of data is more than needed\n\nUsing name + date of birth + phone + email together creates a near-unique identity profile. From a privacy point of view:\n\n* Date of birth is especially hard to justify for ad exclusion\n* Combining multiple identifiers goes beyond what is typically necessary\n\n{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}\n*Risk 2:* Regulators expect data minimization → “only what is strictly required”. \n{panel}\n\nh3. 3. Couriers would not reasonably expect this\n\nEven though our privacy notice mentions sharing data with advertising partners in general terms, Couriers would not reasonably expect:\n\n* Their personal details to be shared with Meta\n* Their data to be matched against social media profiles\n\n{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}\n*Risk 3:* Fairness and trust issue – This is important because privacy rules are strongly based on reasonable expectations.\n{panel}\n\nh3. 4. Fragile legal basis\n\nThe only realistic legal basis here is Bolt’s *Legitimate Interest*. That requires showing that:\n\n* Bolt’s interest (ad cost optimization)\n* Does not override courier rights and expectations\n\nGiven – the scale, the platform (Meta), the data types, the Courier context\n\n{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}\n*Risk 4:* Weak and easily challengeable legal basis.\n{panel}\n\nh3. 5. DPIA likely required\n\nA Data Protection Impact Assessment *(DPIA)* is very likely required before proceeding. Because this is: large scale, involving Couriers, using identity matching, involving a major external platform.\n\n{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}\n*Risk 5:* A DPIA may end up with recommendation not to proceed.\n{panel}\n\nh2. 👉 👈  What this means for the business\n\n* Higher likelihood of regulatory scrutiny\n* Potential orders to stop processing\n* Fines and mandatory changes if challenged\n* Reputational risk\n* Brand reputation & trust\n* Commercial risk: marketing gains are indirect and uncertain → Reg or PR fallout would likely outweigh savings\n* High internal cost to implement and defend\n\nh2. :pleading_face: What if marketing team still wants to proceed?\n\nTo lower the risk, Privacy recommends:\n\n💚 Reducing the data shared: avoid names and date of birth\n\n💚 Use hashed identifiers only (email _or_ phone number, not both)\n\n💚 Put in a formal data sharing agreement in place (I was not able to find one on Meta website that we may have agreed to when signing up)\n\n💚 Let Privacy know so that we can complete LIA and DPIA\n\n\n\nEven then, residual risk remains high. Bottom line is that this activity is not a small marketing optimization, it’s a high-risk data use. Privacy strongly recommends re-thinking the approach or using lower-risk alternatives that do not require uploading identifiable courier data to social media platforms.\n\n\n\nIn case of any questions or requests, please let me know. 🙏 \n\nCC: [~accountid:5a670f010c10ac2e28964251] [~accountid:614ad8fe47a8b5006f846ec4] ","2026-01-22T13:14:06.999Z"],["3830718","XP-2950","XP","yaroslav.morozevych@bolt.eu","Yaroslav Morozevych","h2. Results [[PR|https://github.com/bolteu/data-experimentation/pull/1125/]]\n\n* Deprecated the remaining food v3 metrics {{v3/metrics/targeting_user/food/pricing/*_report.yaml}} by adding the {{deprecated: true}} flag to 24 YAML metric configuration files.","2026-01-22T13:14:10.703Z"],["3830719","LSS-61865","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:4031005b-be5e-413a-b7da-919304795012] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^31.12.2025 Dubai taxi company balance (a32a88c1-385d-438f-9bc7-15958459467e).pdf] [^31.12.2025 Dubai taxi company balance.pdf] ","2026-01-22T13:14:15.672Z"],["3830722","PFI-836125","PFI","kulli.tuka@bolt.eu","Külli Tuka","!image.png|width=1358,height=762,alt=\"image.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-22T13:14:47.235Z"],["3830723","PFI-836777","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Diana, we’re seeing and increased amount of such orders. Most likely explanation for these are either a double-swipe from the driver, changing statuses after “Driving with client“ - this translates to a driver rejection.. or a double-input from the app.\nI see they accepted the next ride from roughly the same location, meaning no offline trip took place and seemingly no one was incorrectly charged.\nI’ll be including this as one of the examples once I escalate this to rides-order devs.\nThank you for reporting.","2026-01-22T13:15:07.793Z"],["3830725","MKP-9913","MKP","abdelhalim.machehalek@bolt.eu","Abdelhalim Machehalek","Hi. To launch hopp plus in canada we what to restrict getting hopp plus benefits in the bolt app. As I can see we integrate with you using two endpoint on our end({{subscription-benefits-internal}}) :\n1.   {{/internal/getPricingConfiguration}}\n2. {{/internal/getSubscriptionParametersForRides}}\nPlease propagate application brand(hopp/bolt) to this endpoints.\ncc: *@user-U05M7R0937T* *@user-U09JJC4EG0K*.","2026-01-22T13:15:52.025Z"],["3830726","MKP-9913","MKP",null,"Slack","[Abdelhalim Machehalek|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:5290f272-66ef-467e-a008-8904b3bc928d] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CGLJZE1SA/p1769082859427249?thread_ts=1769082859.427249&cid=CGLJZE1SA|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CGLJZE1SA/p1769082859427249?thread_ts=1769082859.427249&cid=CGLJZE1SA|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-22T13:15:53.324Z"],["3830727","MKP-9913","MKP","mateja.sela@bolt.eu","Mateja Sela","Hey [@abdelhalim.machehalek|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:5290f272-66ef-467e-a008-8904b3bc928d] would this fall under your team? This would be a P0 and we can align priorities with product. [@prateek.gauba|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:6f095333-c438-429c-9660-a9de5d845fe7] maybe we should go through the official dependency process through IDEAs?","2026-01-22T13:15:54.212Z"],["3830728","MKP-9913","MKP","mateja.sela@bolt.eu","Mateja Sela","[@artem.markov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:786a23a6-5409-4cc1-9e53-e525f53a4332] how hard would it be to do this ourselves and have the PR approved by pricing? If it's a small change maybe LLM can help :eyes::claude-code:","2026-01-22T13:15:55.651Z"],["3830729","MKP-9913","MKP","abdelhalim.machehalek@bolt.eu","Abdelhalim Machehalek","Hey,\n\n[@artem.markov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:786a23a6-5409-4cc1-9e53-e525f53a4332] what are the pricing endpoints that you call from your service ?","2026-01-22T13:15:56.947Z"],["3830730","MKP-9913","MKP","artem.markov@bolt.eu","Artem Markov","this.pricingOrderApi.getFinalPrice\nthis.pricingApi.removeOffersForUser","2026-01-22T13:15:58.317Z"],["3830731","MKP-9913","MKP","artem.markov@bolt.eu","Artem Markov","and you are calling getPricingConfiguration. And getSubscriptionParametersForRides is called by multiple services\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AA749M6DT/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AA749M6DT/image.png|smart-link]\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AA8G18RQW/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AA8G18RQW/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-22T13:15:59.655Z"],["3830732","MKP-9913","MKP","abdelhalim.machehalek@bolt.eu","Abdelhalim Machehalek","for search-worker dependency, you'd need to ask *#channel-C02LWCMELDD*\nand for order-client-create you need to check with riderX","2026-01-22T13:16:01.287Z"],["3830733","MKP-9913","MKP","abdelhalim.machehalek@bolt.eu","Abdelhalim Machehalek","We can handle the pricing-calculator dependency","2026-01-22T13:16:04.487Z"],["3830734","MKP-9913","MKP","artem.markov@bolt.eu","Artem Markov","Thx. Please add brand there.","2026-01-22T13:16:05.973Z"],["3830735","LSS-62011","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-22T13:16:07.965Z"],["3830736","DSR-3959","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T13:16:07.998Z"],["3830737","LSS-55652","LSS","tomas.mulac@bolt.eu","Tomáš Mulač","Hi [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] \n\nI'd like to reopen this ticket so we can finalize the contract signing. Below I'm sharing the latest version of the agreement, which has already been reviewed from your side as well as by Peakforce.\n\nKey updates in this version:\n\nAll your legal amendments have been implemented, including:\n\n* Clause 4.6: Addition of \"as for your own actions\"\n* Clause 4.7: Specification of weekly reports (by Tuesday of the following week, unless otherwise agreed in writing)\n* Clauses 5.1, 6.5, 8.3, 9.1: All amendments included\n* Clauses 11.1-11.3: Revised termination terms implemented\n* New provisions after clause 11: Added as per your requirements\n\nBolt's DPA template has been implemented (replacing Peakforce's original DPA template), as required.\n\nAttached documents:\n\nFinal contract version (with all amendments)\n\nCould you please confirm that everything still looks correct and aligned, and that we can proceed to signature? If you notice any remaining issues or required updates, please let me know.\n\nThank you for your support throughout this process.\n\nBest regards,\n\nTomáš Mulač\n\nDocument: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/196TJDUd6t_Ev4LUA0MUEOPZzg0INzw_o/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/196TJDUd6t_Ev4LUA0MUEOPZzg0INzw_o/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T13:16:15.069Z"],["3830738","WEBSD-1498","WEBSD","vit.sztogryn@bolt.eu","Vít Sztogrýn","Hey!\nthank you for your answer. Yes, these should be a new support pages for new category in Prague. It is quite important to have these pages live to reduce the tickets of drivers and riders in the future. I will talk to the CS Knowledge Management team.\nThank you","2026-01-22T13:16:26.940Z"],["3830739","BDMCD-49","BDMCD","mercedes.ramirezmolina@bolt.eu","Mercedes Ramírez Molina","Driver asked for a deferral of payment due to an illness (providing proof). Current income below 600€ so we granted a six month extension before enforcing payments.","2026-01-22T13:16:43.201Z"],["3830741","DRX-28218","DRX","fedor.sokovikov@bolt.eu","Fedor Sokovikov","No need to test it, this is a base implementation. Feature is hidden and is under a ff.","2026-01-22T13:17:52.890Z"],["3830743","LSS-61934","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:61f116071c42100069544016] ! The invitation to sign is not visible yet.","2026-01-22T13:18:03.908Z"],["3830744","LSS-58645","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","Hi team, the partner has accepted all changes recommended. We can proceed to send it out for signatures. \n\nThanks. ","2026-01-22T13:18:06.986Z"],["3830745","LSS-61883","LSS","jessie.fernandes@bolt.eu","Jessie Fernandes","Hey [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742], hope you’re doing well!\n\nCould you please give us an ETA on this request?\n\nLet me know if you have any question, thanks!\n\nBest regards,","2026-01-22T13:18:45.890Z"],["3830746","TS-4658","TS","aleksandr.bregin@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Bregin","Let’s figure it out as sub-teams.","2026-01-22T13:18:59.485Z"],["3830747","FPD-1564","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","[~accountid:712020:3a4d1838-5610-4f85-a454-883aeab2b150] let me know what you think of this, since you’ve developed the conversion models you might have a strong opinion about this idea.","2026-01-22T13:19:14.455Z"],["3830749","RS-1946","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:603cb85ec58c720071175949]\n\nMakes sense now! Data can be disclosed","2026-01-22T13:19:29.455Z"],["3830751","LSS-61971","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","\n[^Bolt Technology OÜ_POA for TMP.docx] ","2026-01-22T13:19:51.196Z"],["3830752","TS-4658","TS","laura.kaselaid@bolt.eu","Laura Kaselaid","[~accountid:5bec40ab90dcd93d2d534fce] Alrighty, then just seminar day, so people don’t roam too far away 😄 ","2026-01-22T13:20:05.675Z"],["3830754","DRX-26882","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-26840 has been resolved","2026-01-22T13:20:18.130Z"],["3830755","DRX-26940","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-26840 has been resolved","2026-01-22T13:20:18.115Z"],["3830756","DRX-26866","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-26840 has been resolved","2026-01-22T13:20:18.109Z"],["3830757","DRX-26881","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-26840 has been resolved","2026-01-22T13:20:18.110Z"],["3830758","DRX-26883","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-26840 has been resolved","2026-01-22T13:20:18.209Z"],["3830759","DRX-26898","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-26840 has been resolved","2026-01-22T13:20:18.280Z"],["3830760","DRX-26889","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-26840 has been resolved","2026-01-22T13:20:18.831Z"],["3830761","DRX-26864","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-26840 has been resolved","2026-01-22T13:20:20.277Z"],["3830766","ADS-117","ADS","olga.vyrostko@bolt.eu","Olga Vyrostko","QoL improvement: separated from the main migration epic to keep it cleaner. ","2026-01-22T13:21:01.043Z"],["3830769","DRX-16704","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-16695 has been resolved","2026-01-22T13:21:35.655Z"],["3830770","CNT-461","CNT","anton.sljussarev@bolt.eu","Anton Sljussarev","[~accountid:6163ec849cdb930072d02e8e] \n\nI was asked to expand on the Eater emails – added  4-6 emails with cashback promotion.\n\nOther comment – lets add section with mentioning restaurants in each of the emails.\n\n*Emails 1-3*\n\n# *Start fresh with XX% off and free delivery:* [https://www.figma.com/design/U7wnv1Gz61rZREc4SMWg4c/LCM-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Storytelling-Emails?node-id=5-95565&t=fCiACrmN1NARd5pM-0|https://www.figma.com/design/U7wnv1Gz61rZREc4SMWg4c/LCM-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Storytelling-Emails?node-id=5-95565&t=fCiACrmN1NARd5pM-0|smart-link]  \n# *Enjoy XX% off your next order:* [https://www.figma.com/design/U7wnv1Gz61rZREc4SMWg4c/LCM-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Storytelling-Emails?node-id=1260-35487&t=d5idaGhpwBATrpWK-0|https://www.figma.com/design/U7wnv1Gz61rZREc4SMWg4c/LCM-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Storytelling-Emails?node-id=1260-35487&t=d5idaGhpwBATrpWK-0|smart-link] \n# *Save XX% on your next order:* [https://www.figma.com/design/U7wnv1Gz61rZREc4SMWg4c/LCM-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Storytelling-Emails?node-id=1266-29135&t=d5idaGhpwBATrpWK-0|https://www.figma.com/design/U7wnv1Gz61rZREc4SMWg4c/LCM-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Storytelling-Emails?node-id=1266-29135&t=d5idaGhpwBATrpWK-0|smart-link] \n\n*Emails 4-6*\n\n* Get XX% Cashback + Free Delivery\n* Loyal customers offer. XX% Cashback. Free Delivery.\n\n* 1. Earn XX% Cashback. Order Food you love: [https://www.figma.com/design/U7wnv1Gz61rZREc4SMWg4c/LCM-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Storytelling-Emails?node-id=1252-24450&t=d5idaGhpwBATrpWK-0|https://www.figma.com/design/U7wnv1Gz61rZREc4SMWg4c/LCM-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Storytelling-Emails?node-id=1252-24450&t=d5idaGhpwBATrpWK-0|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T13:22:17.795Z"],["3830772","L10N-29583","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29543](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29543)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T13:22:33.222Z"],["3830773","L10N-29584","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29543](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29543)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T13:22:36.578Z"],["3830774","LSS-61772","LSS","domantas.dabrukas@bolt.eu","Domantas Dabrukas","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432], Could you please let me know why it is taking so long to sign this document?","2026-01-22T13:22:51.224Z"],["3830778","LSS-61908","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] , thank you for your explanations. \n\nBelow I am sharing the response draft: \n\n[~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] can you please review it and amend if needed as this is more of a privacy related question than purely legal. This rider is very persistent and we need to be sure to handle this appropriately. \n\nThank you very much! \n\n_Dear Mr Wixted,_\n\n_Thank you for your message and for sharing your concerns in such detail. We appreciate the seriousness with which you are approaching this matter._\n\n_At Bolt, we are fully committed to complying with our obligations under UK data protection law, including the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR), and to supporting law enforcement and regulatory bodies in accordance with the law and our operator licensing requirements._\n\n_We understand that your concerns relate both to the outcome of a police investigation and to the data that Bolt provided to law enforcement and to you directly under your subject access request._\n\n_To ensure clarity, we would like to set out the following key points in response:_\n\n_1._ *_Disclosure to Police and Law Enforcement_*\n\n_Bolt responds to police requests for information under the relevant lawful bases set out in UK GDPR, including where necessary for the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences under the Data Protection Act 2018, Part 3._\n\n_We do not “sanitise” or selectively withhold evidence. We provide responsive information as requested by the investigating authority, ensuring that we respect both our legal duties and the privacy rights of all individuals involved. This includes our responsibility under Article 5(1)(c) UK GDPR to limit disclosure to what is adequate, relevant and not excessive in relation to the purpose._\n\n_We are not investigators or adjudicators, and the decision on whether to pursue or close a criminal investigation rests solely with the relevant police force. If you believe that material facts were not considered, we respectfully recommend submitting any new evidence directly to the investigating officer or through a formal complaint to the Metropolitan Police Service._\n\n_2._ *_Driver Information and Data Protection Law_*\n\n_Under UK GDPR, your right to access personal data (Article 15) does not extend to data that solely identifies another individual, such as the driver, unless you are also identifiable from it and there is no adverse impact on their rights. Information such as GPS logs, internal driver notes, or operational details that relate only to the driver are classified as third-party personal data and are legally protected under Article 15(4) UK GDPR and Recital 63._\n\n_We have carefully reviewed your request and shared all personal data to which you are lawfully entitled, including records of your ride, relevant communications, and copies of the disclosures made to authorities. Redactions were applied where necessary to protect third-party rights, which is not only lawful but required under data protection legislation._\n\n_3._ *_Preservation of Records_*\n\n_We acknowledge your request regarding the retention of specific data. Please be assured that Bolt maintains operational and safety-related records in accordance with our legal obligations and internal retention schedules. While no evidence of unlawful destruction has occurred, we take such concerns seriously and have ensured that the relevant records are preserved in line with applicable legal and regulatory frameworks._\n\n_4._ *_Cooperation with Transport for London_*\n\n_We fully recognise the importance of our responsibilities under our Private Hire Operator's Licence issued by Transport for London. This includes the duty to cooperate with law enforcement and to maintain high standards of safety and transparency. Where serious incidents are reported, we notify TfL as required and in a timely manner._\n\n_No regulatory breach has occurred in this matter. We continue to work constructively with authorities and comply with all applicable licensing and privacy obligations._\n\n_5._ *_Closing Remarks_*\n\n_We understand the gravity of the concerns you have raised and assure you that we do not take them lightly. At the same time, we must act in strict compliance with the law. We are unable to disclose information about third parties, or resubmit data to law enforcement in the absence of a lawful request._\n\n_Should the Metropolitan Police Service wish to reopen or further review the case, we will of course respond fully and lawfully to any renewed request._\n\n_We thank you again for your engagement, and should you have additional queries relating to your own personal data, we would be happy to assist via our Privacy Office at [privacy@bolt.eu]._\n\n_Yours sincerely,_","2026-01-22T13:23:07.000Z"],["3830779","LSS-61865","LSS","angelina.korol@bolt.eu","Angelina Korol","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] , is it possible to add the amount 15,088,076.95 AED to the template? At the moment, the amount field is empty, so it’s not visible which amount has been confirmed by us.\n\n","2026-01-22T13:23:09.062Z"],["3830783","LSS-61983","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:9c4a8cc2-68e4-4823-8ce8-1919a40a76f5] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^DECEMBER25_INTRA_FORM_SALES (1) (97c76844-8734-433f-a47e-c33c65169b54).PDF] ","2026-01-22T13:23:39.620Z"],["3830787","DSR-3947","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Invoice link sent out","2026-01-22T13:24:49.553Z"],["3830788","LSS-61721","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:712020:6f563341-b27c-4653-b7d4-c67e881cc931] , in which Polish entity are you employed in? ","2026-01-22T13:24:59.683Z"],["3830790","PFI-813837","PFI","felicia.oprea@bolt-outsource.eu","Felicia Ștefania Oprea","Hello, \n\nany updates? ","2026-01-22T13:25:21.975Z"],["3830797","WEBSD-1504","WEBSD","jevgeni.komkin@bolt.eu","Jevgeni Komkin","can you provide the link that requires to be shortened?","2026-01-22T13:26:26.055Z"],["3830800","MLC-3830","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*W4 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:*\n** Created a new horizontal banner for in-apps due to vertical banner launch cancellation. Shared strings with local teams in the channel.\n* *Next steps:*\n** Nida processing tickets","2026-01-22T13:27:08.486Z"],["3830802","MLC-3416","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*W4 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:*\n** Activation comms setup in progress.\n* *Next steps:*\n** Finish setting up comms and share previews with the local team to review.","2026-01-22T13:27:45.591Z"],["3830803","LSS-59597","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","If helpful [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] I found the ticket from the previous time we changed offices. It was however not reviewed by myself (just handled registering the new address) and the review was before I joined but please see here: [FI Real Estate: Please review potential new office contract|https://taxify.atlassian.net/issues?jql=textfields%20~%20%22office%20finland*%22&selectedIssue=LSS-29957] ","2026-01-22T13:27:53.583Z"],["3830804","TAXP-2007","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filing and payment completed in time\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1h5rPO_Dk-weMt1wQ3NeKheANwFjZ0GNP|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1h5rPO_Dk-weMt1wQ3NeKheANwFjZ0GNP]","2026-01-22T13:28:04.473Z"],["3830805","MP-3486","MP","taxifyqa@bolt.eu","QA Testing","PR comment for QA:\n- Verify the navigator chooser shows \"Bolt navigation\" when TBT is ready.\r\n- Confirm internal navigation button icon switches between follow and default modes.\r\n- Ensure external navigation button visibility behaves correctly with internal navigation.\r\n- Check TbT map recenters on the follow when moved by user after 5 seconds","2026-01-22T13:28:34.875Z"],["3830806","LSS-58897","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:6ca2307e-6766-4d7e-a7b5-7f3b9a6cb0b6] - thank you for your responses from last week.\n\nI have no further concerns beyond the announcement. I would like to check that the campaign's T&Cs will clearly state that participants' names will be publicly announced and that Bolt will rely on an appropriate lawful basis such as inferred consent. I will wait for [~accountid:61addb80b0b630006a695081] to provide the adopted T&Cs for this campaign.\n\nAdditionally, if you wish to promote the winner in our marketing materials and use their photos/videos, they must sign an Image Release Consent Form. This is crucial. If needed, you can coordinate with [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a].","2026-01-22T13:28:44.274Z"],["3830807","PFI-837013","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello [~accountid:712020:3e9e9420-805b-4052-8edd-e17b6a40436e], \n\nUnfortunately, we can’t provide a proof of the reversal of the payment. The user should be able to get the amount within 14 days according to their bank internal processes.","2026-01-22T13:28:51.927Z"],["3830808","TAXP-2010","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filing and payment completed\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1PeJ_mi1FIHsy7lnbGM3wArcPcsbJXOvk|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1PeJ_mi1FIHsy7lnbGM3wArcPcsbJXOvk|smart-card]","2026-01-22T13:29:35.075Z"],["3830809","LSS-59252","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n# No personal data would be collected beyond existing Hopp account information; winners would be contacted via their registered email.\n# Privacy is awaiting the T&Cs copy to check the privacy section. Key concern is to ensure public announcement of winners is done lawfully.","2026-01-22T13:29:50.483Z"],["3830810","LSS-61721","LSS","darius.poursiami@bolt.eu","Darius Poursiami","Hi [~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c] , it would be Bolt Services Sp. z o.o.","2026-01-22T13:29:55.245Z"],["3830811","WEBSD-1504","WEBSD","abhishek.gupta@bolt.eu","Abhishek Gupta","It is: [https://bolt.onelink.me/sbJ2/ffce81ec|https://bolt.onelink.me/sbJ2/ffce81ec] \n\n","2026-01-22T13:30:01.846Z"],["3830812","TAXP-2012","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filing and payment done on time\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1zEoqU9lb8kIWMHEx5-UyxF39-MbB6CEW|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1zEoqU9lb8kIWMHEx5-UyxF39-MbB6CEW|smart-card]","2026-01-22T13:30:38.584Z"],["3830813","LSS-61874","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] thank you! I’m off for vacation tomorrow and for two weeks so [~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] can help you during this time 🙏 ","2026-01-22T13:30:45.397Z"],["3830814","MTE-1284","MTE","mateusz.sabat@bolt.eu","Mateusz Sabat","There is “Lux Ride Finished” when searchSubcategoryGroup is one of {{[\"vip\", \"vip_plus\", \"vip_xl\"]}} categories, do you want to add new not-related to “Lux”?[~accountid:6321aad6cf721d09b0166767] ","2026-01-22T13:31:14.614Z"],["3830815","TAXP-2013","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filing and payment made on time\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1AI_J2M2EzImg4EWF321NGq-87AqDzV43|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1AI_J2M2EzImg4EWF321NGq-87AqDzV43]","2026-01-22T13:31:25.608Z"],["3830816","DSR-3961","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T13:31:36.359Z"],["3830818","LSS-58897","LSS","kristjan.okas@bolt.eu","Kristjan Okas","Hey!\n\nNoted and I am on it - reporting back soon.","2026-01-22T13:32:20.665Z"],["3830819","LSS-55235","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n# The timeline for a decision on AU is still unclear, despite the business case review.\n# Legal & Tax will retain the AU entity until we receive clearer direction from Paddy & Markus.\n\nSince the project has been on hold for nearly six months, I will close the ticket and reopen it once the expansion timelines are established.","2026-01-22T13:32:52.851Z"],["3830820","LSS-61772","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:618d20acfba4d0006ae30dd3] ! This happened due to the high workload this week. The document will be ready today.","2026-01-22T13:32:59.514Z"],["3830821","RCE-368","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769088766151449]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-368 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-22T13:33:00.199Z"],["3830822","TAXP-2014","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filing and payment made and completed on time\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1uZfHavtGOIqhRhwBWGX6rJULg4Xc_JXB|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1uZfHavtGOIqhRhwBWGX6rJULg4Xc_JXB|smart-card]","2026-01-22T13:33:00.619Z"],["3830823","RCE-368","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Alisher Matkurbanov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769088772464709]*{color}:\nIncorrect translation for Lativan language\nCorrected version\n\n{code}{minutes, plural, =0 {# minūtes} one {# minūte} other {# minūtes}} {seconds, plural, =0 {# sekundes} one {# sekunde} other {# sekundes}}{code}\n\n{quote}","2026-01-22T13:33:05.538Z"],["3830825","LSS-61659","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team,\n[~accountid:60c88e6e8f2cc1006909fcf6] thank you for the ticket! I have reviewed the agreement and left my suggestions and comments, please review. \n\n[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432], could you please assist [~accountid:60c88e6e8f2cc1006909fcf6] in filling out the KYC I have tagged you in? Document can be found [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QS32P1s5jLc81pm7fLVwjEQGSmSgyXHDDjvtP29Ppq8/edit?tab=t.0], thanks a lot 🙏 \n\nIf you have any additional questions, please let me know, thanks! ","2026-01-22T13:33:36.816Z"],["3830826","LSS-61743","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:6177b596f6da6a006af89fc3] , can. you please share job description of Vehicle Operator for the Autonomous Driving?\n\nI am checking this and currently it looks like our employment contract + internal rules are a solid baseline and would usually be “enough” but for Autonomous Driving Vehicle Operators it would be advisable to add another layer—preferably a signed AV-specific confidentiality/security/data-handling addendum. Especially if they will handle sensor data/test routes/prototypes daily. \n\nFor Autonomous Driving Vehicle Operators the biggest sensitivity is often not classic “IP creation” but (a) operational secrecy + safety/security-sensitive procedures, (b) large-scale sensor/video data capture, (c) physical access to expensive prototypes, and (d) reputational blast radius if leaked. Also, our trade secret protection is stronger when we can show that we took “reasonable measures” to keep info secret (contractual + practical). Currently our confidentiality obligations are very wide and not AV specific.","2026-01-22T13:33:40.542Z"],["3830827","RS-1947","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:616ec4e4e79ff6006f259f57] ,\nThank you for clarifying! I would suggest explaining to the Police that we don’t have this information. Maybe we can provide a card issuer. ","2026-01-22T13:33:51.740Z"],["3830828","LSS-61925","LSS","elisabeth.gunnarsson@bolt.eu","Elisabeth Gunnarsson","Hi [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] - realized I haven’t given you a copy of their draft for DPA nor the contract info - I’m so sorry! Adding the docs here. \n\n[^Bilaga 7- Mall för personuppgiftbiträdesavtal-MASTER-v2-1 en-GB (1).docx]\n\n\n\nRelevant chapters in the procurement doc (pdf): \n\n* 4.13 - Riders with protected identity\n* 5.11.2 - How to handle personal data in our system (we’re using a supplier\n* 8.19 - Personal data \n\n[^Hela anbudsformuläret (5) en-GB.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T13:34:12.496Z"],["3830830","LSS-61713","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","[~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] In view of the description provided above by [~accountid:712020:1d0a34aa-e1ae-4c55-bae7-010cdaef89e3] , and on the information below related to exchange of personal data (ie. the only information we share is the names of the participating drivers—no additional data is communicated), please advise on whether we should make additions to the service agreement i+*n relation to Data Privacy clauses.*+\n\nThank you,\n\nAlex","2026-01-22T13:34:20.093Z"],["3830832","UXA-2223","UXA","razvan-matei.carpen@bolt.eu","Matei Carpen","Seems to be from [this|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/2375545879d17ec9d8a3683f51822669d237bc58/src/platform/user/user/main/table/UserLoginTable.ts#L206] query. Old login sessions have null as authentication_method and the query does not return rows with null values. Basically we need to replace the condition with (authentication_method <> 'cross-app' *OR authentication_method is null*)\n\n\n\nOtherwise, all data in the db looks correct for these sessions.","2026-01-22T13:34:42.159Z"],["3830834","MLC-185","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*Week 4 updates*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* progress 92%\n* *Blockers:* None\n* *Status update:* \n** Vertical banners rollout [cancelled|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08EY6QA98E/p1768927440819769] due to negative impact on key metrics.\n** Investigated issue reported that Bolt Send banner was shown in markets where it didn’t exist; found that it was live for 6 markets (CY, FI, MT, KE, PY, PT) where Bolt Send hasn’t been launched (according to [this tracker|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/16eJRnUNjesRO3eIqNp4PUfWH9bVI4REg-shMberOOyM/edit?gid=1050408448#gid=1050408448] for the feature) + we had duplicate banners live for Bolt Send; both these issues are fixed now.\n** Discussed control groups situation with Cristina; current decision is to not worry about control groups for now until we validate that this is the best way to measure uplift + we have a technical solution for adding them that doesn’t involve enrolling the entire user base to tests.\n** ^ Will proceed instead with rolling out planned experiments for Airports + Loyal Churn that haven’t been launched yet.\n\n* *Next steps:*\n** [~accountid:6203a0ea1fec260068c20327] prepare city + country-level analysis of banner performance for next week following Product team’s report that there were large differences in banner performance per market.\n** [~accountid:6203a0ea1fec260068c20327] create setups for remaining planned use cases (Bolt XL, Bolt Comfort, Scheduled Rides, Bolt Drive, Family Profile) and release to internal test group for feedback. → *will pick up in next sprint.*\n** [~accountid:6203a0ea1fec260068c20327] review experiment plan for Airports + Loyal Churn, roll out the experiments → *will pick up in next sprint.*","2026-01-22T13:35:04.943Z"],["3830837","RS-1948","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] , the official letter and legal basis is attached to the ticket. Can you please have a look","2026-01-22T13:35:21.735Z"],["3830838","PFI-835640","PFI","fiona.achieng@bolt-outsource.eu","Fiona Achieng","[~accountid:712020:2df9667e-bef1-459f-9fdb-31f1120f7c9c]  Thank you for the response. Does this mean that he will still receive compensation on future trips?","2026-01-22T13:35:25.772Z"],["3830839","LSS-62014","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","Responded in the main ticket.","2026-01-22T13:35:30.607Z"],["3830841","MLC-2769","MLC","nida.altug@bolt.eu","Nida Altuğ","*Week 4:*\n\n* *Status / Milestone: 27%*\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:*\n* Had meeting w [~accountid:628e5c9d8026a10068b1e457] [~accountid:712020:1e9398f2-efcd-4dcd-8ece-28e6f8578e37] [~accountid:61b6f8b2599f18006a270ae2] and [~accountid:712020:46173f6a-5fa7-4a4d-b038-74eddcadeef2] to sync on how to proceed.\n* Based on the feedback on the meeting adjusted the comms tracking sheet:\n** *Improved Visibility:* Added a \"Previous Comments\" section for better context.\n** *Workflow Tracking:* New \"Approval\" and \"Translated\" sections, featuring a checkmark system with conditional formatting for easy status tracking.\n** *Centralized Comms:* All communications are now in a single sheet, color-coded by priority with deadlines (DDLs) included.\n** *Notes:* Added an \"Additional Comments\" section for any extra details.\n* Defined deadlines as\n** Activation Comms : 30.01.2026\n** Growth Comms : 06.02.2026\n** Churn Comms : 11.02.2026\n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Nu5oZoTwAO6bucTsH_IYJkWdrMdecnWCchIK17dLx_4/edit?gid=869642983#gid=869642983|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Nu5oZoTwAO6bucTsH_IYJkWdrMdecnWCchIK17dLx_4/edit?gid=869642983#gid=869642983|smart-card]","2026-01-22T13:35:42.182Z"],["3830842","WEBSD-1505","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:712020:996ce528-b0dc-49e2-89b8-a8b37096b3ab]  👋 \n\nPlease follow the link [https://cms.bolt.eu/admin/auth/register?registrationToken=7dc08b7851a06938ad77577ae5c14b290bf7cc4c|https://cms.bolt.eu/admin/auth/register?registrationToken=7dc08b7851a06938ad77577ae5c14b290bf7cc4c]\n\nSo you can register. Let me know so we can close the ticket.\n\nRegards,","2026-01-22T13:35:44.398Z"],["3830843","DSR-3963","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T13:36:07.200Z"],["3830846","WEBSD-1497","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi 👋 \n\nIs this for Blog?\n\nRegards,","2026-01-22T13:36:59.884Z"],["3830847","LSS-61894","LSS","john.faye@bolt.eu","John Joseph Faye","Just wanted to add this T&Cs reference point from another “Clipping” organisation, this might give better context about how our agreement needs to be shaped: [https://www.vyro.com/clipper-terms|https://www.vyro.com/clipper-terms|smart-link] \n\nReading these, there are a few things that I think would be good to have in our own terms:\n\n\n# *Anti-Fraud:* Vyro is very explicit about banning purchased followers/engagement, botting, spam, and paid boosting, and it includes clawback rights. Could we look at including:\n## Creator warranty: no artificial engagement / no purchased followers/likes/views\n## Explicit ban on: botting, engagement pods, paid boosting, comment spam, mass DMs\n## Right to withhold payment and/or claw back if fraud is detected\n## Right to terminate immediately for fraud\n# *Payout Eligibility:* Vyro solves the “you can’t approve 3–5 posts/day” problem by making approval about eligibility for payout, not permission to publish. Can we include:\n## We don’t pre-approve every post\n## But we reserve the right to deem posts ineligible for payout\n## And require takedown/removal upon request\n# *Third-party payout provider:* Vyro bakes in a clear “payout provider registration process” and disclaims liability if a creator fails KYC. Can we include: Payments may be processed via a third-party payout provider\n## Creators must complete KYC/tax onboarding with that provider\n## If a creator doesn’t pass verification / doesn’t submit required documents → payouts may be delayed/forfeited\n## Creator confirms they’re responsible for their own tax reporting\n# *Eligibility + one-account rule:* Vyro is explicit on 18+, eligible jurisdictions, and prohibiting multiple identities. Can we include:\n## 18+ requirement (and age-of-majority where relevant)\n## One participant identity per person (no multiple accounts to double-dip)\n## Bolt reserves right to reject participants at its discretion\n# *Campaign/pilot can be changed or terminated at any time:* Vyro clearly states campaigns can change, and that payouts may stop if campaign terms change/end. Can we include:\n## Pilot terms may be updated with notice (including payout tiers/caps)\n## Bolt can terminate the pilot at any time\n## No future earnings are guaranteed\n## Only compliant posts meeting requirements are eligible for payout\n# *Platform compliance + removal risk:* Vyro states if the platform removes the post, payout becomes ineligible and may be clawed back. Can we include:\n## Creator must comply with platform ToS and local laws\n## If a platform removes/flags content → payment can be voided\n## If payment already issued and removal was due to violation/fraud → clawback\n# *Data/metrics access + evidence standards:* Vyro formalises analytics access/verification. You might not do API linking, but you _do_ need evidence. Can we include:\n## Creator must provide proof of metrics (screenshots at 48h, post link, handle)\n## Bolt may request additional evidence for audit\n## Bolt can withhold payment if evidence isn’t provided or is inconsistent.\n\n","2026-01-22T13:37:07.458Z"],["3830848","L10N-29591","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29589](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29589)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T13:37:08.420Z"],["3830849","L10N-29592","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29589](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29589)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T13:37:09.182Z"],["3830850","L10N-29595","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29589](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29589)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T13:37:11.173Z"],["3830852","PRV-515","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update (26 March):*\n\n# *dLocal* - *signed DPA* update to address the payment sub-processors  for Vietnam. Tracked via a separate ticket.\n# *Cellulant* - *standard DPA* *completed & signed*. Was missing before.\n# Bank of Georgia & TBC Bank - no progress in Q4-Q1 due to focus on higher priorities re/ EMI. To be resumed in Q2.","2026-01-22T13:37:15.602Z"],["3830853","L10N-29600","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s