|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T13:37:50.035Z"],["3830874","LSS-57807","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Same status since December - no updates.","2026-01-22T13:38:00.434Z"],["3830876","HS-29287","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-22T13:39:09.171Z"],["3830877","WEBSD-1502","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi 👋 \n\nFor support Articles please create e a ticket [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/4]\n\nRegards,","2026-01-22T13:39:32.415Z"],["3830878","DSR-3809","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] thanks for escalating! ❄️  Good guess. \n\nLet’s go with something in this manner:\n\n{quote}Dear *[DATA SUBJECT]*,\n\nThank you for your request.\n\nWe confirm that your Bolt account will be deleted in accordance with your request.\n\nPlease note that once your account is deleted, any consents you have provided in connection with the use of the Bolt services will no longer apply, as we will no longer process your personal data based on consent.\n\nSome personal data may be retained for a limited period where required by applicable law or where necessary for the establishment, exercise or defense of legal claims. In such cases, the processing is based on legal obligations or our legitimate interests and not on your consent.\n\nFor additional information on how Bolt processes personal data, please refer to tour Privacy Notice at [https://bolt.eu/hr-hr/privacy/privacy-for-eaters/?category=delivery|https://bolt.eu/hr-hr/privacy/privacy-for-eaters/?category=delivery|smart-link] .\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nBolt{quote}","2026-01-22T13:39:35.300Z"],["3830879","BDB-1513","BDB","liam.wentworth@bolt.eu","Liam Wentworth","Hi Polina - yep everything has been submitted and I haven’t heard back about any fixes being needed.\n\nAppreciate your support on this!","2026-01-22T13:39:35.433Z"],["3830880","LSS-61459","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:a9500cde-28bc-4a8e-95d6-7818a2252cf8] i added changes to the campaign T&C based on your comment\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pppsn1Bi_DWZfYO8zOhi2U1BAjgcRSCY/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pppsn1Bi_DWZfYO8zOhi2U1BAjgcRSCY/edit|smart-link] \n\nPlease ask Apple to fill their details ","2026-01-22T13:39:51.751Z"],["3830882","BDB-1513","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:5d5a47614aeeb80c2cc0d00a] Thank you!","2026-01-22T13:40:00.550Z"],["3830883","XP-2133","XP","pavel.kiper@bolt.eu","Pavel Kiper","[~accountid:641d5e7c9796ea0a8718ca5e] is this still relevant?","2026-01-22T13:40:00.923Z"],["3830886","CSDT-976","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Aligned with Product & CS Data that we are building all 4 versions. Need to build 1 and allow people to review & criticize. ","2026-01-22T13:40:31.238Z"],["3830888","DSR-3965","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T13:41:09.264Z"],["3830889","MLC-3906","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 4*\n\n* *Context of the project/initiative:* Multiple initiatives to support the expansion and growth of the Bolt Plus membership.\n* *Status / Milestone:*\n* *Blockers:* None.\n* *Status update:*\n* *Uplift validation: Experiment on Plus-ready modals*\n** [+Confluence page+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7018905601/2025-11+Bolt+Plus+Plus-ready+modal+experiment]\n** *Status:* {color:#36B37E}*[ EXPERIMENT RUNNING ]*{color}\n** *Tentative ETA for results:* January 2026, but it also depends on the enrolments\n** *Sync with MarTech on* {{2026-01-23}}: Discussing how to proceed, considering low enrolment numbers due to the fact that the banner was exposed mostly to new enrolments, as advised by the team.\n* *Hopp Plus launch*\n** *Technical preparations:* \n*** *Custom Events:* Getting Bolt Plus events to the Hopp workspace with the correct brand value.\n**** *Status:* delivered (/)\n***** MarTech was able to trigger the events so we could proceed with setting up auto comms — as the events weren’t sent, they weren’t immediately visible.\n*** *Custom Attributes:* in the Hopp space (/)\n**** Checked and confirmed by MarTech that everything’s good with them as well — the brand property is taken from the user-profile service and tied to the app user is using.\n*** *Ad-hoc template*\n**** Assigned a task to [~accountid:712020:07449b81-9129-47a7-bd23-f01775b97cff] to set it up → reviewed the setup\n**** Assigned a task to [~accountid:712020:07449b81-9129-47a7-bd23-f01775b97cff] to assist with setting up the auto comms → we’ll start working on it next week.\n* *Annual discount*\n** Status to be confirmed. Product will likely want to test this again to understand the impact. We should hear about it soon.\n* *Next steps:*\n** *Hopp Plus launch*\n*** Align with [~accountid:712020:07449b81-9129-47a7-bd23-f01775b97cff] on setting up the automated comms.\n*** Test 1—2 events once the comms are set up (just to ensure everything’s correctly triggered).\n*** Share the ad-hoc comms setup with Vertical Marketing once the visuals are finalised.\n*** Start setting up in-app comms.","2026-01-22T13:41:23.508Z"],["3830890","PTWS-2124","PTWS","alexandru.cerveanu@bolt.eu","Alex Cerveanu","Hello,\n\nUnfortunately there is no possibility to map 3PL Mechanics as subtype for Agency.\nAn alternative will be to create a specific job profile for 3PL Mechanics and then to ask IT to switch the access, we can change the contingent worker type to Agency but we need a specific Job Profile for Mechanic.","2026-01-22T13:41:24.657Z"],["3830891","TS-4658","TS","aleksandr.bregin@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Bregin","Just seminar day as in have everyone eat together during the seminar day?","2026-01-22T13:41:25.182Z"],["3830893","G3IOT-1214","G3IOT","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","Setting REG01 to 4V doesn't have effect on VSYS. Seems like is always tries to keep Vsys at least 200mv higher comparing to Vbat","2026-01-22T13:41:34.833Z"],["3830894","LSS-61721","LSS","darius.poursiami@bolt.eu","Darius Poursiami","Sorry, Bolt Services PL Sp. z o.o.","2026-01-22T13:41:55.080Z"],["3830895","PFI-835648","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Thank you for the ticket. I understand before we are able to make any adjustment, engineers need to complete their changes. Will keep an eye on this. \n\n[~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] FYI","2026-01-22T13:42:11.711Z"],["3830896","PFI-837289","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-22T13:42:31.852Z"],["3830899","G3IOT-1214","G3IOT","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","For example I have set REG01 to 4V. BB level is currently at 4.092 and not charging, Vsys 4.316","2026-01-22T13:42:50.503Z"],["3830900","RS-1955","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:603cb85ec58c720071175949] , Looks good! Can be disclosed","2026-01-22T13:43:13.970Z"],["3830902","SRED-1098","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done, no restarts caused, config maps updated.","2026-01-22T13:43:28.944Z"],["3830903","LSS-61846","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] \nI’ve reviewed the lease agreement and made suggestions to the privacy clause.\n\nI confirmed with Ann Kõljalg that the landlord will not receive customer data and will receive at most minimal employee information (potentially a name for access cards, if needed). The clause has been aligned with this setup, clearly confirms the landlord as an independent controller, and limits Bolt’s assistance obligation accordingly.\n\nPlease check at your conveinience 🙏 \nThank you!","2026-01-22T13:43:35.421Z"],["3830904","WEBSD-1499","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:712020:2f68ebec-bff7-4acf-a855-0eeaf1c88737]  👋 \n\nWe do not have global under TnC Legal documents. It was a required from them a while ago.\n\nThe question for the legal team/you is where it should go?\n\nRegards,","2026-01-22T13:43:49.891Z"],["3830905","MLC-3471","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*Week 4*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* 99%\n* *Blockers:* none\n* *Status update:* \n** Received the list of users to target, processed and uploaded them to Braze. Users are mostly in FR, additional markets with 10k+ users are PT, ES, TH, GB, MT, BE, RO.\n** Tracked down the localisation ticket and added push with localisations to the canvas setup. \n* *Next steps*\n** Aligning with Marija to confirm that we’re ready to send out comms (also confirmed with FR team that we aren’t blocked to send out here, since they approved an ad-hoc for tomorrow - agreed with them to shift theirs to Saturday)","2026-01-22T13:43:53.432Z"],["3830906","MVRT-1495","MVRT","teele.vallimae@bolt.eu","Teele Vallimäe","Hey, [~accountid:632d4729fedc6169aed5c944] i have a problem with Khankendi awareness campaign as once again it’s not on the google city list and even with radius targeting of the area +20km, the campaign did not start running. Please make a ticket for Meta to launch it there. Thank you!","2026-01-22T13:43:55.674Z"],["3830909","RS-1955","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","There is no confidential information involved, we can share how we operate in a generic way","2026-01-22T13:44:05.222Z"],["3830910","DPO-159","DPO","mengel.paula@bolt.eu","Paula Maria Mengel","[FF|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/featureflags/edit/15004] for enabling the feature","2026-01-22T13:44:26.449Z"],["3830911","PFI-837290","PFI","shahnaz.huseynova@bolt-outsource.eu","Shahnaz Huseynova","!Screenshot 2026-01-22 5.43.18 PM.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 5.43.23 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T13:44:43.772Z"],["3830913","LSS-59633","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","verify re insurance + deposit","2026-01-22T13:44:47.265Z"],["3830914","LSS-61821","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi Mo, sorry to say but they have now have deleted *Article 6. Confidentiality, Article 7. Data Protection and Security, Article 8. Liability* which we definitely need. \n\nI just spotted that they had duplicated numbering of Article 6. 7. and 8. in Clyde’s contract so I guess they have mistakenly deleted the other Articles that had duplicated numbers but are still needed.","2026-01-22T13:44:56.927Z"],["3830917","PFI-837290","PFI","shahnaz.huseynova@bolt-outsource.eu","Shahnaz Huseynova","other [payment|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4047924233] link\n\nand [order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders?source_id=1768815704263272&city_id=335&user_id=17729803]","2026-01-22T13:45:41.267Z"],["3830918","CNT-441","CNT","liisi.tamra@bolt.eu","Liisi Tamra","In what form do we need these? Is just a copy ok, since all my written SM posts are usually in spreadsheets? [~accountid:610a6c97ec92ab0070d4d852] ","2026-01-22T13:45:57.222Z"],["3830920","SRED-1098","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Diff before/after:\n\n{noformat}k get configmap/rfr-rental-car-slack-alert-redis -oyaml\napiVersion: v1\ndata:\n  redis.conf: |\n    slaveof 127.0.0.1 6379\n    port 6379\n    repl-diskless-sync yes\n    repl-timeout 900\n    save \"\"\n    oom-score-adj yes\n    activedefrag yes\n    client-output-buffer-limit normal 0 0 0\n    client-output-buffer-limit replica 1gb 2gb 0\n    client-output-buffer-limit pubsub 32mb 8mb 60\n    user pinger -@all +ping on >pingpass\nkind: ConfigMap\nmetadata:\n  creationTimestamp: \"2024-01-02T12:08:28Z\"\n  labels:\n    app.kubernetes.io/component: redis\n    app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: redis-operator\n    app.kubernetes.io/name: rental-car-slack-alert-redis\n    app.kubernetes.io/part-of: redis-failover\n    bolt.eu/codeowner: carsharing-safety-backend\n    bolt.eu/costcenter: eng-drive\n    bolt.eu/role: redis\n    kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/name: kubernetes-configless\n    kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/namespace: flux-system\n    redisfailovers.databases.spotahome.com/name: rental-car-slack-alert-redis\n  name: rfr-rental-car-slack-alert-redis\n  namespace: redis-prelive\n  ownerReferences:\n  - apiVersion: databases.spotahome.com/v1\n    blockOwnerDeletion: true\n    controller: true\n    kind: RedisFailover\n    name: rental-car-slack-alert-redis\n    uid: e99928d1-c8ba-4378-ba96-8c362f86de24\n  resourceVersion: \"591396388\"\n  uid: e3488441-e787-4f6b-9475-82e9bc871d09{noformat}\n\n\n\n{noformat}k get configmap/rfr-rental-car-slack-alert-redis -oyaml\napiVersion: v1\ndata:\n  redis.conf: |\n    slaveof 127.0.0.1 6379\n    port 6379\n    repl-diskless-sync yes\n    repl-timeout 900\n    save \"\"\n    oom-score-adj yes\n    activedefrag yes\n    client-output-buffer-limit normal 0 0 0\n    client-output-buffer-limit replica 1gb 2gb 0\n    client-output-buffer-limit pubsub 32mb 8mb 60\n    enable-debug-command no\n    enable-module-command no\n    user pinger -@all +ping on >pingpass\nkind: ConfigMap\nmetadata:\n  creationTimestamp: \"2024-01-02T12:08:28Z\"\n  labels:\n    app.kubernetes.io/component: redis\n    app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: redis-operator\n    app.kubernetes.io/name: rental-car-slack-alert-redis\n    app.kubernetes.io/part-of: redis-failover\n    bolt.eu/codeowner: carsharing-safety-backend\n    bolt.eu/costcenter: eng-drive\n    bolt.eu/role: redis\n    kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/name: kubernetes-configless\n    kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/namespace: flux-system\n    redisfailovers.databases.spotahome.com/name: rental-car-slack-alert-redis\n  name: rfr-rental-car-slack-alert-redis\n  namespace: redis-prelive\n  ownerReferences:\n  - apiVersion: databases.spotahome.com/v1\n    blockOwnerDeletion: true\n    controller: true\n    kind: RedisFailover\n    name: rental-car-slack-alert-redis\n    uid: e99928d1-c8ba-4378-ba96-8c362f86de24\n  resourceVersion: \"913094240\"\n  uid: e3488441-e787-4f6b-9475-82e9bc871d09{noformat}","2026-01-22T13:46:33.117Z"],["3830921","LSS-62015","LSS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] ,\n\nPlease help with the legal basis check🙏 ","2026-01-22T13:46:42.439Z"],["3830924","RS-1956","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Escalated to Privacy for review","2026-01-22T13:47:08.189Z"],["3830925","PFI-836638","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Hmm, but I don’t think we even generate the additional_delivery_costs_and_compensations_invoices report for individual couriers - this is only for fleets? \n\nBut in general, we do not provide a full earnings overview as a document. Their earnings are made up of invoices from courier → eater (so the regular delivery invoices) and then any invoices bolt ↔︎ courier (this is for any bonuses, compensations or deductions). The total of these are the earnings for the couriers. ","2026-01-22T13:47:12.709Z"],["3830926","TS-4658","TS","laura.kaselaid@bolt.eu","Laura Kaselaid","Fork cards for seminar day for lunch - dinner as we agreed above either f-hoone etc. Other days sub-teams organise, it’ll still be comped and all","2026-01-22T13:47:24.312Z"],["3830928","PFI-837292","PFI","jutathip.songcharoen@bolt-outsource.eu","Jutathip Songcharoen","!IMG_1945.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_1967.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260122-134418.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T13:47:45.018Z"],["3830929","LSS-61827","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] we will be renewing with Open AI (ChatGPT licenses). 26Jan is the date of renewal. We still don’t have renewal order but apparently terms should be the same. We will tag you if we see that there are privacy related changes to the order. \n\n[~accountid:712020:985a985c-b403-41bd-b116-abbf44b22175] please share updated order. ","2026-01-22T13:48:04.974Z"],["3830930","LSS-59597","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team, \n[~accountid:712020:e81c1984-54f1-46ce-bc81-864b3748de94], good catch, already resolved that comment 😉 thank you!\n[~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] thank you! ","2026-01-22T13:48:12.804Z"],["3830931","DO-5816","DO","monika.goralczyk@bolt.eu","Monika Góralczyk","I read the instructions in the link and my understanding is that my personal dev schema should have been created automatically. However, I don’t think it exists (screenshot attached).\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 14.46.53.png|width=1167,height=492,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 14.46.53.png\"!\n\nMy request for Data Platform Authorisation was approved around two weeks ago (screenshot attached). I have access to Databricks too. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 14.42.02.png|width=1257,height=213,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 14.42.02.png\"!\n\nAny ideas what I might be missing?\n\n","2026-01-22T13:48:13.716Z"],["3830933","WEBSD-1497","WEBSD","woraruethai.chantana@bolt.eu","Woraruethai Chantana","Yess","2026-01-22T13:48:30.142Z"],["3830937","PFI-836816","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! Can you send some examples of profiles that do get the invoices sent correctly? Just so I can compare","2026-01-22T13:49:40.961Z"],["3830939","LSS-58970","LSS","sandra.bergstrom@bolt.eu","Sandra Bergström","[~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] Thanks for looking into this too. Awesome to hear we’re good to go!","2026-01-22T13:49:58.337Z"],["3830944","LSS-61848","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:60cb48dc758a5d006a07896b],\n\nI just finished the review of the Agreement (see [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uXttIbfANYsnfVrGY0pC26T6fcdJq6cw/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=106403837992168217990&rtpof=true&sd=true]). I made some amendments in track changes, and I tagged you in the comments in which I need some input from your side.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions and if you want us to comment in a call.\n\nThanks! \n\nAngela","2026-01-22T13:50:54.783Z"],["3830945","DSR-3967","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T13:51:07.462Z"],["3830948","WEBSD-1505","WEBSD","dominika.kozub@bolt.eu","Dominika Kozub","All good, thank you!","2026-01-22T13:51:20.006Z"],["3830950","DPX-3514","DPX","eerik.magi@bolt.eu","Eerik Mägi","Translations ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101099|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101099|smart-link]  (you will likely not have access to this though)\n\nAt time of posting, missing only Slovak.","2026-01-22T13:51:59.686Z"],["3830954","XP-2317","XP","pavel.kiper@bolt.eu","Pavel Kiper","🟢 [~accountid:712020:469d02b5-abf2-42fb-9357-94b8c8901f09] is this still an issue in the new scorecard","2026-01-22T13:52:34.704Z"],["3830955","MARTECH3-1519","MARTECH3","mohd.goh@bolt.eu","Ameer Goh","[~accountid:712020:5d3eb1bb-0d0e-487e-8912-069bb3f5f2b0] can you add the tasks here, please","2026-01-22T13:52:36.244Z"],["3830956","BEE-3549","BEE","michal.bielecki@bolt.eu","Michał Bielecki","Put on hold for now because data-lake team started figuring out POC of live streaming and maybe then can experiment with this particular table.","2026-01-22T13:52:37.899Z"],["3830959","CAMLE-9864","CAMLE","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","prefilled data using one time cron, 28 holdout labels added.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 15.48.28.png|width=650,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 15.48.28.png\"!","2026-01-22T13:53:11.507Z"],["3830961","RS-1950","RS","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c], the data has been disclosed. Thank you!","2026-01-22T13:53:37.689Z"],["3830962","MLC-2742","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*W4 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* None.\n* *Status update:*\n** Synced with Mariann on next steps.\n** Helped with testing templates from the updated web builder - all looks good (🤞 ).\n* *Next steps:*\n** Start rolling out updates once we’ve confirmed that updated templates aren’t causing issues (rolling them out in a few markets together with Mariann)","2026-01-22T13:53:37.994Z"],["3830963","PFI-837297","PFI","valeriia.slietkova@bolt-outsource.eu","Valeriia Slietkova","!IMG_5641.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T13:53:41.299Z"],["3830964","MLC-186","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 4*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* in progress\n* *Blockers:* Dropping email Open Rates\n* *Status update:*\n** *26Q1 planning*\n*** Prioritised comms for [~accountid:6203a0ea1fec260068c20327] based on volume + OR correlation → Activation is around 20% which means we should focus on comms with high volume and low OR for higher impact. E.g. Airport Fares\n** *Testing the email builder + first email template*\n*** [~accountid:6203a0ea1fec260068c20327] worked on creating the Content Blocks\n*** [~accountid:5fb225a6f2df6c00762b994d] worked on setting up new footers for both non-incentive and incentive use cases\n*** QA on the first campaign setups, HTML code, email weight testing, and testing on different email inboxes.\n*** Reporting on the findings to the Web team ([Slack thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0900469E6N/p1769073822494909])\n*** First A/B test is live (GB, Airport Fares) → aiming to have the rest going out tomorrow morning. \n**** Roman had to deprioritise the task, so I’m working on it as well to push things live.\n** *Sharing feedback about Poe*\n*** Shared the initial feedback with the Content team → waiting for them to get back to us with a potential ETA for the tool to be updated ([Slack thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08C1KFLYM8/p1769085718329399?thread_ts=1767974633.003749&cid=C08C1KFLYM8])\n** *2026 planning*\n*** Finalising this week. Battling with data + getting the number of setups (for estimations), etc., has taken a bit of time.\n* *Next steps:*\n** *Results from the first A/B tests* → if everything’s good, we can proceed with setting up the rest of the templates.\n** *Working with Poe* –> hoping to continue with converting the copies.","2026-01-22T13:53:45.254Z"],["3830970","DO-5816","DO","monika.goralczyk@bolt.eu","Monika Góralczyk","Perhaps I should modify Instance profile to something like: [dap-hu-monika.goralczyk@bolt.eu|mailto:dap-hu-monika.goralczyk@bolt.eu]. However, this option is locked for me.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 14.53.27.png|width=901,height=354,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 14.53.27.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-22T13:54:51.317Z"],["3830971","XP-2169","XP","pavel.kiper@bolt.eu","Pavel Kiper","[~accountid:6268ef8e429789006946b1ac] is this still relevant?","2026-01-22T13:55:06.631Z"],["3830974","MLC-3472","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*W4 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:*\n** Finalizing [results summary|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gbaur2SK9jBzTRgMkNFWtsyVr-aTZ4LRzKEHGciW-cI/edit?tab=t.i808357h8xpf] by 9AM tomorrow according to Cristina & Mihai’s comments.\n* *Next steps:*\n** TBD following results review.","2026-01-22T13:55:16.243Z"],["3830977","LSS-61867","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:13ae7353-697f-46e7-99dd-8fc938931751] ,\n\nCould you please share here the document that needs to be reviewed? \n\nThank you!\n\nAngela","2026-01-22T13:55:26.983Z"],["3830978","XP-2121","XP","pavel.kiper@bolt.eu","Pavel Kiper","Are we doing this, [~accountid:6268ef8e429789006946b1ac] ?","2026-01-22T13:55:29.608Z"],["3830980","LSS-62015","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] \n\n\n* *Requesting authority:* Taipei City Government Police Department, Da’an Precinct\n* *Purpose:* Criminal investigation\n* *Personal data requested:* Ride and user information related to a specific trip\n* *Legal basis cited:* Personal Data Protection Act, *Article 15*\n\n\n\nArticle 15 of the Taiwanese Personal Data Protection Act is already listed as not approved by Bolt and does not, on its own, create a clear legal obligation on Bolt to disclose personal data to law enforcement.\nThe request does not cite a specific criminal procedure provision or court order that would mandate disclosure.\n\n\n\nThe legal basis relied upon is not valid for disclosure. CS should ask the authority to re-submit the request with a valid legal basis, for example a specific provision of criminal procedure law or a court order requiring Bolt to provide the data.\n\n\n\nCC: [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] ","2026-01-22T13:55:44.904Z"],["3830981","LSS-59597","LSS","ann.koljalg@bolt.eu","Ann Kõljalg","[~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] I see you are updating the lease agreement - thank you! Just let me know when you are completed then I will share it with landlord","2026-01-22T13:55:48.143Z"],["3830983","WEBSD-1503","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:557058:d3d19a9f-5bfa-49d0-8b45-41790d3b326e] \n\nAll privacy documents can be uploaded already for privacy team.\n\nContact [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e]  or [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd]  .\n\nRegards,","2026-01-22T13:56:11.586Z"],["3830985","PFI-836967","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","\n\n\n\nHello Team!\n\nI completely understand why this might look like a double charge, but I can assure you that the user was only charged once. This is a common part of how card payments are processed. Here's what happens:\n\n# When the user first makes a payment, the bank temporarily ‘reserves' the funds and this is just the bank setting aside the amount for the transaction. The user’s account balance might show less amount but the payment hasn’t actually been taken out by the bank yet.\n# Later, when the payment is fully processed, that reserved amount is now “officially” debited from the user’s account. At that point, some banks send a second notification, which can make it seem like a second charge.\n\n\nI would advise the user to check their final account balance or statement, where they can confirm that only one payment was actually withdrawn. The earlier “pending” amount will either drop off or convert into the final charge.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-22T13:56:15.197Z"],["3830986","PFI-835640","PFI","caroline.kruberg@bolt.eu","Caroline Kruberg","Hi, \n\nYes, the driver will receive compensation as usual for future trips","2026-01-22T13:56:21.331Z"],["3830987","LSS-61976","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","The first document is ready, second one in progress.\n\n[^Formular_DGPR_pers_juridice-RO.docx.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T13:56:26.341Z"],["3830988","MLC-3755","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*W4 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:*\n** Following up on missing localisations.\n* *Next steps:*\n** Monitoring the results of A/B testing + continue with creating test setups as localisations come in (deprio’d a bit this week due to other tasks)","2026-01-22T13:56:29.346Z"],["3830989","LSS-61922","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:605ae66414a23b0069c98a55] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Vendor_Info_and_Bank_Account_details_Telecel...docx.pdf] ","2026-01-22T13:56:48.714Z"],["3830990","TS-4658","TS","aleksandr.bregin@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Bregin","Keep in mind if lunch & dinner is comped the daily allowance is lowered - we should ask the team if they’d want that or not 🤔 ","2026-01-22T13:56:49.250Z"],["3830993","LSS-59597","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:712020:e81c1984-54f1-46ce-bc81-864b3748de94] \nYes, I’m updating the privacy clause in the lease agreement.\nI’ll let you know when it is finalized 🙂 ","2026-01-22T13:57:25.389Z"],["3830994","MLC-2609","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 4*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* in progress\n* *Blockers:* None\n* *Status update:*\n** *Visibility update:* Shared an update with the whole department on the Identity team finalising the roll-out.\n** *Working on* *actual’/current location tagging*\n*** [+Slack thread+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0669RP1EMS/p1765871835519259]\n*** Got back to the Product team on why we would need to work on the user's current city (+ country code) as well.\n* *Next steps:*\n** Keep an eye on the status of working on the actual’/current location tagging. Currently, no ETA from them.","2026-01-22T13:57:27.128Z"],["3830996","LSS-61989","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] !\n\nPlease find the signed document(s) attached [^Bolt_Services_EE_OÜ_-_Åberopande_av_kapacitet,_referensuppdrag_copy.docx.pdf] ","2026-01-22T13:58:01.457Z"],["3830997","MLC-2438","MLC","gerardo.gomez@bolt.eu","Gerardo Gomez","w3 2026Q1 updates:\n\n* Blockers: none.\n* Status update:\n** Documented existing communications and finalised ad hoc guide for Bolt Chauffeur Stakeholders. \n** Aligned with team in our involvement looking towards new ad hoc requests and what the process should look like. We agreed that in terms of targeting we can help out to plan and define, meanwhile the campaign’s content should be driven by the Chauffeur team with alignment with local marketing. Additionally we’ll be reporting in a biweekly timeframe the performance of auto-comms and ad hocs. \n* Next step\n** Nothing yet. ","2026-01-22T13:58:02.750Z"],["3830999","PFI-836935","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-22T13:58:48.621Z"],["3831000","LSS-61919","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Letter_of_Termination_.pdf]  ","2026-01-22T13:58:52.769Z"],["3831001","HS-29138","HS","louisa.ayad@bolt.eu","Louisa Ayad","Hi Valentin\n\nWill check on this for you\n\nLA","2026-01-22T13:58:54.735Z"],["3831002","PFI-837115","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","მეგობრებო \n\nაღნიშნული ტრანზაქციები რეფანდდება \n\n  \n\n  \n\nმადლობა, \n|  *{color:#00ADEE} *სოფიო ტაბატაძე /*{color}**{color:#00ADEE} *Sophio Tabatadze*{color}* {color:#595959}საბარათე ბიზნესისა და ლოიალობის განვითარების ლიგა/{color} {color:#595959}Cards Business and Loyalty Growth Tribe{color} {color:#595959}სერვის ექსპერტი /{color} {color:#595959}Service Expert{color} {color:#595959}{color} {color:#595959}{color} {color:#595959}{color} {color:#595959}Tel{color}{color:#595959}:{color} {color:#595959}{color} {color:#595959}{color}{color:#595959}+(995 32) 2 27 27 27{color}{color:#595959}{color} {color:#595959}Mob:{color} {color:#595959}{color}{color:#595959}+(995 597) 35 00 84{color}{color:#18355E}{color} | |{color:#172B4D}{color}\n \n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!{color:#172B4D}{color}","2026-01-22T13:59:07.231Z"],["3831004","LSS-61992","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Bolt_Operations_OÜ_-_Åberopande_av_kapacitet.docx.pdf] ","2026-01-22T13:59:35.771Z"],["3831005","L10N-29542","L10N","oksana.naidjonova@bolt.eu","Oksana Naidjonova","Wow, how did you sync it? I've never seen this before","2026-01-22T13:59:44.853Z"],["3831006","LSS-61589","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hello, [~accountid:712020:38ef5817-1c12-4bf5-b0d1-116b99b69ddf] thank you for the cooperation and all information I received from you for this letter. [Here’s the draft.|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qv1Ka3AtifClTkmUt2_NrllorCOK3YWk/edit] \n\n# Please have a look and let me know if you have any reservations hereto. \n# If not, I will be proceeding with the signing (we need a signature of [~accountid:5b18f5574bec0e53fdb555d5] as a representative of Bolt Poland). \n# Once he signs it off, I would like *you* to send the signed letter + the attachment (KRS copy) via e-mail to the Authority according to my following instructions:\n\n* e-mail address of the Authority: *ih_warszawa@wiih.org.pl* (Mazowiecki Wojewódzki Inspektor Inspekcji Handlowej)\n* when (deadline): *Friday, 23.01.2026 (tomorrow)*\n* the cover mail (in Polish):\n\n\n\n*_Title: Dot. SK.837.952.2025 (BOLT)_*\n\n*_Content_*_:_ \n\n_Szanowni Państwo,_\n\n_w związku z nadesłaniem pisma od tut. Organu z dnia 5 stycznia 2026 r. (doręczone spółce 13 stycznia 2026 r.) w załączeniu przesyłam stanowisko spółki Bolt Poland sp. z o.o. z siedzibą w Warszawie w sprawie w sporze konsumenckim z wniosku o sygn. SK.837.952.2025._\n\n_Pozdrawiam_\n\n_Klaudia Bochenko_\n\n_Zespół Bolt_ \n\n\n\nThe KRS attachment here [^Odpis_Aktualny_KRS_0000980293 (7).pdf] ","2026-01-22T13:59:54.989Z"],["3831008","LSS-61948","LSS","paula.pihelgas@bolt.eu","Paula Joanna Pihelgas","Hey, please see the signed contract: \n\n\n\n[^Services Agreement_ Bolt Support Sweden AB_ Hallvarsson & Halvarsson AB.docx (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T14:00:13.985Z"],["3831013","HS-29032","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountid:712020:9dcaf049-08b3-4db3-8347-9b88531a3941], we haven’t heard from you in a while. \n\nIf you’d like to keep this request open or have any additional information, please leave a comment, and we’ll get back to you as soon as possible.\n\nIf we don’t hear from you soon, we’ll proceed with closing the ticket, but feel free to reopen it anytime if needed.","2026-01-22T14:00:37.847Z"],["3831015","LSS-62009","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:54a2ee67-0b63-4efa-bc93-807aac06dda8] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached. The strictly confidential nature is acknowledged.\n\n[^Decision_on_Position_Abolishment.docx.pdf] ","2026-01-22T14:01:21.275Z"],["3831016","LSS-61930","LSS","paula.pihelgas@bolt.eu","Paula Joanna Pihelgas","[^APP REG PREMIO BOLT 24 25 (1).pdf]\n\nHey, signed ","2026-01-22T14:01:33.830Z"],["3831018","RS-1959","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] ,\n\nIt’s very hard to identify due to a translation issue. This looks like a court order. It has a court stamp on it. ","2026-01-22T14:01:45.390Z"],["3831019","DSR-3969","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T14:02:02.144Z"],["3831020","PFI-836773","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Carlos, thanks for reaching out.\n\nThe rule name gives some context here. This user is linked to business accounts that have previously been marked as fraud ([Example1|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/370794?tab=business_company], [Example2|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/370792?tab=business_company]), including connections to an older, discarded account. Given these links, along with the attempt to create both a new rider and a new business account, this raises sufficient concern for us to continue rejecting this.","2026-01-22T14:02:11.756Z"],["3831021","PFI-832641","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! The fleet has 0 drivers and no orders, so there’s nothing there. If the issue persists, please create a new ticket and provide the driver link, time period, order link (if applicable) and the amounts so we could better troubleshoot, thanks! ","2026-01-22T14:02:18.481Z"],["3831022","LSS-62012","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:6169660ebfa2c1006b56c18f] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^AIM_fase_1_intentiebrief_Bolt_v1.0.docx.pdf] ","2026-01-22T14:02:24.889Z"],["3831024","LSS-60534","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:66939b2f-e5c1-42e2-8cbe-244458fd12f9] Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Nicchiano_BOOK_OF_SHARES_(1).docx.pdf]\n[^Nicchiano_LIST_OF_SHAREHOLDERS_(1).docx.pdf]\n\n [^Nicchiano_statement_of_MB_on_contributions_(1).docx.pdf] \n\n[^Nicchiano_statement_on_aquisition_of_shares_(1).docx.pdf] ","2026-01-22T14:03:33.878Z"],["3831025","SREC-379","SREC","kourosh.tafreshi@bolt.eu","Kourosh Tafreshi","All done.\nMoved, tested and cleaned-up the infrastructure.","2026-01-22T14:03:32.893Z"],["3831029","MLC-3683","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 4*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* in progress\n* *Blockers:*\n* *Status update:*\n** Received information from the Growth team on how many duplicated accounts there are among dormant users. \n*** [Slack thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0682D79LQG/p1768909195176399]\n*** Picking this up next week instead → storytelling has taken a bit more time than I anticipated.\n** *Next steps:*\n*** *Planning the next steps* ","2026-01-22T14:04:06.478Z"],["3831030","LSS-61517","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","(!) [~accountid:712020:0285a595-6608-4335-9a5a-60b50674c696] för denna upphandling krävs nu en svensk PoA - detta har vi ingen förlaga på. Det innebär: \n1. Vi behöver översätta fullmakten till svenska (Elisabeth att läsa igenom, använd DeepL och läs sen igenom)\n2. Vi behöver få den signad på nytt\n\nEng version: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/14csCJs1dhHm8NK4DtIgs4a70zXaGiKidozzXYTchWTo/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/14csCJs1dhHm8NK4DtIgs4a70zXaGiKidozzXYTchWTo/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\nKan du hjälpa till med detta? \n\nPrata med [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] om några frågor uppstår. \n\nTack!","2026-01-22T14:04:10.135Z"],["3831033","HWMISC-849","HWMISC","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] \n\nI have a couple of questions. \n\n* The solution to cover the battery storage area, right? It doesn’t have anything to do with the battery charging shelves/area?\n* What is the target cost?  \n** For ex. 2mx5m area with 2.4m walls needs 90m2 insulation board. Insulation boards are around 45-100 €/m2. The total cost per 10 m² area starts from € 4,000. \n** If we order in bulk to the central warehouse and send from there, then we can decrease the cost to 25-40 €/m2. So the total cost can come down to € 2250. \n* Will the barrier be permanently there or removable? \n** We could also use fireproof rockwool to cover around the pallet. Rockwool will be a lighter option. \n* Perhaps we can ask WHs to store batteries on euro pallets with a limited height. So we have a certain bounding box size. And we can control the number of batteries on each pallet better. This will allow us to optimise the solution better and cheaper. \nOtherwise, each warehouse will make a different solution. If the area is big, then they need some good structure to support these boards. It will get heavier. \n* Also, if we use this kind of [+calcium silicate boards+|https://www.promat.com/en/industry/technologies/calcium-silicates/] then they can use drywall metal studs profiles and screws. \n\n!image-20260122-131518.png|width=289,alt=\"image-20260122-131518.png\"!","2026-01-22T14:04:40.952Z"],["3831034","LSS-59413","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:61374989bba6c7006a2616ba] !\n\nThanks you for your comments.\n\nA couple of key thoughts from a PT risk perspective (reclassification + privacy/monitoring):\n\n+*Regarding the fake GPS fraud:*+\n\nEven if this has been running since late 2024, the risk analysis stays the same: the more we rely on GPS anomalies as “automatic triggers” for restrictions, the easier it is for a claimant to frame this as platform control/disciplinary power (and, in an employment framing, “remote surveillance” style monitoring).\n\nSo generally, we maintain our position describe bellow and, in our view, this is high risk.\n\nThat said, this is a business decision and what we can do is to support and try to minimize the risks as much as possible. \n\nHaving this in consideration, we believe this can be structured in a way that is operationally effective and legally safer:\n\n+What we’re OK with (with guardrails):+\n\n* Keep the 72h measure explicitly as an “investigative hold” (temporary access restriction to preserve platform integrity while we verify), not as a punitive sanction.\n* Ensure human review happens within that window and is documented.\n* Only apply the 7-day suspension (or longer/shorter, depending on proportionality) once we have a “fraud conclusion” (i.e., indicators + corroboration).\n\n+Critical guardrails to reduce exposure:+\n\n* GPS anomalies (speed/distance/route ratio) should be treated as signals, not “proof”. For a fraud conclusion, try to require at least one additional corroborator, for example:\n** repeated pattern across multiple orders / days,\n** device/app integrity signals (where available),\n** clear impossibility indicators (e.g., teleport-like jumps),\n** inconsistency with pickup/provider confirmations, timestamps, etc.\n* Transparency + process: courier gets a short notice of the reason category (“suspected GPS manipulation”), an option to provide context, and a documented outcome (upheld / released / escalated).\n\nThe core issue is what evidence base gets you to the suspension and whether it looks “automatic/disciplinary” versus “fraud prevention with verification and proportionality”.\n\n\n\n+*Regarding multiapping during active deliveries:*+\n\nThe PT Fleet T&Cs explicitly allow multi-apping “at the same time” (clause 2.7) and do not include an exception for “during an active delivery”. So I don’t think we should frame enforcement as “multi-apping is prohibited during deliveries” on the basis of the current text.\n\nThat said, if the team wishes to proceed with this, we _can_ address the user experience problem effectively by enforcing service performance / order integrity, rather than “multi-apping” itself:\n\n* Once an order is accepted, the courier must pick it up at the time/location shown in the app (clause 5.1) and must deliver it to the drop-off address as soon as reasonably possible (clause 6.1).\n* The courier can choose the route at their discretion, and the app’s suggested route/ETA is non-binding (also in 6.1), so OSRM/GPS comparisons should be supporting evidence, not a standalone “breach”.\n* There is also a general prohibition on using the platform in a way that is not in line with the terms / “cheating the system” (clause 4.3), which can help where there’s a clear pattern of abuse.\n\nOperationally, that means the trigger should be outcome-based, e.g.:\n\n* repeated material delays vs expected delivery time (beyond reasonable traffic/weather explanations),\n* repeated “courier not moving” / similar complaints tied to orders,\n* repeated, unexplained patterns of significant detours _with clear delivery impact_.\n\nGPS path deviations / OSRM route discrepancies can then be used to corroborate the performance issue, but we avoid saying “we are sanctioning you for multi-apping”.\n\nIf Ops ultimately wants a bright-line prohibition (“no multiapping during an active Bolt delivery”), that would likely require a PT T&Cs update because current clause 2.7 is broadly permissive. However, from a PT reclassification angle, I’d treat that as higher-risk move than a performance-based approach, because it directly restricts autonomy.\n\n\n\nThanks,","2026-01-22T14:04:41.878Z"],["3831036","PFI-837300","PFI","elena.popa@bolt.eu","Elena Popa","[^RO1425-9246719 (1).pdf]","2026-01-22T14:04:45.742Z"],["3831037","LSS-62016","LSS","mihaela.vatamanu@bolt.eu","Mihaela Vatamanu","[^2025-12-08-SOW Bolt Services DE GmbH_Aon Pensions Insurance Broker GmbH.docx] _(846 kB)_","2026-01-22T14:04:55.093Z"],["3831038","PFI-837300","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-22T14:05:02.358Z"],["3831039","LSS-62016","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nMihaela Vatamanu has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-22T14:05:04.349Z"],["3831041","LSS-61937","LSS","paula.pihelgas@bolt.eu","Paula Joanna Pihelgas","Hey, please see the signed contract \n\n[^Schlussbesprechung-GSV_UV_83266716.tvx (1) (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T14:05:15.088Z"],["3831044","LSS-62009","LSS","anja.smrek@bolt.eu","Anja Smrek","thank you!","2026-01-22T14:05:59.888Z"],["3831045","LSS-58645","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:608009c6f74b3f006a326795] - thank you for getting back!\n\nApologies for joining this thread at a later stage - I was looped in to support after my colleague, and only now noticed that the agreement is drafted between Bolt Operations OÜ and the Ghanaian partner entity.\n\nIf this is indeed intended to be Bolt’s EU entity, and given that we will be directly exchanging personal data of drivers with the partner, the inclusion of the EU standard contractual clauses for data sharing is required. This is a mandatory legal requirement applicable to Bolt as an EU company and can be satisfied straightforwardly by incorporating the clauses by reference via a short table.\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nI have reflected this update in both MOUs:\n\n* MOU 1 - CCGL and Bolt Ops: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sD4FYNJWF7YPsEXAX6xexdcs2HqcvOn9/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sD4FYNJWF7YPsEXAX6xexdcs2HqcvOn9/edit|smart-link]\n* MOU 2 - CCGL and Bolt Ops and NEIP: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Hj9Rtsd-OrWzS2W5AygQGx-E1FsJ6zW3/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Hj9Rtsd-OrWzS2W5AygQGx-E1FsJ6zW3/edit|smart-link]\n{panel}\n\n----\n\nI would appreciate it if you could please confirm alignment with the partner ahead of signature.\n\nKind regards,","2026-01-22T14:06:19.687Z"],["3831047","LSS-61592","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:e7c4988a-ccaf-44c1-8546-2d01d1217937] \n\nWith Privacy we provided analysis of Zendesk terms below. \n\n*Please request from Zendesk the updated order for review and signing.* \n\nThey agreed to change: \n\n* Change governing law to English law (clause 11.10) \n* Make changes to agreement (incl. DPA) only by mutual agreement of both parties (clause 11.4) ","2026-01-22T14:06:32.716Z"],["3831048","LSS-61947","LSS","paula.pihelgas@bolt.eu","Paula Joanna Pihelgas","Hey, please see the signed contract \n\n[^3822_Bolt Services FI Oy_Power of attorney (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T14:06:43.476Z"],["3831049","LSS-61816","LSS","ololade.olanipekun@bolt.eu","Ololade Olanipekun","Hi,\n\nI’ll like to confirm whose signature is pending on this contract, as the external vendor (the landlord) has already signed the document.\n\nThank you","2026-01-22T14:06:42.645Z"],["3831050","PFI-836915","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-22T14:06:46.169Z"],["3831051","LSS-61827","LSS","alex.bucse@bolt.eu","Alex Bucșe","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] - we do not have it yet, pending with OpenAI as we still need to confirm minimum purchase commitment, [~accountid:712020:4afbd60d-276d-4d8c-8d4c-5669fd772468] will share it ASAP. This is the existing order form, so most likely this year will be the same format.\n\n[^Order Form_Bolt Technology_OpenAI_31.01.2025 (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T14:06:56.243Z"],["3831052","RS-1947","RS","elena-roxana.iordachel@bolt.eu","Elena-Roxana Iordăchel","Thank you! I have now informed them that we do not store this data. 🙏 ","2026-01-22T14:07:27.395Z"],["3831054","DO-5823","DO","mikhail.kliasheu@bolt.eu","Mikhail Kliasheu","Done","2026-01-22T14:07:49.648Z"],["3831056","LSS-61865","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:4031005b-be5e-413a-b7da-919304795012] ! of course! Apologies - uploaded an old version before\n\n[^bolt (4) (c5fe8040-8c0c-4375-89da-09fc743aa67f) (4eaa661c-3617-4b5c-aa80-c5dae2490c26).pdf] [^bolt (4) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-22T14:07:58.319Z"],["3831058","PFI-836813","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Nazarii, thanks for reaching out. I don’t see any fraud-related checks here, nor does it look like the issue is fraud-related. I’d suggest you provide this as feedback to food-tech [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/76/create/474|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/76/create/474|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T14:08:01.657Z"],["3831060","DO-5825","DO","mikhail.kliasheu@bolt.eu","Mikhail Kliasheu","Done","2026-01-22T14:08:16.183Z"],["3831062","MLC-1059","MLC","gerardo.gomez@bolt.eu","Gerardo Gomez","Q12026\n\n\n* Blockers: none\n* Status update:\n** Provided input for the push notification builder inside targeting platform.\n** Testing the html builder and liquid syntax. \n\n* Next steps:\n** Create variants where the journey builder will have to pick and send an email based on the correct variant. \n** Finalised adding feedback for the HTML builder and personalisation liquid. ","2026-01-22T14:08:39.466Z"],["3831063","LSS-58899","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n# The agreements (MOUs) are drafted between Bolt Operations OÜ and the Ghanaian partner entity.\n# The inclusion of the EU standard contractual clauses for data sharing is required. \n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nPrivacy have reflected this update in both MOUs under Schedule 2:\n\n* MOU 1 - CCGL and Bolt Ops: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sD4FYNJWF7YPsEXAX6xexdcs2HqcvOn9/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sD4FYNJWF7YPsEXAX6xexdcs2HqcvOn9/edit|smart-link]\n* MOU 2 - CCGL and Bolt Ops and NEIP: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Hj9Rtsd-OrWzS2W5AygQGx-E1FsJ6zW3/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Hj9Rtsd-OrWzS2W5AygQGx-E1FsJ6zW3/edit|smart-link]\n\nThe partner confirmed to accept the previous update of both MOUs (including description of data transfer under Schedule 1) and is ready to sign. Inclusion of SCCs is the last step before signature.\n{panel}\n\n----","2026-01-22T14:08:43.357Z"],["3831064","PFI-837301","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-22T14:08:51.999Z"],["3831065","PFI-837301","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:627cf5040d1e73006f7d2aa9] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-22T14:08:53.952Z"],["3831066","LSS-58645","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","The partner will be required to sign out standard co-invesment partnership as well which contains the information you are pointing out. \n\nI will however relay the information to the partner. ","2026-01-22T14:08:57.347Z"],["3831067","VERIFY-4100","VERIFY","andrei.balaban@bolt.eu","Andrei Balaban","Temporary fix: apply a dedicated threshold for predictions of this document type (french company registration smth).","2026-01-22T14:09:00.001Z"],["3831069","SCM-1077","SCM","helen.erg@bolt.eu","Helen Erg","Due date change - it is noce to have not a high priority, with on-going problems, planned vacations I will delay this until end of May.","2026-01-22T14:09:07.393Z"],["3831080","LSS-61816","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:0c90413b-741f-4463-8f2a-012d18e770c7] ! The document will be ready in an hour","2026-01-22T14:09:45.979Z"],["3831092","RS-1960","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:603cb85ec58c720071175949] the domain looks legit","2026-01-22T14:10:37.885Z"],["3831093","LSS-61769","LSS","aire.vaigu@bolt.eu","Aire Vaigu","Hi! Added, please see the new version: [https://cloud.app.box.com/sign/document/255d8091-4446-4d74-98c4-b4b74ed15baf/1cffbb12-a35b-4667-ab10-ccc20807e361/?utm_source=signrequest&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=signrequest-received&signer_token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJ1dWlkIjoiMWNmZmJiMTItYTM1Yi00NjY3LWFiMTAtY2NjMjA4MDdlMzYxIiwiZW1haWwiOiJhaXJlLnZhaWd1QGJvbHQuZXUiLCJpYXQiOjE3NjkwODcxNTYuMTQ4MTEsImV4cCI6MTc2OTY5MTk1Ni4xNDgxMjEsImxpbmtfdHlwZSI6InNpZ25pbmcifQ.FejCVEeox_JIeskmPdRYH9uLpMKpbp_fu6e3aZbWjPs|https://cloud.app.box.com/sign/document/255d8091-4446-4d74-98c4-b4b74ed15baf/1cffbb12-a35b-4667-ab10-ccc20807e361/?utm_source=signrequest&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=signrequest-received&signer_token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJ1dWlkIjoiMWNmZmJiMTItYTM1Yi00NjY3LWFiMTAtY2NjMjA4MDdlMzYxIiwiZW1haWwiOiJhaXJlLnZhaWd1QGJvbHQuZXUiLCJpYXQiOjE3NjkwODcxNTYuMTQ4MTEsImV4cCI6MTc2OTY5MTk1Ni4xNDgxMjEsImxpbmtfdHlwZSI6InNpZ25pbmcifQ.FejCVEeox_JIeskmPdRYH9uLpMKpbp_fu6e3aZbWjPs] ","2026-01-22T14:10:46.977Z"],["3831095","TS-2878","TS","aleksandra.saropova@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Šarõpova","22.01.26 they reached to work on the integration again","2026-01-22T14:11:10.916Z"],["3831096","LSS-61882","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:6151832899b4b8006a366830] , hey! Were there any changes in the agreements?","2026-01-22T14:11:23.719Z"],["3831098","MLC-1717","MLC","yulia.nikitina@bolt.eu","Yulia Nikitina","\n\nPerformance can be found here:\n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1jKlNPfoeD8H4r5wVlTSw6jNvnXNgU3H5PsX-bD8OPHE/edit?gid=1525273651#gid=1525273651|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1jKlNPfoeD8H4r5wVlTSw6jNvnXNgU3H5PsX-bD8OPHE/edit?gid=1525273651#gid=1525273651|smart-link] \n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1TfJ3jHCMaZZjHZrtUXv_8ckwdUW_xGHN2uchWP3X0v4/edit?gid=2116110471#gid=2116110471|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1TfJ3jHCMaZZjHZrtUXv_8ckwdUW_xGHN2uchWP3X0v4/edit?gid=2116110471#gid=2116110471|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T14:11:39.651Z"],["3831100","LSS-58645","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:608009c6f74b3f006a326795] - I was unaware that the co-investment partnership would include this information, and I do not see this document reviewed in the ticket.\n\nFrom what I can see in the ticket, it makes sense to add the EU standard clauses in both MOUs. Since it's a short one-page document added under new Schedule 2, I hope the partner will not have issues with this, especially if they are already aware this will be in the co-investment agreement.","2026-01-22T14:11:52.203Z"],["3831101","PFI-834149","PFI","jakub.kavina@bolt.eu","Jakub Kavina","Already solved, the payout was finished and I have PoP","2026-01-22T14:12:03.965Z"],["3831104","MLC-4064","MLC","nida.altug@bolt.eu","Nida Altuğ","[~accountid:628b4f089c617b006a6c6efb] :partying_face: ","2026-01-22T14:12:26.256Z"],["3831106","VERIFY-4100","VERIFY","andrei.balaban@bolt.eu","Andrei Balaban","If it still reproduces after GDC v3, discuss a solution from admin panel flow run page to update the skills for the task.","2026-01-22T14:12:49.525Z"],["3831107","SREDESK-7458","SREDESK","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","Switched from 4g.large to m7g.xlarge","2026-01-22T14:12:53.224Z"],["3831108","LSS-61920","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Thank you [~accountid:712020:1d4eb168-65d8-4fe2-9240-3537fd827409] - I have accepted your changes 🙂 \n\nPlease could you confirm if tomorrow is a *hard deadline* for the agreement to be finalised?\n\nGiven the short timeframe, the agreement has been prepared internally as we don’t have an internal template for this type of agreement. Due to the complexities of real estate law, this approach may carry some legal risk.\n\nPlease could you let me know the value of the agreement, and whether you are comfortable proceeding with a degree of risk? If not, we would need *at least until Tuesday* to involve external counsel.\n\nCC - [~accountid:712020:7bfaad56-f8bf-45b0-b951-dfd37b5ed5c2], [~accountid:628b3e951a437e0070414307].","2026-01-22T14:13:44.680Z"],["3831109","LSS-61678","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^DE20260114-001 Exleasing cars - Bolt Drive DE.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-22T14:13:50.995Z"],["3831110","PAW-15093","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-22T14:13:53.978Z"],["3831113","BDRIV-16","BDRIV","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] [~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] The link should be accessible now.","2026-01-22T14:14:01.255Z"],["3831114","MLC-4062","MLC","gerardo.gomez@bolt.eu","Gerardo Gomez","W3Q1 2026\n\n\n\n* Blockers: none\n* Status update:\n** Finalised QBR for Northern Europe.\n** Started building pivot tables for Africa’s QBR\n** Downloading data for Africa’s QBR. \n\n* Next steps:\n** Collect data for the other regions and their QBR. \n** Start building tables for the other regional QBRs. ","2026-01-22T14:14:02.439Z"],["3831117","LSS-61816","LSS","ololade.olanipekun@bolt.eu","Ololade Olanipekun","Thank you ","2026-01-22T14:14:17.143Z"],["3831119","LSS-61657","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:60a37337391e56006e62277c] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Bolt x Sophie - Car Simulator Agreement 2025-2026 (1).pdf] ","2026-01-22T14:14:23.790Z"],["3831120","LSS-61908","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] - many thanks for taking the time to draft this!\n\nIt all looks good to me, the only comment I would raise here is concerning point 1): currently, it reads as if the authorities (police) requested information from Bolt on this case. As far as I am aware, this is *not* the case (i.e., we didn’t _respond_ to a police requests for information _per se_): Bolt reported the rider’s complaint to the Metropolitan Police because it is part of the standard procedure when users report theft or in cases similar to this one. Still as per procedure, Transport for London was also notified. [~accountid:5dde532fcdc2d20d05377446] could you perhaps confirm this? I trust @Vivien Antoniou was the POC who aligned with CSPC concerning this case.\n\nThe above is to say that it may be beneficial to slightly alter the angle, so that it is clear that we reported the information to the police because we have a legal obligation to do so (? ) and it is what we always do as per our procedures. The core of what’s being said here is right, it’s simply that we “voluntarily” reported this rather than responsively did so based on an authority’s request.","2026-01-22T14:14:35.655Z"],["3831121","DAEN-751","DAEN","kaarel.tamuri@bolt.eu","Kaarel Tamuri","*Thoughts on Looker SDK*\n\n* Good tool to “mass“ view and edit dashboards/tiles/looks/merged queries\n* Adding/removing/hiding columns, read/edit metadata, etc\n* Can not make changes to the query, but you can make a copy of the query, change it and then replace it\n* No safeguards!\n** Can edit everything without “access“\n** No testing env. Changes go live after they are made.\n** No good solutions to revert\n* How to make safeguards?\n** Make a copy of the standalone element (dashboard/look) before changes\n** Developing on your own folder (on copies)\n** Add logs to your code (without knowing what was changed you can not go back)\n** Add plenty print statements outputting info about the metadata and code status, so the user can pull the plug if something looks off","2026-01-22T14:15:18.073Z"],["3831123","LSS-61761","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^EE20260114-001 Rover SUD - Bolt Drive EE.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-22T14:15:28.824Z"],["3831126","LSS-61763","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc]  Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^LV20260114-001 Rover SUD - Bolt Drive LV.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-22T14:16:07.046Z"],["3831129","SOBB-797","SOBB","lucas.santossilva@bolt.eu","Lucas Oliveira dos Santos Silva","(flag) Flag added \n\nReview with [~accountid:712020:55f8d571-60a5-4faf-bb90-1d80d8fad9e3] (Sales Operations) if the field Calling_Number__c still make sense to exist in SFDC once that we already have two phone fields (phone and mobile)","2026-01-22T14:16:23.346Z"],["3831130","CMO-12980","CMO","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Bolt Restaurant app is no longer called that, it is called Bolt Merchant app","2026-01-22T14:16:23.943Z"],["3831133","LSS-61820","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] ! May I ask you to check this company?","2026-01-22T14:17:31.280Z"],["3831135","PFI-837202","PFI","caroline.kruberg@bolt.eu","Caroline Kruberg","Hi,\n\nDriver’s top-up was adjusted by 13 GBP due to a single order that the driver didn’t finish properly:\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/610043213/25?orderTryId=1520514093|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/610043213/25?orderTryId=1520514093]\n\nThe estimated duration was around 9 minutes, but the driver kept the order active for over 1 hour. At the end, price was recalculated to the upfront, and the driver accepted the low price, indicating that our recalculation was correct and that he indeed made a mistake by keeping the order active. If the order really happened as it was logged, the driver would’ve requested a price review, complaining about the 8.68 GBP price. You can share the trip details with the driver and educate him to be more cautious with the order states to prevent this situation from happening again.\n\nIn terms of his appeal, we won’t adjust his NLW compensation further. Our action was justified.\n\nBest,\nCaroline","2026-01-22T14:17:35.523Z"],["3831139","LSS-61887","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^LV20260120-002 United Motors - Bolt Drive LT.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-22T14:17:57.065Z"],["3831140","LSS-61822","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^EE20260120-002 Bulsink Auto's - Bolt Drive EE.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-22T14:18:27.995Z"],["3831146","PFI-837306","PFI","monika.civrag@bolt.eu","Monika Čivrag","!Slika zaslona 2026-01-22 u 15.16.52.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Slika zaslona 2026-01-22 u 15.17.01.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Slika zaslona 2026-01-22 u 15.17.08.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T14:19:06.518Z"],["3831149","LSS-59597","LSS","mikael.uusivuori@bolt.eu","Mikael Uusivuori","[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] yes understand and already some good flags spotted! just wanted to ensure we can move forward and not have it delayed much longer. thanks again for reviewing 🙏","2026-01-22T14:19:28.163Z"],["3831150","SCM-1136","SCM","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1j75Y7Qctvdh1IlNNImbNADgZ4S_THc6upLTBYLXq0Es/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1j75Y7Qctvdh1IlNNImbNADgZ4S_THc6upLTBYLXq0Es/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T14:19:29.839Z"],["3831153","LSS-61589","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Thanks [~accountid:712020:38ef5817-1c12-4bf5-b0d1-116b99b69ddf] for approval via Slack 😉 \n\nHere’s the instruction for the signing:\n\n* the file: [^Bolt_MWIIH_response_letter_23012026.docx.pdf] \n* the signature: e-PUAP (a Polish signature)\n* we need to send it to the Authority on Frida, 23.01, so I will be grateful if you arrange the signing as soon as possible. 🙏 \n\nThank you!","2026-01-22T14:20:03.564Z"],["3831157","DO-5816","DO","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","Please check the cluster setup section in the doc. It has step by step instructions.","2026-01-22T14:20:37.391Z"],["3831158","DSR-3971","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T14:21:06.277Z"],["3831159","LSS-61940","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","Legal advice by {{2026-01-28}}","2026-01-22T14:21:29.347Z"],["3831160","WD-22638","WD","alexandru.cerveanu@bolt.eu","Alex Cerveanu","Hi Sirly,\n\nI see that Bolt Payroll Accountant role is already assigned, can you please confirm if other role should be assign to Edit-Richelle?","2026-01-22T14:21:40.335Z"],["3831164","LSS-61970","LSS","paula.pihelgas@bolt.eu","Paula Joanna Pihelgas","Hey, please see the signed NDA \n\n\n\n[^NDA (Non-disclosure agreement).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T14:22:50.847Z"],["3831165","LSS-61769","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi, thanks, all good, we can proceed with the signing.\n\nLegal Ops, please organize Ahto signature on the Service Order which has been shared by Box via their [signing link|https://cloud.app.box.com/sign/document/255d8091-4446-4d74-98c4-b4b74ed15baf/1cffbb12-a35b-4667-ab10-ccc20807e361/?utm_source=signrequest&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=signrequest-received&signer_token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJ1dWlkIjoiMWNmZmJiMTItYTM1Yi00NjY3LWFiMTAtY2NjMjA4MDdlMzYxIiwiZW1haWwiOiJhaXJlLnZhaWd1QGJvbHQuZXUiLCJpYXQiOjE3NjkwODcxNTYuMTQ4MTEsImV4cCI6MTc2OTY5MTk1Ni4xNDgxMjEsImxpbmtfdHlwZSI6InNpZ25pbmcifQ.FejCVEeox_JIeskmPdRYH9uLpMKpbp_fu6e3aZbWjPs ].\n\nThanks!","2026-01-22T14:23:31.495Z"],["3831167","HS-29254","HS","eduard.szekelyi@bolt.eu","Eduard-Filip Szekelyi","Hello [~accountid:712020:dc4824f4-a6bc-41f2-af89-59d155dc0cc8] ,\n\n\nFor first Tick *“Ein Versicherungspflichtverhältnis zur Bundesagentur für Arbeit besteht / bestand”*\n-The employee has a regular employment subject to social insurance contributions.\nFor second *Do NOT tick anything* in the ELStAM section\n-This part is only for employees *not registered* in the German electronic tax system.\nThe employee *is registered in ELStAM*, so it does not apply.\n\n","2026-01-22T14:23:32.570Z"],["3831168","PAW-15123","PAW","mihai.casandra@bolt.eu","Mihai Casandra","Started clarification with InfoSec on whitelist review ownership: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06EQD6QJRW/p1769091524817509|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06EQD6QJRW/p1769091524817509|smart-link] \n*Who will approve any exceptions added to the list?*\n\nThe response does not influence the technical solution in any way, but it must be known before implementation rollout.","2026-01-22T14:23:53.305Z"],["3831169","LSS-62018","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Legal Ops, please organize Ahto signature on the Service Order which has been shared by Box via their [+signing link+|https://cloud.app.box.com/sign/document/255d8091-4446-4d74-98c4-b4b74ed15baf/1cffbb12-a35b-4667-ab10-ccc20807e361/?utm_source=signrequest&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=signrequest-received&signer_token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJ1dWlkIjoiMWNmZmJiMTItYTM1Yi00NjY3LWFiMTAtY2NjMjA4MDdlMzYxIiwiZW1haWwiOiJhaXJlLnZhaWd1QGJvbHQuZXUiLCJpYXQiOjE3NjkwODcxNTYuMTQ4MTEsImV4cCI6MTc2OTY5MTk1Ni4xNDgxMjEsImxpbmtfdHlwZSI6InNpZ25pbmcifQ.FejCVEeox_JIeskmPdRYH9uLpMKpbp_fu6e3aZbWjPs].","2026-01-22T14:23:57.584Z"],["3831175","PFI-833185","PFI","aisma.austruma@bolt.eu","Aisma Austruma","Thank you for this information. \n\nI’m trying to explain to the company how they were billed for the coupons. \n\nSo for example - this trip - it was not included in the Coupon section, but was included in the trips made by the Business Users - so basically the trip counts as 0€. \n\nBut if the expenses - the actual discount code they issued is not counted in the Coupn section, then. it turns out we have not charged them for the coupon at all? \n\nPlease help me understand how this is setup - as they are having trouble tracking the expenses and I’m trying to add and count with them on the CSV report - but the CSV report also does not seem to match the Invoice data. :melting_face: \n\nThank you for your help here [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] ","2026-01-22T14:25:09.950Z"],["3831176","SREDESK-7454","SREDESK","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","Access granted","2026-01-22T14:25:41.049Z"],["3831188","CNT-474","CNT","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","[~accountid:621c92ba4160640069c52776] no rush, next week would be perfect. Jina is reviewing it now. ","2026-01-22T14:26:52.973Z"],["3831189","VERIFY-2584","VERIFY","alexander.zhigulich@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Zhigulich","[Analysis|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04HZ4X12UQ/p1766156349805749]\n\nShows distribution by check type:\n\n!image-20260122-155325.png|width=905,alt=\"image-20260122-155325.png\"!\n\n!image-20260122-155408.png|width=905,alt=\"image-20260122-155408.png\"!\n\nOPS costs are negligible for cross checks.\nNote: we do not calculate the opportunity loss (GMV loss)","2026-01-22T14:26:58.416Z"],["3831191","CRC-1917","CRC","romet.varts@bolt.eu","Romet Varts","This is covered in EPICS Linnet has been working on 25q4 and 26q1. Closing these epics","2026-01-22T14:27:18.144Z"],["3831192","PFI-837202","PFI","fiona.achieng@bolt-outsource.eu","Fiona Achieng","Thank you for the update. I will inform the driver.","2026-01-22T14:27:25.461Z"],["3831194","CRC-1918","CRC","romet.varts@bolt.eu","Romet Varts","This is covered in EPICS Linnet has been working on 25q4 and 26q1. Closing these epics","2026-01-22T14:27:39.537Z"],["3831196","LSS-62019","LSS","alina.solomka@bolt.eu","Alina Solomka","[^01.2026 Bolt-Partner Special Terms (LV) ENG-LV - Sky (006) (1).docx] _(2.70 MB)_","2026-01-22T14:27:53.831Z"],["3831197","PFI-835316","PFI","bruno.pereira@bolt.eu","Bruno dos Reis Pereira","Thank you Ketlin, let me know if you do find something.","2026-01-22T14:27:57.747Z"],["3831200","LSS-62020","LSS","mihaela.vatamanu@bolt.eu","Mihaela Vatamanu","[^AFFS Intermediary Service SLA Personal Insurance_Bolt ZA_ALEXANDER FORBES FINANCIAL SERVICES_29.05.2025.pdf] _(527 kB)_\n\n[^Template cancellation letter- Alexander Forbes Financial Services (Pty) Ltd.gdoc] _(0.2 kB)_","2026-01-22T14:28:16.069Z"],["3831201","FPD-1435","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","Progress has been made over the week in the task [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FPD-1503|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FPD-1503|smart-link] \nResults are being compiled and will be added to that specific ticket, a spreadsheet with consolidated results will also be provided. Expected to have all that by tomorrow.","2026-01-22T14:28:17.640Z"],["3831203","LSS-61882","LSS","isabella.danso@bolt.eu","Isabella Danso","I just included the liability link and the benefits as suggested on the original template","2026-01-22T14:28:43.948Z"],["3831206","LSS-60455","LSS","anna.hultengard@bolt.eu","Anna Hultengård","Hi [~accountid:61542c1e07ac3c0068bc7768] , here is the signed agreement. I will now close this ticket. [^Services Agreement_ Bolt Support Sweden AB_ Hallvarsson & Halvarsson AB.docx.pdf] ","2026-01-22T14:29:22.849Z"],["3831208","LSS-61939","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:63314e9e9b32cfef93265252] I’ve reviewed both municipal e-scooter agreements (Rijeka and Osijek) in light of the decision to exit Croatia. Below is the  legal position and what I recommend we do.\n\n\nNeither contract gives Bolt a right to walk away early because the business is no longer profitable. There is no “clean” unilateral exit. \n\n* *Rijeka*\n** 3-year contract.\n** The City has the right to terminate (mainly for breach).\n** Bolt has no unilateral termination right.\n* *Osijek*\n** 1-year contract.\n** The City can terminate unilaterally on 30 days’ notice.\n** Bolt again has no equivalent right.\n\nIn both cases, non-profitability/closing the business is not a valid termination ground, either under the contracts or Croatian law.\n\nIf Bolt simply stops operating, that is a clear breach under both contracts.\n\n* *Rijeka*: The City may terminate the contract for breach, retain any fees already paid, and potentially claim damages for non-performance. Given the public nature of the contract, there is also a reputational risk with the City and other municipalities.\n* *Osijek*: The City may likewise terminate for breach, keep a proportional part of the annual fee, and seek compensation for any losses. Because the City also has a right to terminate for convenience on 30 days’ notice, it would likely exercise that right instead of pursuing litigation, but the reputational impact would remain.\n\n*Realistic options*\n\n# *Agree a mutual termination with the Cities*\n\nThe message is straightforward: the service is no longer economically viable, Bolt is exiting Croatia entirely, and we want to close responsibly with minimal disruption.\n\n *2. the City terminate (mainly relevant for Osijek)*\nIn Osijek, the City can terminate on 30 days’ notice anyway.\n\n* Legally safer than Bolt breaching the contract.\n* Downside: we lose control over timing and narrative, and the City can keep a proportional part of the annual fee.\n\nThis is an acceptable fallback if a mutual termination cannot be agreed quickly.\n\n# *Rely on “changed circumstances” under Croatian law*\nThis is not a strong exit route.\n\n* Croatian courts are very reluctant to accept non-profitability as a reason.\n\nAt best, this is negotiation leverage, not a strategy we should plan to litigate.\n\n# *Unilateral shutdown by Bolt*\nI do not recommend this.\n\n* It puts us clearly in breach.\n* It maximises legal and reputational risk for no real upside\n\n*Recommendation* \n\n#  approach both Cities to propose a mutual termination.\n# Keep the communication factual :\n#* decision to exit the Croatian market,\n#* economic unsustainability of continuing,\n#* commitment to an orderly and responsible wind-down.\n# Avoid any admission of breach or non-compliance.\n# If Osijek does not engage, be prepared to let the City use its 30-day termination right.\n# Treat Rijeka as the higher-risk contract and prioritise a negotiated outcome there.","2026-01-22T14:29:54.101Z"],["3831209","RS-1962","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:5bbde236ee5d7e7580edbb02] ,\n\nThis seems like a Consumer Protection-related ticket, usually such tickets are handled by the Legal support. I am not sure if [~accountid:628dd71f40b157006f734818]  , you are the relevant POC, can you please have a look?","2026-01-22T14:29:56.354Z"],["3831211","HS-29200","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:7f339fc8-1d2a-4500-903a-50ef7065e24d],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-22T14:30:07.833Z"],["3831213","DLSP-2035","DLSP","habib.fikri@bolt.eu","Fikri Sundayana","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08C4EDHVKJ/p1768915384210219|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08C4EDHVKJ/p1768915384210219|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T14:30:19.768Z"],["3831214","CRC-2131","CRC","romet.varts@bolt.eu","Romet Varts","[~accountid:712020:3f99cfdf-ccce-430b-94b3-85ea01b54df4] should we keep this open?","2026-01-22T14:30:38.678Z"],["3831215","PFI-836901","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba\n\n[^Refund_Letter_QNWND48RBVFZW6Q9_R74NS9XT5QMQ3NQ9.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T14:30:42.152Z"],["3831216","PFI-836816","PFI","wiktoria.dziego@bolt.eu","Wiktoria Dzięgo","Hi - added in the ticket - Example of same provider with same email that received the invoice - 70740\nmore here - [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-provider/providers?tz=Europe%2FWarsaw&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"provider_name\"%3A\"costa\"}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-provider/providers?tz=Europe%2FWarsaw&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22provider_name%22%3A%22costa%22%7D%7D] \n(all except the ones in the ticket)","2026-01-22T14:30:50.374Z"],["3831218","RNTL-30311","RNTL","aleksei.antonov@bolt.eu","Aleksei Antonov","out of scope","2026-01-22T14:30:54.622Z"],["3831219","CRC-2131","CRC","linnet.puskar@bolt.eu","Linnet Puskar","Yes, but it is probably Q2","2026-01-22T14:31:13.335Z"],["3831220","DSR-3973","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-22T14:31:24.854Z"],["3831221","LSS-62019","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-22T14:31:25.085Z"],["3831222","LSS-61517","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","As communicated in Slack: \n\nHi [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9], sharing comments and considerations from a legal perspective here as well (summary of what we just discussed). \n\n* *Employment considerations/reclassification risk:*\n** Requires employed drivers only (incl if we engage subcontractors), meaning we can only engage FOs that actually employ their drivers, which is however better from a reclass perspective for us;\n** Strict driver continuity (same driver + max 2 substitutes; breach = SEK 5,000 unless unforeseeable). This raises reclass risk and needs to be considered how we're planning to handle this (FO scheduling their employed drivers etc);\n** Branded clothing/name badges (with Bolt's name), detailed conduct rules and mandatory training;  \n** Municipality can immediately request us to ban drivers and require replacement.\nI assume this will only be on the basis of serious misconduct but including here anyway as we'll need to be cautious on which basis we will suspend drivers.\n* *Penalties are frequent and high (as you've already flagged in the business case):*\n** Multiple penalties can apply. Examples: delays (50% fare cut / SEK 2,000 per passenger), service issues (SEK 5,000), hand-in-hand failure (SEK 10,000), traffic safety breaches (SEK 25,000). 7 business days to dispute or penalty is deemed accepted. Penalties do not limit claims for actual damages.\n* *Uncapped liability:*\n** Indirect damages excluded, but otherwise uncapped liability:question:@elisabeth.gunnarsson I would include a question to the Municipality in this regard, as we discussed.\n* *Interpretation precedence:*\n** Clause 8.23 gives the Municipality unilateral interpretation precedence in case of disagreement on contract meaning. In my view, this could potentially be inconsistent with procurement principles (transparency/equal treatment). :question:As discussed, I recommend raising a clarifying question.\nPlease align with @anna.hultengard if further legal assistance is needed.\n* *Audit & control rights:*\n** Far-reaching audit, site visit and information access rights for the Municipality, which we'll need to pay for should they engage a third-party to conduct this.  \n\nFYI for the Privacy Team ([~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] ) - [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] has created a separate ticket here for the privacy review (incl. DPA review). \n\nAs I'm soon off for vacation, will be poc for the subcontracting agreement with Roslagstaxi and [~accountid:712020:0285a595-6608-4335-9a5a-60b50674c696] or general tender support. ","2026-01-22T14:31:27.190Z"],["3831224","MARTECH3-1519","MARTECH3","prakhar.saini@bolt.eu","Prakhar Saini","*Task 1*\n\nAnalyze the following experiments using the v1.3 framework: \n\n# Nigeria TikTok iOS Reach Launch:\n## Start Date: 2025-10-30\n## End Date: 2025-11-20\n## Geo Level: Country\n## ROI Threshold: 3\n## Revenue Allocation: 0.9\n# Kyiv Google Android Increase\n## Start Date: 2025-08-26\n## End Date: 2025-09-16\n## Geo Level: City\n## ROI Threshold: 8.3\n## Revenue Allocation: 0.9\n\nNotebook template stored [here|https://bolt-datascience.cloud.databricks.com/browse/folders/179722328510958?o=3829506390716583].\n\nExpected deliverable: Confluence page with experiment details and comments + post analysis notebook. ","2026-01-22T14:31:43.348Z"],["3831225","LSS-62021","LSS","margarita.sargautyte@bolt.eu","Margarita Sargautytė","!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 12.21.24.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T14:31:50.691Z"],["3831227","WD-22575","WD","kristiine.murd@bolt.eu","Kristiine Murd","Hi [~accountid:712020:42c95fcc-665c-491a-9341-767b89230c32] \nPlease share the screenshot from Telema PreLive with the invoice coding so that I can add additional explanation what should be visible in WD and what we actually see.","2026-01-22T14:31:59.400Z"],["3831228","PFI-836887","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-22T14:32:11.930Z"],["3831231","PFI-833185","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Not really, if Coupons were used by the Employees, the Trip goes under the Transportation section, it’s still a coupon, but just a way how we invoice is different. \n\nI may be wrong, but I believe csv report doesn’t include the data for the coupons that are not done by Employees. I believe you should ask from the Business Analytics Team for the reports with Coupons.\n\nGenerally, on the photo below is group of trips the company was charged for.\n\n!image-20260122-143153.png|width=657,alt=\"image-20260122-143153.png\"!","2026-01-22T14:32:29.933Z"],["3831232","PFI-836886","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-22T14:32:37.892Z"],["3831233","LSS-61948","LSS","anna.hultengard@bolt.eu","Anna Hultengård","Thanks so much!","2026-01-22T14:32:41.109Z"],["3831234","RNTL-30437","RNTL","illyaveklenko@bolt.eu","Illia Veklenko","duplicate","2026-01-22T14:32:48.289Z"],["3831235","DPX-3589","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","Waiting for translations\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101692?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101692?created=true|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T14:32:51.023Z"],["3831236","LSS-61934","LSS","erich.pullerits@bolt.eu","Erich Pullerits","Heya!\nIt should be there for quite some time now. They are from AXA","2026-01-22T14:33:19.526Z"],["3831238","RDXENG-4736","RDXENG","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:5e0f0e7f0242870e996ebba8] Hey thanks, I’ve reviewed. Looks good to me. \n\nThere’s one more kinda-sorta related case around SR blocking in Georgia. Right now, the experience is terrible, and we’ve received multiple reports about confused users. \n\nMy suggestion and context:\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CKYJD8AC8/p1762857839978379?thread_ts=1762632384.397569&cid=CKYJD8AC8|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CKYJD8AC8/p1762857839978379?thread_ts=1762632384.397569&cid=CKYJD8AC8|smart-link] \n\n!image_720_720.png|width=628,alt=\"image_720_720.png\"!\n\nOr ideally we should just disable this category for all non-business users in Georgia. Maybe someone can help do that. ","2026-01-22T14:33:30.077Z"],["3831239","DPX-3546","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","Extracted Sunmi V3 guide into a separate task: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPX-3588|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPX-3588]","2026-01-22T14:33:34.891Z"],["3831240","PFI-836773","PFI","carlos.segovia@bolt.eu","Carlos Segovia","Hi Karl!\n\nThanks for the insight.\n\nI see that both accounts were rejected and weren’t used. So, given that, is it considered a problem that the new account was created with the same user/phone number? I see that the company “Premisa” is different than the other ones. \n\nOr are there any other reasons on why should we reject this new company?\n\nI’ll appreciate if you could let me know, that way we could give a proper response to the company as well (without oversharing, of course).\n\nThanks in advance!","2026-01-22T14:33:59.351Z"],["3831241","RNTL-30130","RNTL","illyaveklenko@bolt.eu","Illia Veklenko","duplicate","2026-01-22T14:34:28.596Z"],["3831242","LSS-61545","LSS","ewoma.jerryogeme@bolt.eu","Ewoma Jerry-Ogeme","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] please confirm, counterparty says they have signed. Thank you","2026-01-22T14:34:33.633Z"],["3831244","PFI-836940","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Joao, thanks for reaching out. Devices unblocked 🙂 ","2026-01-22T14:35:06.026Z"],["3831245","LSS-61987","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:5dbb027ba766000da47cf09d] , thanks a lot for escalating this! 🙏 \n\nAs the driver is essentially making a DSAR, could you please confirm whether a copy of all data related to this driver’s account has already been provided? If not, then I suggest you _also_ open a DSRR ticket as per our usual channels so that we tackle this request ASAP - the ticket is dated 16 January.\n\nWhen preparing the answer letter, we may then want to consider asking additional questions as to the driver’s claim in order to gain a better understanding of what he’s reporting to us.\n\nMy understanding is that the “Disclosure and Barring Service” is a body that processes and issues DBS checks in the UK - that is a check on an individual’s criminal record, which aims to show details of all spent and unspent convictions, cautions, reprimands and final warnings held on central police records. Perhaps something came up in that driver’s DBS that he believes is not right. We’ll need to investigate this further the driver provides more context.","2026-01-22T14:35:09.077Z"],["3831247","DSR-2883","DSR","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","[~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] Hi! The new external google drive is here: [https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0AK1yA4P_a3nVUk9PVA|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0AK1yA4P_a3nVUk9PVA]\n\n* Please create a folder with the Driver’s full name and add the data inside it. You might need to download it from our internal GDrive and then upload it to this drive (as we don’t want to move the data and risk this being deleted). \n* Once that’s done, the hyperlink for the driver’s folder (not the whole drive) can be referenced in the response\n* I can then grant access + set a reminder to remove it after 7 days\n** Before I do that, please confirm if WIE want the data or it’s being sent to the Driver directly?","2026-01-22T14:35:28.299Z"],["3831250","LSS-58592","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^2025_01_16_Acordo_Colaboração_BOLT_OPO_ANA_revisto (77eeeea3-9485-434e-839b-70b71e51aad8).pdf] ","2026-01-22T14:36:15.303Z"],["3831253","L10N-29638","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29637](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29637)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T14:37:10.203Z"],["3831254","RS-1734","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] Let’s not piss them off and proceed with the disclosure! Seems like we won’t get any further details about the crime. ","2026-01-22T14:37:10.908Z"],["3831255","PFI-837319","PFI","timofey.shapovalov@bolt-outsource.eu","Timofey Shapovalov","!0F9AB6AA-5DDD-4C9F-822A-4D28EEF51989.png|thumbnail!\n\n!2A842BBA-98FA-433F-908E-5D4A1AE7719B.png|thumbnail!\n\n!597FE0D6-2A0C-4D72-94AB-F4663559C2C3.png|thumbnail!\n\n!9254C308-85B9-4F77-B87E-79BDFE226D77.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T14:37:11.272Z"],["3831256","L10N-29642","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","