ng up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29637](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29637)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T14:37:26.448Z"],["3831265","L10N-29655","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29637](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29637)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T14:37:27.618Z"],["3831268","L10N-29662","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29637](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29637)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T14:37:33.687Z"],["3831269","LSS-62019","LSS","alina.solomka@bolt.eu","Alina Solomka","[^01.2026 Bolt-Partner Special Terms (LV) ENG-LV - Sky (006).docx]\n\n","2026-01-22T14:37:54.158Z"],["3831270","WFM-10098","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Request raised here: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541833|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541833]","2026-01-22T14:37:54.924Z"],["3831271","LSS-59845","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:5d7b698997d8980d8ead4b01] [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] please share with Sentry DPA and MSA. MSA is fully negotiated, we closed all points. After comments from InfoSec Privacy confirmed that we need to enter into a separate DPA. \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/11KzGix_DomZbxteXT-pczx-itBK83M46ijKheJRzV-M/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/11KzGix_DomZbxteXT-pczx-itBK83M46ijKheJRzV-M/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link]  [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1civphqW3YQ_IWAYXn77GQ2nd2WasUy9w/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1civphqW3YQ_IWAYXn77GQ2nd2WasUy9w/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T14:38:11.810Z"],["3831272","LSS-61920","LSS","emma.angelova@bolt.eu","Emma Angelova","Hi Sasha, \n\nWe can wait until Tuesday. Tomorrow is not a hard deadline but ideally we would like to finalise it before the launch date, which is 1st Feb. \n\nMany thanks,\n\n\n\n","2026-01-22T14:38:18.231Z"],["3831273","L10N-29671","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29637](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29637)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T14:38:21.329Z"],["3831274","LSS-61920","LSS","georgia.heathman@bolt.eu","Georgia Heathman","Hi [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] the deadline for the agreement was being driven largely so we could include the airport at launch and in the media announcement which may go out on the 27th. \n\nGiven this is the first time we are doing this in the UK I’d prefer we have the external review as you have recommended and we will remove the airport from the launch until the agreement is ready and signed. \n\nThe 27th would still be helpful ahead of the 1st February date however so if that is possible that would be brill. We can then make a media announcement further down the line if needed. \n\nThank you again.\n\nGeorgia ","2026-01-22T14:38:25.289Z"],["3831278","PFI-836881","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThis is related to a new feature called re-use preauthorisation. Instead of placing a new hold for every trip, we now *re-use an existing pre-authorization* for a set period.\n\nThis means if you take multiple trips, we use the same hold to cover the cost, so you won't see multiple temporary charges on your statement.\n\nIn this specific case, the charge for a new completed order [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1510644064/437?orderTryId=2904668178|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1510644064/437?orderTryId=2904668178] was simply applied to a pre-authorization from a cancelled order that was already reserved on the card.","2026-01-22T14:39:20.278Z"],["3831281","RDS-1089","RDS","andreas.palm@bolt.eu","Andreas Palm","We investigated this request and found a blocking issue.\n\nAbout a year ago, the push permission prompt was moved from app launch to after signup completion. Because of this, users who start but do not finish signup never grant push permission. As a result, the existing reminder push and the proposed experiment are currently not working. This is confirmed on Android and is likely the same on iOS.\n\nThis means the request is not a timing change. It would require changing where in the signup funnel we ask for push permissions.\n\nThis change was originally made for valid reasons:\n\n* Asking for push permission early caused user frustration during signup.\n* Push token registration on the backend is tied to user_id, so pushes could not work before auth completed.\n* A “phoneless auth” project was planned to make signup almost instant and solve this cleanly, but that project is currently frozen.\n\nGiven the current state, we see these options:\n\n* Keep status quo: safest and consistent with current architecture, but non-signed users remain unreachable by push.\n* Move permission request earlier: enables the use case but reintroduces known UX issues and cannot be properly A/B tested.\n* Larger rework (anonymous or pre-signup flows): not realistic short term due to platform and security complexity.\n\n\n\nGiven the trade-offs and that even the current version doesn’t function, we will close this dependency for now. This can be revisited if and when the signup or auth flow changes in a way that allows push permissions to be granted earlier.","2026-01-22T14:39:59.774Z"],["3831283","WD-22575","WD","lysette.ranne@bolt.eu","Lysette Ranne","Hi [~accountid:623c7881562ab90069f8f044], screenshot added\n\n[^Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 16.39.33.pdf]\n\n \n\n\n","2026-01-22T14:40:24.721Z"],["3831284","PFI-827148","PFI","jakub.seibert@bolt-outsource.eu","Jakub Seibert","FO has sent his bank account statement to show us that no money truly arrived to them in this [case |https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/728036692]\n\n","2026-01-22T14:41:12.402Z"],["3831285","WEBSD-1500","WEBSD","emma.sjoo@bolt.eu","Emma Sjöö","[~accountid:712020:f0f7cc2d-5968-45e9-91ec-ea445d725066] I have to wait for the product team to create one as there were no existing. But can you please create a QR code for this view:\n\nbolt://action/subscriptionOffer ","2026-01-22T14:41:13.880Z"],["3831287","WFM-10097","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Request raised here: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571848|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571848] (approved)\n\nWFM team, please take over with the queue assignment.","2026-01-22T14:41:21.799Z"],["3831288","DRAG101-405","DRAG101","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","Speedometer test was completed today. No official test result yet, but comment from test personnel is that everything was gut (/) ","2026-01-22T14:41:29.019Z"],["3831290","RS-1962","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","*I have dublicate ticket(*[+RS-1964+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RS-1964]) *with the following information:*\n\nTomislav Lukachevich received an email from the 3rd Police Department of the Tbilisi City Police Department ([e.khokhiashvili@mia.gov.ge|mailto:e.khokhiashvili@mia.gov.ge]) requesting courier information related to a specific delivery dated 11.12.2025 (6V6EA). The email was sent without any additional recipients in CC and did not include an official signed document/letter as an attachment.\n\nWe are familiar with this case. The courier previously visited the office and reported that a customer was pursuing legal action against him.\n\nOrder timeline / handling details:\n\n* 17:33:19 - Courier arrived at the customer’s location.\n* 17:34:54 - Courier call attempt initiated (approx. 1 minute after arrival), screenshot from courier indicates 4 missed calls to the customer.\n* Courier contacted Customer Support approximately 8 minutes after arrival and opened a courier support ticket.\n* Courier remained on-site for approximately 37 minutes (exceeding the standard 10-minute waiting time).\n* 18:10:14 - Customer Support manually finished the order.\n\nOrder link: [+https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/275609609?cityId=15&showUserTz=false+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/275609609?cityId=15&showUserTz=false]\nCourier beehive case link: [+https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/702720687+|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/702720687]\nUser Beehive case link: [+https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/702495119+|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/702495119]\n\nCustomer Complaint: \nThe customer claims the courier stole the order and did not attempt to contact her.\n\nCould you please assess this situation and provide guidance on next steps?\n\nI am adding Tomislav Lukachevich, Ban Beidas, and Kaha to this thread for additional context and details.","2026-01-22T14:41:35.111Z"],["3831292","CNT-474","CNT","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","[~accountid:621c92ba4160640069c52776] Jina left her comments. ","2026-01-22T14:41:44.541Z"],["3831293","WD-22427","WD","paula.noulik@bolt.eu","Paula Nõulik","thank you so much Iryna! This ticket can be closed.\n\n","2026-01-22T14:42:12.068Z"],["3831296","LSS-57342","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (22.01)*+\n\n* Zellis appears to have accepted our data protection amendments to the DPA, and not included any further data protection changes. As such, provided that the business is willing to accept the previously-flagged risks, I have no further comments on the DPA ✅ \n* Zellis also attached their Customer Agreement (via email).\n** Term is 5 years, nine-month break clauses after 3 years have passed. Primarily summarises costs and services (including payroll, Helpdesk and training).\n** In short, no comments ✅ ","2026-01-22T14:42:22.008Z"],["3831299","RS-1964","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Thank you [~accountid:63d2814195cff7f585c3e2b8] for the details! I have 2 tickets about this issue so I am closing this one. I have added you to the other ticket.\ndub ticket - [RS-1962|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RS-1962]","2026-01-22T14:42:54.467Z"],["3831300","WFM-10047","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","please share updates","2026-01-22T14:42:54.677Z"],["3831305","PAR-119","PAR","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","[~accountid:5d428d25d9cd0e0da3a1b03e] Is there another ticket where it is described what has been done? It is quite an important bit\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:fc7ada41-3f9c-4d74-95f1-90300ecbe201] ","2026-01-22T14:43:38.276Z"],["3831312","LSS-61200","LSS","thalemarie.bo@bolt.eu","Thale Marie Bø","Hi [~accountid:5f52461dfdc3f5003f51865e] unfortunately not yet, but I will get back to you. Might not be able to until next week though. ","2026-01-22T14:45:11.484Z"],["3831313","CSDT-983","CSDT","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","discussion - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C069Y8DNN7L/p1769076165384719|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C069Y8DNN7L/p1769076165384719|smart-link] \n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15480|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15480|smart-link] \n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/looker-customer-support/pull/1935|https://github.com/bolteu/looker-customer-support/pull/1935|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T14:45:26.340Z"],["3831314","LSS-59587","LSS","thalemarie.bo@bolt.eu","Thale Marie Bø","[~accountid:5f52461dfdc3f5003f51865e] sorry for not responding yet. I will look into this tomorrow. ","2026-01-22T14:45:43.585Z"],["3831315","LSS-62021","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-22T14:46:07.008Z"],["3831316","LSS-61920","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Thank you both [~accountid:712020:7bfaad56-f8bf-45b0-b951-dfd37b5ed5c2] and [~accountid:712020:1d4eb168-65d8-4fe2-9240-3537fd827409].\n\nAll understood and agreed. I have a call with Osborne Clarke tomorrow at 11am to discuss the Liverpool warehouse arrangement and this Liverpool Airport parking agreement - will keep you updated.","2026-01-22T14:46:25.751Z"],["3831318","RS-1961","RS","mariia.nedosekova@bolt.eu","Mariia Nedosekova","I’ll be closing the ticket as we connected over Slack. The events were shared [+here+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1bj63fIZtJ2y_lKTxjSj2MFp_d8WpENPRadY9tqg2V0g/edit?gid=0#gid=0].\n\nPlease, let me know if you have any questions! ","2026-01-22T14:46:42.613Z"],["3831319","WD-22575","WD","kristiine.murd@bolt.eu","Kristiine Murd","Thank you [~accountid:712020:42c95fcc-665c-491a-9341-767b89230c32] \n[~accountid:5e5cecb04befbd0c96cab72a] the expected result in WD Supplier invoice is when in Telema coding field *07. Company* is marked {color:#bf2600}difference{color} {color:#bf2600}Entity{color} then the invoice receiver than in WD Supplier invoice line company *must* *match* with the Telema field *07. Company* .\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 16.42.08.png|width=2003,height=1023,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 16.42.08.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-22T14:47:27.307Z"],["3831321","XP-2317","XP","irina.lim@bolt.eu","Irina Rein","[~accountid:712020:3f46b943-bb22-4289-83f6-326f708a1f24] Should be resolved. Correct, [~accountid:712020:53be219b-8d47-4ba0-8cd1-a8b886503164] ?","2026-01-22T14:47:53.035Z"],["3831322","LSS-59403","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:0285a595-6608-4335-9a5a-60b50674c696] , status for these two agreements: \n\n# [Branding Agreement: Nordic Taxi och Gods Transport AB, CHK Logistik AB, Mian Transport AB |https://docs.google.com/document/d/1reo61pHzk3wGIzn-ryWouZ-BYJh0BZox/edit]\n## All done except for one pending confirmation from Axel. \n## Once approved - clean up comments and include date for signing (last page)\n## Send ticket to Legal Ops\n#  [DRAFT - Branding Agreement: Hekam AB .docx|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XFZeChuD9VR4YryeJY9wRDg5WI9DDgzF/edit] \n## Several questions to Axel outstanding. \n## Once approved - clean up (please see the 1 above if unsure re wordings). Axel has a general template as well if set up is to be amended (old agreements). \n## Once approved - clean up comments and include date for signing (last page)\n## Send ticket to Legal Ops\n\nPlease doublecheck corporate information / signatories with Alla bolag before processing for signatures. \n\nThank you!","2026-01-22T14:48:18.971Z"],["3831323","CCM-22301","CCM","alexandra.anastasiei@bolt.eu","Alexandra Anastasiei","[^Training Request Form.xlsx]","2026-01-22T14:49:10.233Z"],["3831325","LSS-59403","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:632d88e0748d1bfcb858128d] a few outstanding questions still: \n\n# [Branding Agreement: Nordic Taxi och Gods Transport AB, CHK Logistik AB, Mian Transport AB|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1reo61pHzk3wGIzn-ryWouZ-BYJh0BZox/edit]\n## One last question pending response. \n#  [DRAFT - Branding Agreement: Hekam AB .docx|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XFZeChuD9VR4YryeJY9wRDg5WI9DDgzF/edit]\n## Please see outstanding questions.\n\n[~accountid:712020:0285a595-6608-4335-9a5a-60b50674c696] will help finalize the agreements and assist with signature collection, once done!","2026-01-22T14:49:23.245Z"],["3831326","PFI-835566","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Do they mean this one: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5953141058?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5953141058?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-22T14:49:39.210Z"],["3831329","LSS-61592","LSS","catherine.stiff@bolt.eu","Cathy Stiff","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] response from Zandesk: \n\n“The Service Order remains unchanged, the updates will be reflected in the ZCA and DPA, and our legal team is currently working on them. As the renewal date is tomorrow, I kindly ask that you sign the Service Order today. I’ve attached it for your reference.”","2026-01-22T14:49:55.660Z"],["3831334","CCM-22301","CCM","alexandra.anastasiei@bolt.eu","Alexandra Anastasiei","Hi! We need to create MKA for TP Safety, because they struggle with the Business Critical elements of the quality score card. I will take care of the quiz itself (10-12 questions with multiple choice answers), and I need your help with creating it in TalentLMS, and of course, rolling it out. I was thinking of a 90% pass rate with 1 chance to retake it. Please let me know if you can help and what you think of my proposal. Thank you!\n\n","2026-01-22T14:50:49.329Z"],["3831335","RS-1967","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:5dbb027ba766000da47cf09d] , das.gov.py is a pre-approved domain:done:! ","2026-01-22T14:51:48.350Z"],["3831337","PAW-15095","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-22T14:51:59.048Z"],["3831338","L10N-29686","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project 