d team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29677](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29677)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T14:52:33.635Z"],["3831352","L10N-29716","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29637](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29637)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T14:52:36.161Z"],["3831353","DBRE-8487","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","A couple notes:\n\n# Buckets have replication to Stockholm region. \n# TiDB nightly sync restores from such buckets\n# TiDB restore tests restore from such buckets\n# Not sure if anything else is using them, would be good to ask rest of team\n\nFeel free to reach out if you have any questions.\n\n\n\n","2026-01-22T14:52:37.076Z"],["3831354","RLONE-93","RLONE","christian.johannessen@bolt.eu","Christian Ingdal Johannessen","Changed the deadline to 28. Feb. ","2026-01-22T14:52:41.247Z"],["3831355","FX-3694","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769093571997779]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@angela.gray>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3694] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-22T14:53:06.483Z"],["3831356","VERIFY-2286","VERIFY","andrei.balaban@bolt.eu","Andrei Balaban","[~accountid:63184a43b433b060db570f4b] have a link if this is still relevant","2026-01-22T14:53:26.133Z"],["3831360","RNTL-29426","RNTL","karolina.epifantseva@bolt.eu","Karolina Epifantseva","Closed, not testable","2026-01-22T14:54:29.044Z"],["3831361","RS-1966","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:5dbb027ba766000da47cf09d] , Section 3(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code is in the list of valid legal basis:done: ","2026-01-22T14:54:34.487Z"],["3831362","LSS-61592","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:e7c4988a-ccaf-44c1-8546-2d01d1217937] clear, we will send for signing \n\nwill they send to us word docs of DPA and MSA  tomorrow ? ","2026-01-22T14:54:49.955Z"],["3831363","VERIFY-2235","VERIFY","andrei.balaban@bolt.eu","Andrei Balaban","Let’s make an admin-panel page with the mapping.","2026-01-22T14:55:11.662Z"],["3831365","LSS-61592","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[^Bolt Operations OÜ_Renewal_Q-670898_V1 (1) (1).pdf]\n\nhi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] please send for signing asap \n\nWe need it to be signed tomorrow ","2026-01-22T14:56:07.002Z"],["3831366","PFI-837325","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThese two payments match the description provided:\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4040068459|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4040068459]\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4039938596|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4039938596]\n\nThey were made by the user with Bolt ID 107477351.","2026-01-22T14:56:07.763Z"],["3831368","LSS-61798","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:62567ec6a872710069210b83] !\n\n[^Registry card_change of directors_22.06.2022.pdf] \n\n[^Memorandum of Incorporation.pdf] \n\n[^17.07.2023 COR39 Certificate.pdf] \n\n[^Bolt Services ZA PTY Ltd_certificate of incorporation_07.03.2016.pdf]\n\n(we do not provide certified copies)\n\n[^orgchart (2).pdf] \n\nreach out in case you ve got any questions","2026-01-22T14:57:38.455Z"],["3831370","FPD-1503","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","First portfolio results have been generated. I still need to double check some numbers (if actuals for GMV are correct, if optimization logic was successful for every city included in the analysis), however I’ll share these first few points as they are quite interesting. A spreadsheet with consolidated numbers will be generated once this validation is done, and should be ready by tomorrow. \n\n----\n\nIn terms of portfolio uplift in GMV (EUR), the overall uplift tends to be quite good: on average it’s around 2.5% across all folds, usually varying between 2 and 2.8%. Note that here are considered only the cities which had models trained and did not fail the optimization process.\n\n!image-20260122-143330.png|width=781,alt=\"image-20260122-143330.png\"!\n\n----\n\nLooking at a city-level perspective, in most cities the suggested action would be to increase the demand spend (and thus reduce supply spend), which could be explained in some cases partially due to small effects of supply spend into the increase of OH / AP metric (e.g. low incrementality / poor experimental results).\n\nAmong the cities where the optimal uplift is achieved by an increase in supply spend are:\n\n* Abuja (9 folds)\n* Baku (8 folds)\n* Lviv (5 folds)\n* Kyiv (4 folds) - was mentioned in a thread as a city with supply constraints ([link|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C05E2MY5ED6/p1769077919541069?thread_ts=1768480341.030199&cid=C05E2MY5ED6])\n\nAdditionally, around 15% of all cities have a recommendation of dropping supply spend to virtually zero (allocate all of the incentives spend to demand), which might also be a side effect of poor supply incrementality (or even no supply incrementality at all!) in those cities. Among these are included:\n\n* Tartu (6 folds) \n* Madrid (5 folds)\n* Helsinki (5 folds)\n* Lisbon (4 folds)\n\n!image-20260122-143344.png|width=786,alt=\"image-20260122-143344.png\"!\n\n----\n\nAnd if we look at the distribution of GMV uplift over all cities for each fold, we see that they’re usually very close to 1.0% (median value), and seem to very rarely go above 5%.\n\n!image-20260122-143420.png|width=705,alt=\"image-20260122-143420.png\"!\n\nCities with high average GMV uplift across all folds:\n\n* Nuremberg (+24.6%)\n* Berlin (+15.5%)\n* Vilnius (+8.7%)","2026-01-22T14:58:48.175Z"],["3831371","PFI-837331","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-22T14:59:01.586Z"],["3831372","RS-1974","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] ,\n\nCan you please have a look at this case? Maybe someone from CS PC can support","2026-01-22T14:59:55.555Z"],["3831375","PFI-837071","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C019YPJMGSC/p1769068924955769|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C019YPJMGSC/p1769068924955769]","2026-01-22T15:00:51.489Z"],["3831378","LSS-62024","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-22T15:01:26.283Z"],["3831379","BDRIV-16","BDRIV","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","Went through some placements for 4695 cells. Will add one placement with 4695 and continue with 46120 {{2026-01-22}} \nAnd then we should have rough understanding how much volume cells will take.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1WfOtQKaPpArKsYtJD9uK0FUt6_Yu9--yf4hXsNnLPu4/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1WfOtQKaPpArKsYtJD9uK0FUt6_Yu9--yf4hXsNnLPu4/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T15:01:29.602Z"],["3831380","RS-1974","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","[~accountid:60bf49438f2cc1006972698a] , please make sure to seek support from the CS PC team. They are equipped with all the necessary knowledge ","2026-01-22T15:01:45.017Z"],["3831381","FPD-1564","FPD","matteo.casolari@bolt.eu","Matteo Casolari","I definitely agree, this is a good idea. \n\nI would move this ticket under the [Hyperparameter tuning optimization|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FPD-1540?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiMWM0YjQzMjg4N2I2NGZjYWFjMzI2MzIzMDI4MDU2ODIiLCJwIjoiaiJ9] epic tho, since [~accountid:712020:1534b9a1-6efe-4e9f-860e-39b8f161f56b]  was planning to tackle this at some point (prioritization of hyperparameter initiatives can be found in the [project board|https://www.figma.com/board/HgdoImAfbtFR6EMgA56w9D/IM-RH-2026-Goals?node-id=0-1&p=f&t=QpWwXsp5zjHUgWY8-0]).\n","2026-01-22T15:01:48.214Z"],["3831383","LSS-53316","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:637f67fb2acfad92d7b14abc] hi \n\nWe briefly discussed with [~accountid:712020:c190ab8b-4add-4eb3-bd6e-ab39d6c1cd0c] \n\nAs long as we use *“usually”* it should be ok and “up to” can be removed for the claims where we communicate savings. \n\n*“Save with Bolt Plus”* without numbers - also ok to be used","2026-01-22T15:01:59.957Z"],["3831384","LSS-61958","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hi [~accountid:62134a797580350068337097] , is this a new supplier, or do we already have an existing valid agreement and only need to update the commercial terms?\n\nI see one comment in the contract regarding the term - is this the only commercial deviation from our standard terms?","2026-01-22T15:02:02.903Z"],["3831386","PFI-836773","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Thanks for getting back to me, for external communication, you can frame it along the lines of:\n\n“Due to recent unusual account creation activity, this payment method is currently unavailable for business use. We recommend re-adding the card to the rider account instead.”","2026-01-22T15:02:37.348Z"],["3831388","LSS-61302","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:52c03b81-3e44-455b-a71d-0e9088f7c7ad], will this business customer be using the Ride Booker as well? Just trying to understand what kind of API is the customer talking about. Thank you! ","2026-01-22T15:03:24.090Z"],["3831389","FPD-1564","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","[~accountid:712020:3a4d1838-5610-4f85-a454-883aeab2b150] Thanks for the heads-up! I’ll move it to the other Epic then.","2026-01-22T15:03:27.612Z"],["3831390","PFI-834132","PFI","norbert.kato@bolt.eu","Norbert Kato","Hi [~accountid:557058:b2aaf2b9-4465-40fe-b31b-1711dbe61946] \nMy question is, as it is an error in the operation for the company, that somehow, can we delete this transaction from the client, as they do not have to pay a service fee? I've already switched off for the company, but the payment stucked in our system due to card issues.\nIt turned out, that it was enabled for the company by accident.😟 \n\nIt would be great, if we can delete this, as they manage to fix the card issue, our system will charge them, but it is not right.\nThe payment: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4003426449|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4003426449]Waiting for your feedback, as it is an urgent case!\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5989403477?filter=%7B%22limit%22[…]ffset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5989403477?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] ","2026-01-22T15:03:58.781Z"],["3831391","RS-1965","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:5dbb027ba766000da47cf09d] , this seems to be a legal matter, I can not support in this case. Please escalate to the legal team","2026-01-22T15:03:59.160Z"],["3831393","LSS-61751","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","Hey [~accountid:62134a797580350068337097] Quick nudge here. It would be great if we can get the information requested below. Thanks. ","2026-01-22T15:04:31.041Z"],["3831398","PC-4940","PC",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - PC-4939 has been resolved","2026-01-22T15:07:15.062Z"],["3831399","HS-29282","HS","kristin.runnel@bolt.eu","Kristin Runnel","sent back, new effective date needs to be agreed","2026-01-22T15:07:25.900Z"],["3831401","L10N-29722","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29677](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29677)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T15:07:40.195Z"],["3831402","HS-29293","HS","dieulinh.tran@bolt.eu","Diệu Linh Tran","[^02122025 (1).docx]\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 16.07.28.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T15:08:07.717Z"],["3831404","BD-2001","BD","agnes.kuus@bolt.eu","Agnes Kuus","h3. Testing data\n\nI created 2 orders in Prelive for testing, one with 3€ tip (incl VAT), other with 1€ tip (incl VAT):\n\n# [https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/168640275|https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/168640275]\n# [https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/168640272|https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/168640272]\n\n\n\nh3. Testing results\n\n(/)  For both orders *Invoicing Records* were correctly calculated with VAT for the Tip record types:\n\n* courierTip\n* aggregateCourierTip\n* deliveryFleetAggregateCourierTip \n\n\n\n(/)  For both orders the *Bolt to Eater invoices* were generated with correct VAT amounts:\n\n* Order [168640275|https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/168640275] - 1€ tip as separate line item, includes 20% VAT - [^168640275_Bolt_to_Eater_invoice.pdf] \n* Order [168640272|https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/168640272] - 3€ tip as separate line item, includes 20% VAT - [^168640272_Bolt_to_Eater_invoice.pdf] \n\n\n\n(/)  The weekly *aggregate* *Fleet to Bolt invoice* was also generated with correct VAT amount:\n\n* [^Fleet_to_Bolt_invoice.pdf] \n* The aggregate tip (sum of 3€ + 1€ courier tips) is on the second row (Бакшиш за куриера), includes 20% VAT.\n\n\n\n(/)  Emre validated the generated invoices with the Tax team and gave a green light for moving forward\n\n* Next step is to create a detailed launch plan and launch the VAT-liable tips for BG: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BD-2005|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BD-2005|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T15:08:18.235Z"],["3831405","PFI-836916","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\r\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-22T15:08:21.897Z"],["3831406","PFI-836912","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\r\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-22T15:08:24.058Z"],["3831407","CSXRD-63","CSXRD","david.tomes@bolt.eu","David Tomeš","h3. *Status update – Driver Coach rollout*\n\n*Current status*\n\n* The *Driver Coach experiment has been stopped* following cross-functional review (CX, CS, Analytics).\n* Based on experiment results and local feedback, we are *not proceeding with rollout in the current form*.\n\n*What we observed*\n\n* ~*64% of callback requests were untagged*, meaning drivers requested a callback without stating a clear reason.\n* A large share of calls were *accidental, exploratory, or low-value*, rather than driven by a real need for support.\n* Treatment markets saw *~17% higher support volume*, without clear evidence that this translated into a consistently better driver experience.\n* Retention signal (Activated → 7D Activity) was *small and uneven across markets*, and not strong enough to confidently rule out random variation.\n\n*Cost & value context*\n\n* Tested markets (TH, KE, NG, PL, UA; excl. PY):\n** Annualized profit impact: ~*€1.05M*\n** Estimated annual CS cost: ~*€90k*\n* While the value appears positive on paper, the *experience signal is weak*, and current design drives significant CS effort without clear benefit.\n\n*Conclusion*\n\n* From an experience and program perspective, the feature is *not ready to scale*.\n* The lack of intent capture makes it difficult to ensure callbacks are actually helping drivers.\n* Rolling out in this state would scale inefficiency and noise rather than proven value.\n\n*Next steps / dependencies*\n\n* Revisit the feature only if *basic intent friction* is introduced (e.g. requiring drivers to state a reason before requesting a callback).\n* Align with Product/Eng on whether such changes are feasible.\n* If the feature is reconsidered in the future, WFM will be looped in early to allow sufficient staffing lead time.","2026-01-22T15:08:41.684Z"],["3831413","LSS-61816","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:0c90413b-741f-4463-8f2a-012d18e770c7] ! May you please kindly tell me who from the legal team approved signature of this contract?","2026-01-22T15:09:43.888Z"],["3831414","RS-1972","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","[^9V-21 en-US.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T15:09:46.131Z"],["3831415","LSS-59845","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nThank you a lot — shared with Sentry.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-22T15:09:53.040Z"],["3831418","LSS-61816","LSS","ololade.olanipekun@bolt.eu","Ololade Olanipekun","Do you mean who approved the landlord signature or the actual contract?","2026-01-22T15:10:49.431Z"],["3831420","LSS-61545","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:63b59fb7d3aeefa40543d2e5] ! Yes, it was executed!\n\n[^MoU  CGM & BOLT - After Privacy Review v.2.pdf] ","2026-01-22T15:11:15.367Z"],["3831422","XP-1384","XP","pavel.kiper@bolt.eu","Pavel Kiper","[~accountid:61b0698cc75da800725c5dce] what’s the status here?","2026-01-22T15:11:31.058Z"],["3831423","PFI-837333","PFI","success.igbinosa@bolt-outsource.eu","Success Igbinosa","!31K.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T15:11:33.601Z"],["3831424","LSS-61816","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","The terms of the contract.\n\nThank you","2026-01-22T15:11:49.452Z"],["3831428","LSS-62019","LSS","alina.solomka@bolt.eu","Alina Solomka","ln email I have explained to partner about refunds:\n\n\n\nPar *refunds*: mēs kā platforma strādājam ar klientiem arī caur klientu atbalstu, kas uzreiz izvērtē, vai refunds ir pamatots vai nē. Jūsu portālā būs redzami visi refunds gadījumi, un jums būs iespēja tiem nepiekrist. Šādos gadījumos mēs veiksim izskatīšanu un, ja nepieciešams, atgriezīsim jums naudu (payout notiek pirmdienās).","2026-01-22T15:12:32.242Z"],["3831430","LSS-61816","LSS","ololade.olanipekun@bolt.eu","Ololade Olanipekun","[~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] approved from the legal team. Do I add you to the approval ticket, if that will help","2026-01-22T15:13:05.914Z"],["3831431","LSS-61975","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] if you know, could you please share some context for this initiative and any cooperation with Drooniseire Ukrainasse MTÜ we have at Bolt? Have batteries been sent to Ukraine already, per the same process? Thank you! ","2026-01-22T15:13:14.251Z"],["3831432","PFI-836873","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment has now been completed and the shadow credit in the user’s Bolt balance cleared. The reserved amount should be return to the customer within 14 days or more depending on their bank internal processes.","2026-01-22T15:13:27.365Z"],["3831438","PAW-15001","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-admin-panel, pint-product-admin-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-22T15:14:30.173Z"],["3831439","HS-29197","HS","leonora.lukoviczki@bolt.eu","Leonóra Lukoviczki","Hey there [~accountid:712020:dc4824f4-a6bc-41f2-af89-59d155dc0cc8] \n\nThe employee says now, that he would like to get the letter also in English please? The same, but in English too.\n\nThank you so much, ","2026-01-22T15:14:42.891Z"],["3831441","PFI-837334","PFI","christian.barrios@bolt.eu","Christian Junior Barrios Brassel","!Uniflex_2210120.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T15:15:10.661Z"],["3831442","LSS-61655","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:0285a595-6608-4335-9a5a-60b50674c696] re-assigning to you during my vacation, will take it back after this 🙂 Just for you to be able to collate all information during this time (fee estimates, decisions etc). Thanks a lot!","2026-01-22T15:15:13.340Z"],["3831446","DO-5816","DO","monika.goralczyk@bolt.eu","Monika Góralczyk","Ok, so I created a new cluster (you can see my setup in the screenshots)\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 16.08.44.png|width=1000,height=632,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 16.08.44.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 16.08.36.png|width=1124,height=840,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 16.08.36.png\"!\n\nBut now it seems that I have permission issues to run queries (which wasn’t the case before):\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 16.12.55.png|width=1396,height=289,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 16.12.55.png\"!\n\nCan you help me with that?","2026-01-22T15:16:12.332Z"],["3831450","FIS-4219","FIS","iurii.shikanov@bolt.eu","Yurii Shykanov","[~accountid:712020:8b906c76-e5e5-4982-a2e9-3b1fc964a2e7] please, help with the mapping. ","2026-01-22T15:16:35.389Z"],["3831451","LSS-57822","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","A confirmação explícita por parte do estafeta pode não evitar a fraude","2026-01-22T15:16:48.466Z"],["3831453","RS-1972","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:5dbb027ba766000da47cf09d] , I couldn’t find an approved legal basis. Escalating to Privacy","2026-01-22T15:16:51.375Z"],["3831456","LSS-62027","LSS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] ,\n\nWe need your support with the legal basis🙏 ","2026-01-22T15:17:30.988Z"],["3831463","WD-22575","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] ,\ncan you please confirm the logic based on which we are assigning the company value on the line level data of the invoice? \n\n[~accountid:623c7881562ab90069f8f044] [~accountid:712020:42c95fcc-665c-491a-9341-767b89230c32] can you please clarify in more details:\nWhat you actually need integration to do?\nWhy you need it to do that?\nIn which cases you need it to do that?\n\nThe reason I’m asking is because this seems to be a integration change, any change we do will have an impact to the whole integration. Just trying to clarify the scope and problem statement. ","2026-01-22T15:18:10.743Z"],["3831464","DPX-3794","DPX","aleh.zibrou@bolt.eu","Aleh Zibrou","Hey [~accountid:624b0ac545ece00069cc6017] we shouldn’t have the smaller save button at all\nconfirm means save\nback means cancel changes","2026-01-22T15:18:26.734Z"],["3831465","LSS-53316","LSS","olga.kulitska@bolt.eu","Olha Khmelenko","thanks","2026-01-22T15:18:33.708Z"],["3831466","PFI-837341","PFI","wannapat.huang@bolt-outsource.eu","Wannapat Huang","!image-20260122-151101.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260122-151105.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260122-151110.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T15:18:46.740Z"],["3831467","RS-1945","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","She confirmed that we can resolve this ticket for now","2026-01-22T15:19:01.756Z"],["3831468","FIS-4219","FIS","iurii.shikanov@bolt.eu","Yurii Shykanov","[^KPD_2025_struktura.xlsx]\n\nList of possible codes from the gov site","2026-01-22T15:19:05.602Z"],["3831470","DELIVERY-1125","DELIVERY","aleh.zibrou@bolt.eu","Aleh Zibrou","Hey [~accountid:61a78f31ebce470067821b11] , did you find anything new, eg. specific edge cases I could do a design for? Or all fine","2026-01-22T15:20:11.207Z"],["3831475","LSS-61132","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","Hey [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] the agreement that is requested in the ticket above is a Fleet Agreement. We need not use a [+*Fleet Deal Agreement Template*+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/16d3vGGsnkwAbyqrY6dzQcos_GPR4JKZV/edit]. Let me know in case you have any further questions. ","2026-01-22T15:21:42.782Z"],["3831477","CSP-459","CSP","oleg.alieksieienko@bolt.eu","Oleg Alieksieienko","26W03: We started building Admin panel for have understandable UI for “number of interactions” per issues key. Right now it is hardcoded in remote config. And almost impossible to find it. ","2026-01-22T15:21:57.927Z"],["3831478","PTWS-2135","PTWS","octavian.todor@bolt.eu","Octavian Todor","Worked together with [~accountid:611537e7eb7aef00696b29c1] and [~accountid:712020:6850b463-f3bb-4458-b00b-b094810b5bcd] to create this. We created in bolt3 a time off plan called *PRT Elections Day Paid Leave*. Only people team should be able to add time off for employees using this plan and it should not show up in self service. \n\nMax 2 days per year, as far as we understood from Bruna and it should be paid.\n\nWe did the following checks:\n\n* Bruna Miguel can only request up to 2 days off for Rita Neeves. If she tries to request 3, an error shows up\n* Time off plan doesn’t show up in self-service, only people team can request this type of absence\n\nWe might need to make it so that an attachment is necessary (not sure how to do this, I checked the Request Leave of Absence BP and I only found a validation for Estonia, so I am not sure if that is the way to go about it)\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 17.09.35.png|width=809,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 17.09.35.png\"!","2026-01-22T15:22:36.287Z"],["3831480","CSP-458","CSP","oleg.alieksieienko@bolt.eu","Oleg Alieksieienko","26W03: We have added A/B testing functionality to it. And aiming to start A/B delivery refund compensation threshold ","2026-01-22T15:23:01.273Z"],["3831481","CSP-457","CSP","oleg.alieksieienko@bolt.eu","Oleg Alieksieienko","26W03: The notebook almost ready PMs are testing it ","2026-01-22T15:23:40.912Z"],["3831483","RS-1947","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Thank you!","2026-01-22T15:23:46.319Z"],["3831486","SCM-1116","SCM","omar.masum@bolt.eu","Omar Faruk Masum","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] 1. Below items will order from China and MMPI initiated in WD by [~accountid:5e9a112618b8ed0c0f776390]. As soon as parts available in WD, I will create the order.\n\n|CASEE-1-R01|\n|CASEE-2-R01|\n|MATE-2-R00|\n|CASEE-5-R00|\n|CASEE-4-R00|\n\nBelow items will source from Estonia, third party website. Service desk ticket created and [~accountid:5fa01e19aea468006a8a298e] ordered the items except “Solder flux” as this item is out of stock.\n\nHi [~accountid:5fa01e19aea468006a8a298e] Please share with us the ETA for below items.\n\n|LED driver chip|[+https://ee.farnell.com/diodes-inc/ap3019aktr-g1/led-driver-boost-40-to-85deg-c/dp/3482890+|https://ee.farnell.com/diodes-inc/ap3019aktr-g1/led-driver-boost-40-to-85deg-c/dp/3482890]|\n|100nF capacitor|[+https://ee.farnell.com/murata/grm155r71h104ke14d/cap-0-1-f-50v-10-x7r-0402/dp/2611912+|https://ee.farnell.com/murata/grm155r71h104ke14d/cap-0-1-f-50v-10-x7r-0402/dp/2611912]|\n|Fine solder wick|[+https://ee.farnell.com/chemtronics/60-1-10/desoldering-braid-0-9mm-3-0m/dp/860670+|https://ee.farnell.com/chemtronics/60-1-10/desoldering-braid-0-9mm-3-0m/dp/860670]|\n|{color:#ff5630}Solder flux{color}|[{color:#ff5630}+https://ee.farnell.com/chip-quik/smd491-10m/flux-tack-rol0-10g-syringe/dp/4715894+{color}|https://ee.farnell.com/chip-quik/smd491-10m/flux-tack-rol0-10g-syringe/dp/4715894]|\n|fine ended tweezers|[+https://ee.farnell.com/erem/5sasl/tweezer-economic-115mm/dp/1014356+|https://ee.farnell.com/erem/5sasl/tweezer-economic-115mm/dp/1014356]|\n|solder|[+https://ee.farnell.com/weller/t0051388199/solder-96-5-3-0-5-217-deg-0-3mm/dp/2344645+|https://ee.farnell.com/weller/t0051388199/solder-96-5-3-0-5-217-deg-0-3mm/dp/2344645]|","2026-01-22T15:23:59.783Z"],["3831487","LSS-61302","LSS","gauchar.alibayeva@bolt.eu","Gauchar Alibayeva","Hi [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] , they might be using RB in the future, but API would be used only in regards to user management in BA.\n\n!Snímek obrazovky 2026-01-22 v 16.23.40.png|width=686,height=222,alt=\"Snímek obrazovky 2026-01-22 v 16.23.40.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-22T15:24:06.119Z"],["3831488","CSP-456","CSP","oleg.alieksieienko@bolt.eu","Oleg Alieksieienko","26W03: Design doc is ready, next week we will start development ","2026-01-22T15:24:17.548Z"],["3831489","RS-1962","RS","iryna.sahaidak@bolt.eu","Iryna Sahaidak","Hi [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] this is a data request from the law enforcement body (Police). This type of requests are outside of Legal’s responsibility. Previously, they were handled by Privacy team. Now our understanding is that you are handling law enforcement requests.","2026-01-22T15:24:32.776Z"],["3831490","DSR-2751","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:6001a723d364960139286c95] , could you please support with sending this one through? I have already zipped all the files [here|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jKRMTkKsx5bp5IiJ1tUuO4XN3vu2q2h7/view?usp=drive_link] and the response letter is [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ku87SDfCDy1a_s77izSnwXcamhisLy3aP4s1VH53v1k/edit?usp=drive_link]. ","2026-01-22T15:24:47.347Z"],["3831491","CSP-455","CSP","oleg.alieksieienko@bolt.eu","Oleg Alieksieienko","26W03: In development, initial PM already in draf hopefully next week we will have something ","2026-01-22T15:24:59.498Z"],["3831492","LSS-55348","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:63e354e3010d35637974a02c] just heads up that we’re reviewing your request. \n\nWill we share any personal data with supplier? If yes we need to enter into DPA even for trial period. \n\nAdditionally, we need to create infosec ticket and ask InfoSec to review the supplier. Please link the ticket if it was already created. ","2026-01-22T15:24:59.941Z"],["3831493","PC-4092","PC","alexey.efimov@bolt.eu","Alexey Efimov","This task is about extending TTL for tables: {{payment_request_log}} and {{notification}}. To do that we need agree which TTL is acceptable for our needs. Current TTL is 6 months.","2026-01-22T15:25:19.228Z"],["3831495","LSS-61975","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Hey [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] ! I did not encounter this before but please do involve me in case anything is needed from my side here to help this move forward 🙂 ","2026-01-22T15:25:31.849Z"],["3831496","LSS-54833","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:2f68ebec-bff7-4acf-a855-0eeaf1c88737], I have reviewed their input. There are just 2 points, and they are both more commercial than legal. I have left comments for you next to them. Let me know what you think! ","2026-01-22T15:25:52.947Z"],["3831497","LSS-61132","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Thanks [~accountid:712020:c190ab8b-4add-4eb3-bd6e-ab39d6c1cd0c] , sorry, I’m not sure to understand. What should be then the Fleet agreement as requested by Giovanni that you are referring to? My understanding from Giovanni is that he wants a Fleet deal agreement to be adaptd with the Fleet.\n\nThanks for your feedback!\n\nElisabetta","2026-01-22T15:25:57.095Z"],["3831498","LSS-62028","LSS","martin.paroll@bolt.eu","Martin Paroll","[^01_Bilingual Version  CTBC Bank Merchant Service Agreement (General).doc] _(429 kB)_","2026-01-22T15:25:58.671Z"],["3831499","CSP-387","CSP","oleg.alieksieienko@bolt.eu","Oleg Alieksieienko","26W03: Guardrails for routines are done. And initial test shown 13% escalation. We are waiting Multi-agent to have “rewriter” agent to be to rewrite the message and will test again","2026-01-22T15:26:05.829Z"],["3831500","LSS-62015","LSS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] ,\n\nThey have cited Articles 16 and 20 as well. Can you please check if they are also not valid?","2026-01-22T15:26:10.155Z"],["3831502","LSS-62028","LSS","martin.paroll@bolt.eu","Martin Paroll","[^02_Bilingual Version –Special Terms and Conditions for the Collection and Payment Service Platform.doc]\n\nSpecial terms failed to upload initially","2026-01-22T15:26:18.107Z"],["3831503","WFM-10090","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:637b64078fd2d2d5f12d4259]!\r\n\r\nAs the queue data is sent to Assembled from Beehive automatically, that means that one moment the queues are going to be restored to their original/current selection.\r\n\r\nAs a temporary solution for testing purposes (to see schedule difference) it was enough.\r\n\r\nHave a nice day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-22T15:26:40.254Z"],["3831504","CSP-378","CSP","oleg.alieksieienko@bolt.eu","Oleg Alieksieienko","26W03: Working on show “system promt in UI”. It is needed, to avoid any dublication in routine promt.","2026-01-22T15:27:05.469Z"],["3831505","LSS-61816","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","No need, thank you!\n\nHere is the signed contract [^Bolt BOLT LEASE AGREEMENT rev 30-12-2025 (tracked) (1) (699bc23d-4acb-41a4-9720-248445ce6bfd).pdf] ","2026-01-22T15:27:16.302Z"],["3831506","SRED-922","SRED","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","Updated","2026-01-22T15:27:28.652Z"],["3831508","PFI-835566","PFI","marius.poroseci@bolt-outsource.eu","Marius Poroseci","I will send them this one, and if it’s not the right one, I’ll come back with more details","2026-01-22T15:27:37.518Z"],["3831509","PC-4092","PC",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - PC-3010 has been resolved","2026-01-22T15:27:38.994Z"],["3831510","PC-3051","PC",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - PC-3010 has been resolved","2026-01-22T15:27:38.995Z"],["3831511","PC-4971","PC",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - PC-3010 has been resolved","2026-01-22T15:27:39.043Z"],["3831512","SRED-920","SRED","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","All SRED clusters updated.","2026-01-22T15:27:44.666Z"],["3831513","DPO-159","DPO","mengel.paula@bolt.eu","Paula Maria Mengel","[Test|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/tests/edit/14832]","2026-01-22T15:28:45.299Z"],["3831515","DPO-159","DPO","mengel.paula@bolt.eu","Paula Maria Mengel","[Employee ff|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/featureflags/edit/15007]","2026-01-22T15:29:33.169Z"],["3831516","GRACQ-436","GRACQ","borys.symonenko@bolt.eu","Borys Symonenko","From and to filters are now applied by default. {{From}} is set to {{now - 1h}}, {{To}} is set to {{now}}\n\n!image-20260122-153049.png|width=635,alt=\"image-20260122-153049.png\"!","2026-01-22T15:30:56.811Z"],["3831517","SREDESK-7452","SREDESK","henk.versluis@bolt.eu","Henk Versluis","Hi Arnold,\nI am requesting access to the datascience account (287845475429) to use Sagemaker and EC2 for model training.\n\nCould you please add me to the existing Okta group associated with the standard Data Science role: arn:aws:iam::287845475429:role/aws-reserved/[sso.amazonaws.com/eu-central-1/AWSReservedSSO_ENGDSToolsWorkflows287845475429_fae1caed51aecb6d|http://sso.amazonaws.com/eu-central-1/AWSReservedSSO_ENGDSToolsWorkflows287845475429_fae1caed51aecb6d]\n\nIf I need additional permissions at a later stage I will open a separate ticket for that.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-22T15:31:08.165Z"],["3831518","WEB-9954","WEB","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","[~accountid:712020:2bb94136-b4e4-463e-a0f6-8be773ff520f] \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 17.30.38.png|width=429,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 17.30.38.png\"!","2026-01-22T15:31:19.721Z"],["3831520","LSS-61302","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:52c03b81-3e44-455b-a71d-0e9088f7c7ad]! Thank you! Then I am a bit lost about what is the business customer referring to in her email.\n\nIn general the MSA replaces the Bolt Business T&Cs, and this is why T&Cs do not apply to the business customer once the MSA is signed.","2026-01-22T15:31:41.401Z"],["3831523","PFI-837348","PFI","mira-afina.gorskova@bolt-outsource.eu","Mira-Afina Gorskova","!0f3777e6-0dd5-4c38-81cf-47a76d96948f.png|thumbnail!\n\n!4a1f76ff-dc62-4b58-94f0-9d11e5891694.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T15:32:14.255Z"],["3831524","DSR-2751","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","Response and data sent out. ","2026-01-22T15:32:20.014Z"],["3831525","DELIVERY-1125","DELIVERY","aleh.zibrou@bolt.eu","Aleh Zibrou","[~accountid:624b0ac545ece00069cc6017] could you check the design?","2026-01-22T15:32:43.821Z"],["3831526","PAW-15100","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-22T15:32:45.486Z"],["3831528","LSS-61592","LSS","catherine.stiff@bolt.eu","Cathy Stiff","Updated ZCA\n\n[^Zendesk Customer Agreement with Bolt Operations OÜ - OFFLINE -  NEW -  Zendesk Customer Agreement - (England & Wales) AUGUST 2025 (696f64640f) (version 2).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T15:33:04.424Z"],["3831529","PFI-837353","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-22T15:33:10.240Z"],["3831530","PFI-837353","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:712020:3b323097-a7a7-4217-80f0-9db561b5900a] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-22T15:33:12.384Z"],["3831531","PFI-836805","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment has now been cancelled and the reversal should be completed within 14 days or more  according to user’s the bank internal processes.","2026-01-22T15:33:29.870Z"],["3831533","PFI-836706","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-22T15:34:36.157Z"],["3831535","TAXP-1790","TAXP","tiiu.albin@bolt.eu","Tiiu Albin","Link to Deloitte’s draft report [https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VADJL_ueBDxNrAOf4uRw1MCI3OmJBrvs/view?usp=sharing|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VADJL_ueBDxNrAOf4uRw1MCI3OmJBrvs/view?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T15:35:21.300Z"],["3831537","LSS-58970","LSS","thalemarie.bo@bolt.eu","Thale Marie Bø","[~accountid:619cad8cb43d5b006af304cc] the comment about average benchmarks was found here under “dependencies”: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jm0dNJmdboOfMTnhSk8Gun8olauVBhocgQOhAz6acKk/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jm0dNJmdboOfMTnhSk8Gun8olauVBhocgQOhAz6acKk/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\nI’d like to look at the UGC contracts and the contracts you mentioned that the drivers enter into, if you have them available? ","2026-01-22T15:35:25.911Z"],["3831538","LSS-62029","LSS","dovile.zykute@bolt.eu","Dovilė Zykutė","[^2 priedas_Pasiulymo forma Policijos departamentas.pdf] _(181 kB)_","2026-01-22T15:37:14.427Z"],["3831539","DSR-2999","DSR","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df],\n\nThank you for sharing the additional information (and thank you [~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] as well). As discussed on Slack, having reviewed the facts in detail, I agree that there is no evidence to support the rider’s allegations.\n\nOn that basis, I’ve prepared the attached response letter. Please let me know if you have any comments, and whether you’d like me to send this directly from the Legal team inbox, or if you’re already corresponding with the rider and would prefer to send it yourself.\n\nThank you!\n\n[^Letter to Mrs Sharon Channer - Bolt Services UK Limited - 22 January 2026.docx.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T15:37:30.998Z"],["3831547","WFM-10075","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:712020:8f5d63c5-8fe5-4ac9-8a6e-fd90ce9c04d7]!\r\n\r\nAll requested queues assigned.\r\n\r\nBest wishes,\r\nArtur","2026-01-22T15:38:11.485Z"],["3831548","PFI-837355","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-22T15:38:49.942Z"],["3831549","PFI-836676","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThis order [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2346120706/159?orderTryId=3018658975|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2346120706/159?orderTryId=3018658975] has been refunded to the customer’s Blik payment method. The debt comes instead from another order that was charge as a negative Bolt balance [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2346126454/159?orderTryId=3018666383|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2346126454/159?orderTryId=3018666383]. ","2026-01-22T15:38:51.278Z"],["3831553","LSS-54531","LSS","miroslava.gorejova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Gorejova","[~accountid:712020:68e3fab1-1f89-4afb-b02b-42fffee9a8c4] ","2026-01-22T15:39:59.177Z"],["3831555","WEB-9954","WEB","samuel.oyekeye@bolt.eu","Samuel Oluseyi Oyekeye","Hi [~accountid:63c11ab62a526608c5506c05] \nCan we get the ecoVadis logo in webp and also this image resized?\n\n\n!Sustainability-Media-36.webp|width=590,alt=\"Sustainability-Media-36.webp\"!","2026-01-22T15:40:17.512Z"],["3831559","GUM-50","GUM","octavian.moraru@bolt.eu","Octavian Moraru","Plan: create a lightweight Spark job in [http://github.com/bolteu/spark-main|http://github.com/bolteu/spark-main]  which reads a stopping forbidden model from S3 and writes into a delta lake table (probably in the {{ng_platform_spark}} schema).\n\nOnce productionalized, the “stopping forbidden” area generation job will be triggered by a DAG and will continue to produce a model on S3. Once finished, we will trigger the “store snapshot” job and pass the model version string generated by the “stopping forbidden” job as a parameter.\n\nI would postpone the implementation until the “stopping forbidden” model is updated to contain area ids.\n\ncc: [~accountid:5f646cbd2b42470070df1e3c] does this make sense?","2026-01-22T15:40:57.969Z"],["3831563","PAW-15096","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-alex-somai\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17275\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-22 15:43:01 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-22T15:43:02.124Z"],["3831565","FPD-1545","FPD","kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu","Kateryna Kolomiiets","PR with a fix for reactivation events for partners by DAE:\n[https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15491|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15491|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T15:44:06.617Z"],["3831566","MLC-3526","MLC","amal.bahar@bolt.eu","Amal Bahar","Final content for Hopp Plus: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rlcJW_094TkEXktpOvlk4O2mFumfhHO0NL5awGSuSvU/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rlcJW_094TkEXktpOvlk4O2mFumfhHO0NL5awGSuSvU/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link]  [~accountid:5fb225a6f2df6c00762b994d] ","2026-01-22T15:44:06.913Z"],["3831568","PC-4956","PC",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - PC-4898 has been resolved","2026-01-22T15:45:51.215Z"],["3831570","PC-4898","PC",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - PC-4956 has been resolved","2026-01-22T15:45:55.186Z"],["3831571","LSS-62029","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-22T15:46:06.670Z"],["3831574","PFI-836420","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nAcquirer reference number: 532415553558\n\nReference: iv_35kpjv10kkRSIuKdwh068T0rETFzcaal\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-22T15:46:42.684Z"],["3831575","LSS-61932","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hi [~accountid:612f31d89976c300693ebaf7]! \nThank you for the question. \n\n* Bolt Business General T&Cs for Denmark already include coupons as a payment method, so no concern here.\n* 4x27\n\nAs far as I recall, the intention of the business at the time we were negotiating the partnership with 4x27 was that rides provided to *Bolt’s business clients should be allocated only to Bolt-affiliated drivers.* This makes sense, as we put extra effort into acquiring these clients. The only exception is where Bolt specifically agrees that rides of certain business clients may be allocated to both Bolt- and 4x27-affiliated drivers. \n\nThe clause 5.3 in the Bolt–4x27 agreement states:\n\n*_Ride Allocation._* _The Parties agree that as long as drivers affiliated with Bolt and the_\n_Partner appear in the same category on the Bolt Platform, the Bolt Platform shall allocate_\n_rides to requesting passengers based solely on driver availability, ensuring equal_\n_opportunity for all drivers regardless of their affiliation to either Party’s dispatch center,_\n_and without enabling passengers to distinguish between them, provided the Partner offers_\n_the type of vehicle requested._ +_This rule does not apply, when a ride is requested by a_+\n+_passenger in a special group, like Bolt Business customer, or any other group that Bolt_+\n+_has, at any time during the Collaboration, informed the Partner to be treated differently_++.+\n\n\n\nI believe the same logic should apply to coupons - normally, *Bolt Business clients should use them only to pay for Bolt rides. Only exceptional business clients, pre-approved by the business team* and whose rides may be allocated to 4x27, *should be allowed to use coupons for 4x27 rides.* These would typically be only business clients where Bolt won the tender jointly with 4x27 (where 4x27 acts as a subcontractor, or in the future as part of a JV or consortium).\n\nThus, the questions are as follows:\n\n# Is my above understanding correct?\n# To my knowledge, none of Bolt’s business clients currently have access to 4x27 rides - only to Bolt rides. This may change if we win the PwC tender, where 4x27 is indicated as our subcontractor.\n# Can the Bolt Business team manually permit the use of coupons for 4x27 rides for specific business clients? If this is permitted and 4x27 is aware, I see no issue with adding coupons as an additional payment method for these exceptional business clients for 4x27 rides - if this is technically possible. Is it?\n\n[~accountid:712020:bc7bca9c-4d13-42b6-9684-04014a47f7aa] [~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14] please help to answer the above questions? 🙏  ","2026-01-22T15:46:52.815Z"],["3831578","LSS-62005","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5],\n\nI have reviewed the proposed IWG/Regus virtual office licence and I’m happy to proceed.\n\nThis is a standard Regus virtual office agreement and, from a legal risk perspective, it actually carries slightly lower risk than our previously approved physical office licences, as it does not involve any physical occupation or access rights.\n\nThe only point to flag is that the *agreement auto-renews unless notice is given* via the Regus portal. As this is a virtual office (and we won’t be physically present), it may be easier for it to fall off our radar, so it would be sensible to diarise the notice date if we don’t intend to renew.\n\nOtherwise, no issues from Legal and you can proceed. Please let me know if you are happy for me to send for signing 🙂 ","2026-01-22T15:47:52.620Z"],["3831580","PFI-836415","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-22T15:47:57.200Z"],["3831581","MVRT-1503","MVRT","amal.bahar@bolt.eu","Amal Bahar","[~accountid:63184a4556010c40d44804e6] thank you! \nWill need the Offer ID, comms date/time locked in as well once finalised please 🙏 ","2026-01-22T15:48:05.082Z"],["3831584","LSS-61975","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Thanks [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] ! ","2026-01-22T15:48:19.024Z"],["3831586","LSS-62031","LSS","juneszeid.djender@bolt.eu","Junes Zeid Djender","[^KamilSiegVehicleSalesContract.docx.pdf] _(196 kB)_","2026-01-22T15:48:50.596Z"],["3831587","LSS-61592","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:e7c4988a-ccaf-44c1-8546-2d01d1217937] since they agreed to mutual changes to MSA, DPA we would need to sign DPA in writing, as well. \n\nCurrently MSA just refers to DPA via link [https://www.zendesk.com/company/data-processing-agreement/|https://www.zendesk.com/company/data-processing-agreement/|smart-link] and it means that DPA can be updated by Zendesk  unilateraly. \n\nPlease request from them DPA, as well. Meanwhile, we’re checking updates to MSA. ","2026-01-22T15:48:59.999Z"],["3831588","LSS-61866","LSS","benjamin.walch@bolt.eu","Benjamin Walch","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] \nThe counterpart has informed me that he didnt receive any NDAs (and he ensured me that it wasnt in spam ).\n\nCan you please doublecheck the email and/or resend it?\n\nThanks","2026-01-22T15:50:15.506Z"],["3831589","LSS-61975","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hey [~accountid:6130eb6c2aa280006894f091] , could you please share some background - in what markets has this been done before?  Do we have any cooperation with Drooniseire Ukrainasse MTÜ on a global level? Do you know who the responsible person for this initiative is? ","2026-01-22T15:50:17.056Z"],["3831592","PFI-837361","PFI","muchchima.saengwerasiri@bolt-outsource.eu","Muchchima Saengwerasiri","!image-20260122-155046.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T15:51:54.363Z"],["3831593","PFI-835592","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba\r\n\r\n","2026-01-22T15:52:55.435Z"],["3831594","PFI-836383","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba\r\n\r\n","2026-01-22T15:52:57.877Z"],["3831595","PFI-835989","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt'