k with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba\r\n\r\n","2026-01-22T15:53:18.434Z"],["3831606","PFI-837362","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-22T15:53:33.407Z"],["3831608","LSS-31377","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Note to self:* I had a meeting with John and Daniel to discuss mediation approach. John is happy to attend the mediation meeting with me. They were both of the view that we should initially *offer nothing* for a settlement figure as our defence is so strong. I raised the risk of litigation costs outweighing a potential commercial settlement figure and they are aware of this. We decided to wait to hear from the claimant’s solicitors on next steps and then ask them to ascertain the amount they are claiming from us as our next move.","2026-01-22T15:55:28.042Z"],["3831609","LSS-62032","LSS","paolo.catani@bolt.eu","Paolo Catani","[^Bolt_Private Regular Confirmation_Filled_15-01-2026 .pdf] _(78 kB)_","2026-01-22T15:55:46.934Z"],["3831611","SCM-1116","SCM","kaarel.vandler@bolt.eu","Kaarel Vandler","[~accountid:712020:16f9a1bd-630a-44fc-acfd-57a270c13c42] this can be ordered instead if the initially proposed product is not available:\n[https://ee.farnell.com/chip-quik/smd291nl-10m/flux-tack-rel0-lead-free-10g-syringe/dp/4715892|https://ee.farnell.com/chip-quik/smd291nl-10m/flux-tack-rel0-lead-free-10g-syringe/dp/4715892|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T15:56:33.625Z"],["3831612","LSS-58970","LSS","teun.esveld@bolt.eu","Teun Esveld","Hey [~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] , I don’t to create confusion here. But quick question for NL: I’m setting up the Driver comms: do we see any reclassification risks? Or should I not consider that as it’s already review by global legal?","2026-01-22T15:57:57.720Z"],["3831615","FX-3694","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dmitrii Bokovikov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769097552498389]*{color}:\nI see that Tax reports are enabled only for Spain and Norway after this change [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3201] <@U04GMBA8DFG> do you remember why did we want to have this change?\n\nLinked messages:\n[no preview available]\n{quote}","2026-01-22T15:59:30.847Z"],["3831617","RDS-951","RDS","andreas.palm@bolt.eu","Andreas Palm","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] We should keep because, even when optional, we still occasionally gain verified users through it - and if fully removed the markets where identity verification is mandatory wouldn’t have the option anymore (unless we leave it only for such markets). We should just take in the plans to fix sometime in the near future.","2026-01-22T15:59:41.397Z"],["3831618","WD-22659","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Thanks [~accountid:63e354dd8978d7a4353ce08d] , I am closing this case now. ","2026-01-22T16:00:21.694Z"],["3831619","LSS-60863","LSS","barbara.duartecosta@bolt.eu","Bárbara Duarte Costa","Hello Catarina! They agree 🙂 Can you add it so we can move forward with signing?\n\nThanks!","2026-01-22T16:00:29.105Z"],["3831620","LSS-62005","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","Hey [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] , auto renewal is fine as we typically keep track of notice periods. Thanks!","2026-01-22T16:00:31.939Z"],["3831621","LSS-61866","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:bc7bca9c-4d13-42b6-9684-04014a47f7aa] !\n\nJust to reassure – I have sent the invitation to this email (see the screenshot below). Is that correct?\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 18.00.29.png|width=265,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 18.00.29.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 18.00.39.png|width=380,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 18.00.39.png\"!","2026-01-22T16:00:50.912Z"],["3831623","PFI-837364","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-22T16:01:05.830Z"],["3831625","PTWS-2135","PTWS","steve.white@bolt.eu","Steve White","{panel:bgColor=#e3fcef}\n*TESTING PASSED*\n{panel}\n\nTried to add more than 2 days over the year and was unable.","2026-01-22T16:01:45.916Z"],["3831627","LSS-61974","LSS","birgit.tohvrel@bolt.eu","Birgit Tohvrel","Hi [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a], \nThis can be sent for signing to following: \n\nBen Richards\n\nHead of Legal\n\n[ben.richards@complyadvantage.com|mailto:ben.richards@complyadvantage.com]","2026-01-22T16:02:51.802Z"],["3831629","LSS-62005","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Sounds good, thanks [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5]!\n\n*Legal Ops:* please can you kindly arrange the signing of the attached by Alex Wong on behalf of Bolt Operations UK Limited?\n\nThank you in advance 🙂 \n\n[^Reigate Virtual Office Agreement (c0996710-fc92-46ad-9ada-dd3c23cdd6a6).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-22T16:03:14.589Z"],["3831634","PFI-814703","PFI","aiga.gegere@bolt-outsource.eu","Aiga Gegere","Hello, team! Can we receive an update?","2026-01-22T16:04:34.390Z"],["3831636","FPD-1534","FPD","anastasia.serebryannikova@bolt.eu","Nastya Serebryannikova","Summary:\n\n* the configs for the spark tables into which the data will be ingested are stored here: [https://github.com/bolteu/change-data-capture/blob/master/src/ingestion_config/ng/s3/financial_planning_input_based_model.json|https://github.com/bolteu/change-data-capture/blob/master/src/ingestion_config/ng/s3/financial_planning_input_based_model.json|smart-link] \n** ingestion is configured to happen every 2 hours\n* the data that needs to be ingested will be placed into the {{presto-ingestion}} folder in our s3 bucket:\n** {{s3://bolt-datascience-financial-modeling/LIVE/presto-ingestion/fp-ibm-rh-cycle-metadata/}}\n** {{s3://bolt-datascience-financial-modeling/LIVE/presto-ingestion/fp-ibm-rh-city-dataset-metadata/}}\n** {{s3://bolt-datascience-financial-modeling/LIVE/presto-ingestion/fp-ibm-rh-scenario-metrics-forecast/}}\n* {{presto-ingestion}} folder has been chosen (despite its confusing name) because it already had all the necessary configurations for the ingestion","2026-01-22T16:06:57.046Z"],["3831638","FX-3694","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Carlo Leone Fanton [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769098030022909]*{color}:\n<@U02DHFUNR4J> it's an open thread with billing, they are making sure reports are expected and should give green light for enabling in other countries in this month\n• [previous|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0576CT9MQD/p1762935863075279] support request\n• [request/main thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1767098785549429] in billing\n\nLinked messages:\n[November 12th, 2025 12:24 AM] alina.sovtan: Hi Team, up until recently each fleet in Slovak market had a \"tax report\" subsection in the FOP (in the invoice section). It seems that this section has disappeared (screenshot, one section is missing). Could this be turned on again? :pray::skin-tone-3:\n\n[December 30th, 2025 4:46 AM] carlo.fanton: hello, about [this|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0576CT9MQD/p1762935863075279] topic: an increasing number of markets are requesting to have tax report available.\nCan we turn it on?\n{quote}","2026-01-22T16:07:25.072Z"],["3831639","LSS-61415","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hello [~accountid:6052892160d39e006f72f166], en tant que centrale de réservation, nous sommes conformes à toutes les obligations légales relatives à la vérification des documents des exploitants VTC qui réalisent des prestations de transport. Le Code des transports ne nous impose pas de vérifier les éventuelles dérogations, souvent nominatives, qui relèvent de la responsabilité des conducteurs ou exploitants eux-mêmes.\n\nDans ce contexte, pourrais-tu demander au chauffeur de nous transmettre la dérogation qui semble lui être applicable ?\n\nÀ réception, nous pourrons analyser cette dérogation, en particulier si elle est nominative ou non. Cela nous permettra d’évaluer la possibilité d’envisager son application plus large à d’autres véhicules rattachés à cette préfecture.\n\ncc. [~accountid:712020:cf457436-e17c-4575-8d48-f2b9135ccc82] [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] ","2026-01-22T16:07:26.524Z"],["3831646","LSS-56945","LSS","thalemarie.bo@bolt.eu","Thale Marie Bø","[~accountid:712020:1d87c9ca-9bd8-46e5-b8f3-21ed693b4ca6] So it is not possible to find any data about the scooter that could indicate whether a malfunction actually happened, and we have no evidence from his side about the damages he suffered? \n\nAdding the privacy team since I see that he is requesting his personal information from us. ","2026-01-22T16:10:47.413Z"],["3831649","PAW-15103","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-22T16:11:12.710Z"],["3831651","WDFT-3546","WDFT","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/OYJAuwE|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/OYJAuwE|smart-link] \n\nDocumentation in detail on this process \n\n\n\ncc: [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] , [~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] ","2026-01-22T16:12:09.861Z"],["3831655","FX-3694","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dmitrii Bokovikov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769098430326919]*{color}:\nThank you!\n{quote}","2026-01-22T16:14:03.301Z"],["3831656","FX-3694","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Carlo Leone Fanton [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769098403733069]*{color}:\nabout the change of the dyn cfg: initially there was a *blacklist* config.\nbut then we should have turned on only for spain, so it made sense to have a *whitelist* config, adding only spain (instead of excluding every country except spain)\n{quote}","2026-01-22T16:14:09.811Z"],["3831658","LSS-62035","LSS","paolo.catani@bolt.eu","Paolo Catani","[^BOLT_Audit Confirm Request_12.31.2025_Filled.pdf] _(230 kB)_","2026-01-22T16:14:46.783Z"],["3831659","LSS-58953","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey team,\n\nThis hearing took place today and Dr. Thomas Bugeja already gave us feedback:\n\n\n\n_“Hi Catarina_\n\n_Sitting was done earlier today._\n\n _The Court took long to call the case, as there was an earlier compilation of evidence before our case._\n\n_Everything went well – we explained the connection between the Rider platform info and the rest of the rides, and connected them through the unique user ID._ \n\n_Cross-examination was reserved but will probably not happen.”_\n\n\n\nHaving this in consideration, it seems that no additional court attendances will be required from our end, reason why I will now close this ticket.\n\nIf we receive another summons related to this case, please write here and I will reopen the ticket.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-22T16:14:51.798Z"],["3831660","DPX-3536","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","[~accountid:712020:3408d64a-d0d3-407f-aa6a-b3114d0b6178] , unfortunately, not. I was going over the new designs and took all the new strings from there.\n\nI will need to request this one separately\n\n\n\nI assume it can still be: “Dispute a refund”, not “Dispute a Refund”, as previously “deduction” was in lower-case as well","2026-01-22T16:15:59.527Z"],["3831663","PRIV-513","PRIV","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}\n*SPECIFIC REGISTRATION REQUIREMENTS*\n{panel}\n\n+*DPO*+\n\n* Must be registered on the “Electronic Registry of Data Protection Officers” (DPO Registry), as maintained by the Commissioner for the Right to Information and Protection of Personal Data (on its [website|https://idp.al/en/eng/]).\n* Information to include: *Name*, identity of *controller*, *contact* details (email address and phone number), place of work (business *address*), and *training / certification* records (what precisely this entails is unclear (?) )\n** NB. Secondary data will also be sourced from other national registries (e.g., civil status, commercial registry, and registry of nonprofit organisations).\n* Data subjects have read-only access (i.e., they can only see limited data online).\n* It appears that we need to send the details to the Commissioner, who will then upload them to the database.\n** Apparently this is via an online portal. Might be [here|https://idp.al/en/obligation-to-inform/], but unclear. May not actually have been rolled-out yet; just approved (?) \n** This may need to include a DPO appointment pack (e.g., board decision).\n* There does not appear to be a specific deadline. As such, we should do so before the driver funnel opens.\n* *Conclusion*: When the time comes, local counsel / DPO input may be needed here.\n** External counsel: “_The decision itself does not specify go-live timing or the filing procedure for companies. Those are expected to be further defined by the IDPC._”\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n*Decision No. 347, dated 19.6.2025*\n\n*_III._* _RENMDHP contains data on the Data Protection Officers (hereinafter “NMDHP”) designated by controllers and processors._\n\n_…_\n\n*_IV._* _The data contained in RENMDHP are divided into primary data and secondary data, as follows:_\n\n# *_Primary data are:_*\n_a) data relating to the NMDHP;_\n_b) email address;_\n_c) address where the activity is carried out;_\n_ç) contact number;_\n_d) data relating to the controllers/processors in which the NMDHP has been designated;_\n_dh) trainings and certificates of the NMDHP in the field of personal data protection._\n# *_Secondary data are_* _those data obtained through interoperability with state databases, as follows:_\n_a)_ *_From the National Civil Status Register_*_, it obtains the following data:_\n_i. first name and surname of the NMDHP;_\n_ii. personal number of the NMDHP;_\n_b)_ *_From the Commercial Register of the National Business Centre (QKB)_*_, it obtains the following data:_\n_i. NIPT (tax identification number) of the controller/processor;_\n_ii. official email address of the controller/processor;_\n_iii. address of the controller/processor;_\n_iv. telephone number of the controller/processor;_\n_c)_ *_From the National Electronic Register of Non-Profit Organisations_*_, it obtains the following data:_\n_i. identification data of the non-profit organisation;_\n_ii. official email address of the controller/processor;_\n_iii. address of the controller/processor;_\n_iv. telephone number of the controller/processor._\n\n*_V._* _The provider of information for RENMDHP is KDIMDHP._\n{panel}\n\n+*Representative*+\n\n* Apparently this notification can be completed online via the e-Albania Portal, or by printing and sending a notification form to the IDPC.\n** NB. It seems that there is an official form to declare the controller’s details, including local representative. Perhaps the form is [here|https://idp.al/en/obligation-to-inform/#:~:text=%E2%80%9CManually%E2%80%9D,of%20Controlling%20Subjects%20(in%20Albanian)] (?) \n* *Conclusion*: We may also need local counsel help here.","2026-01-22T16:17:22.326Z"],["3831664","BP-13504","BP","raman.zhyshkevich@bolt.eu","Raman Zhyshkevich","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101700?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101700?created=true|smart-link]  ","2026-01-22T16:17:30.678Z"],["3831665","DPM-2355","DPM","razvan.nastase@bolt.eu","Răzvan Năstase","Will not do for the moment. We can revise this decision when we will decide on how to handle Nutritional Data for all providers.","2026-01-22T16:17:41.909Z"],["3831667","LSS-62036","LSS","samuel.ojo@bolt.eu","Samuel Ojo","[^2020.07.30 VAT certificate (1).pdf] _(469 kB)_","2026-01-22T16:19:09.498Z"],["3831668","PFI-829943","PFI","tamara.baptiste@bolt.eu","Tamara Latia Baptiste","[~accountid:5f896b8ee357dd006e937d7b] I am just following up on [~accountid:712020:1f6c1fe9-0a65-49ae-b40f-fa69270b3167] and [~accountid:5ee35a7d1c63760ab025cb47]'s request. We do not have the ability to download the ‘Proof of Payout’ documents, and the driver is growing impatient.","2026-01-22T16:19:26.310Z"],["3831673","BDB-1528","BDB","sandra.bergstrom@bolt.eu","Sandra Bergström","Hey [~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79], sorry for the silence here. The team is checking whether we can use the SDG name and likeness without permission. We might need to include an additional disclaimer. I’ll keep you posted. In the meantime, I’ve added the assets to the media plan in columns X and Y.","2026-01-22T16:20:28.408Z"],["3831675","LSS-62037","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","[^20260122 Resolution in writting .pdf] _(59 kB)_","2026-01-22T16:21:21.812Z"],["3831677","LSS-61075","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Raised ticket for signature collection in the PoA: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LSS/queues/issue/LSS-62037|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LSS/queues/issue/LSS-62037|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T16:21:53.830Z"],["3831678","L10N-29493","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.174Z"],["3831679","L10N-29478","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.195Z"],["3831680","L10N-29474","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.254Z"],["3831681","L10N-29477","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.262Z"],["3831682","L10N-29494","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.284Z"],["3831683","L10N-29488","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.289Z"],["3831684","L10N-29495","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.295Z"],["3831685","L10N-29484","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.330Z"],["3831686","L10N-29492","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.398Z"],["3831687","L10N-29483","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.399Z"],["3831688","L10N-29475","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.420Z"],["3831689","L10N-29497","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.418Z"],["3831690","L10N-29498","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.476Z"],["3831691","L10N-29496","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.545Z"],["3831692","L10N-29476","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.657Z"],["3831693","L10N-29485","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-22T16:21:59.695Z"],["3831695","LSS-59929","LSS","alistair.blaza@bolt.eu","Alistair Blaza","Hi we are still waiting for CAIXA to come back to us. Will let you know once they have. Thanks.","2026-01-22T16:22:48.845Z"],["3831696","PFI-834210","PFI","sofija.danilevica@bolt.eu","Sofija Daņileviča","Replied privately. Please use clean link to the look [+https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/23126+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/23126], issue was solved by removing Total orders >0 filter as there are transactions which are not linked to any order. \nThe blank line shown on the reporters screenshot are totals from the csv file, which were not excluded. Totals row doesn’t have a country value, so it shows up as blank. \n\nLet me know if solution works for you.","2026-01-22T16:25:19.001Z"],["3831697","FC-568","FC","mirjam.arrak@bolt.eu","Mirjam Arrak","Process not changing starting January 2026 actuals. CS concerned about accuracy.","2026-01-22T16:25:21.038Z"],["3831698","PFI-837380","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-22T16:26:39.311Z"],["3831699","PFI-837380","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:712020:4d6f2e98-6f14-4b28-83df-3e157e011e10] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-22T16:26:40.763Z"],["3831700","RDS-1179","RDS","dmitry.lazarev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Lazarev","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-27589|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-27589|smart-link] ","2026-01-22T16:26:41.199Z"],["3831702","LSS-61958","LSS","aleksandr.parshikov@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Parshikov","Hi [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] ! Yes","2026-01-22T16:27:03.763Z"],["3831703","DO-5816","DO","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","[~accountid:712020:d76d4a7a-0daa-4508-b73c-866e2f1cfc87] please refer to the doc again, we suggest using `dev_first_last_spark` now. Although, you can request access to the dbt_first_last_spark via unified auth in admin panel.","2026-01-22T16:27:36.539Z"],["3831704","LSS-60177","LSS","thalemarie.bo@bolt.eu","Thale Marie Bø","[~accountid:63dba2fb1b13d42998e22e00] any objections? Otherwise I will go ahead and close the ticket. ","2026-01-22T16:27:46.111Z"],["3831705","LSS-61866","LSS","benjamin.walch@bolt.eu","Benjamin Walch","That is the correct mail - Let me ask him to double check in spam etc.\n\nDo you have a link that I can share with him as well?","2026-01-22T16:27:47.103Z"],["3831706","LSS-58970","LSS","sandra.bergstrom@bolt.eu","Sandra Bergström","Thanks [~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3]. I believe that refers to the metrics outlined in [this|https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1cB7UTqgBJOj5KQymYEN2Xx1NGMtVT42-ObuHtriWdyo/edit?slide=id.g30dd3bd9a62_0_1241#slide=id.g30dd3bd9a62_0_1241] deck.\n\nYou can find an example of the UGC contract [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1j1wbTnFpHQ8tDjPYnQMW9t_NZHTx4ALV?ths=true] — there shouldn’t be anything unusual, as this template comes from the Legal Central team.\n\nI’m also sharing an example of the driver contract [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1YVBHfmvqnS2douzvRsVj_eZYpTfMqVKq/edit], which has already been approved internally as well.","2026-01-22T16:27:51.477Z"],["3831708","FDBT-4827","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-22T16:28:03.486Z"],["3831709","LSS-61866","LSS","benjamin.walch@bolt.eu","Benjamin Walch","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-22T16:28:07.005Z"],["3831711","PFI-837381","PFI","vidyur.trehan@bolt.eu","Vidyur Trehan","!IMG_5644.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_5645.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T16:29:00.338Z"],["3831712","LSS-59827","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Hi [~accountid:5d9c300987dd6f0dcb4d2b58] \n\nI’ve attached an updated version of the agreement [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VGAwQk1nxubHOLZEti0UeDFAkd63VwWW/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=114805727268611303315&rtpof=true&sd=true] (clauses 6 and 7 have been amended).\n\n*In answer to your questions:*\n\n* ✅ _Does driver employment status affect Boost?_\nYes — drivers employed by the fleet will not be eligible for Bolt Boost.  This is explicitly reflected in the agreement. \n* ✅ _Can we require employed drivers only?_\nYes — the agreement requires Abbis to engage all drivers as employees and confirms they’re responsible for all related obligations (e.g. PAYE, pensions, compliance).\n\n*Additional protections added:*\n\n* A warranty confirming the employment structure\n* A TUPE clause and indemnity to protect Bolt from any claims that drivers were employed by Bolt or should transfer if the fleet is replaced.\n\nPlease review the updated agreement in full and let me know if you are happy with it.  Please note that you must complete the commencement date at the top of the agreement before signature - the 8 week pilot will run from that date. \n\n\nThanks","2026-01-22T16:29:38.842Z"],["3831713","WFM-10077","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571856|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571856] \n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601784|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601784] ","2026-01-22T16:30:45.675Z"],["3831714","LSS-61300","LSS","thalemarie.bo@bolt.eu","Thale Marie Bø","[~accountid:712020:156f9ae9-89c5-45e2-aa47-046973fdf898] Could you confirm that your team is aware of this case already, and that the insurance firm has notified you that this specific law firm will be representing Bolt?\n\n\nIn that case I will send the PoA for signature.","2026-01-22T16:30:51.355Z"],["3831715","PFI-833026","PFI","martin.barrail@bolt.eu","Martín Nicolas Barrail Baez","[~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e] Hi! what customer need it’s a receipt of the payment made, not a payment match. Can we move forward with this?","2026-01-22T16:31:36.052Z"],["3831716","WFM-10077","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","queue added","2026-01-22T16:32:14.120Z"],["3831719","PFI-827199","PFI","martin.barrail@bolt.eu","Martín Nicolas Barrail Baez","Hey team, it depends on us to move forward (or not) in this request in order to have this T1+ customer onboard again. Tks\n[~accountid:610279973900e60070a3495c] [~accountid:712020:3d61a90f-075b-45b7-9c84-a1bd1d8b0166] ","2026-01-22T16:32:54.502Z"],["3831720","PAW-15105","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-22T16:33:19.611Z"],["3831721","WFM-10084","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","country access req> [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541836|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541836] approved \n\nrole already there","2026-01-22T16:34:03.735Z"],["3831722","LSS-61874","LSS","thalemarie.bo@bolt.eu","Thale Marie Bø","Hi [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] , I think it might be easier to ask [~accountid:616e6953e79ff6006f20aefa] for the written request from the Norwegian Road Administration with the information you need. ","2026-01-22T16:35:10.523Z"],["3831724","PFI-827205","PFI","martin.barrail@bolt.eu","Martín Nicolas Barrail Baez","[~accountid:712020:3d61a90f-075b-45b7-9c84-a1bd1d8b0166] pls I need a support here\n[~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] pls set the status in Pending","2026-01-22T16:36:00.941Z"],["3831727","L10N-29729","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29723](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29723)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T16:37:10.357Z"],["38