,"Declan Giles","Hi [~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] thanks for your message. Yes our team are aware of this case already. Also the insurance company notified us that this law firm will be representing Bolt. Thanks","2026-01-22T16:39:55.928Z"],["3831748","SAI-1429","SAI","anton.belski@bolt.eu","Anton Belski","Random idea for the routine tool - create a unit test from the live chat conversation.\nLet me know what you think. I can create a ticket for that\n\np.s.\nLOVE the live chat :newgreenheart:","2026-01-22T16:40:27.258Z"],["3831749","SAI-1429","SAI",null,"Slack","[Anton Belski|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:de49345c-1803-4c3b-a519-8499b60153fe] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09HK2JA6GM/p1769099876903289?thread_ts=1769099876.903289&cid=C09HK2JA6GM|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09HK2JA6GM/p1769099876903289?thread_ts=1769099876.903289&cid=C09HK2JA6GM|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-22T16:40:28.182Z"],["3831750","SAI-1429","SAI","anton.lapin@bolt.eu","Anton Lapin","yeah, why not, feel free to create a task in the epic","2026-01-22T16:40:28.984Z"],["3831751","PFI-837390","PFI","dominika.wozniak@bolt-outsource.eu","Dominika Woźniak","[^Potwierdzenie_1769099351300.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-22T16:40:51.451Z"],["3831752","WFM-10077","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! Roles were added, queue was added as well; Please let me know if anything else is missing","2026-01-22T16:41:07.398Z"],["3831753","PFI-837392","PFI","darja.borkina@bolt-outsource.eu","Darja Borkina","!Screenshot_2026-01-22-15-00-50-962_com.bolt.deliveryclient.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T16:42:28.787Z"],["3831754","LSS-62038","LSS","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","As per comments on slack:\n\nHi [@rachel.sallnow|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U09P3L4283Y]\n\n* yes this is a topic I've been involved with previously, there is a humungous thread on it [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07R84XBR45/p1759934248423269?thread_ts=1754649029.929589&cid=C07R84XBR45].The key document for it was [this|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1l5pCPTzy7D60f04qFh3eNZ4H4vLoIEZYbjxKI8QL6BU/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.nzi8yychjk4z] - [@ieva.fowler|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U07C3TZRYBG] and I both gave a thumbs up to it, after a lot of back and forth. Have a quick look and just double check that the changes look the same. Re: risk profiles, we're mitigating this for Flex by saying it's a suggested price. Other solutions were deemed as being unhelpful and unwanted from the driver / rider experience.What's not clear on the post is what they are planning to do for Bolt Standard. I've just spent the last 15 minutes deciding whether there is any merit in going with different wording. One one hand, on the basis that the change in destination is optional, 'suggested price' works. On the other, it is very slightly unhelpful to have identical wording to Flex... but that's putting things under a microscope. On balance, it's probably OK to keep them the same.Subject to what you think, I'd suggest going back to them as follows, leveraging slightly on that you're \"new\", then I can follow up to say I think it is the same and nudge [@aleksei.sivkov|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/UBD80HY8J].\n\n_Hey_ [_@chidubem.nneji_|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U0441LCV9QS]\n\n* _Yes this looks good for Bolt Flex._\n** [_@michael.roberts_|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U02GWMHMNKH] [_@aleksei.sivkov_|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/UBD80HY8J]_, just to make sure we're all aligned, am I right in saying that this is following what was decided in_ [_this_|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1l5pCPTzy7D60f04qFh3eNZ4H4vLoIEZYbjxKI8QL6BU/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.nzi8yychjk4z] _doc?_\n* _What's the plan for Bolt Standard? To have the same wording / approach? If so, this is OK._","2026-01-22T16:43:42.871Z"],["3831755","LSS-62038","LSS","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","[~accountid:612f31d89976c300693ebaf7] and [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5] reverted on the channel confirming this was OK for Flex and Bolt Standard.","2026-01-22T16:44:27.210Z"],["3831760","L10N-29542","L10N","anna.cherentcova@bolt.eu","Anna Cherentcova","I just followed your hints :wink:","2026-01-22T16:46:46.490Z"],["3831763","LSS-61890","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Did you mean that the agreement with Volkswagen could be of an amount of over EUR 1M? Basically we don’t grant PoA for transaction threshold of such amount. Such PoA for sure cannot be general ones, then a board member (Ahto Kink) would sign the contract after CFO approval. \n\nReferring to the agreement (section 12) as a contact person you will not be entitled to make an order and conclude purchase agreement of the amount of >1m.  I would suggest to rephrase these section 12 then.","2026-01-22T16:48:44.291Z"],["3831765","LSS-58932","LSS","afonso.azevedo@bolt.eu","Afonso Varão de Azevedo","[~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] \nJust got a call from Targa, let go with the link.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-22T16:50:49.458Z"],["3831766","LSS-62039","LSS","robin.schneider@bolt.eu","Robin Schneider","[^Bolt Werbevereinbarung_ Frankfurt Fleet Noman Ahmad Naheed (2).pdf] _(127 kB)_","2026-01-22T16:51:23.658Z"],["3831767","LSS-61616","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Thanks a lot for sharing this document, [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d]  — very useful.\n\n[~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] [~accountid:624c3242f40798007059a081] [~accountid:6169660ebfa2c1006b56c18f] [~accountid:5d0c8f1621a5d30bc4e096a8] [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] : we’ve drafted a [letter |https://docs.google.com/document/d/1UMJmqVDMw0NO6lYNDzxbmfMCg6nv-IFXepVzkSr1t1A/edit?tab=t.0]to be sent to the Public Prosecutor, which will also be reviewed by external counsel. Before sharing it externally, could you please take a look and provide any comments or suggested amendments directly in the document, if needed?\n\nOnce we’ve incorporated your input, we’ll share the revised version with outside counsel. It would be great if you could provide your input *by EOW/Monday evening latest.*\n\nThank you!\n\nElisabetta \n\ncc: [~accountid:610a3ee66051c5006aeeeea1] ","2026-01-22T16:51:31.006Z"],["3831768","L10N-29765","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29723](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29723)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-22T16:52:27.042Z"],["3831769","BEE-3491","BEE","anton.lapin@bolt.eu","Anton Lapin","[~accountid:5ff4436491bb2e0108d1548d] ","2026-01-22T16:53:55.666Z"],["3831770","LSS-62040","LSS","robin.schneider@bolt.eu","Robin Schneider","[^Bolt Werbevereinbarung_ Frankfurt Fleet Reza Rajabi.pdf] _(127 kB)_","2026-01-22T16:54:11.773Z"],["3831774","PFI-837405","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^Bolt.pdf (7).pdf]","2026-01-22T16:56:16.874Z"],["3831775","LSS-62041","LSS","catalin.jitariu@bolt.eu","Cătălin-Ioan Jitariu","[^Annex no. 5 to lease agreement_Bolt Services RO S.R.L._SC Chimirex RO SRL_15.03.23.pdf] _(166 kB)_\n\n[^Annex 4 to lease agreement - Contract extension_Bolt Services RO S.R.L._KERMANY GRUP S.R.L._10.10.25.pdf] _(217 kB)_\n\n[^Kookoo act aditional 4.pdf] _(980 kB)_","2026-01-22T16:59:08.160Z"],["3831778","LSS-62042","LSS","robin.schneider@bolt.eu","Robin Schneider","[^Bolt Werbevereinbarung_ Frankfurt Fleet Oleksandr Kovalchuk.pdf] _(127 kB)_","2026-01-22T17:00:52.735Z"],["3831779","PFI-837364","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Rider needs to change details on invoice*\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\n*Invoice in Romania is missing a number*\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\n*Where to find the invoice*\nPlease use KB article to find the invoice: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003866399\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-22T17:00:54.374Z"],["3831780","PFI-837331","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Rider needs to change details on invoice*\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\n*Invoice in Romania is missing a number*\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\n*Where to find the invoice*\nPlease use KB article to find the invoice: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003866399\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-22T17:00:55.139Z"],["3831781","LSS-62041","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-22T17:01:42.540Z"],["3831783","LSS-62043","LSS","robin.schneider@bolt.eu","Robin Schneider","[^Bolt Werbevereinbarung_ Frankfurt Fleet Taregh Kazemy.pdf] _(127 kB)_","2026-01-22T17:02:55.860Z"],["3831792","PFI-835503","PFI","carolina.patricio@bolt.eu","Carolina Patrício","Hey [~accountid:557058:b2aaf2b9-4465-40fe-b31b-1711dbe61946] (long time no see 🥲),\n\nThanks for adding me to the loop. I believe [~accountid:712020:d77c5e6c-f92f-4d79-955d-9f88e6d0a883]  and [~accountid:5b7bea09d08e47445d6fd01e]  might be more helpful going forward, as I don’t work on these topics frequently anymore.\n\n[~accountid:610279973900e60070a3495c]  I’m not sure if you can help here — the problem communicated from FO is a bit confusing. They say that after creating a user in AT, Bolt generates a specific billing series, but then stops using it and creates a new series without properly closing the old one. I’ll add the text in Portuguese below to see if it makes more sense:\n{color:#ff5630}_Ao abrigo do utilizador criado para o efeito a Bolt cria séries de faturação em nome da Maratona de Surpresas. Quando cria novas séries e deixa de utilizar as anteriores deve encerrar essas séries comunicando o último documento emitido e o motivo do encerramento. Este procedimento não está a ser cumprido mantendo ativas séries que já não estão a ser utilizadas._{color}\n\n\nThanks in advance!!","2026-01-22T17:08:17.635Z"],["3831812","LSS-55858","LSS","tom.bishop@bolt.eu","Tom Bishop","Ok Sasha, no problem.\n\nIn any case, can we go ahead with the contract to remove the constraints? I’d like to ensure we’re good to go in that regard. We can also start with the existing setup - I have communicated that drivers will decrease until we expand to B4B","2026-01-22T17:17:24.869Z"],["3831814","BP-13497","BP","uladzislau.tsyrkunou@bolt.eu","Uladzislau Tsyrkunou","For PR\n\n!image-20260122-172012.png|width=395,alt=\"image-20260122-172012.png\"!","2026-01-22T17:20:25.607Z"],["3831816","HS-28825","HS","aire.vaigu@bolt.eu","Aire Vaigu","[~accountid:712020:6051a399-1d8d-4067-8ca4-4776ebcad004] - can you help, please? He doesn’t seem to be an employee in WD","2026-01-22T17:21:29.526Z"],["3831817","LSS-58363","LSS","anna.hultengard@bolt.eu","Anna Hultengård","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] and [~accountid:616ec4e4e79ff6006f259f57] I apologise for the delay - our team has also been dealing with a high influx of cases. I will take a look at this and get back to you as soon as possible. ","2026-01-22T17:21:41.455Z"],["3831819","PFI-837424","PFI","george.ghiveciu@bolt.eu","George-Mihai Ghiveciu","[^DOC-20260102-WA0031.-3 (3).pdf]","2026-01-22T17:30:16.966Z"],["3831824","PFI-836676","PFI","patrycja.florczuk@bolt-outsource.eu","Patrycja Florczuk","We have no possibility to issue a refund from the ride you provided. Can you please cancel his debt via system?","2026-01-22T17:33:33.517Z"],["3831826","LSS-61932","LSS","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","Thanks for the swift response [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] 🔥  - I’ll review this tomorrow 🙂","2026-01-22T17:34:49.904Z"],["3831828","LSS-60542","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Hi [~accountid:633ebe49140ba0bf651e341a] I’ve attached a draft letter before action [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NgUvFCGCu62y6C8T6hAzc9J-5V5Odm3ELSrq1Bjz9Cc/edit?usp=sharing].  Please review and fact check the letter, let me know if I have misrepresented anything and if you have any comments. Thanks ","2026-01-22T17:38:09.945Z"],["3831830","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] Hey! yes, this works. You may close the ticket","2026-01-22T17:39:40.324Z"],["3831831","HS-28690","HS","pedro.sousa@bolt.eu","Pedro Sousa","Just checked - all looks good! Thanks!","2026-01-22T17:39:42.480Z"],["3831832","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] Thank You!","2026-01-22T17:39:53.864Z"],["3831833","LSS-61488","LSS","carolina.patricio@bolt.eu","Carolina Patrício","Hey [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac],\n\nThanks for the update, the other countries where it’s live are:\n- Ghana\n- Kenya\n- Nigeria\n- Tanzania\n\n[~accountid:712020:d77c5e6c-f92f-4d79-955d-9f88e6d0a883] reached out to some of these countries and it seems that at least Ghana has a separated flow for courier registration. Let me know how we can help you!\n\nThanks in advance","2026-01-22T17:40:17.591Z"],["3831834","CMO-12981","CMO","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Status period change for Closed and Solved and Pending [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/announcements/overview/120164|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/announcements/overview/120164]","2026-01-22T17:40:23.091Z"],["3831835","PFI-829102","PFI","mary.abura@bolt.eu","Mary Abura","Hey team, please follow up on this ","2026-01-22T17:42:13.526Z"],["3831836","LSS-59868","LSS","jack.cook@bolt.eu","Jack Cook","Hi [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] sorry for my delay here! Answers below - \n\n\n\n* *Securitas Internal policies* - {color:#ff5630}I’ve requested these from the client.{color}\n\n\n\n* *Section 2* - The counterparty wants us to have some sort of SLA’s for our Business Portal while we usually provide the portal on “as is” basis without promising any quality standards. Is this something you would like to accept for this specific customer? If yes, what would these SLAs be? {color:#bf2600}I’ll pull some SLAs from a prior agreement and get back to you with these (we can usually commit to SLAs that involve customer support response times).{color}\n* *Section 6.3* - Customer would like us not to use customer data for training AI algorithms and models - Can you confirm if we can ensure that to the customer? {color:#ff5630}Can we please make a change that says no PII will be used for training algorithms and models? Safer to assume metadata will be used for this.{color}\n* *Section 7.3* - Customer wants us to be liable for the costs of recreating or reloading any customer  information that is lost or damaged due to failure by Bolt - Is this fine for us to accept? If yes, then what would be the cap to the damages per incident? {color:#ff5630}Yes that’s fine as we have failsafes for this - is there a cap you could suggest or ask advice within the Legal team? {color}\n* *Section 7.8* - Are we able to ensure customer’s name and/or trademarks are not used anywhere? {color:#ff5630}Anywhere public facing yes.{color}\n\n\n\nThe customer has also offered to connect you directly with their legal team on a call. I’ll get back to you with their internal policies as well as an SLA framework so can keep this in our back pocket for now. \n\n\n\nThanks!\n\n\n\nJack\n\n","2026-01-22T17:42:54.005Z"],["3831838","LEG-1325","LEG","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","[Regional Legal ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-61932]","2026-01-22T17:44:55.082Z"],["3831841","PFI-822375","PFI","yaroslav.lapshyn@bolt-outsource.eu","Yaroslav Lapshyn","Hello, payouts was finished","2026-01-22T17:53:07.582Z"],["3831842","HS-29298","HS","alice.gorobets@bolt.eu","Alice Gorobets","no pq yet","2026-01-22T17:53:48.702Z"],["3831843","CMO-12981","CMO","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Missed calls are now reverted into callbacks: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/5189888897554?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/5189888897554?country=global&language=en]","2026-01-22T17:53:54.186Z"],["3831844","HS-29288","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-22T17:55:30.307Z"],["3831845","CMO-12981","CMO","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","All updated, along with the quiz :done: ","2026-01-22T17:55:42.409Z"],["3831852","LSS-62044","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-22T18:02:11.180Z"],["3831855","PAW-15106","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @BoltCristianLupu\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161549\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-22 18:09:16 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-22T18:09:16.697Z"],["3831856","PFI-818927","PFI","aydan.kazimova@bolt-outsource.eu","Aydan Kazimova","Hello???  We can't provide the proof of payout. Could you send it through the SD request?","2026-01-22T18:12:02.446Z"],["3831857","GRWA-1527","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","The backfilling was failing due to “OutOfMemoryError”.\n\nInstead of backfilling in one go, I’m breaking it down into monthly runs. Now it’s running - [here|https://airflow-common.data.boltint.net/dags/dbt_mart_rides_campaign_cuped_bootstrapping_test_treatment_cohort/grid?search=dbt_mart_rides_campaign_cuped_bootstrapping_test_treatment_cohort&dag_run_id=manual__2026-01-22T14%3A47%3A34%2B00%3A00&tab=details&num_runs=100]","2026-01-22T18:12:20.883Z"],["3831860","PFI-837450","PFI","anna.savsajeva@bolt-outsource.eu","Anna Šavšajeva","!Screenshot_20260122_110417_Bolt Driver.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot_20260122_170839_WhatsApp.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T18:21:09.699Z"],["3831861","PFI-837450","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-22T18:21:11.802Z"],["3831863","GRWA-1543","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","PR: [Link|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15438]","2026-01-22T18:22:54.657Z"],["3831864","PFI-837452","PFI","george.ghiveciu@bolt.eu","George-Mihai Ghiveciu","[^transaction-confirmation-report_ro-ro_72dbe2-1.pdf]","2026-01-22T18:24:48.784Z"],["3831866","PAW-15097","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @daysleeperx\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17272\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-22 18:25:16 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-22T18:25:17.281Z"],["3831869","PFI-837455","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-22T18:33:12.485Z"],["3831870","PFI-837455","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:712020:92672895-e990-4451-9f97-baec95337272] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-22T18:33:14.128Z"],["3831881","PAW-15098","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @daysleeperx\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161621\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-22 18:44:58 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-22T18:44:58.445Z"],["3831885","PFI-837457","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 3.48.07 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T18:50:00.185Z"],["3831886","PFI-837459","PFI","chonlada.sasorn@bolt-outsource.eu","Chonlada Sasorn","!image-20260122-185112.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T18:52:00.224Z"],["3831887","PFI-837460","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 3.50.07 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T18:52:04.534Z"],["3831889","PFI-837461","PFI","bisola.ajayi@bolt-outsource.eu","Bisola Ajayi","!image-20260122-185627.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260122-185642.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T18:56:55.114Z"],["3831892","PFI-794556","PFI","oluwabunmi.vivian@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwabunmi Vivian","The driver is still reporting that the payment has not reflected.","2026-01-22T18:57:37.221Z"],["3831893","PFI-837462","PFI","george.ghiveciu@bolt.eu","George-Mihai Ghiveciu","[^Tranzactie_30-12-2025_13-10-41 (10).pdf]","2026-01-22T18:59:09.176Z"],["3831895","WEBSD-1504","WEBSD","jevgeni.komkin@bolt.eu","Jevgeni Komkin","Try this one:\n[https://go.bolt.eu/app|https://go.bolt.eu/app]","2026-01-22T19:09:46.953Z"],["3831896","WEBSD-1504","WEBSD","jevgeni.komkin@bolt.eu","Jevgeni Komkin","FYI: you might be able to omit “https://” from sms.","2026-01-22T19:10:20.061Z"],["3831897","WEBSD-1500","WEBSD","jevgeni.komkin@bolt.eu","Jevgeni Komkin","Where/how will this be used?","2026-01-22T19:11:11.605Z"],["3831898","LSS-46087","LSS","karoli.kesner@bolt.eu","Karoli Kesner","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] could you please initiate electronic signing for this lawyer’s confirmation; signatory: Ahto Kink\n\n[^Audit Letter Lawyer 2025 - Bolt Services DE GmbH.pdf]\n\n. Thank you and best wishes, Karoli","2026-01-22T19:16:25.623Z"],["3831899","EBIKE1-396","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","The test below focused on fitment to ensure the flap fits between the tire and mudguard.\n\nFor the next:\n\n# Source *actual material 2mm silicone sheet* to test the safety of the low flap on the front side.\n## Ride over bumps where the flap contacts the ground.\n### Define the minimum height for the front flap to balance safety and splash protection.\n# Test if the silicone sheet retains its shape.\n## Ensure it does not touch the tire during left or right movements or get stuck to the wheel and mudguards.\n# In the warehouses bikes have to be mooved on the rear wheel because fixed hub lock do not enable to move bikes on both wheels. Therefore the length of the flap on the rear side is limited.\n## Measure the max length for the flap from this point of view described above.\n# Rubber material is available for shaping at [etra.ee|http://etra.ee].\n## Will ask for a quotation to cut it\n## will ass quoatation for min qty material\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"align-start\",\"localId\":\"9ababac4-6c3a-4c74-a3e3-22e901702157\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"orderedList\",\"attrs\":{\"order\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"test rivet and washer size\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"orderedList\",\"attrs\":{\"order\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Marking & drilling\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"orderedList\",\"attrs\":{\"order\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"if it`s possible to fit the flap to the space available between the tire and fender\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"orderedList\",\"attrs\":{\"order\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"riveting comfort\"}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"rivet: MFX 1031 AL/FE 3.2x8 (fender 3mm, flap 2mm, washer 0.5mm) 55mm max required for 8mm rivet\"}]},{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"8mm rivet is suitable\"}]}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"washer: DIN9021 ID3.2 OD9\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"on the front side it fits as well as on the rear\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"on the rear fender the flap can be eaily fitted between the tire and inner side of the mudguard\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"on the rear it was relatively simple to fit fingers to the inner side of the fender to install washer\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"on the front it was \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"not doable without removing mudguard\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"},{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#ff5630\"}}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" due to lack of space.\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":140,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"8a94b52351410cf8442b07a74ca2d169-20260122-190825.jpg\",\"alt\":\"8a94b52351410cf8442b07a74ca2d169-20260122-190825.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":175,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"4cecd40bf37415077035cb368fdc03fe-20260122-185951.jpg\",\"alt\":\"4cecd40bf37415077035cb368fdc03fe-20260122-185951.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":140,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"b9c0c58595aef8a2a098aca83dbda3cd-20260122-190921.jpg\",\"alt\":\"b9c0c58595aef8a2a098aca83dbda3cd-20260122-190921.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":143,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"631d7aaa62050f7e05358568420ab4ef-20260122-191205.jpg\",\"alt\":\"631d7aaa62050f7e05358568420ab4ef-20260122-191205.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":175,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"ec48a6295e579632832a248cd613b7cc-20260122-190006.jpg\",\"alt\":\"ec48a6295e579632832a248cd613b7cc-20260122-190006.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":140,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"89033cf76708192bf53e27afc2bb95af-20260122-190931.jpg\",\"alt\":\"89033cf76708192bf53e27afc2bb95af-20260122-190931.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n|!7bd12a83d7957ea9713f962af1cb9981-20260122-191352.jpg|width=302,alt=\"7bd12a83d7957ea9713f962af1cb9981-20260122-191352.jpg\"!|!76eac987940e06b019ff4995c49a1ef9-20260122-191406.jpg|width=297,alt=\"76eac987940e06b019ff4995c49a1ef9-20260122-191406.jpg\"!|!0e84338a61416da9f039d1cdaea0420c-20260122-191415.jpg|width=297,alt=\"0e84338a61416da9f039d1cdaea0420c-20260122-191415.jpg\"!|!bb32bb6e2c7217217e48081d237977e1-20260122-191452.jpg|width=223,alt=\"bb32bb6e2c7217217e48081d237977e1-20260122-191452.jpg\"!|\n|!b7db3b4b53fa3f6104a5298a71da01c2-20260122-191534.jpg|width=223,alt=\"b7db3b4b53fa3f6104a5298a71da01c2-20260122-191534.jpg\"!|!5f15f35e3cad8ca378c99481181fe554-20260122-191543.jpg|width=218,alt=\"5f15f35e3cad8ca378c99481181fe554-20260122-191543.jpg\"!|!401b776fc2a71c69eb76537fd57c1400-20260122-191600.jpg|width=223,alt=\"401b776fc2a71c69eb76537fd57c1400-20260122-191600.jpg\"!|!b20641aa859665347f746416e0fd58b5-20260122-191426.jpg|width=218,alt=\"b20641aa859665347f746416e0fd58b5-20260122-191426.jpg\"!|","2026-01-22T19:18:14.606Z"],["3831900","LSS-60472","LSS","alexia.lia@bolt.eu","Alexia Lia","Hello [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] any updates on this please? 🙏 ","2026-01-22T19:19:38.525Z"],["3831903","PFI-837472","PFI","olubunmi.bakre@bolt-outsource.eu","Olubunmi Bakre","!{4F47EB23-A842-4F96-82F3-B935009EC082}-20260122-193518.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T19:37:35.185Z"],["3831904","HS-28790","HS","anna.tiurina@bolt.eu","Anna Tiurina","Hey [~accountid:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db],\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nCould you please clarify for which year the 6 vacation days were allocated - 2025 or 2026?","2026-01-22T19:40:24.944Z"],["3831905","PFI-827064","PFI","omotola.richard@bolt-outsource.eu","Omotola Richard","Hello Team please provide an update for this ticket ","2026-01-22T19:40:42.788Z"],["3831910","PFI-837476","PFI","ana.pelivanu@bolt-outsource.eu","Ana Pelivanu","[^ING_Consolidated_statement_30-12-25_INEDIT PARTNER CONCEPT SRL (1).pdf (1).pdf]","2026-01-22T19:59:37.281Z"],["3831912","BEE-3491","BEE","adam.kudybinski@bolt.eu","Adam Kudybiński","[~accountid:63ede82e40d0fe7090750298] Do I understand correctly in the last thread you shared that the item was partially refunded to a card, and now the agent wants to return the remaining part of the item value to BB? If yes, then potentially this is not the right task or needs additional requirements. This task is about enabling double refund of the same item (if the first refund was to BB, then we should still allow 2nd refund to the card acoring to policies). Am I correct?","2026-01-22T20:01:32.254Z"],["3831914","CCM-22302","CCM","ademola.oloja@bolt-outsource.eu","Ademola Oloja","[^Ajayi Food Delivery LMS Request x.xlsx]","2026-01-22T20:03:17.649Z"],["3831916","LSS-60549","LSS","simon.fournier@bolt.eu","Simon Fournier","Hi legal team, \n\nThe product team should release the feature tomorrow or early next week. \nFind below: \n\n* [The draft of the communication for riders|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cIZ3fs32ad2sqjRsrrSP5bhca9ksM1LV7zvVNaIwqtw/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.e0zu1xiy37zh]\n* [The draft for the message to add at the price confirmation done by the driver |https://docs.google.com/document/d/11MlsfZRihXHmbrCxPXTe4zvwvg1zhsdtVzt0qKbIHh0/edit?tab=t.0]\n* We probably need to update T&S as well\n\nLet’s talk about it ! \nThanks\nSimon\n\n\n","2026-01-22T20:06:48.764Z"],["3831924","PFI-837479","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-22T20:27:38.022Z"],["3831930","PFI-837479","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Adjustments, Compensations*\n* If driver was compensated a while ago in some CS ticket - and this compensation is still not added to driver's balance -> please raise it with Local operations.\n\n*Why?* \nWhen Compensation is created in CS ticket -> it gets added to a csv file. Then local ops take it once a month and submit it into Manual Adjustment tool. They might submit it late, or submitting csv file gets delayed.\n\n\n*Campaign Bonus*\n* If driver did not recevei a bonus for a campaign -> please raise it with campaign team.\n\n*Why?*\nBilling team does not handle campaign setups. So we do not know when, why, how drivers should receive bonuses.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-22T21:00:50.512Z"],["3831931","PFI-837450","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\n\nLooks like you've selected an *invalid Request Type* which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\n*PAYMENTS*\n* *[Customer Payments]* Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Manual payout request to Payments team: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Driver/Fleet payout issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312]\n* *[Customer Payments]* Rider payment/charge issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307]\n\n----\n\n*TECH SUPPORT*\n* *Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597]\n* *Driver app/backend/earning screen issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66]\n* *Rider app/backend issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103]\n* *Wrong price calculation for the order:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354]\n\n----\n\n*FRAUD*\n* *Fraud related issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308]\n\n----\n\n*BILLING*\n* *Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247]\n* *Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301]\n\nCheers,\n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-22T21:00:51.168Z"],["3831933","WFM-10102","WFM","kauan.sousa@bolt-outsource.eu","Kauan Victor Barros De Sousa","Additional info needed, a new request was made here [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WFM-10103|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WFM-10103|smart-link] since i ain’t able to cancel the request","2026-01-22T21:02:14.182Z"],["3831938","FX-3660","FX","adam.sokolowski@bolt.eu","Adam Sokołowski","[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] I believe we also need to add a Substituted in? box in the Created new enrolment section so the user can check it when creating the enrolment. Otherwise, they will need to create and then edit to tick the box. ","2026-01-22T21:07:56.107Z"],["3831940","PFI-837331","PFI","daniel.covas@bolt-outsource.eu","Daniel Covas","Issue was resolved, thank you!","2026-01-22T21:26:50.337Z"],["3831941","PFI-837331","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-22T21:26:54.234Z"],["3831943","LSS-58645","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","Hey [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e],  \nI initially misunderstood your point about what’s missing. The partner is okay with the new addition. We can prepare the document for the partner to sign. \n\n\nEmail address: [jignesh@amicafrica.com|http://Director@theccgl.com/jignesh@amicafrica.com]\n\nFull name: Jigneshkumar Hasmukhbhai Viradia\n\nRole: Director\n\nThanks. ","2026-01-22T21:27:55.004Z"],["3831946","LSS-58917","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","Hello [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1], please review the document as we’ve filled in the data for the supplier. \n\nLet’s see if all is good and then we can proceed to send it out to the fleet partner for signatures. \n\nThanks. ","2026-01-22T21:47:34.985Z"],["3831947","WD-22575","WD","kristiine.murd@bolt.eu","Kristiine Murd","*What we intend to achieve?*\nIf the Supplier invoice has other company on the invoice line, that ill automatically create in WD Intercompany transaction by posting the actual cost to the entity that is marked on the ‘Invoice line Company’ using 2112:Trade Payments as sort of clearing account. While on the same time the Purchase VAT from the invoice will be still posted to the Company were the invoice is posted.\n\n*_For example_* _(Company on the invoice line changed manually in SB):_\nIN-PL003-26-000003\n\n!image-20260122-214926.png|width=2013,height=398,alt=\"image-20260122-214926.png\"!\n\n!image-20260122-215112.png|width=1994,height=850,alt=\"image-20260122-215112.png\"!\n\n!image-20260122-215215.png|width=1988,height=906,alt=\"image-20260122-215215.png\"!\n\n*When do we use it?*\nFor Poland case we could use it for the Supplier invoice that are issued to Bolt Rides PL with issue date of 2026 for the services/goods provided in prior year (part of business transfer). So that the accrued cost in Dec 2025 will be booked in 2026 and Accountant wouldn’t have to make manual corrections.\n\nAlso right now this solution (manual Supplier invoice line company change) is used by Bolt OPS and Bolt Tech.","2026-01-22T21:56:09.060Z"],["3831949","PFI-837450","PFI","anna.savsajeva@bolt-outsource.eu","Anna Šavšajeva","Hey! When I tried to create a ticket to tech team, they said to raise it here\n\n","2026-01-22T22:16:17.316Z"],["3831962","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Gonna try this:\n\n{noformat}root@ti-payments-dba.sqldb:taxify_payment>SELECT NOW()\n+---------------------+\n| NOW()               |\n|---------------------|\n| 2026-01-22 23:23:29 |\n+---------------------+\n1 row in set\nTime: 0.004s\n\n\nroot@ti-payments-dba.sqldb:taxify_payment>show variables like '%tidb_ttl_delete_rate_limit%'\n+----------------------------+-------+\n| Variable_name              | Value |\n|----------------------------+-------|\n| tidb_ttl_delete_rate_limit | 10    |\n+----------------------------+-------+\n1 row in set\nTime: 0.005s\n\nroot@ti-payments-dba.sqldb:taxify_payment>SET GLOBAL tidb_ttl_delete_rate_limit = 20;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.018s{noformat}","2026-01-22T23:38:36.257Z"],["3831964","PFI-837503","PFI","sevinj.babazada@bolt.eu","Sevinj Babazada","!Снимок экрана 2026-01-23 в 03.51.39.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-22T23:52:27.059Z"],["3831966","PFI-837504","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-22T23:54:49.099Z"],["3831967","FX-3695","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769127636681329]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@test_ci_notifier>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3695] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-23T00:20:49.638Z"],["3831969","PFI-806995","PFI","oskar.staszak@bolt-outsource.eu","Oskar Staszak","hi, any updates?","2026-01-23T00:35:44.118Z"],["3831971","PFI-837504","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\nIf you need a _report_, please refer to FleetX (DriverX). If your request concerns an _invoice_, follow these steps:\n\nPlease try:\n* Open the *Client page in Admin*: [link|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D].\n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ → The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see to_execute → it means that the invoice still needs to be generated. You either look at the invoice for the current month (which does not have an invoice yet because month is still going). If you see that to_execute is for the invoice for multiple months → it means that in the past months it was not generated and will be generated in the end of the month.\n* If you see another _error_ → provide us a link.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the {{Partner Invoices}}) tab\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-23T01:00:50.593Z"],["3831973","PFI-837509","PFI","chatrawee.saenwerm@bolt-outsource.eu","Chatrawee Saenwerm","!image-20260123-014146.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T01:42:11.202Z"],["3831974","SCM-1116","SCM","lisha.ye@bolt.eu","Lisha Ye","The Farnell order 17801093 is sent out by FedEx *501772610142*, ETA {{2026-01-26}} ","2026-01-23T01:45:27.534Z"],["3831977","SCM-1074","SCM","yong.lin@bolt.eu","Yong Lin","[~accountid:5e4a421e691b8a0c95c2cdec] We have Hopp","2026-01-23T02:31:25.871Z"],["3831981","PFI-833151","PFI","hannah.yang@bolt.eu","Hannah Yang","Hi [~accountid:712020:c152e340-503c-4822-bf8e-89c9f6cffb24] ,\n\nthanks for help! Will proceed to the next step😇 ","2026-01-23T03:10:14.893Z"],["3831982","LSS-62045","LSS","susan.shao@bolt.eu","Cancan Shao","Here is the document needs to be signed. \n\n[^INCAP Confirmation Request 2025_Bolt Operations OÜ.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-23T03:12:17.883Z"],["3831983","PFI-837516","PFI","pimchanok.pipattanakij@bolt-outsource.eu","Pimchanok Pipattanakij","!image-20260123-033707.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260123-033722.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T03:38:23.096Z"],["3831986","PFI-837517","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","\n\n[^M2309128.TXT] _(2 kB)_","2026-01-23T04:01:18.032Z"],["3831987","PFI-837518","PFI","favour.chijioke@bolt-outsource.eu","Favour Chijioke","!image-20260123-040422.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T04:05:03.155Z"],["3831988","LSS-58832","LSS","jana.jilkova@bolt-outsource.eu","Jana Jilkova","Hello, \n\nSadly I would like to answer for the other agent, but I am unable to see the details of the issue that was posted here. If you are able to see them could you share them with us ?\n\nBest regards,\nJana. ","2026-01-23T04:05:53.221Z"],["3831990","LSS-61372","LSS","ewalexx.steenvasilopoulos@bolt-outsource.eu","Ewalexx Steenvasilopoulos","Any updates?","2026-01-23T04:15:15.906Z"],["3831994","PFI-837521","PFI","alimot.adewale@bolt-outsource.eu","Alimot Adewale","!image-20260123-045214.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T04:52:56.503Z"],["3832001","FX-3695","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dzmitry Andryienka [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769144605625389]*{color}:\nDuplicate flaky tests\n[https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161675]\n{quote}","2026-01-23T05:03:39.591Z"],["3832002","FX-3695","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769144613129609]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3695 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-23T05:03:58.325Z"],["3832003","FX-3672","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dzmitry Andryienka [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769144804616729]*{color}:\nFix for flaky tests\n[https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161675]\n{quote}","2026-01-23T05:06:58.311Z"],["3832005","FX-3582","FX","dmitry.andrienko@bolt.eu","Dzmitry Andryienka","Draft spec for API integration\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/pages/resumedraft.action?draftId=7428243988&draftShareId=fe8c30f5-1392-4e1e-9cfe-12fa4dd2b52d|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/pages/resumedraft.action?draftId=7428243988&draftShareId=fe8c30f5-1392-4e1e-9cfe-12fa4dd2b52d|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T05:10:48.703Z"],["3832006","FX-3601","FX","dmitry.andrienko@bolt.eu","Dzmitry Andryienka","Draft spec for API integration\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/pages/resumedraft.action?draftId=7428243988&draftShareId=fe8c30f5-1392-4e1e-9cfe-12fa4dd2b52d|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/pages/resumedraft.action?draftId=7428243988&draftShareId=fe8c30f5-1392-4e1e-9cfe-12fa4dd2b52d|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T05:11:28.769Z"],["3832007","FDBT-4829","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-23T05:14:18.392Z"],["3832008","FX-3686","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769145401589579]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3686 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-23T05:16:54.037Z"],["3832009","LSS-61975","LSS","colin.reid@bolt.eu","Colin Reid","Hi Elina,\n\n\n\nAFAIK this is only done in Estonia, but I am starting the process of asking other markets, however transporting batteries in this condition has a lot of restrictions and so it would be down to the charity wether they are able to transport from other countries. For now they have expressed interest in other Baltic countries.\n\nI do not know who is the responsible person but I believe it would be [~accountid:712020:282008bf-7f03-4058-8bec-43f7e5a44ace]. I am also linking 2 previous tickets where this was done.\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-57737|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-57737|smart-link] \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-42105|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-42105|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T05:17:33.677Z"],["3832011","PFI-836471","PFI","sikarin.seepol@bolt.eu","Sikarin Seepol","Hi team. Kindly give me an update as this ticket has been pending for too long. Thank you.","2026-01-23T05:23:48.736Z"],["3832012","PFI-837524","PFI","sirichanya.phookrabil@bolt-outsource.eu","Sirichanya Phookrabil","!image-20260123-051846.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260123-051855.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260123-051904.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T05:24:45.592Z"],["3832013","FX-3664","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769146040592139]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3664 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-23T05:27:33.088Z"],["3832016","FX-3664","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dzmitry Andryienka [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769146310945989]*{color}:\nNo urgent need for size change\n*fleet-car-data* (100mCPU_800MiB -&gt; 100mCPU_500MiB) - Memory usage can spike over 500Mb\n• *fleet-owner-reporting-cron* (100mCPU_800MiB -&gt; 100mCPU_1500MiB) - No need as memory consumption is within reasonable range\n• *lead-to-fleet-cron* (100mCPU_500MiB -&gt; 100mCPU_800MiB) - no spikes detected, sron memory consumption is stable, with no traffic depencency, statys within 50 +-10%\n{quote}","2026-01-23T05:32:02.788Z"],["3832018","PFI-837526","PFI","anucha.ruengnok@bolt-outsource.eu","Anucha Ruengnok","!image-20260123-053229.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260123-053239.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260123-053314.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T05:33:24.554Z"],["3832019","DSR-2883","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Thank you [~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] ! I have prepared the folder [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1R9bmDT6xEDJEWMq2ioNEfnAHRJ94OAPm] [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] , waiting for your final confirmation and the data will then be sent out to the driver and a confirmation letter will be sent to the WIE, as they mentioned:\n\n\n\n* _Confirm receipt of this letter, clearly communicating any stages and dates involved in the handling of the request._\n\n* _Ensure that the data is sent in the same, commonly used, structured, machine-readable format (such as a CSV file.)_\n\n* _Inform us by email once the full request has been completed and all individual disclosures have been made._\n\n[Reference|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A76QRPMKK/p1769069287683029?thread_ts=1768902394.202259&cid=C0A76QRPMKK]\n\n","2026-01-23T05:33:40.238Z"],["3832021","PFI-837527","PFI","ales.kvetensky@bolt-outsource.eu","Ales Kvetensky","!Screenshot_20260123-060235_Chrome.jpg.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T05:37:13.807Z"],["3832022","PFI-837527","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-23T05:37:15.957Z"],["3832093","PFI-837538","PFI","pauline.kamau@bolt-outsource.eu","Pauline Kamau","!Screenshot_20260122_194737.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T06:20:00.822Z"],["3832099","FDBT-4828","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-23T06:30:28.167Z"],["3832101","LSS-61744","LSS","monicah.mumina@bolt-outsource.eu","Monicah Mumina","D confirmed email and phone. D was logged out of all devices and advised to log back in.  ","2026-01-23T06:31:44.812Z"],["3832102","CSDA-308","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Thank you for raising a request to our team!\nWe review ad-hoc requests once a day. We'll update you once the request is reviewed and internally assigned.","2026-01-23T06:34:32.154Z"],["3832103","LSS-61648","LSS","migle.zuvelyte@bolt.eu","Miglė Žuvelytė","Just to add from Operations: we do not ensure the ligitamcy of neither of these (address, email, phone) as these details are entered and changed by the driver, we do not verify them (especially the address - drivers are not obligated to provide us with the full or correct address in any way). ","2026-01-23T06:35:28.393Z"],["3832104","PFI-837541","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-23T06:36:12.894Z"],["3832106","WEB-9954","WEB","conor.mclaughlin@bolt.eu","Conor McLaughlin","[~accountid:712020:9c84799a-9aa0-422a-aefb-ff948aabb245] could you help Sam here. Also noticed the item is a different aspect ratio to the other items and flagged with Sam.","2026-01-23T06:42:42.299Z"],["3832107","PFI-837545","PFI","muhammed.hassan@bolt-outsource.eu","Muhammed Hassan","!Screenshot_2026-01-23-07-27-10-705_com.jaizbank.app.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T06:47:41.493Z"],["3832111","HS-29299","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Hi [~accountid:61b851602900b00071ca4597] I think this is something you can help with.","2026-01-23T06:53:51.968Z"],["3832114","LSS-60897","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","You should ask for an invoice, and then share that together with the signed agreement to the finance team. I believe it was Angelina Korol, who is supporting AZ. 🙂 ","2026-01-23T06:55:18.427Z"],["3832120","PFI-828215","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Adrian Kosmecki,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-23T07:00:11.724Z"],["3832124","LSS-60218","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Julian Siemer,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-23T07:00:21.473Z"],["3832125","LSS-59660","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Sakina Balayeva,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-23T07:00:21.524Z"],["3832126","LSS-58372","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Josef Rückl,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-23T07:00:21.556Z"],["3832127","LSS-58783","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Afonso Varão de Azevedo,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-23T07:00:21.657Z"],["3832128","LSS-57358","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Patrycja Rubach,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-23T07:00:22.621Z"],["3832129","LSS-55009","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Philipp-Juraj Rokov,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-23T07:00:29.390Z"],["3832130","LSS-56734","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Adam Sokołowski,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-23T07:00:39.659Z"],["3832131","LSS-60903","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Alex Wong,\n\nThere hasn't been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days. Please:\n1) Close the ticket if the issue has been resolved or is not relevant anymore; or\n2) Give an update; or\n3) Change to “Waiting for customer” status if you are waiting to hear back from the reporter. If the reporter is not responding within a reasonable time, add a comment stating this and close the ticket.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-23T07:01:25.840Z"],["3832133","LSS-53077","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Debora Raudberg,\n\nThere hasn't been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days. Please:\n1) Close the ticket if the issue has been resolved or is not relevant anymore; or\n2) Give an update; or\n3) Change to “Waiting for customer” status if you are waiting to hear back from the reporter. If the reporter is not responding within a reasonable time, add a comment stating this and close the ticket.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-23T07:01:29.497Z"],["3832134","DSR-3975","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T07:02:36.531Z"],["3832135","HS-29304","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-23T07:03:14.118Z"],["3832136","XP-1384","XP","andrey.kuzmin@bolt.eu","Andrey Kuzmin","I am closing this as it seems that it is not needed.","2026-01-23T07:03:34.991Z"],["3832138","XP-1306","XP","andrey.kuzmin@bolt.eu","Andrey Kuzmin","I am closing this as it seems that it is not needed.","2026-01-23T07:03:52.660Z"],["3832139","LSS-61297","LSS","migle.zuvelyte@bolt.eu","Miglė Žuvelytė","Hello, we are expanding the topic a bit here [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd]. Could you please give confirmation on certificates and data handling?\n\nI also have an additional question.\n\nAt the moment, NŠA (the exam provider) does not have a publicly or company-accessible database to verify whether a person has passed the exam. The only way for us to check this is to contact them directly and provide the person’s name, surname, and date of birth. They then confirm whether the person has passed the exam and at what level.\n\nThese external validation checks are crucial, as we have already encountered falsified documents.\n\nWould this method of validating the legitimacy of exam certificates be approved from a privacy perspective? No personal identification codes would be shared; they have confirmed that the date of birth is sufficient.","2026-01-23T07:03:55.344Z"],["3832140","RDS-1084","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:5e0f0e7f0242870e996ebba8] Correct me if I am wrong, but from the description, it is rather a new initiative, not Quality Debt, right?","2026-01-23T07:04:02.766Z"],["3832141","HS-29305","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-23T07:04:26.495Z"],["3832143","RDS-1103","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:73f630c1-899f-4b5d-ac71-8a7e5c89eb30] Added priority, feel free to adjust.","2026-01-23T07:06:19.853Z"],["3832144","WEBSD-1497","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi 👋 \n\nI can see you already had an account but was inactive.\n\nPlease check again and try to logged in (I changed it to active) with your credentials otherwise I will generate a new password for you.\n\nPlease let me know.\n\nRegards,","2026-01-23T07:06:22.245Z"],["3832146","PFI-837135","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-23T07:06:51.939Z"],["3832147","PFI-837434","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-23T07:06:54.765Z"],["3832148","PFI-837497","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-23T07:06:57.361Z"],["3832151","PFI-837552","PFI","estere.modilevska@bolt-outsource.eu","Estere Modilevska","!Screenshot_2026-01-20-15-32-29-831_ee.mtakso.driver.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T07:09:47.153Z"],["3832152","RDS-1064","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:648af4f5-f134-458a-b3aa-9320408d346e] I added priority. Feel free to adjust.","2026-01-23T07:10:44.199Z"],["3832154","WEBSD-1473","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi 👋 \n\nI just assigned this task.\n\nI will start working on it from next week and I will write all the comments in here so we can track them and have a source of truth.","2026-01-23T07:10:45.936Z"],["3832157","PFI-836993","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected by the payment provider; they only returned a generic technical UPI error code without a clear, human-readable reason. Please ask the partner to verify and correct their UPI/beneficiary details (UPI ID/handle, name exactly as per bank records, and that the bank account is properly linked to the UPI ID). The payout will be reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try requesting it again.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-23T07:12:24.924Z"],["3832158","RLONE-872","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","This is in connection to my development plan and more details can be seen [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SZyDamwtaf4QNAz4obHH0hPJDI9yQdOpwMLfJvloCYU/edit?tab=t.6a3pwhuxzdfu].","2026-01-23T07:12:37.462Z"],["3832160","PFI-837006","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected by the bank; unfortunately, they did not provide a specific rejection reason. It will be automatically reprocessed during the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, please ask the partner to request it again. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-23T07:12:58.316Z"],["3832161","LSS-61821","LSS","mo.salama@bolt.eu","Mo Salama","Hi Raivis,\n\nI hope this will be the final version.\n\n[^Bolt x Tilstra_Service Agreement Michel (1).pdf]\n\nSincerely,\n\nMo","2026-01-23T07:13:12.762Z"],["3832162","PFI-837008","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The early cashout requested on Jan 20 is still pending; the last log shows it was accepted by the bank for processing, so it’s in progress. Since the ticket was opened on Jan 22, this is within normal processing time—early cashouts can take up to two business days to reach the account. Please ask the partner to wait a bit longer; if it still hasn’t arrived by the end of the next business day, please reply to this ticket and we’ll take a closer look.\nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase—feedback is welcome.","2026-01-23T07:13:25.762Z"],["3832164","PFI-837038","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The early cashout requested on 20 Jan is still pending; our bank has accepted the transfer request, so it’s currently being processed. Given the last update is from 20 Jan, this is within the normal window—please let the partner know it should be reflected on the bank account shortly (the app status may update the next business day after funds arrive). If it does not arrive within 2–3 business days, it’s likely due to compliance or provider-side processing delays; we are monitoring and will act on any checks as they come in.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-23T07:13:57.772Z"],["3832165","PFI-837054","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This Early Cashout was exported on 14 January and is still in progress on the provider/bank side. Given the time elapsed, the delay is likely due to provider processing or a compliance review; we are monitoring and will act on any requests. Please ask the partner to check with their beneficiary bank for any incoming/held transfer, and if the funds are still not received within 1–2 business days, reply to this ticket for a follow-up. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-23T07:14:24.390Z"],["3832166","PFI-830015","PFI","daumantas.butvila@bolt-outsource.eu","Daumantas Butvila","Hi, any news regarding this?","2026-01-23T07:14:33.080Z"],["3832168","FX-3682","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dzmitry Andryienka [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769152469546579]*{color}:\n<@U01AVSCSG01> there should be a button to apply setting, you do not see it on mobile?\n\nLinked files:\n* [IMG_0314.jpg|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0ABBG8MX5W/img_0314.jpg]\n{quote}","2026-01-23T07:14:43.094Z"],["3832169","PFI-837060","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This Early Cashout is still in progress (pending) — the last update on 20 Jan shows it was accepted for processing, so the status should update and funds should reflect shortly. Please inform the partner they can request another cashout only after this one settles; no action is needed from their side now. If it remains pending beyond 2–3 business days, it may be due to compliance or provider-side checks, and the Partner Payments team is monitoring such cases. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-23T07:15:01.887Z"],["3832170","RDS-1022","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:5e0f0e7f0242870e996ebba8] , do you know what the status of this ticket?","2026-01-23T07:15:09.409Z"],["3832171","HS-29293","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:979961a6-5216-4ee0-aa85-a7302993f5e6],\n\nUnfortunately People Operations is unable to support this. Please reach out to Workday Tech. Maybe they can add the expense report under Bolt Rides Sp. z o.o. You can find their Service Desk [HERE|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/26/group/1274/create/2246]. If they are unable to help, please reach out to [~accountid:712020:b2c09d5d-f839-4294-b3c4-98447cbfb8cb]. \n\nAll the best,\n\nKerilin","2026-01-23T07:15:18.190Z"],["3832172","PFI-837065","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This Early Cashout has been successfully processed; value date 2026-01-21. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if funds are still not received, ask them to contact their bank to trace the incoming transfer. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase — feedback is welcome.","2026-01-23T07:15:20.862Z"],["3832173","PFI-837353","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Thank you - checked Hamilton and this is fixed now. Can you please verify whether the tax structure is the same in Whitby and Oshawa as well or if there are any exceptions? Thanks! ","2026-01-23T07:15:30.448Z"],["3832174","PFI-837084","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout is still pending; the bank has accepted the payment file, but the transfer has not been finalized yet (last update on 2026-01-19). Since it has been pending for a few days, the delay is likely due to ongoing provider processing or a compliance review—we are monitoring it and will respond to any checks immediately. Please inform the partner that no action is required on their side and the funds should post once processing completes; the status will update automatically.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-23T07:15:45.838Z"],["3832177","PFI-837553","PFI","mariam.omogoye@bolt-outsource.eu","Mariam Omogoye","!image-20260123-071513.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T07:16:29.206Z"],["3832178","PFI-837085","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected and the funds were returned by the beneficiary bank; unfortunately the bank did not provide a specific rejection reason. It will be automatically reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, the partner can try to request the cashout again. If the partner needs further clarification on the rejection, please advise them to contact their bank.\nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-23T07:16:30.184Z"],["3832179","PFI-837113","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The latest payout attempt was rejected by the bank on 2026-01-20, and the provider did not return a clear rejection reason. Please inform the partner that the payout will be automatically reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try to request it again. As the reason is not specified, please also confirm with the partner that their beneficiary bank details (account/IBAN, account holder name, bank, and currency) are up to date to avoid further failures. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-23T07:17:03.851Z"],["3832180","PFI-837117","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected because the bank details provided are invalid (incorrect account number and/or bank code). Please ask the partner to update their payout details with the correct IBAN/account number and the correct bank code (BIC/SWIFT) and save them; once fixed, the payout will be reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle. If this was an Early Cashout, they can submit a new cashout after correcting the details.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-23T07:17:32.317Z"],["3832182","PFI-837119","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected by the bank; the provider only returned a technical code and did not give a clear reason. Please inform the partner that the payout will be reprocessed automatically in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try to request it again. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-23T07:18:14.671Z"],["3832184","PFI-837253","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was sent to the bank on 12 Jan 2026 (state: exported), and per the customer’s note the funds were credited on 13 Jan 2026. The app status may lag and will update automatically; no action is needed unless the partner still claims non‑receipt, in which case please ask them to check with their beneficiary bank. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-23T07:18:50.538Z"],["3832185","PFI-837286","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected by the bank, and they did not provide a clear rejection reason in the return message. Please inform the partner that it will be reprocessed automatically during the next regular payout cycle. If this was an Early Cashout, they can try requesting the cashout again.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-23T07:19:16.564Z"],["3832186","PFI-837318","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still in pending status; the last update on 11 Jan 2026 shows “payment validation is in progress,” which means it’s undergoing a provider-side compliance/validation review. Since it has been pending longer than usual, please inform the partner that delays are expected while the review completes and that no action is required from their side right now. We are monitoring it and will have it processed as soon as validation clears; the status will update automatically once completed. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-23T07:19:42.890Z"],["3832187","PFI-837320","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout is still pending; the last update on 11 Jan shows the payment validation is in progress. Since it has been pending longer than usual, it’s likely due to an ongoing compliance review or provider-side checks—our team is monitoring and responding to any requests so it can be released. Please inform the partner that no action is needed from their side right now and the payout will be processed and reflected once the validation is completed.\nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase.","2026-01-23T07:20:09.466Z"],["3832188","PFI-837342","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was successfully processed on 22 Jan 2026. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the driver; if the funds are still not visible, advise them to contact their bank with the proof for a trace.  \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-23T07:20:21.878Z"],["3832191","PFI-837354","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed (state: finished) on 2026-01-22 and should reach the beneficiary shortly. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner. If they still cannot see the funds, ask them to contact their bank with the proof for a payment trace. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-23T07:20:42.173Z"],["3832192","PFI-837356","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed (state: finished; marked Processed/Completed) on 2026-01-22. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if the funds are still not visible, advise them to contact their bank using the proof for tracing. If you need anything else, please reply to this ticket. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-23T07:21:05.659Z"],["3832193","L10N-29768","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29766](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29766)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T07:22:04.124Z"],["3832194","L10N-29769","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29766](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29766)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T07:22:04.334Z"],["3832195","L10N-29773","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n-