"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"IMG_0104.JPEG\",\"alt\":\"IMG_0104.JPEG\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection--1136578425\",\"height\":2048,\"width\":1536}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"IMG_0110.MP4\",\"alt\":\"IMG_0110.MP4\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection--1136578425\",\"height\":1280,\"width\":720}}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":216,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"IMG_0107.JPEG\",\"alt\":\"IMG_0107.JPEG\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection--1136578425\",\"height\":3840,\"width\":2160}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":216,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"IMG_0108.JPEG\",\"alt\":\"IMG_0108.JPEG\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection--1136578425\",\"height\":3840,\"width\":2160}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"It leaked from the 6-pin area. However the O-ring gasket didn’t fail in this test. \"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}","2026-01-23T07:29:17.987Z"],["3832218","EBIKE1-376","EBIKE1","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","YiYou didn’t follow test requirements, they used basically random distance from where to apply force. \nL2 for Roller brake test is around 158 mm, L2 for Drum brake test is around 265 mm. By standard it should have been 305 mm. They are going to remake tests\n\nErki got similar/same result as I got from SW simulation. Erki also checked my setup we both agreed that setup was good. But these still don’t match with test results. Will add results to from Simscale and Sw into confluence {{2026-01-23}} ","2026-01-23T07:29:22.954Z"],["3832219","RLONE-872","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","[Danmark-aktiviteter – Kvartalsrapport|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oGD7Ejs4wK3Iw6pbNgr0nQIsSmX3PUrayIQzhQrqDHU/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.1bdj06dg5q4h]","2026-01-23T07:29:24.529Z"],["3832222","HS-28809","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-23T07:30:20.904Z"],["3832223","HS-28747","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:6271326a2db3080070241cfa],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Cancel*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and cancel the ticket.","2026-01-23T07:30:22.190Z"],["3832226","PFI-837113","PFI","darja.rojenko@bolt-outsource.eu","Darja Rojenko","agent review needed ","2026-01-23T07:30:53.070Z"],["3832228","RS-1734","RS","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Gotcha, thank you [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] . Data has been approved and this ticket can be considered done again 🙏 ","2026-01-23T07:31:22.541Z"],["3832229","SCM-1125","SCM","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","Didn’t mage to check into it, Stratus battery and fork problems took the time","2026-01-23T07:31:37.130Z"],["3832236","RISK2-3200","RISK2","anca.grossu@bolt.eu","Anca-Ioana Grossu","[Here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1VBoKc2kjX6hJZ7vbnR3GU547tsToUpstM-kQ_mdmEaI/edit?gid=0#gid=0] is the YOY tracking sheet 2023 - 2025 for Romania, Germany and Poland.","2026-01-23T07:33:47.602Z"],["3832246","WEBSD-1509","WEBSD","mihai.raucea@bolt.eu","Mihai Răucea","Thank you!","2026-01-23T07:36:45.967Z"],["3832247","COP-1974","COP","mate.varadi@bolt.eu","Máté Váradi","Requested/agreed adjustments to the playbook before experiment:\n\n* removing OH requirements\n* increasing RPH requirement from 60th to 80th percentile\n* adjusting driver population used by budget tool to better match enrolled population by removing drivers with branded cars\n* increasing minimum bonus percentage level from 5% to 10% to avoid too low campaigns\n* round final bonus levels to the nearest 0.5\n\n\nPR: [https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/818|https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/818|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T07:37:12.641Z"],["3832250","LSS-58622","LSS","oliver.vahar@bolt.eu","Oliver Martyn Vahar","Hey [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] , these were the options for the markets, all low reclassification risk markets, to minimise any regulatory risks. Out of these, I would presume that I should choose markets that have looser rules around dashcams/recording etc? Would you have any information on this, otherwise, I can try to source it myself as well.\n\n*Markets*:\n\n* Azerbaijan\n* Ghana\n* Kenya\n* Nigeria\n* Paraguay\n* Saudi Arabia\n* South Africa\n* Tanzania\n* United Arab Emirates\n\n","2026-01-23T07:38:27.396Z"],["3832251","INT-86","INT","mate.varadi@bolt.eu","Máté Váradi","26W4\n\n* Worked and aligned on [+experiment plan+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/18E6V9Dn998GNAjMVXPyqoOLYDMRD9l7S8WGLkK3ezB0/edit?tab=t.0]+.+ Pilot testing will start in Riga in W5. Experiment will launch in Warsaw, Krakow and Valletta in W6.\n* Implemented requested changes to Playbook, such as removing OH requirements; increasing ride requirements by expecting a higher RPH percentile; increasing minimum bonus levels, etc. [[+ticket+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/COP-1974], [+PR+|https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/818]]\n* Worked on optimization rewriting [[+ticket+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/COP-1937]]","2026-01-23T07:38:42.591Z"],["3832252","CSDA-305","CSDA","nargiz.abdullayeva@bolt.eu","Nargiz Karimova","Hey Roman!\n\nThis is very great! Thanks a lot🙏 \n\nJust a small request, maybe we can make it more granular and add frt results per each branch separately, not overall one?\n\nAnd ticket based frt results separately as well. Is it possible to do?","2026-01-23T07:39:18.493Z"],["3832253","PFI-837559","PFI","filip.kieronczyk@bolt-outsource.eu","Filip Kieronczyk","[^1829e68d-952c-47e8-b8b8-3de8cad26621.pdf]","2026-01-23T07:39:24.293Z"],["3832254","PFI-837559","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-23T07:39:26.468Z"],["3832255","MLC-4036","MLC","anette.tiitus@bolt.eu","Anette Tiitus","Modal launched (/) The CTA button’s copy changes, whether the user has free trial available or not. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 09.38.36.png|width=404,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 09.38.36.png\"!\n\nMarkets: SK & RO\n\nDates: 22-26 Jan (5 days)\n\nFrequency: 1x","2026-01-23T07:39:27.539Z"],["3832263","LSS-62045","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] I see this was marked as admin support request however please don’t sign before this request gets the necessary confirmations. Thank you 🙏 ","2026-01-23T07:42:02.169Z"],["3832270","RDS-1228","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:648af4f5-f134-458a-b3aa-9320408d346e] I added priority. Feel free to adjust.","2026-01-23T07:45:37.596Z"],["3832271","WFM-10093","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:63e39f9afb75f8568f63450a]!\r\n\r\nMentioned agents above were added to *02 MM_United Kingdom_T1_Calls* queue.\r\n\r\nHave a nice day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-23T07:45:39.274Z"],["3832272","PFI-837560","PFI","thitinon.decharattanasub@bolt-outsource.eu","Thitinon Decharattanasub","!Screenshot_17.100 thb (f829d8b4-75a5-4afa-a2d1-1414dbc7cccb).jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260123-074044.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260123-074114.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T07:46:37.309Z"],["3832274","LSS-59597","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hey[~accountid:712020:e81c1984-54f1-46ce-bc81-864b3748de94]\nJust letting you know that the suggestions for the privacy clause in the lease agreement are finalized.\nIf anything comes-up, please let me know by tagging me 🙏 \n","2026-01-23T07:47:42.847Z"],["3832276","PFI-837566","PFI","thitinon.decharattanasub@bolt-outsource.eu","Thitinon Decharattanasub","!Screenshot 21.50 thb.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260123-074951.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260123-075000.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T07:50:38.995Z"],["3832277","LSS-62015","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] Articles 16 and 20 are also cited, however:\n\n* *Article 16* regulates limitations on the use of personal data by public authorities. It does not itself impose an obligation on private companies to disclose data to the police.\n* *Article 20* concerns restrictions on the use of personal data by non-public authorities. Again, it does not provide a standalone power for law enforcement to compel disclosure from Bolt.\n\n\n\nI have never seen that Privacy legislation would set out a legal basis for authorities to request personal data. It’s almost always administrative acts or criminal/misdemeanor procedural acts.","2026-01-23T07:50:39.276Z"],["3832278","PFI-837568","PFI","chiamaka.mmeka@bolt-outsource.eu","Chiamaka Mmeka","!{BFA9D6EE-F1E6-405F-8824-635F0F3165B2}-20260123-074934.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T07:51:01.066Z"],["3832280","DSR-3977","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T07:51:23.647Z"],["3832286","G3IOT-1214","G3IOT","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","So how it works is that VREG caps charging voltage but if for some reason the BB is charged say up to 4.2V then bq25798 would still keep Vsys 200mv higher even if Vreg is set say to 4V. Now of course if the BB is inside the scooter and we try not to overcharge then Vsys should never be higher than Vreg capped + 200mv. However there can still be corner cases where a fully charged BB is connected to a scooter resulting in Vsys overshoots.\n\nI have already mentioned this before that this power solution feels fragile, can we please modify it in upcoming revisions so that correct power levels are ensured by hw design not by fw.","2026-01-23T07:52:45.225Z"],["3832287","LSS-61987","LSS","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Hey [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]\n\nI have made a Jira ticket here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DSR-3977|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DSR-3977]\n\nPlease review 🙏 more info there","2026-01-23T07:52:49.661Z"],["3832288","WEBSD-1510","WEBSD","alessandro@bolt.eu","Alessandro Milici","!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 09.40.20.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T07:53:55.740Z"],["3832289","LSS-50851","LSS","jens.zarelius@bolt.eu","Jens Zarelius","Morning,\nThey came back with following message in [BH|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/727573895]:\n\nHello,\n\nOn May 15, 2025 you were provided with a request and an order regarding criminal case No. 90080425003.\n\nWe have not received a response to that request.\n\nPlease let us know if you have reviewed the given request and share the information obtained.\n\nRespectfully,\n\nNino Akhalbedashvili Specialist Department of International Relations and Legal Support Division of International Relations Prosecutor General’s Office of Georgia\n\n----\n\nNote from Tier 2:\nHello Team,\n\nWe are following up on the authority request for personal data that was initially received on May 15, 2025.\n\nThis case was previously escalated to your team. Upon review, we found that the response to the authority was sent from your side; however, it was sent to an incorrect email address. As a result, the authority did not receive our communication and therefore did not provide a response.\n\nThe authority has now contacted us again and is requesting a follow-up on this matter.\n\nFor reference:\n\n* The initial ticket can be found [**here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/573642411].**\n* [*Ticket 1*|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/582394488] and [*Ticket 2*|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/582477775] were sent to the incorrect email address.\n\nPlease let us know the next steps so we can ensure proper follow-up with the authority.","2026-01-23T07:54:17.584Z"],["3832290","PFI-837569","PFI","thitinon.decharattanasub@bolt-outsource.eu","Thitinon Decharattanasub","!Screenshot 21 .10 thb.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260123-075312.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260123-075327.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T07:54:22.277Z"],["3832291","DSR-2999","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] , this looks great! Thanks a lot and no comment from me. I have no strong preference concerning who sends this - perhaps it might come across as more “official” if sent via the Legal team inbox. Would you be all right with handling this? We’ll then remain at the ready should any more help with sourcing data or privacy concerns arise as a follow-up 🙏 ","2026-01-23T07:55:09.750Z"],["3832293","LSS-61302","LSS","gauchar.alibayeva@bolt.eu","Gauchar Alibayeva","Hi [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] ,\n\nI think they were confused by the fact that in order to create a BA they have to agree with T&Cs and now we are saying MSA writes it off and asking what’s the precedence. \n\n[INBEV  Agreement |https://docs.google.com/document/d/18LQrPPXjU34N1RLro-Wh0KgA99A6U59s/edit] please find attached the agreement doc with legal team’s comments. I have a meeting with them on Monday 9 am and would appreciate if you can help with feedback.\n\nThank you🙏 ","2026-01-23T07:55:29.781Z"],["3832297","DSR-3919","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] Sorry my bad, fixed it 😅 ","2026-01-23T07:56:02.080Z"],["3832300","LSS-62046","LSS","migle.zuvelyte@bolt.eu","Miglė Žuvelytė","[^Sutartis Bolt _ Skrivanek 2026.pdf] _(319 kB)_","2026-01-23T07:57:57.119Z"],["3832301","SCM-1116","SCM","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:5fa01e19aea468006a8a298e] thanks! What were the quantities we ordered?","2026-01-23T07:58:08.335Z"],["3832304","FRAUD-5751","FRAUD","ivan.honchar@bolt.eu","Ivan Honchar","Was fixed in scope of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FRAUD-5742|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FRAUD-5742|smart-link] \n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161368|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161368]","2026-01-23T07:58:28.591Z"],["3832306","RDS-1227","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] an important topic, but IMO it is around improving our pricing logic, not Quality Debt. ","2026-01-23T07:58:52.104Z"],["3832307","FX-3679","FX","dmitry.andrienko@bolt.eu","Dzmitry Andryienka","# Suspension status column shows custom mapping for suspension status:\nIf car hase active suspension → “Suspended”\notherwise → “Active”\n\nFilter by “Status” filter out by Car Status correctly, it is just not reflected in table\n# Same reason for “blocked” filter: it filter out cars with “blocked” status, not with active suspension (as it can be in other views)\n# When car is deactivated, it has “Suspended” suspension status in table because it has active suspension, however, the car status is still “Active”\n","2026-01-23T08:00:23.925Z"],["3832309","RDXENG-4736","RDXENG","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","Actually I forgot I already have a ticket for this:\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/RDS/ideas/view/6301152?selectedIssue=RDS-1103|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/RDS/ideas/view/6301152?selectedIssue=RDS-1103|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T08:01:00.979Z"],["3832310","DSR-2883","DSR","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","[~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] Hey! On the response letter you’ve provided a link to our internal CSPC Drive. The data should be here [https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0AK1yA4P_a3nVUk9PVA|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0AK1yA4P_a3nVUk9PVA] and we should include a link from the external drive for the driver-specific folder. ","2026-01-23T08:01:12.635Z"],["3832311","RDS-1103","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","Related:\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDXENG-4736?focusedCommentId=3830496&sourceType=mention|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDXENG-4736?focusedCommentId=3830496&sourceType=mention|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T08:01:14.945Z"],["3832312","SCM-1116","SCM","lisha.ye@bolt.eu","Lisha Ye","!image-20260123-080100.png|width=593,alt=\"image-20260123-080100.png\"!\n\nhere is the list, total price 234.94 EUR [~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] ","2026-01-23T08:01:17.118Z"],["3832313","G3IOT-1214","G3IOT","kaarel.vandler@bolt.eu","Kaarel Vandler","sure, i'll write it down","2026-01-23T08:01:26.378Z"],["3832314","XP-2946","XP",null,"Automation for Jira","The issue has not been updated in the past week.\n\nPlease update the status and/or comment about the progress.","2026-01-23T08:01:33.138Z"],["3832315","EBIKE1-226","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:624b3bdf8678e900705d9004] Let’s make the wall a bit higher and go with this solution. It won’t affect the certification. And let’s get the cost as well. ","2026-01-23T08:02:20.950Z"],["3832317","DRAG-701","DRAG","zixi.chen@bolt.eu","Zixi Chen","I sent the email to TWS and claimed the LG cell issue in September last year.\n\nToday, I also contacted TWS again:\n\nTWS informed me that they had already contacted Janeli and explained that they still needed 20 batteries for analysis. Subsequently, a preliminary result could be obtained. Moreover, the warranty period they have with LG is usually only one year. Still, they will conduct a new round of in-depth negotiations with LG based on the analysis results for the current situation.","2026-01-23T08:02:53.646Z"],["3832318","WEBSD-1500","WEBSD","emma.sjoo@bolt.eu","Emma Sjöö","It will be used on a scooter/e-bike sticker\n\nDen tors 22 jan. 2026 20:14Jevgeni Komkin (JIRA) <jira@taxify.atlassian.net>\nskrev:\n\n> Jevgeni Komkin * added a new comment*.\n> ------------------------------\n> Web Service Desk\n> <https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WEBSD?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiOWRiYzkxMzg1YWE4NGQ1ZGFjZjNjMDYxZmZiMDYzYWYiLCJwIjoiaiJ9>\n>  / WEBSD-1500\n> <https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WEBSD-1500?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiOWRiYzkxMzg1YWE4NGQ1ZGFjZjNjMDYxZmZiMDYzYWYiLCJwIjoiaiJ9>\n> QR Cod – Leading to the Rider Scoter View for rentals in the app\n> <https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WEBSD-1500?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiOWRiYzkxMzg1YWE4NGQ1ZGFjZjNjMDYxZmZiMDYzYWYiLCJwIjoiaiJ9>\n>\n> [image: Avatar]  *Jevgeni Komkin*  09:11 PM Finland Time\n>\n> Where/how will this be used?\n> View work item\n> <https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WEBSD-1500?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiOWRiYzkxMzg1YWE4NGQ1ZGFjZjNjMDYxZmZiMDYzYWYiLCJwIjoiaiJ9>\n> ------------------------------\n> Open the work item to view attachments over 100 KB\n> Get Jira notifications on your phone! Download the Jira Cloud app for\n> Android\n> <https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.atlassian.android.jira.core&referrer=utm_source%3DNotificationLink%26utm_medium%3DEmail>\n> or iOS\n> <https://itunes.apple.com/app/apple-store/id1006972087?pt=696495&ct=EmailNotificationLink&mt=8>\n> . [image: Product logo]\n> Manage Notifications\n> <https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/settings/personal/notifications?emailPreferences=true#emailpreferences>\n>     Give feedback\n> <https://surveys.atlassian.com/jfe/form/SV_9X3zi1X4q1gKsqF>    Privacy\n> Policy <https://www.atlassian.com/legal/privacy-policy>\n>\n>","2026-01-23T08:03:04.801Z"],["3832321","EBIKE1-425","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","FYI. [~accountid:5e9a112618b8ed0c0f776390] ","2026-01-23T08:04:39.401Z"],["3832322","LSS-61958","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:62134a797580350068337097] , in that case, there is no need to sign a new contract, we need to get an amendment to the existing one. \n\nCould you please share the existing contract? ","2026-01-23T08:05:39.421Z"],["3832324","G3IOT-1214","G3IOT","kaarel.vandler@bolt.eu","Kaarel Vandler","Maybe a way to supress this is to turn off/prohibit input (24V/solar) power use and drain the backup battery to allowed voltage","2026-01-23T08:05:59.730Z"],["3832327","FX-3679","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dzmitry Andryienka [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769155625179759]*{color}:\n<@U09D62DKH9P> please take a look at the answers in ticket comments, this can be a new feature request for cars page update\n{quote}","2026-01-23T08:07:17.650Z"],["3832328","LSS-58904","LSS","anca.grossu@bolt.eu","Anca-Ioana Grossu","Hey Gabrielė,\n\n[Here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QWCeAEOx2_4byXNGICnAfBedQHFw2ZJE/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=117143287911929368650&rtpof=true&sd=true] is the contract reviewed by the provider.","2026-01-23T08:07:34.452Z"],["3832331","G3IOT-1214","G3IOT","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","Possible, but the problem with all this algos which rely on measured BB level is that the level changes a lot depending on if BB is under load or not. Makes it hard to come up with reliable sequence.","2026-01-23T08:08:48.052Z"],["3832334","WD-22556","WD","mirell.puusepp@bolt.eu","Mirell Puusepp","Hey! \n\nFollowing up on that - another invoice is issued to Bolt Operations OÜ showing their Estonian VAT code on the invoice. Do you have any updates, are we able to change it to PY VAT code?\n\nBest wishes\n\nMirell","2026-01-23T08:09:04.571Z"],["3832335","SCM-646","SCM","zixi.chen@bolt.eu","Zixi Chen","Until the end of 2025, we still don’t have any new purchase requests for Scud.\n\nI propose to postpone the 8(10) pcs battery compensation to Q1 - {{2026-03-31}}, and let’s wait and see if we will have any new NG batteries reported.\n\n!image-20260123-080610.png|width=386,alt=\"image-20260123-080610.png\"!","2026-01-23T08:09:06.493Z"],["3832338","FX-3682","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Meruzhan Kerobyan [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769155803999199]*{color}:\nnope, not visible on iOS safari\n\nLinked files:\n* [image.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0AAWD8GBBK/image.png]\n{quote}","2026-01-23T08:10:17.445Z"],["3832340","FX-3682","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Meruzhan Kerobyan [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769155842981419]*{color}:\nbut visible on chrome, so problem is with Safari\n{quote}","2026-01-23T08:10:57.163Z"],["3832344","SCM-1116","SCM","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:5fa01e19aea468006a8a298e] thanks!","2026-01-23T08:11:35.388Z"],["3832346","PFI-808708","PFI","leticija.jurjevic@bolt.eu","Leticija Jurjević","Team, please take a look at this case, the user has been waiting a long time for a response.","2026-01-23T08:11:46.589Z"],["3832352","RDS-1215","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:52a73231-4dc8-4054-82a3-d741603d65af] good point, but I believe it is more of a wider “delight” initiative, not necessarily a Quality Debt. Wdyt?","2026-01-23T08:12:19.907Z"],["3832353","EBIKE1-318","EBIKE1","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","Due time updated to {{2026-02-13}} according to IOT firmware modification availability.","2026-01-23T08:13:12.364Z"],["3832355","PAW-15094","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-product-identity-and-communication-management, pint-capability-itgc\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-23T08:13:41.914Z"],["3832361","SAI-1429","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","Yea, I had same idea in mind when developing it initially. Thanks for creating task for it :pepelove-2:","2026-01-23T08:14:30.756Z"],["3832363","PFI-837574","PFI","jeff.irikefe@bolt-outsource.eu","Jeff Irikefe","!Screenshot_20260123_095405_Gallery.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T08:14:45.742Z"],["3832364","WEB-9954","WEB","elina.heno@bolt.eu","Elina Liina Heno","[~accountid:712020:2bb94136-b4e4-463e-a0f6-8be773ff520f] Hey\n\nThe design of the EcoVadis section is [here|https://www.figma.com/design/qz9SOBzRMlbW6kG64veD17/Bolt-Web-3.0-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Company?node-id=2236-61812&t=ehOZ1FbfbAihGnf4-1] in Figma.\n\nThe logo of EcoVadis is [here|https://drive.google.com/open?id=19XR1VlElhw5ovhl_fZKotE0n6n9nIDNg&usp=drive_fs] in Drive.\n\nThe Rohetiiger logo in Driver is already in the right aspect ratio, the media container should be resized from 1:1 to 4:3 in CMS.\n\nI also removed the South Pole card from the list of partners in Figma.","2026-01-23T08:15:03.490Z"],["3832365","BDB-1551","BDB",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Taaniel Malleus 👋. This is a reminder, that the task is due today or it's resolved but hasn't been moved to \"Done\" status yet.\n\n- If the task is resolved, move it to the \"Done\" status. Or if the task is canceled, move it to \"Canceled\" status\n\n- If the task can't be resolved in the initial timeframe, then make sure that the Project Manager(Team Lead, in case PM is not available), and Customer are notified. And change the new due date accordingly.","2026-01-23T08:15:15.979Z"],["3832366","BDB-1528","BDB",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Polina Petuhhova 👋. This is a reminder, that the task is due today or it's resolved but hasn't been moved to \"Done\" status yet.\n\n- If the task is resolved, move it to the \"Done\" status. Or if the task is canceled, move it to \"Canceled\" status\n\n- If the task can't be resolved in the initial timeframe, then make sure that the Project Manager(Team Lead, in case PM is not available), and Customer are notified. And change the new due date accordingly.","2026-01-23T08:15:15.991Z"],["3832367","LSS-61958","LSS","aleksandr.parshikov@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Parshikov","Hi! We do not have an existing contract. It is a partner who was providing services without one. We tendered services with the template shared by Legal - added commercial terms and need to do a small change in the text + Legal approval. ","2026-01-23T08:15:40.780Z"],["3832369","XP-2121","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","[~accountid:712020:3f46b943-bb22-4289-83f6-326f708a1f24] yes, ill add to Methodology","2026-01-23T08:15:46.126Z"],["3832371","LSS-62047","LSS","sami.elchami@bolt.eu","Sami El-Chami","[^MV Luisenweg 99.pdf] _(2.14 MB)_","2026-01-23T08:16:38.528Z"],["3832372","EBIOT-245","EBIOT","kaarel.vandler@bolt.eu","Kaarel Vandler","Measurements were carried out and results are visible here\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cgkb4tcfoZ-80L3oTIe_O8gUnGLdqJaOGcRU1RscdOk/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cgkb4tcfoZ-80L3oTIe_O8gUnGLdqJaOGcRU1RscdOk/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T08:16:45.225Z"],["3832374","XP-2169","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","[~accountid:712020:3f46b943-bb22-4289-83f6-326f708a1f24] No, I don’t think so for new scorecard","2026-01-23T08:17:01.817Z"],["3832375","MLC-3181","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 23rd*+\n\n* *Updates will by added EOD*\n** Will repull numbers today\n** If there is no improvement in the coversion rate to point towards recovery, will revert to initial strategy by EOD Monday.","2026-01-23T08:17:53.409Z"],["3832376","PFI-798762","PFI","martin.paroll@bolt.eu","Martin Paroll","The debt is due to pre 2023 cash orders.","2026-01-23T08:17:59.337Z"],["3832378","PFI-798762","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-23T08:18:03.328Z"],["3832381","LSS-61280","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:712020:ef6a9562-f9aa-4bb5-a4d5-2b18cc77085b] I am closing the ticket since the request is completed. ","2026-01-23T08:18:14.123Z"],["3832384","LSS-62021","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hey [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] took a quick look at this and it doesn’t seem to have any privacy questions, so our support shouldn’t be needed. But shout if you think otherwise and we’ll get right onto it 😉 ","2026-01-23T08:18:30.256Z"],["3832385","DSR-2883","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] ! To recap:\n\n* In the [external Drive|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0AK1yA4P_a3nVUk9PVA], please create a folder with the Driver’s full name and add the data inside it. \nYou might need to download it from your internal GDrive and then upload it to this drive (as we don’t want to move the data and risk this being deleted).\n* Once that’s done, the hyperlink for the driver’s folder (*not the whole drive*) can be referenced in the response\n* [~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] can then grant access + set a reminder to remove it after 7 days\n\n----\n\nOnce the above is done, please carry on as follows: \n\n# *Response letter to the driver*: Once the link has been added to the answer letter, send a copy of the answer letter to the driver in *PDF* format with the below cover message:\n\n{quote}Dear [name],\nThank you for your data subject request, which was submitted by Worker Info Exchange on your behalf (with reference number [*insert reference number listed in WIE letter]*). We provide the information in response to your request in the document attached, including a link to the personal data you requested - please note that this data will remain available for download for *7 days* from the date of sending this message.\nYours sincerely,\nBolt{quote}\n\n# *Response letter to WIE:* Once the answer letter has been sent to the user, send the following message to WIE:\n\n{quote}Dear Worker Info Exchange,\nPlease note that we have actioned the data subject rights request submitted on behalf of [*insert driver's name*] (with reference number [*insert reference number listed in WIE letter*]) by responding to the data subject directly. If you have any questions in this regard, please let us know.\nYours sincerely,\nBolt{quote}","2026-01-23T08:18:33.665Z"],["3832386","MLC-2962","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 23rd*+\n\n* *No Updates this week*\n* *Relaunch of Card BINs / Geofencing* - Templates to be rebuilt and tested next week. Will start with Card BINs and test Signal sequentially to avoid noise - will need a grace period of 1-2 week to ascertain that everything is running as expected and results signal towards an uplift.","2026-01-23T08:18:34.474Z"],["3832387","WD-22666","WD","olesja.timofejeva@bolt.eu","Olesja Timofejeva","Hey! I see in WD, that a region “Accounting 2” was assigned to me, but actually the region Accounting 4 should be assigned instead. \n\nCoudl you please check ASAP? I lost an access to all the entities and I am not able to do the urgent tasks. ","2026-01-23T08:18:46.445Z"],["3832388","CNT-341","CNT","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","[~accountid:621c92ba4160640069c52776] Hey, pics are also ready: [https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/19GM-f_vCyeiOdA4RGix7sOlj55TQP0Tn?usp=share_link|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/19GM-f_vCyeiOdA4RGix7sOlj55TQP0Tn?usp=share_link|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T08:19:06.472Z"],["3832389","LSS-62047","LSS","sami.elchami@bolt.eu","Sami El-Chami","here is the contract - signed pdf is needed \n\n[^MV Luisenweg 99 (f103ca88-0114-488b-bd51-237e9ba9e10f).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-23T08:19:28.658Z"],["3832390","PFI-837581","PFI","mia.hartova@bolt.eu","Mia Hartová","!image001.png.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image005.png.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T08:19:38.645Z"],["3832393","WEBSD-1473","WEBSD","rostislav.popov@bolt.eu","Rostislav Popov","Hi Hector,\n\nAs soon as there is a link with at least one article, please share it. This is needed for the next exercise that is dependant on the current one.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-23T08:20:20.967Z"],["3832394","DELIVERY-1043","DELIVERY","tiberiu.vasile@bolt.eu","Constantin-Tiberiu Vasile","26W3: \n\n* *Done* - Create Admin Panel API\n** Reviewed changes again after returning from vacation and deployed to live\n* *In Progress -* Update multiplier query to include ad-hoc overrides\n** Working on logic to handle aggregation of ad-hoc multipliers with baseline multipliers for clients based on rolling window of the Courier app","2026-01-23T08:20:22.720Z"],["3832396","MLC-2749","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 23rd*+\n\n* *No updates this week*\n* Changes to the new segments by Monday EOD\n* Adding PL to the mix by Monday EOD\n* +*Next steps*+\n** Clone out for the rest of the markets and push live - Next week (allowing one week of testing new approach on a set of markets)\n** Redo templates after confirmation on working template.\n** Implement for CEE markets - then move of to rest of markets","2026-01-23T08:20:54.629Z"],["3832401","CCM-22302","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey [~accountid:64182443b05b4e3e7daa195b]  👋 \n\nOnboarding has been enrolled. 🙂 \n\nBest,\nIrena","2026-01-23T08:22:03.467Z"],["3832402","PFI-836638","PFI","patrik.kupco@bolt.eu","Patrik Kupčo","Hey [~accountid:626a69abb31e6f0068634a56] ,\n\nin that case, how are Individual couriers expected to handle their accounting for the earnings they receive from us?","2026-01-23T08:22:53.553Z"],["3832405","LSS-60908","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","The orders from Thailand (22 Dec 2025 - 23 Jan 2026) I’ve identified in Admin: [2588605564 ↗|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2588605564/1004?orderTryId=3486714221], [2588626290 ↗|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2588626290/1004?orderTryId=3486750144], [2590531300 ↗|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-h