panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2637265151/1003?orderTryId=3566299732], [2644517650 ↗|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2644517650/2059?orderTryId=3578548403], [2644517650 ↗|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2644517650/2059?orderTryId=3578547726], [2644517650 ↗|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2644517650/2059?orderTryId=3578546924], [2644518792 ↗|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2644518792/2059?orderTryId=3578549294], [2651250479 ↗|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2651250479/881?orderTryId=3590205993]\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] ","2026-01-23T08:23:09.586Z"],["3832406","CNT-461","CNT","adam.cherry@bolt.eu","Adam Cherry","[~accountid:632d4729fedc6169aed5c944] Thanks for this. Quick question: How does the cashback work with Bolt Food?","2026-01-23T08:23:54.119Z"],["3832408","MKP-9913","MKP","abdelhalim.machehalek@bolt.eu","Abdelhalim Machehalek","we'll be able to make the change beginning of next week","2026-01-23T08:24:07.544Z"],["3832409","SREDESK-7447","SREDESK","dmitrii.shaburov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Shaburov","Since it's went into next sprint, I'm closing this ticked to keep service desk queue clean","2026-01-23T08:24:13.049Z"],["3832414","INT-578","INT","samuel.castaneda@bolt.eu","Samuel Castaneda","[~accountid:5f23e70bb7a35e002a73ef5d] based on linked epic, it looks like this one is already in development.","2026-01-23T08:24:55.570Z"],["3832415","BP-13321","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","[~accountid:712020:8973d5d2-02e2-4150-b678-3f91914bf467] Daria wants the banner to be in Home (Dashboard) and also in the Billing page. I made a [design|https://www.figma.com/design/KDcUkqeHVRhV6PeHU2SS0y/Team-Account---Billing?node-id=13588-21373&t=IXnpxG2jJeNujW2G-4], pls focus just on the banners, it is an old design that I am flipping to the current, and the architecture of the page content is off, and I am working on it.\n\nAs a rule, the users might have dept notification, it should still be the top one and the new one about the legal entity under it. This rule applies to both the Home (Dashboard) and Billing page. \n\nJust want to confirm, can we tie the Legal entity banner per admin, not company, aka if they press Got it, it will be gone only for the Admin, not whole organisation?","2026-01-23T08:24:57.391Z"],["3832416","DELIVERY-751","DELIVERY","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","\n\n26W4\n\n*Backend*\n\n* Logistic planning finished development of a new endpoint. Next week we will switch to a new endpoint \n* Next week we are going to backfill for missing data, eventually we will have 3 months data\n* Next week will be done development to support city name translation\n\n*Front*\n\n* Continue addressing review notes","2026-01-23T08:25:25.425Z"],["3832417","CCM-22303","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hi Peace 👋 \n\nDorcas is currently under externalOPS branch. Did she change the branch?\n","2026-01-23T08:25:38.152Z"],["3832421","FX-3678","FX","dmitry.andrienko@bolt.eu","Dzmitry Andryienka","Column settings are stored in standard browser local storage, it works on brweser level across tabs, you can see in *Applicaiotn → Local Storage → table_column_settings_driver-list-table* setting in DevTools if needed.","2026-01-23T08:26:33.669Z"],["3832423","FX-3636","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dzmitry Andryienka [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769156815731039]*{color}:\nColumn settings are stored in standard browser local storage, it works on browser level across tabs, you can see in *Applicaiotn → Local Storage → table_column_settings_driver-list-table* setting in DevTools if needed\n{quote}","2026-01-23T08:27:12.151Z"],["3832425","PFI-837235","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","The company has been under the Credit Card Billing Type before the August 26th, so back then each ride was immediately charged from credit card.\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/audit-log/audit-logs?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"start_time\"%3A1711918800%2C\"entity_id\"%3A775160%2C\"entity_type\"%3A\"business_invoicing_company\"}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/audit-log/audit-logs?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start_time%22%3A1711918800%2C%22entity_id%22%3A775160%2C%22entity_type%22%3A%22business_invoicing_company%22%7D%7D]","2026-01-23T08:27:46.263Z"],["3832426","FX-3636","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769156855361869]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3636 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-23T08:27:47.122Z"],["3832428","LSS-61616","LSS","tatsiana.sivukha@bolt.eu","Tatsiana Sivukha","Thanks [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] \n\nI have reviewed the response and left some clarifying comments.","2026-01-23T08:28:13.604Z"],["3832429","PFI-835934","PFI","iryna.tkach@bolt-outsource.eu","Iryna Tkach","[~accountid:62026399c4e2c9006ae5fb59] or [~accountid:5adef5687dd1e556227b7b2a] , can you help me or provide my request to needed agent?","2026-01-23T08:28:16.649Z"],["3832434","LSS-60908","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","I’ve launched an investigation with engineers in #*dev-user-auth-support* [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06R63EQ6CS/p1769156826600099].\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] ","2026-01-23T08:28:45.827Z"],["3832437","PASD-176","PASD","sohail.nikouzad@bolt.eu","Sohail Nikouzad","Hi, the accesses have been granted.\r\n\r\nBest.","2026-01-23T08:29:23.057Z"],["3832438","EBIKE1-396","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","[optitrans.ee|http://optitrans.ee] sheet rubber sourcing place. Quite cheap m2 and min qty relatively low\n\nEPDM\n\noutdoor use\n\n2mm thick \n\nblack\n\n60Sh\n\n20.88eur/m2","2026-01-23T08:29:23.905Z"],["3832440","FX-3679","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769156942650079]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3679 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-23T08:29:27.095Z"],["3832444","PFI-836454","PFI","daniels.kulcihins@bolt-outsource.eu","Daniels Kulcihins","Hello!\n\nThere is a payout link: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"start\"%3A1768168800%2C\"show_empty_rejection_code\"%3Afalse%2C\"show_total\"%3Afalse%2C\"external_client_id\"%3A212911}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start%22%3A1768168800%2C%22show_empty_rejection_code%22%3Afalse%2C%22show_total%22%3Afalse%2C%22external_client_id%22%3A212911%7D%7D]\n\nAs we can see, no payouts were registered for this Fleet. Please assist.","2026-01-23T08:30:09.623Z"],["3832445","FX-3696","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769157032132789]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3696 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-23T08:30:43.949Z"],["3832446","LSS-62049","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-23T08:31:07.401Z"],["3832448","LEG-1325","LEG","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey! Ticket is reassigned to [~accountid:612f31d89976c300693ebaf7]. He is well aware with the DK model for Rides and is the right poc to help you out.","2026-01-23T08:31:36.505Z"],["3832449","INSUR-172","INSUR","alessandro@bolt.eu","Alessandro Milici","Possibility of getting Cargo-style insurance due to the free-floating nature of our assets. \n\nData collection to be confirmed with Carlo and MM Central Ops. \n\n\n\nMessage from Ardo: \n\nOK, I'd urge you to open still a further discussion on what could be done next. Like a coverage for €2m can also be a deal with €1m deductible? Which essentially means that we'll self-insure the expensive part.\nThen it's the third party insurance that's still open.\nFor the insurers \"want to know what is in place at our units regarding fire and theft prevention\" - this is information we can put together extremely quickly and we have it. It can change over time but we've always had this info. Is there an ETA for Alessandro on this? All-in-all - I'd suggest a meeting to go over our current challenges and agree on actions forward.\n\n* TBD with Dan","2026-01-23T08:31:48.917Z"],["3832451","RDS-1212","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] Important thing, but I wonder if it is something we can tackle from the RiderX perspective, and although we can tackle specific localisation examples, improving localisation in general will likely require more procedural changes about how we are tackling localisation. Wdyt?","2026-01-23T08:31:51.747Z"],["3832454","HS-29290","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Task sent to Global Mobility.","2026-01-23T08:32:01.705Z"],["3832459","MLC-3821","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","* Email and Pushes campaign live 21.01 - 5,2k compliant already.\n* In-apps live 21.01","2026-01-23T08:32:39.437Z"],["3832461","FX-3679","FX","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","hey [~accountid:712020:3081727f-5ce0-4ec9-9ebc-e80faceb3d21] \n\n# Suspension status column shows custom mapping for suspension status:\nIf car hase active suspension → “Suspended”\notherwise → “Active”\n_Yes agreed, my point was the column header says suspension status and then the same logic is not applied to the ‘status’ when I open the car, which is inconsistent_\n\nFilter by “Status” filter out by Car Status correctly, it is just not reflected in table\n_Not sure what you mean by this?_ \n\n# Same reason for “blocked” filter: it filter out cars with “blocked” status, not with active suspension (as it can be in other views)\n_Is there actually a blocked status? Is this one of our values in the DB? The customer cannot set a car to ‘blocked’, I don’t see a user in Admin UI can update status to blocked, so I don’t see that this can actually be set anywhere, hence why no results. I believe the intention here is probbaly that blocked = active suspension, which was my interpretation._ \n\n# When car is deactivated, it has “Suspended” suspension status in table because it has active suspension, however, the car status is still “Active”\n_Agreed, but this should show universally in all status fields, not status = suspended in table and status = active when you click on a car._ ","2026-01-23T08:32:51.081Z"],["3832462","INSUR-12","INSUR","alessandro@bolt.eu","Alessandro Milici","The policy has been renewed with PROBITAS. \n\nWaiting for documentation from HWS. ","2026-01-23T08:33:09.712Z"],["3832463","BEE-3491","BEE","anton.lapin@bolt.eu","Anton Lapin","Yeah, and the problem why we cannot process refund to Bolt Balance is because one of the items was refunded to card, so it is marked on the UI as refunded and cannot be refunded once again:\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/283151526?cityId=427&showUserTz=false|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/283151526?cityId=427&showUserTz=false] - full order price is 362.06 czk\n\nagent refunded Fried Rice Noodles with Chicken for 84.08 czk to card (this is how much was paid from card), but fried noodles costed 141 czk so remaining amount that needs to be refunded to bolt balance is not possible because fried noodles item is displayed as refunded, so we need to allow it and just care amount refund items, not quantities of the items refunded as you can potentially refund for one item twice.\n\n!image-20260123-083112.png|width=650,alt=\"image-20260123-083112.png\"!","2026-01-23T08:33:25.487Z"],["3832465","DRX-28362","DRX","anton.grunichev@bolt.eu","Anton Grunichev","It's a feature request, not a duty item","2026-01-23T08:33:58.970Z"],["3832466","LSS-56938","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hi[~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] \nI’ve made suggestions to the [DSA|https://docs.google.com/document/d/125o395bpmCwcIyETink5Eb72-twZ0SvE/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=116489701835779910985&rtpof=true&sd=true] and closing the ticket.\nIf anything comes-up, please let me know by tagging me 🙏 \n\nThank you and have a wonderful day ahead!","2026-01-23T08:34:02.578Z"],["3832468","FX-3679","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769157241329309]*{color}:\nokay, responded to you in the ticket, i'm still not clear. happy to treat it as an improvement (although i consider it a bug :wink: ) but let's just transition this ticket, it has all the requirements and comments, versus closing this and making me do another :slightly_smiling_face: you can move it to the improvements epic and backlog.\n{quote}","2026-01-23T08:34:13.857Z"],["3832472","RDS-1191","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:648af4f5-f134-458a-b3aa-9320408d346e] added prio. Feel free to adapt.","2026-01-23T08:34:53.736Z"],["3832477","INSUR-171","INSUR","alessandro@bolt.eu","Alessandro Milici","* *English Global insurance hub* - {{/en/insurance/}} - the main hub (English Global) with regional selector (the same we have on [this page|https://bolt.eu/en/legal/]). No buttons/CTAs on single vertical insurance pages, so we should have an H1/title, a subheading (if needed), and intro text here. When you select the region, it will be redirected to the main language's hub page of this region (if Italy is selected, then {{/it-it/insurance/}} in Italian will be open)\n* *Regional insurance hub* - {{/xx-xx/insurance/}} (like {{/en-it/}} or {{/it-it/}}) - basically the same content and structure as the English Global hub page (below), but with variables like {country} and buttons/CTA of only available insurance per each region (in {{/en-it/}} and {{/it-it/}} it will be only \"Micromobility\", and so on), we can leave the regional selector here as well (the same as we have [here|https://bolt.eu/de-at/legal/]).\n** *Single vertical insurance page* - {{/xx-xx/insurance/{vertical}}} (rides _(both riders and drivers)_, micromobility, delivery, drive) - we will be having single vertical insurance pages (upon availability), but also with the limited content from [@liisi.tamra|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U0558FR765R] (H1, intro, etc. - we just need to add there each vertical and for whom this page was created) as the main content will be the one that [@alessandro|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U5SMD1URZ] and [@erich.pullerits|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U030W2JPF7D] are gathering in their file [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Z3ogAVqt5RWxwlflr7qakpHpddmfa4JRBVMCDVENG60/edit?gid=0#gid=0] per each region and each vertical. Examples of these pages:\n*** {{/xx-xx/insurance/rides/}}\n*** {{/xx-xx/insurance/delivery/}}\n*** {{/xx-xx/insurance/micromobility/}}\n*** {{/xx-xx/insurance/drive/}}\n\n*Things to consider in the future:*\n\n* We can also create the English Global single vertical pages with the generic content for each vertical's insurance (which is applicable for all regions and languages), the same way that Lime has it [here|https://www.li.me/en-pt/insurance]:\n** {{/en/insurance/rides/}}\n** {{/en/insurance/delivery/}}\n** {{/en/insurance/micromobility/}}\n** {{/en/insurance/drive/}}\n* Later on, we can create a single page (like Lime has it [here|https://www.li.me/insurance/insurance-docs]) with all countries and insurance list, it can be done in two ways:\n** 1 - We create only one page under {{/en/insurance/}}, like {{/en/insurance/countries/}} (or {{/docs/}}) and have all verticals and regions there, everything in one place (regions (the main heading) and then subheadings with verticals for each region):\n*** Example:\n**** Italy is mentioned in this list, but only for the Micromobility section, like Italy -> Micromobility and then doc or page\n** 2 - We create 4 pages under each vertical and show regions there where we have this or that insurance:\n*** {{/en/insurance/rides/countries/}}\n*** {{/en/insurance/delivery/countries/}}\n*** {{/en/insurance/micromobility/countries/}}\n*** {{/en/insurance/drive/countries/}}\n**** Example:\n***** Italy we have mentioned only here - {{/en/insurance/micromobility/countries/}}","2026-01-23T08:35:42.226Z"],["3832478","DRAG101-287","DRAG101","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] [~accountid:63d0ecd1d73cd1e44e22078f] do we still have interest in this development with retyre?\n\nI sent a quick email them to remind about us, but do we actually want to go forward with this any more?","2026-01-23T08:35:53.434Z"],["3832482","WD-22672","WD","dieulinh.tran@bolt.eu","Diệu Linh Tran","[^02122025 (1).docx]\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 09.33.55.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T08:36:37.157Z"],["3832483","LSS-61412","LSS","kristiana.hoha@bolt.eu","Kristiāna Hoha","Thank you very much! Yes, sorry — normally I also ask the client to make all the changes themselves. Thank you very much for the edits. Contract send to client for approval .","2026-01-23T08:36:39.414Z"],["3832486","MARTECH3-1554","MARTECH3","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","*HTML editor*:\n\n* Highlighting Braze liquids is a nice feature and worked as expected. \n* Typos in user properties were also highlighted correctly, but it’s a bit difficult to find the exact problem when the text is also highlighted in green. Since the error is also displayed as text below the editor, it’s not a critical issue. Example:\n!Screenshot 2026-01-21 at 12.19.14.png|width=709,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-21 at 12.19.14.png\"!\n\n\n\n💡  Suggestion: It would be good if we were able to change the size of the content vs preview sections. Right now, they are 50:50, but having the option to move where it splits would make reading the HTML a bit easier in some cases. Braze example here:\n\n!Screen Recording 2026-01-23 at 10.41.13.mov|width=528,alt=\"Screen Recording 2026-01-23 at 10.41.13.mov\"!\n\n\n\n*Preview testing*:\n\n* Sending a test email inside the content editor worked as expected.\n* The “User data to oveerride” section could be a bit easier to use. \n** For example, it could detect which properties are used in the content and show a drop-down list of them. Selecting one would make the property appear in the code field, e.g. {{{\"user_profile\": {\"first_name\": \"X\"}},}} where X can be replaced with your value. This approach would save our team a lot of time.\n* *-The “testing“ tab does not allow me to send any tests-*-. It’s giving “Failed to send test message“ error each time. Maybe I am setting it up incorrectly?- Solved (/) \n\n\n\n\n\n💡 NB this is unrelated to the task, but these improvements would be really good to have:\n\n* After selecting “Make ready for translation“, there is no way to roll it back to make changes in it. Unfortunately, there are many cases where we need to make small edits to templates later, so it would be useful to move them back to the draft status.\n* I’d appreciate having the option to open the email templates, email variants, and content blocks in another tab (usually with command + click). We often need to open multiple at once, and it saves a lot of time when you don’t need to start your search from 0 again.","2026-01-23T08:36:52.861Z"],["3832488","LSS-61245","LSS","kristiina.taube@bolt.eu","Kristiina Taube","Hey [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] In case of a corporate card payment, the payer’s payment which is made by card may ultimately not go to the Bolt account which is indicated in the Company Dashboard. As I understand, the account we display in the Company Dashboard is the account to which Company will pay based on their monthly invoice. \n\nWe should also consider, as much as possible today, how the platform payments will flow in the future via the Bolt Payments (EMI), where Bolt Business customer’s payments (either based on monthly invoice or card) might go to Bolt Payments, not the Bolt Platform Entity account. So with [~accountid:712020:822a759a-daf0-4161-afbf-8b79a2985fba] when we discussed potential wording for the debt settlement clause, we tried to come up with a wording as generic as possible to cover the potential use cases.","2026-01-23T08:37:10.737Z"],["3832489","PAW-14756","PAW","cristian.lupu@bolt.eu","Cristian Lupu","I have unassigned myself because I couldn’t find anything wrong 😞\n\nHopefully the next person can actually help and close the support ticket","2026-01-23T08:37:38.187Z"],["3832490","LSS-61965","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:5c2e559fb4d5d75a3b51c7c8] unfortunately I can’t access Beehive, if there are any relevant portions of the ticket please will you screenshot them and compile into an incident report for me, thanks. ","2026-01-23T08:37:47.753Z"],["3832491","CSP-344","CSP","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","26W04: Fix blocking the release was released. Canary testing will continue now.","2026-01-23T08:37:50.483Z"],["3832492","INSUR-178","INSUR","alessandro@bolt.eu","Alessandro Milici","* HWS provided a form that needs to be filled out. \n** Jira Ticket for InfoSec team submitted: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/17/ISS-1169?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ0Z3QiOiJhbm9ueW1vdXMtbGluayIsInFzaCI6IjY4NWEyYTRkNmZhMjk1Mzg0ZDc2NDE5NmE5NjFhYzA2MDM0N2JmMDYyMGY1MjU4Yjk1MTcwZmI3NmQ4M2I5M2MiLCJpc3MiOiJzZXJ2aWNlZGVzay1qd3QtdG9rZW4taXNzdWVyIiwiY29udGV4dCI6eyJ1c2VyIjoiMTA3NTciLCJpc3N1ZSI6IklTUy0xMTY5In0sImV4cCI6MTc3MTQwMDk0MiwiaWF0IjoxNzY4OTgxNzQyfQ.CgfD3kG4GLNsuKAQ5AMpTa3S-jCxve5bpGOuKthzeu0|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/17/ISS-1169?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ0Z3QiOiJhbm9ueW1vdXMtbGluayIsInFzaCI6IjY4NWEyYTRkNmZhMjk1Mzg0ZDc2NDE5NmE5NjFhYzA2MDM0N2JmMDYyMGY1MjU4Yjk1MTcwZmI3NmQ4M2I5M2MiLCJpc3MiOiJzZXJ2aWNlZGVzay1qd3QtdG9rZW4taXNzdWVyIiwiY29udGV4dCI6eyJ1c2VyIjoiMTA3NTciLCJpc3N1ZSI6IklTUy0xMTY5In0sImV4cCI6MTc3MTQwMDk0MiwiaWF0IjoxNzY4OTgxNzQyfQ.CgfD3kG4GLNsuKAQ5AMpTa3S-jCxve5bpGOuKthzeu0|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T08:37:59.183Z"],["3832494","MLC-657","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","*Taiwan*\n\n* WP: All stages set up in Figma and sent for proofreading.\n\n*Dubai* \n\n* *WP:* Acquisition, Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Retention, Churn *LIVE*\n* *BU:* Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Retention, Churn, Promo Codes, HVO *LIVE*\n* *BA:* *Acquisition - 7 strings needs translation and proofreading - no updates from the localisation team.* \n* *BA:* Onboarding, Product Education, 0 Orders, Awareness, HVO, Promo Codes, Churn *LIVE*","2026-01-23T08:38:19.825Z"],["3832498","LSS-61302","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","hi, [~accountid:712020:52c03b81-3e44-455b-a71d-0e9088f7c7ad] [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] . I would suggest to incorporate an explicit provision in the MSA that any BB T&C technically accepted in BA while registering do not apply to the customer and the MSA is binding only. \n\nI am not practically able to review the agreement by Monday, 9 am due to other priorities booked for today before). \n\nMy ETA is Tuesday eod. ","2026-01-23T08:39:47.980Z"],["3832500","WD-22623","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello [~accountid:62ea2a72da8620d53392aa71] all accesses granted","2026-01-23T08:40:35.629Z"],["3832503","MLC-3710","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 23rd*+\n\n* Worked with Martech to define methodology to finalize queries.\n* We noticed multiple mismatches across all stages. Core reasons are:\n** Changes is user state from observable month (September 2025) to current date. Examples: Users opted out, became Business Users / Admins.\n** Discrepancies between data in Braze vs data in source tables\n* Numbers are now closer to expected numbers, but gaps are still sizeable enough not to be considered accurate.\n\n\n\n+*All Stages Issue:*+ User custom attributes used (consents, is business user, company status) for targeting changed values from true to false (and vice-versa) since September.\n\n*Next Steps:*\n\n* We are pivoting to a more recent month to avoid this. Although initially we discussed using September as an observable month since it had less tests going on, this has proved to be more complex due to changing attributes value.\n* We will also investigate the logic behind the company status to understand how it is being populated in Braze and what is the source data.\n\n\n\n+*Onboarding Issue:*+ The current logic looks only at Company creation in observable month. This leaves out users who did other onboarding actions (verified email, added billing details). This leaves out a big portion of our targetable companies and again creates cases where if seems we contact user that fall outside of the addressable base.\n\n*Next Steps:*\n\n* Map all core actions for observation month - Sign Up, Email Verified, Add Billing Details. Right now we have cases of users Signing up in previous months and performing Email Verification in observation month.\n\n\n\n+*Activation Issue:*+ We have found multiple data inconsistencies: orders before activation, null activation dates, mismatch with Braze. Core reason is the activation date in source table does not capture all activation paths, has timezone differences vs orders, and contains legacy inconsistencies (pre-2022), so it does not always reflect the true moment a company became active.\n\n*Next Steps:*\n\n* Due to finding that the Account Activated event can trigger multiple times, we need to exclude companies with order count > 0. We have the needed attribute, we just need to make updates in Braze\n* Continue collaborating with the data team on cases where first_activation_date is completely missing\n\n\n\n+*Churn Issue:*+ Found use cases where table last order is different in the source table vs Braze data. We also found discrepancies between different business tables where orders with different tracking countries are not updated in the Business Company last_order_date data. \n\n*Next Steps:*\n\n* Deepdive in the Business Order Finished event query to understand which tables the data is pulled from and how is it flowing in Braze\n* Work with Data team to understand logic between the two tables and why some orders are not reflected in both tables.","2026-01-23T08:40:53.735Z"],["3832507","WD-22673","WD","vlad.badea@bolt.eu","Vlad-Dumitru Badea","!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 10.38.50.png|width=707,height=223,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 10.38.50.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-23T08:42:33.465Z"],["3832508","WD-22624","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:624d3e6a45ece00069cdb4e5] [~accountid:712020:0d3126a8-2815-43c2-bdb3-c600f5679aaf] accesses are granted","2026-01-23T08:43:49.690Z"],["3832509","WD-22660","WD","darja.netjaga@bolt.eu","Darja Netjaga","\n\nHi [~accountid:712020:f9db2690-f2bb-46be-95c6-8a0862ee5033] , it seems that it is already set.\n\n\n\nKind regards,\n\nDarja Netjaga \n\n!image-20260123-084034.png|width=611,alt=\"image-20260123-084034.png\"!","2026-01-23T08:44:25.585Z"],["3832510","RDS-1212","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] you’re probably right that this is misclassified, but I don’t think it’s a localisation issue in the sense that translators are doing their job poorly. It’s a localisation issue in the sense that the design and development doesn’t accommodate non-Latin text strings. So it’s more of a design/tech issue, I think. \n\nFor example, this text is written correctly in Thai. But it should have padding along the left side (currently, words are cut off) and we should not have currency overlapping content:\n\n!image-20260123-083954.png|width=620,height=663,alt=\"image-20260123-083954.png\"!\n\nMy hunch is that the designs were never specced for longer strings and wrapping behaviour, so devs never considered this case. And this is the result. But it’s just a hunch. No idea why there’s no padding, though.\n\nAnd the examples from Saudi Arabia feel like purely tech issues:\n\n!image-20260123-084311.png|width=667,height=613,alt=\"image-20260123-084311.png\"!\n\nAlso here:\n\n!image-20260123-084331.png|width=670,height=603,alt=\"image-20260123-084331.png\"!","2026-01-23T08:44:29.448Z"],["3832514","RDS-1212","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","But yeah, to be sure this is not a RiderX issue alone. One screenshot above is from the driver app. So this is a deeper problem for sure. ","2026-01-23T08:44:58.576Z"],["3832516","LSS-62050","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-23T08:46:07.368Z"],["3832518","CCM-22303","CCM","peace.anumia@bolt-outsource.eu","Peace Anumia","Yes, she was moved to TalentLMS-Teleperformance as she is now in Ride-hailing team, no longer Back office.","2026-01-23T08:46:17.981Z"],["3832520","PFI-836399","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-23T08:46:35.630Z"],["3832521","CNT-474","CNT","kristjan.konsap@bolt.eu","Kristjan-Johannes Konsap","[~accountid:610a6c97ec92ab0070d4d852] Thanks, I’ll send it into review.","2026-01-23T08:46:44.201Z"],["3832524","CNT-441","CNT","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","[~accountid:712020:fb31b9ff-3976-48ce-9899-290738b4fee2] [~accountid:712020:c7e5b826-6f9d-454b-83a6-a7755ef1ff9c] \n\nScope-wise: this is strictly for Employer Branding. The goal is to create a reusable EB LinkedIn toolkit.\n\nh3. *What I’m looking for:*\n\n* Figma-based LinkedIn organic post templates (visuals, not copy docs)\n* Templates that are very easy for me to edit myself (swap text, images, numbers)\n* Also a few quick paid-ad–friendly variants (e.g. “Analysts wanted!”, “Apply for 2026 internship program”)\n* Formats can be 1:1 and 9:16\n\nh3. Template types / main use cases\n\nA *set of pre-made building blocks*, covering different content needs:\n\n*Text-only templates*\n\n* Big announcement / shoutout (e.g. _“We’re hiring! 40+ open roles — check out_ [http://careers.bolt.eu|http://careers.bolt.eu|smart-link] _”_)\n* Open roles / campaign-style messages\n* Internship or graduate program announcements\n\n*Text + photo templates*\n\n* Meet the team / Meet the role\n* Engineering spotlight (photo + short quote)\n* Join our X team\n\n*More expressive / graphic-led templates*\n\n* Highlighting growth or scale (e.g. hubs, teams, milestones)\n* Big number moments (e.g. _“500+ engineers”_, _“10+ markets”_)\n* Quote + photo layouts\n* A few playful or eye-catching graphic elements (e.g. rocket / motion / growth metaphor) that we can reuse when we want something more energetic\n\n*Core EB scenarios these should cover*\n\n* We’re hiring (role-focused)\n* Join our X team\n* We’re growing in [hub]\n* Open roles / hiring push\n* Meet the team / Meet the role\n* Engineering spotlight\n\nh3. How the templates should work\n\n* Simple swap-in fields for:\n** Job title\n** Team name\n** Location / hub\n** Seniority level\n* Designed to be:\n** Fast to update\n** Visually consistent\n** Easy to reuse across posts, campaigns, and advocacy\n\n*In short:* A clean, flexible *EB LinkedIn template set in Figma* that covers our core hiring & people stories, includes multiple use cases (text-only, text + photo, graphic-led), and is easy for me to maintain and scale going forward.\n\nFor reference, this is what we currently have: [https://www.figma.com/design/dtX7Rz103wChEym1dXqN2x/EB-LinkedIn?node-id=456-9&p=f&t=wr3D1Ruyg32XZu5i-0|https://www.figma.com/design/dtX7Rz103wChEym1dXqN2x/EB-LinkedIn?node-id=456-9&p=f&t=wr3D1Ruyg32XZu5i-0|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T08:47:25.671Z"],["3832525","LSS-62050","LSS","susan.shao@bolt.eu","Cancan Shao","[^INCAP Confirmation Request 2025_Bolt Operations OÜ urgent.pdf]\n\nHere is the document needs to be signed. ","2026-01-23T08:47:38.951Z"],["3832526","SRED-1100","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done","2026-01-23T08:48:11.227Z"],["3832527","SRED-1097","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done","2026-01-23T08:48:23.912Z"],["3832528","LSS-62050","LSS","kaija.riismaa@bolt.eu","Kaija Riismaa","Hi Cancan\n\nJust letting you know that I do not see any documents attached to the ticket. \n\nBest regards, \nKaija","2026-01-23T08:48:26.130Z"],["3832529","TAXP-3386","TAXP","maret.ansperimalberg@bolt.eu","Maret Ansperi-Mälberg","[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/18bB63P_vskE7s1UEfjBc_YFIduoR6QxW|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/18bB63P_vskE7s1UEfjBc_YFIduoR6QxW|smart-link] \n\nReturn submitted in due time, tax payment processed automatically in bank.","2026-01-23T08:48:39.289Z"],["3832530","LSS-62051","LSS","angelina.korol@bolt.eu","Angelina Korol","[^INVOICE NO260109.pdf] _(320 kB)_","2026-01-23T08:48:44.660Z"],["3832532","LSS-59597","LSS","ann.koljalg@bolt.eu","Ann Kõljalg","Amazing! Thank you! [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] \n[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] share the contract now with the landlord and propose the following process proposed above. \nThank you everyone!","2026-01-23T08:48:50.725Z"],["3832533","SRED-948","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Research done, tests and other stuff will be checked in next tasks.","2026-01-23T08:49:20.844Z"],["3832534","CCM-22303","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey [~accountid:5e343da79029c30ca0bcbe0d]  👋  Can you move [dorcas.badmus@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:dorcas.badmus@bolt-outsource.eu] back to Teleperformance branch?\n\nThank you in advance 🌷 ","2026-01-23T08:49:29.954Z"],["3832535","PFI-837593","PFI","robert.buzukasvili@bolt.eu","Robert Buzukašvili","!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 9.46.22.png|thumbnail!\n\n[^Zaplaceno TREATLEY_BOLT 04-01-26.pdf]","2026-01-23T08:49:37.288Z"],["3832537","XP-3066","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","outlined [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1z_9cw1xxbwIbZ3rw_KyBHmZKov8j0owHJiJ_5HOPwQo/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-23T08:49:50.037Z"],["3832538","LSS-60939","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:614ae82ed747e80075f8baa5] ! Please find the signed doc attached\n\n[^benas_ahto_vincent_wet ink.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-23T08:49:56.400Z"],["3832539","CSP-401","CSP","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","26W04: Still waiting for PEX team to build a first proposal for the first routine covering a full process description. In the meantime we started planning the implementation for future features:\n\n* Showing other possible actions/decisions for historical steps on a case - ETA Feb 6th, owned by Beehive\n* Allowing an agent to reset the state of the routine to earlier steps - ETA Feb 6th, owned by Beehive\n* Exposing case context datapoints in Beehive workflows - ETA TBD, depends on Automations, will require Beehive involvement as well","2026-01-23T08:50:26.159Z"],["3832540","CEBF-1845","CEBF","pradeep.yadav@bolt.eu","Pradeep Kumar Yadav","Cancelled as we cannot control SLA for integrations.\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:9d55cde8-4889-4cc5-9d25-472a197c7697] ","2026-01-23T08:50:31.878Z"],["3832542","LSS-60758","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:a7ebf346-db0b-4f06-bc12-308859fa0e02] , thanks for your patience! I apologise for the delay. \n\nThe identity team confirmed that the {{is_blocked}} flag is a hard block. It blocks users access their account: they cannot log in and they are kicked out if they were already logged in. I was further informed that the process to follow is this:\n\n➡️ On the user profile, click on Fraud Actions. Then select \"Robbery/Lost Phone\" and provide the BH link. This will block the user and device.\n\nThis should solve the issue.","2026-01-23T08:50:34.871Z"],["3832544","LSS-62050","LSS","susan.shao@bolt.eu","Cancan Shao","I was not able to upload to the ticket at the beginning, just added it to the comment.  Thanks. [~accountid:5f0ea3c39d9a1200294cef2c] ","2026-01-23T08:50:48.461Z"],["3832545","HS-29309","HS","anastasiya.ivanova@bolt.eu","Anastasiya Ivanova","Can it be issued today or Monday?","2026-01-23T08:50:50.661Z"],["3832548","LSS-61924","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Signing process:\n\nplease sign the agreement already signed by the Partner [^BOLT_FOOD___Umowa_marketingowa__Sushi_Szop___Hawaiian_Poke_Bowl_-km.mroczkowski_gmail.com (4103ca9f-a64e-467d-8d20-b927245ba133).pdf] . The signature of [~accountid:5b18f5574bec0e53fdb555d5] on behalf of Bolt Operations OU. *Spotdraft*, please.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-23T08:51:20.031Z"],["3832551","CSDA-305","CSDA","roman.trohhalev@bolt.eu","Roman Trohhalev","Hi [~accountid:61fbf8daf5f5b80070c83fac]!\n\nWhen you say branch, do you mean provider_id / restaurant name, and for ticket-based FRT, do you want case-level FRT metrics (P75, avg, etc.) grouped by branch?","2026-01-23T08:52:13.208Z"],["3832555","PFI-837594","PFI","otis.wella@bolt-outsource.eu","Otis Wella","!{7C698BF2-2AAA-4851-B5E4-6F47B11112F9}-20260123-085046.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T08:52:55.411Z"],["3832556","DPX-3794","DPX","mark.bogdanov@bolt.eu","Mark Bogdanov","[~accountid:60bd1bad00bdd900683be69c] \n\nBack in this menu doesn’t cancel the changes, this is why I find it counter intuitive making it cancel the changes now. \nFor example you can add a replacement, and then press back button, and the replacement still would be there.\n\nAlso keep in mind we can have multiple items with multiple weight inputs, each of them can throw an error on apply (not enough product quantity for the inputted weight), which would just force us to not update all weighted products or apply it just partially. \n\nCombining multiple changes with return button not really canceling the changes (we don’t have pending changes in this screen per implementation) and that we don’t seek into big alterations to the flow already, I would propose to leave the button, but maybe change the style and/or text for better UX. \n","2026-01-23T08:53:12.409Z"],["3832559","BDB-1509","BDB","agata.bieniek@bolt.eu","Agata Bieniek","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] we have media plan here: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1aFIu7IAGxaQYUg51yiGyufWSb6SOSp6EoDyD5y3OjQw/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1aFIu7IAGxaQYUg51yiGyufWSb6SOSp6EoDyD5y3OjQw/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link]  We are waiting for last specs - I will add it today, but we can start working on the assets. Thank you!","2026-01-23T08:53:37.963Z"],["3832561","CSDA-296","CSDA","iuliia.vlasenko@bolt.eu","Iuliia Vlasenko","Hi Team, \n\nCan we extract cases with the issue tag promised_discount_was_not_applied_eater for Estonia and Romania 1 compete month. We need ticket links and Provider name. \n\nThanks","2026-01-23T08:54:16.079Z"],["3832564","LSS-61481","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:61c02e8de7637900682fe2b2], there is no legal age limit for hybrid or electric vehicles in France. If you want to establish a 20-year maximum age for hybrid and electric vehicles, this would be a *Bolt policy*, not a regulatory requirement. The rationale would be operational and would be portrayed a safety measure: older vehicles pose greater safety and reliability risks. \n\n*Key Risks*\n\n* ⚠️ No legal backing — must not present this as a regulatory rule.\n* ⚠️ Potential pushback from drivers or associations if perceived as arbitrary.\n* ⚠️ Reputational risk if poorly communicated.\n\n*Recommendations*\n\n* ✅ Frame as a Bolt quality/safety standard — not a legal rule.\n* ✅ Apply consistently to all drivers/vehicle types.\n* ✅ Optional review pathway for exceptional cases (e.g. enhanced inspection).\n* ✅ Prepare clear messaging for support/comms.\n\n\n\nAs this is implementing a policy which is deliberate by Bolt, and not legally founded - *please could you confirm that this decision has been discussed and approved by Mélanie and Julien?*\n\nThank you !\n\ncc. [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] ","2026-01-23T08:55:40.485Z"],["3832567","WD-22634","WD","steve.white@bolt.eu","Steve White","Sorry that was an error in setup.  By me 😞 \n\nCorrected now.","2026-01-23T08:56:02.215Z"],["3832568","PFI-837595","PFI","jantima.chanoonan@bolt-outsource.eu","Jantima Chanoonan","!image-20260123-085615.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260123-085643.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T08:56:51.688Z"],["3832571","MLC-3171","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","*Finland*\n\n* *BA:* Product Education, 0 Orders, Awareness, HVO, Promo Codes - *sent to proofreading*","2026-01-23T08:57:12.718Z"],["3832572","CSDA-296","CSDA","iuliia.vlasenko@bolt.eu","Iuliia Vlasenko","!Screenshot at Jan 23 10-40-46.png|width=2592,height=1390,alt=\"Screenshot at Jan 23 10-40-46.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-23T08:57:16.434Z"],["3832576","PFI-836396","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-23T08:57:36.340Z"],["3832578","LSS-61412","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Thank you [~accountid:712020:aa9604d8-cd49-4f98-bc6e-9c46af871b6b] ! 😊 ","2026-01-23T08:58:11.355Z"],["3832584","CSDT-918","CSDT","roman.trohhalev@bolt.eu","Roman Trohhalev","*1-1 with Ayush Jain — Product Data Analytics Manager*\n11.01.2026\n\n*Topics covered:*\n\n* Key challenges in Customer Support overall and from a data perspective\n* Exchange of perspectives on current pain points and opportunities\n* Differences between data roles at Bolt:\n** Product Data Analysts\n** Analytics Engineers\n** Product Engineers\n* Ownership boundaries and collaboration models between data roles\n* Overview of data tooling used across Bolt analytics teams\n\n*Key takeaways:*\n\n* Clearer understanding of how responsibilities are split across data roles\n* Alignment on expectations and interaction between Analytics, Analytics Engineering, and Product Engineering\n* Shared view on main CS data challenges and areas where better tooling and structure can help\n* Better context on how analytics tooling choices impact scalability and ownership\n\n*Follow-ups / Notes:*\n\n* Review [Customer Support | Analytics Engineering Target & 2025 Roadmap|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QcqTx-GyNMzItSRCzWFTpKXDpUNXjMghBZdTv7YuXvs/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.g4wig92a92rj] shared by Ayush","2026-01-23T08:58:56.014Z"],["3832585","LSS-61827","LSS","tatsiana.sivukha@bolt.eu","Tatsiana Sivukha","Hi [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] \n\n* We have to replace the DPA {{Term; Data Return and Deletion}} section with the following:\n** *Term; Data Return and Deletion.*\nThis DPA shall remain in effect for so long as OpenAI processes Customer Data on your behalf pursuant to the Agreement. Notwithstanding the foregoing, OpenAI shall not retain Personal Data processed using OpenAI products for longer than eighteen (18) months from the date such Personal Data is collected or otherwise obtained, unless a longer retention period is agreed between the Parties separately. Upon expiry of the applicable eighteen (18)-month retention period, OpenAI shall, and shall direct each Sub-processor to, promptly delete or irreversibly anonymise such Personal Data.\nUpon termination of the data processing services, and upon your reasonable request, OpenAI shall return or delete any remaining Customer Data, unless Data Protection Laws prevent OpenAI from returning or destroying all or part of the Customer Data.\nFor clarity, OpenAI may continue to process information derived from Customer Data that has been deidentified, anonymized, and/or aggregated such that it is no longer considered Personal Data under applicable Data Protection Laws and does not identify any individual or Customer, including for the purpose of improving OpenAI’s systems and services.\n* We should request to provide the Zero Data Retention Agreement as well. Can you please support with getting it?","2026-01-23T08:58:56.616Z"],["3832587","LSS-61821","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi Mo, it is. We can proceed with the signing. \n\nIf you need support with the signature collection, please approve that this is the correct signatory from their side: Chester Tilstra, [chester@tilstraservices.nl|mailto:chester@tilstraservices.nl] and I will forward this for signature collection.","2026-01-23T08:59:18.389Z"],["3832588","WD-22673","WD","steve.white@bolt.eu","Steve White","[~accountid:712020:067b96b5-97ee-46c1-b0fb-bad5e80a63d0] this person is live in Workday under [adrian.tarna@bolt-rentals.eu|mailto:adrian.tarna@bolt-rentals.eu]\n\nAccount not deactivated in Workday\n\nif you need to add me to the IT Okta ticket please do so i can help any issue they have","2026-01-23T08:59:37.467Z"],["3832589","LSS-61434","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","Hi [~accountid:61fba8d88d9e3c00688fac2e] Please find separate annexes for UA and BG as requested by Boolanga:\n\nUA: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zsDxmuPiz6l7SNduMDUUqKqA-4ZzbNSr1QK8O8x3w08/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zsDxmuPiz6l7SNduMDUUqKqA-4ZzbNSr1QK8O8x3w08/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\nBG: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1z3EELf_9oxZob6M4_HGJz2rFh7evd9pmaJdSvr95MO4/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1z3EELf_9oxZob6M4_HGJz2rFh7evd9pmaJdSvr95MO4/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\nIf BG version suits to Boolanga as it is, then let’s sign this first. With UA I understood they wanted to add some additional terms. \n\nLiisa","2026-01-23T08:59:50.963Z"],["3832590","CEBF-1832","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","!image-20260123-085954.png|width=468,alt=\"image-20260123-085954.png\"!","2026-01-23T08:59:58.889Z"],["3832594","LSS-60177","LSS","tatjana.ainson@bolt.eu","Tatjana Ainson","Yes, we can close the ticket for now","2026-01-23T09:00:25.820Z"],["3832595","LSS-62053","LSS","agata.bieniek@bolt.eu","Agata Bieniek","[^Agreement (2).pdf] _(277 kB)_\n\n[^Bolt_40x.pdf] _(66 kB)_","2026-01-23T09:00:29.326Z"],["3832597","HS-29253","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hello [~accountid:6204f020a294020068797e7c] \n\nI think the letter has been already requested in the past as it has been completed on the 12th of January already but we can send out the reference letter after the end of the employment so Miguel will receive his to his personal email once his contract ends.\n\nRegards,\nKadri","2026-01-23T09:00:59.647Z"],["3832600","LSS-59767","LSS","oluwatosin.ogunsanwo@bolt.eu","Oluwatosin Ogunsanwo","Hey [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] \nPlease see below the client’s feedback:\n\n{color:#36b37e}_”I couldn't implement these changes as you requested. Instead, I made the changes to support this in three different spots in the document. First, I needed to add a defined term for Other Party, because it is a deficiency of our document that this is not a defined term in the preamble. Second, I added most of what you had indicated to the definition as you requested. However, the last portion \"unless expressly identified in writing...\" functions more as an exception to confidentiality, which is clause 9, so I added it as new subpoint (f). I'm attaching the PDF here, but I understand you may have additional changes because I did not implement this directly as you requested._ {color}\n\n{color:#36b37e}_Just let me know and I will endeavor to accommodate you in any way I can.”_{color}\n\nI have also attached the revised NDA for your review. Please advise on next steps.\n\n[^Non-Disclosure Agreement with Bolt (692d78e053) (version 4).pdf]\n\nThanks!\n\n","2026-01-23T09:01:33.804Z"],["3832602","PFI-837598","PFI","ernests.suskevics@bolt-outsource.eu","Ernests Suskevics","!Screenshot 2026-01-23 110102.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T09:02:07.309Z"],["3832605","LSS-58592","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ,\n\nI am so sorry, but the Partner now told us that he wants the agreement signed by Ahto via Docusing, with signature on the last page of the Agreement and in each of the annexes.\n\nCan you kindly arrange it, please?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-23T09:02:48.421Z"],["3832608","LSS-61821","LSS","mo.salama@bolt.eu","Mo Salama","Hi Raivis,\n\nYes Chester should be the signatory.\n\nSincerely,\n\nMo","2026-01-23T09:03:11.786Z"],["3832613","LSS-61415","LSS","anais.jourdain@bolt.eu","Anaïs Jourdain","Hello [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742], \nIl nous a envoyé ce message, est-ce suffisant ? \n\n” Il vous suffit juste de contacter le service REVTC Registre des Exploitants VTC au ministère des transports. Ils confirmeront ce que j'explique depuis le début, même si ça prend du temps, ils répondent toujours au téléphone. Voici le numéro de téléphone : +33.(0)9.74.36.31.72\n\n_Ils vous confirmeront que mon véhicule TPMR bénéficie de la dérogation d'âge en application de l'Article L.3120-5 du code des transports._\n\nVoici tous les points importants concernant les exigences techniques pour les VTC et les dérogations applicables aux VTC TPMR (transport de personnes à mobilité réduite) en droit français :\n\n# _Règles générales applicables aux VTC (hors TPMR) que vous connaissez :_\n\n_Conditions techniques obligatoires :_\n\nUn véhicule VTC doit répondre à certaines caractéristiques techniques et de confort définies par voie réglementaire :\n\n_Places :_\n\nEntre 4 et 9 places, conducteur inclus.\n\n_Caractéristiques définies par arrêté :_ Un arrêté ministériel fixe des critères (sauf pour certains cas particuliers, voir ci-dessous)  :\n\nAncienneté maximale du véhicule (généralement 6–7 ans selon arrêtés en vigueur)\n\nDimensions minimales (par exemple longueur hors tout : ≥ 4,50 m × largeur ≥ 1,70 m)\n\nPuissance minimale du moteur (par exemple ≥ 84 kW)\n\n_Autres obligations techniques :_\n\nContrôle technique annuel conforme à la réglementation du transport de personnes.\n\nSignalétique VTC obligatoire (macaron autocollant réglementaire apposé à l’avant et à l’arrière).\n\n_Interdictions :_\n\nLe véhicule ne doit pas posséder de dispositifs lumineux ou équipements pouvant créer une confusion avec un taxi : par exemple enseigne lumineuse.\n\nCes conditions figurent principalement aux _articles R.3122-6 à R.3122-8 du Code des transports_ et aux arrêtés ministériels qui précisent les dimensions, la puissance, l’ancienneté, etc.\n\n# _La dérogation prévue par l’article L.3120-5_\n\nL’article L.3120-5 du Code des transports prévoit que les prestations de transport (incluant VTC) peuvent être réalisées avec des véhicules électriques ou hybrides, par dérogation aux caractéristiques techniques ordinaires définies par règlement.\n\nCela signifie concrètement que les véhicules électriques et hybrides ne sont pas soumis à l’ensemble des critères techniques habituels (comme l’âge, la puissance minimale ou certaines dimensions) dès lors qu’ils sont utilisés pour un service de transport public particulier de personnes.\n\n# _Dérogation spécifique pour les VTC TPMR :_\n\nPour les VTC TPMR (VTC adaptés aux personnes à mobilité réduite), la loi et la réglementation _(notamment dans le cadre de la Loi d’Orientation des Mobilités – LOM)_ reconnaissent une dérogation importante :\n\nPourquoi cette dérogation existe\n\nLes véhicules adaptés au transport PMR (fauteuils roulants, accès par rampe, espace intérieur adapté, etc.) ne peuvent pas toujours satisfaire aux caractéristiques techniques et de confort standards des VTC (dimensions, puissance, métriques arrêtés).\n\n*La loi permet donc à ces véhicules de déroger à certaines obligations techniques et de confort prévues pour les VTC, afin de pouvoir exercer l’activité de VTC tout en étant aménagés pour transporter des personnes à mobilité réduite. *\n\n# _Ce que couvrent ces dérogations TPMR :_\n\nCaractéristiques techniques\n\n_Un VTC TPMR peut ne pas respecter :_\n\nLes dimensions minimales définies par l’arrêté (longueur/largeur)\n\n_L’ancienneté maximale habituelle exigée pour les VTC_\n\nLa puissance minimale du moteur parce que ces caractéristiques sont souvent incompatibles avec un véhicule aménagé pour PMR.\n\n_Objectif de la dérogation :_\n\nCette mesure a pour but de :\n\n# Faciliter l’accès au transport pour les personnes en fauteuil roulant ou avec mobilité réduite,\n# Permettre l’usage de véhicules aménagés qui seraient autrement exclus par les critères standard,\n# Éviter que l’accessibilité PMR soit un frein à l’activité professionnelle des VTC adaptée.\n\n_Cela permet à un VTC équipé d’une rampe d’accès PMR_, d’un plancher surbaissé ou d’un espace pour fauteuil roulant _d’être déclaré comme VTC même si_ sa taille, _son ancienneté_ ou sa puissance* ne répondent pas exactement aux critères standards.*\n\n# _Ce que la dérogation ne couvre pas :_\n\nCes dérogations ne dispensent pas le véhicule ou l’exploitant de respecter :\n\nLes obligations générales de sécurité routière.\n\nLe contrôle technique et l’assurance professionnelle.\n\nL’immatriculation correcte au registre VTC.\n\nLa conformité des équipements d’ancrage et de sécurité pour les PMR, ce qui reste essentiel pour un service légal et sûr. “\n\n\n\n","2026-01-23T09:04:50.407Z"],["3832616","WD-22663","WD","steve.white@bolt.eu","Steve White","done, she’ll be eligible in July 2026","2026-01-23T09:05:19.349Z"],["3832617","PFI-837197","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello,\n\nThe company is under Resale Billing model so they receive one invoice per month; I believe all invoices for the period are available in Invoices tab; also, it’s possible to download the report Ride.csv with all rides and separate food statement, if needed.\n\nIf you can provide more information about why the Customer believes we overcharged them, I can advise more.","2026-01-23T09:05:38.206Z"],["3832618","LSS-62049","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:712020:aa9604d8-cd49-4f98-bc6e-9c46af871b6b] I have changed the wording a bit to keep our standard approach for adjusting clause 6.5: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Lm3shAe6ulCIPwanNPoZo46PnhPtO0jBMDjDCaNL5FQ/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Lm3shAe6ulCIPwanNPoZo46PnhPtO0jBMDjDCaNL5FQ/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \nNext time you can do the same yourself without raising a legal ticket 🙂 Thank you! ","2026-01-23T09:05:40.780Z"],["3832620","PFI-836975","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Ketlin, thanks for reaching out. The user was identified as a card tester and their account has now been blocked. No further follow up is needed on this escalation in my opinion. \nIf you still need to follow up with this, you may answer with something in the realms of: “We’ve reviewed the account and identified activity that doesn’t align with our platform’s terms and security requirements. As a result, access to the account has been restricted.“\nThank you!","2026-01-23T09:06:22.226Z"],["3832622","RNTL-29745","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] ETA → {{2026-01-30}}","2026-01-23T09:06:42.314Z"],["3832623","WD-22674","WD","remi.simson@bolt.eu","Remi Simson","!Screenshot 2026-01-23 110647.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T09:07:03.899Z"],["3832625","INT-726","INT","alexander.tsyba@bolt.eu","Alexander Tsyba","[~accountid:712020:853cbe25-4d18-40c3-8211-69c3936bf72f] [~accountid:5ffbfc6a44065f013fdd66e9] As discussed this week, we will do a static banner. We need some specific guidance from you on what to communicate on this banner, where it should lead to, etc. 🙂 ","2026-01-23T09:07:19.808Z"],["3832628","LSS-57933","LSS","marketa.hlavac@bolt.eu","Marketa Hlavacova","Hi [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2] thanks a lot, I have finalised my comments, can you please review it so I can share it with Pickitoo. \n\n\n\nI will check with tax team, in case there would be a problem, we can always have a separated contract for each country / provider. \n\nThank you\n\n","2026-01-23T09:08:11.921Z"],["3832630","PFI-833185","PFI","aisma.austruma@bolt.eu","Aisma Austruma","Thank you for the reply. \n\nI checked the screenshot you provided and notice the VAT was applied to the trip  -  the 34.2 sum.\n\n*Question* is - Should it realy be like that, if we do not apply VAT for the Coupons? \n\nIt seams this was an error, because the Coupon was used by the Business User? \n\nThis VAT and depiction is not shown in the [+*CSV doc,*+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/15lMAezUdVSbC3P_iW6bAGugIOvkFqggoOPoPhtpkTQs/edit?gid=1622566300#gid=1622566300] and the company has issues because of this. \n\nThe 2nd position in the screenshot shows the CSV Sum - 591.98 without VAT, but the Invoice shows 620.24 - and that understandably is added with the 28.26 price without VAT. \n\n","2026-01-23T09:08:33.300Z"],["3832634","LSS-62020","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:712020:f50af85a-3d8b-4b5c-b19d-ad552b86d158] I cannot open the attached termination letter, please try to upload it one more time or send me the google doc link. Thanks!","2026-01-23T09:09:09.318Z"],["3832635","PFI-837603","PFI","jasmine.ashun@bolt.eu","Jasmine Nana Ama Ashun","!IMG_7403.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T09:09:36.611Z"],["3832636","WEBSD-1511","WEBSD","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","I will add full description above [~accountid:712020:9e668ce4-0877-43c6-bae9-52f1ecbc753f] I accidentally submitted ticket halfway writing description 😅 \n\nLiisa","2026-01-23T09:09:37.232Z"],["3832642","LSS-61821","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi Legal Ops, please organize signing of the attached document. \n\nCounterparty signatory: Chester Tilstra, [chester@tilstraservices.nl|mailto:chester@tilstraservices.nl]\n\nBolt: Ahto\n\nThanks!\n\n[^Bolt x Tilstra_Service Agreement Michel (1) (ba1592a0-1bff-46ac-bba4-c0c7d701121a).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-23T09:10:14.387Z"],["3832643","DSR-3577","DSR","laura.newton@bolt.eu","Laura Newton","Hi [~accountid:712020:50057dc7-d3c1-4f13-9a33-a34da3415c60], what exactly do you need from me?","2026-01-23T09:10:34.594Z"],["3832644","WD-22671","WD","arina.vorozhtsova@bolt.eu","Arina Vorozhtsova","Hi Yaroslav,\n\nI have updated the country in the payment election options, so you should now be able to add your Finnish IBAN to Workday. \n\n Let me know if you encounter any issues.\n\nRegards,  \nArina","2026-01-23T09:11:11.716Z"],["3832646","LSS-62020","LSS","mihaela.vatamanu@bolt.eu","Mihaela Vatamanu","hi Raivis, here is the link to the termination letter: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rysfVomO0Y8t8qRUSMWce9APCM0LkuFMjY7uC2lwwec/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rysfVomO0Y8t8qRUSMWce9APCM0LkuFMjY7uC2lwwec/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link]  thanks!","2026-01-23T09:11:25.655Z"],["3832647","DSR-3979","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T09:11:26.006Z"],["3832648","PLUS-20","PLUS","artem.markov@bolt.eu","Artem Markov","!image-20260123-091143.png|width=344,alt=\"image-20260123-091143.png\"!","2026-01-23T09:11:48.975Z"],["3832649","BP-13321","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","[~accountid:712020:f7f7320d-7e3a-4389-8726-f082352b7487] \n\n{quote}can we tie the Legal entity banner per admin, not company, aka if they press Got it, it will be gone only for the Admin, not whole organisation?{quote}\n\nYes, should be easily doable.","2026-01-23T09:12:06.611Z"],["3832650","WD-22656","WD","darja.netjaga@bolt.eu","Darja Netjaga","Hi Sittinam,\n\nIf the TH local ops is the manager of future employee, the manager just needs to start job requisition in Workday. Please let me know if more help is needed. \n\nKind regards,\n\nDarja Netjaga","2026-01-23T09:12:11.365Z"],["3832651","RDS-1324","RDS","dias.sadykov@bolt.eu","Dias Sadykov","Agree this is Growth not Quality and it’s very important","2026-01-23T09:13:01.749Z"],["3832653","SRED-1099","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done, released","2026-01-23T09:13:31.914Z"],["3832654","DRX-26012","DRX","andrii.pustovoit@bolt.eu","Andrii Pustovoit","no need","2026-01-23T09:13:32.610Z"],["3832655","CNT-461","CNT","anton.sljussarev@bolt.eu","Anton Sljussarev","[~accountid:6163ec849cdb930072d02e8e] They will get money back into their Bolt Food balance account from every order they make. Then, they can use these money for future orders.","2026-01-23T09:13:47.471Z"],["3832656","ING-667","ING","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała"," A sample idea from gemini:\n\n\n\n{noformat}case class Latest(\n    cols: ListSet[String], \n    sAlias: String, \n    tAlias: String, \n    parentCol: Option[String] = None\n) extends UpdatePredicate {\n\n  def render(schema: StructType): Column = {\n    val prefix = parentCol.map(p => s\"$p.\").getOrElse(\"\")\n\n    val predicates = cols.map { c =>\n      val fullName = s\"$prefix$c\"\n      \n      // Use our safe helper\n      val sourceCol = SparkUtils.safeCol(schema, s\"$sAlias.$fullName\")\n      val targetCol = SparkUtils.safeCol(schema, s\"$tAlias.$fullName\")\n\n      // Logic: (Source exists & Target is null) OR (Source >= Target)\n      // If Source is missing, sourceCol is NULL, so this whole predicate becomes false/null\n      (sourceCol.isNotNull && targetCol.isNull) || (sourceCol >= targetCol)\n    }\n\n    predicates.reduceOption(_ || _).getOrElse(lit(true))\n  }\n}{noformat}","2026-01-23T09:13:51.360Z"],["3832658","RDS-1164","RDS","dias.sadykov@bolt.eu","Dias Sadykov","We have “No internet connection snackbar” already?","2026-01-23T09:14:15.023Z"],["3832661","MP-3486","MP","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DA.127.0 (1513) Firebase build on Samsung A12, OS:13 and Google Pixel 8 Pro, OS:16\n\n|| || ||\n|!Screenshot_20260123-094943 (1).png|width=178,alt=\"Screenshot_20260123-094943 (1).png\"!|!Screenshot_20260123-095712.png|width=178,alt=\"Screenshot_20260123-095712.png\"!|\n|!Screenshot_20260123-095703.png|width=178,alt=\"Screenshot_20260123-095703.png\"!|!Screenshot_20260123-095622.png|width=178,alt=\"Screenshot_20260123-095622.png\"!|","2026-01-23T09:14:52.174Z"],["3832662","EBIKE1-367","EBIKE1","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","The Stratus platform vehicle pairing feature has been released.\nThis feature describes how controller and IoT on EB1 and D3 (and cruiser) \"decide\" in which vehicle mode the controller must operate.\n\nRelevant documentation:\n\n[Feature flowchart|https://drive.google.com/open?id=12s7ilaIIxZNwapOC5m3c83M1F9uDOP28&usp=drive_fs]\n[Vehicle detection matrix|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LdBVIMrFiteme1ryWymSexsqez-BniHRaoh4RlZbwGY?usp=drive_fs]\n[Bolt CAN protocol 3.0|https://drive.google.com/open?id=1wA6YVoRtuOr5cH-lgex02INg4qf7ZgSS&usp=drive_fs]\n\n\n\nThe documents have been sent to Genfo.","2026-01-23T09:15:16.098Z"],["3832665","LSS-61712","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi [~accountid:5d3ff51eb7f3ac0da80c815c] no concerns with the document. Its their usual amendment template and the only change is the fee. Lets please ask dLocal to send it for signing to the Directors of the company Ahto Kink and Nathadon Suksiritarnan to [ahto.kink@bolt.eu|mailto:ahto.kink@bolt.eu] and [nathadon.suksiritarnan@bolt.eu|mailto:nathadon.suksiritarnan@bolt.eu] and to cc [signing@bolt.eu|mailto:signing@bolt.eu] \n\ncc [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] please keep an eye on it. ","2026-01-23T09:15:44.700Z"],["3832671","WD-22482","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","To create BNB issue","2026-01-23T09:16:30.184Z"],["3832672","PFI-836920","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","No unenrollment, pinged Tommy\nRaised [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C063CK8C540/p1769178481407629?thread_ts=1765203709.780469&cid=C063CK8C540]","2026-01-23T09:16:36.678Z"],["3832673","DRAG101-469","DRAG101","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","I have removed the dates as this task is not relevant at the moment","2026-01-23T09:16:47.605Z"],["3832675","PRV-984","PRV","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Updates in the linked MVRA ticket. Playbook almost ready.","2026-01-23T09:16:53.091Z"],["3832676","RNTL-29748","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","Agreed:\n\nWe do create one additional explore which will be ‘collect-deploy’ cycles and it will have collect task id exposed and kms ridden and rides done since the last deployment task ","2026-01-23T09:17:03.313Z"],["3832677","PRIV-485","PRIV","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Playbook almost ready from Privacy part","2026-01-23T09:17:04.952Z"],["3832678","LSS-57933","LSS","marketa.hlavac@bolt.eu","Marketa Hlavacova","Tax ticket here [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/TAX-3499|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/TAX-3499|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T09:17:08.244Z"],["3832679","WFM-10091","WFM","valeria.tiilikainen@bolt.eu","Valeria Tiilikainen","Already solved","2026-01-23T09:17:15.283Z"],["3832681","RDS-503","RDS","dias.sadykov@bolt.eu","Dias Sadykov","Not sure if this is relevant, tips are allowed midride in the app already.","2026-01-23T09:17:27.655Z"],["3832682","DRAG101-287","DRAG101","arvind.jayashankar@bolt.eu","Arvind Jayashankar","[~accountid:5e4658b55a495e0c91a7a011] I think it could still be interesting if the price is compelling enough - to have a European tire supplier would save on shipping time, and 40k tires a day is really fast. Other than being eco friendly and emission free, we would have to be sure performance is still suitable. If they can send us some samples to evaluate then we can decide. This is not urgent but would still keep the door open and see what they’re currently up to.","2026-01-23T09:17:30.087Z"],["3832685","UXA-2229","UXA","alexandru.craciun@bolt.eu","Alex Crăciun","After running [+some queries+|https://thanos.nodemonitor.boltint.net/graph?g0.expr=sum%20by%20(app_type)%20(increase(nodejs%3Auser_verify%3Averify_confirmed{method%3D%22sms%22}[1d]))%20%2F%20sum%20by%20(app_type)%20%20(increase(nodejs%3Auser_verify%3Averify_requested{method%3D%22sms%22}[1d]))&g0.tab=0&g0.stacked=0&g0.range_input=4w&g0.max_source_resolution=0s&g0.deduplicate=1&g0.partial_response=1&g0.store_matches=[]&g0.engine=prometheus&g0.analyze=0&g0.tenant=&g1.expr=sum%20by%20(phone_country)%20(increase(nodejs%3Auser_verify%3Averify_confirmed_phone{method%3D%22sms%22%2C%20app_type%3D%22CA%22}[1d]))%20%20%2F%20%20sum%20by%20(phone_country)%20(increase(nodejs%3Auser_verify%3Averify_requested_phone{method%3D%22sms%22%2C%20app_type%3D%22CA%22}[1d]))%20and%20sum%20by%20(phone_country)%20(increase(nodejs%3Auser_verify%3Averify_requested_phone{method%3D%22sms%22%2C%20app_type%3D%22CA%22}[1d]))%20%3E1000&g1.tab=0&g1.stacked=0&g1.range_input=4w&g1.max_source_resolution=0s&g1.deduplicate=1&g1.partial_response=1&g1.store_matches=[]&g1.engine=prometheus&g1.analyze=0&g1.tenant=&g2.expr=sum%20by%20(phone_country)%20(increase(nodejs%3Auser_verify%3Averify_confirmed_phone{method%3D%22sms%22%2C%20app_type%3D%22CI%22}[1d]))%20%20%2F%20%20sum%20by%20(phone_country)%20(increase(nodejs%3Auser_verify%3Averify_requested_phone{method%3D%22sms%22%2C%20app_type%3D%22CI%22}[1d]))%20and%20sum%20by%20(phone_country)%20(increase(nodejs%3Auser_verify%3Averify_requested_phone{method%3D%22sms%22%2C%20app_type%3D%22CI%22}[1d]))%20%3E1000&g2.tab=0&g2.stacked=0&g2.range_input=4w&g2.max_source_resolution=0s&g2.deduplicate=1&g2.partial_response=1&g2.store_matches=[]&g2.engine=prometheus&g2.analyze=0&g2.tenant=] in Thanos it seems like there was a noticeable drop in confirmed vs. requested SMS OTPs in Saudi Arabia around 07.01.2026. [+Asked+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CND9AL5LY/p1769159259098239] comms and privacy team if something changed around that time.\n\nAnother idea was that maybe fraud rules were relaxed a bit around NYE to reduce false positives and the decrease in ASR is a side effect of that. Will wait to see what comms reply before taking it to fraud team.","2026-01-23T09:18:35.395Z"],["3832689","WD-21708","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Create test ER and try to change it during different stages. Users are unable to change tax applicability. Maybe some notification with certain attributes","2026-01-23T09:19:13.600Z"],["3832692","LSS-61833","LSS","tatsiana.sivukha@bolt.eu","Tatsiana Sivukha","Responded in the main ticket","2026-01-23T09:19:39.140Z"],["3832694","LSS-61707","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:5bf2989995a1f935f7db9e66] !\n\nAssuming that you raised this ticket on the same day we received CICAP’s email, the deadline to respond is on Monday.\n\nCan you kindly check my questions bellow?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-23T09:19:56.517Z"],["3832696","PFI-835934","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","[~accountid:712020:1a99e337-a650-4a85-a8ed-f0825a04e850] please, could you assist here?","2026-01-23T09:20:17.854Z"],["3832698","CEBF-1787","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","All fields are created in custom meta data. Details [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1DILiOmwmKspYV5q5meFeeVjK_UPT7qfu9nwe-nBcYlU/edit?usp=sharing]","2026-01-23T09:20:31.582Z"],["3832702","PFI-836676","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\n\n\nThe Customer Payments Operations Team does not have the required tools/permissions to issue refunds. If you are not able to issue the refund then we kindly ask you to check with your Team Lead on how to solve this case. You may need to request the following accesses in Admin to be able to issue refund for orders if you previously do not have such: \n\n\n\n* *Rides*: refund_payments and customer_support_beehive_ridehailing_order_refund\n* *Delivery*:  delivery_order_refund\n* *Rentals*: rental_order_refund, rental_subscriptions_refund and rental_order_refund_city_fine\n* *Carsharing*: rental_car_order_refund\n* *Bolt+*: subscription_offer_customer_support\n\n\n\n{color:#bf2600}*Note: A failed card payment can’t be refunded to the card. Only successful card payments can be refunded to card.*{color}\n\nFor issues with refunds from Beehive, kindly reach out to #beehive-agent-support on Slack.\n\n{color:#ff5630}For older orders refund, kindly check with your team lead as they have the required accesses to perform such operations.{color}\n\n","2026-01-23T09:21:11.880Z"],["3832703","RNTL-30272","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","[~accountid:712020:8d272f38-d046-4ad2-a5b3-a47b219e9fa1] this table is too heavy to be processed in Looker, especially with window functions. \n\nLooker is *not* a suitable tool for that query.\n\nI suggest we do a deep dive on analytical tools like Databricks for the hardware team and you’ll be able to run such queries there. ","2026-01-23T09:21:16.475Z"],["3832704","CAMLE-9234","CAMLE","adil.ansar@bolt.eu","Mohammad Adil Ansar","Better solution already developed here => https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/152791","2026-01-23T09:21:24.205Z"],["3832705","LSS-61245","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] +1 to what [~accountid:712020:29d8b602-d17f-40cd-9cae-5653bc2c54b7] commented (thank you). I remember discussing and aligning on this wording with Armin previously, but it looks like it didn’t make it into the global version. It is just better wording that reflects reality and its flexible for future use cases/flows. We should make the same update across all Bolt Business T&Cs (global + each local market version). \n\nThanks! ","2026-01-23T09:21:28.480Z"],["3832706","LSS-58667","LSS","yolandah.chinyani@bolt.eu","Yolandah Chido Chinyani","Hi [~accountid:712020:822a759a-daf0-4161-afbf-8b79a2985fba] , I have added the files to the folder. Could you please sign when you get a chance? Thank you. \n\n","2026-01-23T09:21:38.966Z"],["3832707","MKP-9913","MKP","mateja.sela@bolt.eu","Mateja Sela","Hey [@abdelhalim.machehalek|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:5290f272-66ef-467e-a008-8904b3bc928d], thanks for picking this up! What about dependencies to RiderX and matching? Can we only do those after your changes?","2026-01-23T09:21:41.953Z"],["3832708","PFI-837608","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-23T09:22:03.466Z"],["3832709","BDRIV-17","BDRIV","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","I will talk to Supply Chain team how to approach the possible Cell manufacturers.\n\nCurrently I see 2 ways.\n1. Ask TWS for their experiences and what specification sheets they have available. - More likely way to get info and get it fast\n\n# Supply chain will have to communicate to the cell manufacturers directly. - Probably more time consuming as we do not have NDAs etc.","2026-01-23T09:22:03.656Z"],["3832710","RNTL-30272","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","[@norman.tamm|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:8d272f38-d046-4ad2-a5b3-a47b219e9fa1] hey, this table is too heavy to be processed in Looker, especially with window functions.\nLooker is *not* a suitable tool for that query.\nI suggest we do a deep dive on analytical tools like Databricks for the hardware team and you’ll be able to run such queries there.","2026-01-23T09:22:07.230Z"],["3832712","RNTL-30272","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","or, we can discuss alternatives in the next Hardware-data sync","2026-01-23T09:22:57.553Z"],["3832715","CCM-22303","CCM","leila.toomet@bolt.eu","Leila Toomet","!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 11.23.26.png|width=1077,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 11.23.26.png\"!\n\nPlease delete the user. If it is done let me know!","2026-01-23T09:23:53.616Z"],["3832719","PASD-177","PASD","aleksandr.bregin@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Bregin","Figured it out, all good","2026-01-23T09:24:26.913Z"],["3832720","LSS-59929","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Thank you for the update [~accountid:712020:d59118c4-a302-4b14-bfb9-2a1051013c63] .  ","2026-01-23T09:24:39.418Z"],["3832721","PAW-15112","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-alex-somai\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161657\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-23 09:24:40 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-23T09:24:40.690Z"],["3832722","CAMLE-9899","CAMLE","uladzislau.tolkach@bolt.eu","Uladzislau Tolkach","*@user-U01AY6XE86N* while I'm looking into it, I've noticed that in the branding tags older tags are in the top, while more recent are in the bottom, I think it makes sense to reverse sorting, wdyt?","2026-01-23T09:24:51.196Z"],["3832723","CAMLE-9899","CAMLE",null,"Slack","[Uladzislau Tolkach|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6305dd67cf3340e8737f8f66] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CDQN2UG9X/p1768900934200219?thread_ts=1768824687.848569&cid=CDQN2UG9X|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CDQN2UG9X/p1768900934200219?thread_ts=1768824687.848569&cid=CDQN2UG9X|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-23T09:24:52.150Z"],["3832724","MKP-9913","MKP","artem.markov@bolt.eu","Artem Markov","[@mateja.sela|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:233144b7-8984-4e6b-922e-2ed0d6700d5f] {{/internal/getPricingConfiguration}} this is needed for free cancelations, other {{/internal/getSubscriptionParametersForRides}} is for priority pickups. But we are not planning to use it in canada so it could wait.","2026-01-23T09:25:01.038Z"],["3832727","DO-5797","DO","mattias.siimar@bolt.eu","Mattias Siimar","I still do not have access to table {{ng_mixpanel_riders.ride_hailing_cross_domain_tap}}\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 11.25.48.png|width=1131,height=259,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 11.25.48.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-23T09:25:57.958Z"],["3832728","DRAG101-287","DRAG101","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","[~accountid:63d0ecd1d73cd1e44e22078f] They have nothing today. They wanted to do development for us, but it turned out they had no funds for it. I will see what they say now, 6 months have passed.","2026-01-23T09:26:04.877Z"],["3832730","CCM-22303","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Thanks [~accountid:5e343da79029c30ca0bcbe0d] , user deleted. :done: ","2026-01-23T09:26:29.300Z"],["3832731","RDS-1108","RDS","dias.sadykov@bolt.eu","Dias Sadykov","This is Pre Order\n\nFor Active Order payment method change we don’t change the price and the feature is not rolled out anywhere due to UX friction\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04HCL32LUU/p1741333061640579|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04HCL32LUU/p1741333061640579|smart-link] \n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/tests/edit/11928|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/tests/edit/11928]\n\nMay also convert it to Active Order Payment Method Change","2026-01-23T09:26:31.984Z"],["3832734","CSDT-971","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","After PR is merged need to:\n\n* Re-generate mart_support_case_metrics\n* Backfill mart_support_case_metrics\n* Backfill other marts\n* Looker sync not needed? → check with Kevin","2026-01-23T09:27:27.863Z"],["3832735","MM-924","MM","kristjan.praks@bolt.eu","Kristjan Praks","First mockups: [https://www.figma.com/board/uFka8MLcxiDYaI8lixBwnC/GAC-tab-unifier?node-id=0-1&t=uM7lPAbzG7QzIHyU-1|https://www.figma.com/board/uFka8MLcxiDYaI8lixBwnC/GAC-tab-unifier?node-id=0-1&t=uM7lPAbzG7QzIHyU-1|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T09:27:33.135Z"],["3832739","PFI-809177","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hi team, the invoice for this order has been issued.","2026-01-23T09:28:28.895Z"],["3832740","PRF-1780","PRF","marianne.kaarma@bolt.eu","Marianne Kaarma","Hi [~accountid:5c2f512d36647b5b91017d0c] ! I checked this one, looks like something is off:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 11.27.35.png|width=579,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 11.27.35.png\"!\n\nCould you review and let me know once they’re ready to launch? Thanks 🙂 ","2026-01-23T09:28:30.928Z"],["3832741","LSS-61430","LSS","valentin.descas@bolt.eu","Valentin Descas","Thanks a lot [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] ! ","2026-01-23T09:28:46.999Z"],["3832742","HS-29138","HS","valentin.descas@bolt.eu","Valentin Descas","Thanks [~accountid:712020:ad0f28bc-2e04-43b5-8352-a3a48fd3f720] !! ","2026-01-23T09:29:21.586Z"],["3832743","DO-5797","DO","mattias.siimar@bolt.eu","Mattias Siimar","With my pii cluster with common workspace the queries work\n\n","2026-01-23T09:29:38.367Z"],["3832744","HS-29222","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:7f339fc8-1d2a-4500-903a-50ef7065e24d],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-23T09:30:26.813Z"],["3832745","HS-29223","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:7f339fc8-1d2a-4500-903a-50ef7065e24d],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-23T09:30:29.656Z"],["3832746","PRF-1412","PRF","marianne.kaarma@bolt.eu","Marianne Kaarma","Duplicate","2026-01-23T09:30:30.538Z"],["3832747","HS-29224","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:7f339fc8-1d2a-4500-903a-50ef7065e24d],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-23T09:30:33.592Z"],["3832749","HS-29225","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:7f339fc8-1d2a-4500-903a-50ef7065e24d],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-23T09:30:37.040Z"],["3832750","HS-29226","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:7f339fc8-1d2a-4500-903a-50ef7065e24d],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-23T09:30:41.437Z"],["3832751","HS-29227","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:7f339fc8-1d2a-4500-903a-50ef7065e24d],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-23T09:30:43.605Z"],["3832752","HS-29228","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:7f339fc8-1d2a-4500-903a-50ef7065e24d],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-23T09:30:47.490Z"],["3832753","CCM-22303","CCM","leila.toomet@bolt.eu","Leila Toomet","Not entirely, please turn to [refilwe@bolt.eu|mailto:refilwe@bolt.eu] → she should know how to delete the user.","2026-01-23T09:30:48.200Z"],["3832754","PRF-1781","PRF","marianne.kaarma@bolt.eu","Marianne Kaarma","Duplicate","2026-01-23T09:30:52.897Z"],["3832756","DSR-3981","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T09:31:06.089Z"],["3832758","FPD-1503","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","Validated data and it all seems good.\nSpreadsheet with consolidated results: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/13rw-RMH4UvD0dfjNB58-EeFzi34ZjIXNaG1rvIeiKZs/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/13rw-RMH4UvD0dfjNB58-EeFzi34ZjIXNaG1rvIeiKZs/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] \nI’ll be looking at some other interesting conclusions and insights from the analysis to share later today.","2026-01-23T09:33:03.499Z"],["3832760","FPD-1488","FPD","andrei.kuchev@bolt.eu","Andrei Kuchev","Update - the pipeline has been executed successfully for all cities: [https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/414849519429571/runs/275005916440721?o=2472566184436351|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/414849519429571/runs/275005916440721?o=2472566184436351] ","2026-01-23T09:33:35.010Z"],["3832761","FPD-1435","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","Results from [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FPD-1503|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FPD-1503|smart-link]  are consolidated in [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/13rw-RMH4UvD0dfjNB58-EeFzi34ZjIXNaG1rvIeiKZs/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/13rw-RMH4UvD0dfjNB58-EeFzi34ZjIXNaG1rvIeiKZs/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] \nFurther insights and conclusions will be shared in the ticket’s comments section later today.","2026-01-23T09:33:42.206Z"],["3832763","DO-5797","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Hey [~accountid:631aec119796033b256e3421] ,\n\nThis ticket is not approved from your manager yet and closed because there is no response from you.\nPlease ask your manager approval","2026-01-23T09:34:25.490Z"],["3832768","PFI-837617","PFI","chatrawee.saenwerm@bolt-outsource.eu","Chatrawee Saenwerm","!image-20260123-093411.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260123-093418.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T09:35:18.390Z"],["3832769","PRF-1850","PRF","marianne.kaarma@bolt.eu","Marianne Kaarma","Duplicate","2026-01-23T09:35:20.884Z"],["3832771","FPD-1215","FPD","andrei.kuchev@bolt.eu","Andrei Kuchev","Doing as a part of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FPD-1488|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FPD-1488|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T09:35:35.560Z"],["3832772","FPD-1227","FPD","kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu","Kateryna Kolomiiets","PR started by [~accountid:61027991627b560068c6ec21] \n[https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15106|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15106|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T09:35:43.348Z"],["3832774","FPD-1489","FPD","andrei.kuchev@bolt.eu","Andrei Kuchev","Done","2026-01-23T09:36:32.043Z"],["3832775","DSR-2999","DSR","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Thank you [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]. No problem - I have now sent the attached out and will keep you posted on any response we may receive. Thank you!\n\n[^Letter to Mrs Sharon Channer - Bolt Services UK Limited - 23 January 2026.docx.pdf]\n[^Bolt Mail - Response to your letter dated 9 January 2026.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-23T09:36:41.097Z"],["3832777","FX-3694","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dmitrii Bokovikov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769161020835589]*{color}:\nHi <@U018QFU5G2X> tax reports page is temporarily disabled for most countries in Fleet Portal but we plan gradual rollout in February. You can use [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/reports/fleetReport] to download and send them manually instead\n{quote}","2026-01-23T09:37:15.050Z"],["3832780","SAI-1435","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","Created PR [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161002|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161002|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T09:37:34.183Z"],["3832781","PFI-836395","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\n\n\nThe Customer Payments Operations Team does not have the required tools/permissions to issue refunds. If you are not able to issue the refund then we kindly ask you to check with your Team Lead on how to solve this case. You may need to request the following accesses in Admin to be able to issue refund for orders if you previously do not have such: \n\n\n\n* *Rides*: refund_payments and customer_support_beehive_ridehailing_order_refund\n* *Delivery*:  delivery_order_refund\n* *Rentals*: rental_order_refund, rental_subscriptions_refund and rental_order_refund_city_fine\n* *Carsharing*: rental_car_order_refund\n* *Bolt+*: subscription_offer_customer_support\n\n\n\n{color:#bf2600}*Note: A failed card payment can’t be refunded to the card. Only successful card payments can be refunded to card.*{color}\n\nFor issues with refunds from Beehive, kindly reach out to #beehive-agent-support on Slack.\n\n{color:#ff5630}For older orders refund, kindly check with your team lead as they have the required accesses to perform such operations.{color}\n\nThere must have been issues issuing a full refund in case there are limits stating that the total refunded amount to both Bolt balance and original payment method should not exceed the total order amount. These limits are set by the Beehive team, kindly reach out to #beehive-agent-support on Slack.","2026-01-23T09:37:54.290Z"],["3832782","CSDA-296","CSDA","roman.trohhalev@bolt.eu","Roman Trohhalev","Hi [~accountid:5d3d9afd7e09400be06bcb30]!\n\nI’ve added a Case Issue Keys filter, that is applied to all tiles.\n\nLast tile *Delivery Type - Case Overview* has per case data with links and Provider name\n\nPlease let me know, if this solution works for you","2026-01-23T09:38:02.031Z"],["3832784","SREP-1121","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","Reason here: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02HNCHRMRA/p1769161081537719?thread_ts=1769010923.454349&cid=C02HNCHRMRA|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02HNCHRMRA/p1769161081537719?thread_ts=1769010923.454349&cid=C02HNCHRMRA] ","2026-01-23T09:38:20.809Z"],["3832785","LSS-59597","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team, \n\n[~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] thank you for your input! \n\n[~accountid:712020:e81c1984-54f1-46ce-bc81-864b3748de94] when reviewing agreements and sharing them with partners, the process typically works as follows:\nAs the owner of the matter, please share the draft with the landlord. Once you receive their reviewed version, including any comments indicating whether they agree or disagree with the proposed changes, kindly share it in this ticket for our review 😉 \n\nBased on the scope of their comments and the overall situation, I will then assess and advise on the most appropriate next steps, thank you! ","2026-01-23T09:38:35.585Z"],["3832787","MM-941","MM","kristjan.praks@bolt.eu","Kristjan Praks","First mockups: [https://www.figma.com/board/uFka8MLcxiDYaI8lixBwnC/GAC-tab-unifier?node-id=0-1&t=0CnLChgsyIqZIlG6-1|https://www.figma.com/board/uFka8MLcxiDYaI8lixBwnC/GAC-tab-unifier?node-id=0-1&t=0CnLChgsyIqZIlG6-1|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T09:38:38.398Z"],["3832788","XP-2317","XP","yaroslav.morozevych@bolt.eu","Yaroslav Morozevych","[~accountid:712020:469d02b5-abf2-42fb-9357-94b8c8901f09] No, I think there’s still a “bug” there. That’s because before we do the dashboard metadata composition, we apply selected treatments to the data, so the data get’s filtered. And, given that we only have the required sample size info for the whole test (for all treatments included), we see this “Not reached“. \n\nOne way of fixing it is to divide the metadata onto two groups – the selection dependent metadata and dashboard related metadata, and compose it separately. \n\nAnother way is, given the full required sample size and expected distributions, adjust the required sample size calculation based on the treatments selected. \n\nBut it’s not only an API bug, it is rather the whole UX bug as it’s a broader question. We can discuss how to properly handle it.","2026-01-23T09:38:40.030Z"],["3832792","CCM-22303","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Found it, permanently deleted. ","2026-01-23T09:38:56.208Z"],["3832793","DSR-2999","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Thanks a million [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] 🔥 \n\nCSPC - I have set this ticket to “waiting for user”, in case the user follows-up with us instead of on [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f]'s side. Please ping both of us here if we receive an answer on the existing thread. Many thanks! ","2026-01-23T09:39:23.569Z"],["3832794","SAI-1434","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","Created doc: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CD/pages/7390298328/2026-01+Agentic+and+Multi+Agentic+approach|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CD/pages/7390298328/2026-01+Agentic+and+Multi+Agentic+approach|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T09:39:23.955Z"],["3832795","CSP-372","CSP","david.tomes@bolt.eu","David Tomeš","Hi folks,\n\nI have an example, maybe it will help to understand the current pain. Let’s go step by step.\n\n*Context:* We received [a complain|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/702495119]t from an eater about the courier, and we needed the ticket for the legal team. So, we are looking for the courier ticket to figure out if he contacted our support. \n\nThe initial steps are the following: \n\n# Find the [order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/275609609?cityId=15&showUserTz=false]\n# Copy the courier ID\n# Go to Beehive and paste the ID\n\n*So now you’re in the situation where:* \n\n* Support cases tied to the delivery order are not visible on the order page in Admin, so that’s why we opt for manual search in the first place\n* The ticket created field is not present, so comparing the order creation date with the support case creation date is impossible\n* With the two pieces of the above information missing, you have to look for the ticket manually, but since *_I’m unable to contact the customer_* is quite a common issue type for courier cases, good luck :melting_face: ","2026-01-23T09:39:28.672Z"],["3832801","HS-29229","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:7f339fc8-1d2a-4500-903a-50ef7065e24d],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-23T09:40:18.529Z"],["3832802","FPD-1515","FPD","andrei.kuchev@bolt.eu","Andrei Kuchev","Update - first scenario “Planned spend” has been executed here: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1SvqdiHsTz5j5IsNxBwV4BEVMmZDkkXOzXgJ5PXU3nSQ/edit?gid=406601848#gid=406601848|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1SvqdiHsTz5j5IsNxBwV4BEVMmZDkkXOzXgJ5PXU3nSQ/edit?gid=406601848#gid=406601848|smart-link] \n\nThe models have been improved (thanks to [~accountid:712020:1534b9a1-6efe-4e9f-860e-39b8f161f56b]), and deviation from budget is now small for most of the cities\n\nThe next steps are:\n\n# Explore remaining cities (~5)\n# Explore if we can reduce even further\n# Add remaining scenarios to MTD\n# Use it as a shadow MTD for the February with the goal to release in March","2026-01-23T09:40:19.855Z"],["3832803","CCM-22303","CCM","leila.toomet@bolt.eu","Leila Toomet","Thank you! user: [dorcas.badmus@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:dorcas.badmus@bolt-outsource.eu] was pushed to TalentLMS side.","2026-01-23T09:40:20.116Z"],["3832804","HS-29230","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:7f339fc8-1d2a-4500-903a-50ef7065e24d],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-23T09:40:20.712Z"],["3832806","DSR-3983","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T09:41:20.837Z"],["3832812","PFI-835173","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey, we saw no improvement. We’ve disabled in-app for this driver.","2026-01-23T09:42:02.641Z"],["3832814","WD-22675","WD","kadi.ilinoh@bolt.eu","Kadi Ilinõh","Please also remove validation from account 5100, so spend category Operational Fines could be used with this account. There is balance on this account and needs to be corrected to 5101 spend category Operational Fines.","2026-01-23T09:42:26.476Z"],["3832815","PFI-836392","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThat payment was made on a different account [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4041350398|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4041350398]. Kindly follow up with your team on how to resolve this case as an unknown charge one.","2026-01-23T09:42:27.198Z"],["3832816","PFI-837212","PFI","zuzanna.stanislawiak@bolt-outsource.eu","Zuzanna Stanisławiak","[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/728480082|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/728480082] same problem","2026-01-23T09:42:32.602Z"],["3832818","LSS-61595","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi [~accountid:712020:3b6b3bd5-c905-4a63-9b41-178bc47054f7] I’m sorry for the delayed reply! \n\nPlease find my comments to the proposed changes below:\n\n* 3.2.3 - they have deleted this from the original template. This is not ideal situation for us. If our partner gets bought by a competitor—say, Uber or another ride-hailing company—we'd be stuck in a marketing deal that's now helping our rival. This clause lets us walk away immediately if that happens, rather than being locked in until the contract expires. My proposal is to modify the clause in a way that allows us to terminate only if the partner is acquired by a direct competitor in the ride-hailing space. \nFor example: 3.2.3. _there is a change of controlling interest in the Partner resulting in the Partner becoming controlled by a direct competitor of Bolt in the ride-hailing industry._\n* 11.11 - the prevailing language close was deleted. Are we signing the agreement only in Chinese? If yes, then we are fine with removing this.\n\nRegarding all the other changes, these are acceptable for us.\n\nPlease let me know if anything remained unclear!\n\nThank you!","2026-01-23T09:42:43.842Z"],["3832820","CNT-474","CNT","kristjan.konsap@bolt.eu","Kristjan-Johannes Konsap","The copy is in review with our copy editors. Deadline: Wednesday.","2026-01-23T09:43:01.620Z"],["3832822","INT-578","INT","olga.vyrostko@bolt.eu","Olga Vyrostko","Not really - some investigative work was done here, but real full scale development was postponed due to change of priorities. This was less actionable than some other initiatives - some discovery from DA side is still needed here to get this ready for dev. ","2026-01-23T09:43:22.916Z"],["3832823","CCM-22303","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Thank you so much, Leila! 🌷 ","2026-01-23T09:43:35.987Z"],["3832824","PTWS-2135","PTWS","octavian.todor@bolt.eu","Octavian Todor","moving this to prod","2026-01-23T09:43:59.828Z"],["3832825","CCM-22303","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey Peace 👋 \n\nDorcas should now be able to open the TalentLMS. Let me know if she needs some courses assigned. 🙂 ","2026-01-23T09:44:37.144Z"],["3832827","LSS-62056","LSS","merve.yilmaz@bolt.eu","Merve Yilmaz","First round of review done. Waiting for the rest to get finalised.","2026-01-23T09:44:43.049Z"],["3832828","LSS-61592","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/346132|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/346132|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T09:44:52.628Z"],["3832830","WD-22677","WD","siret.saks@bolt.eu","Siret Saks","!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 11.43.20.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T09:45:15.530Z"],["3832831","CSDA-296","CSDA","jevgeni@bolt.eu","Jevgeni Beloussov","Thanks, Roman. This helps.\n\nQQ: we can only collect tickets from users who had completed a payment/order? can users submit tickets if they were unsuccessful to use the service (in our case, when they were denied to pay using DineOut)?","2026-01-23T09:45:28.359Z"],["3832832","SUPX-2313","SUPX","pranav.dineshkumar@bolt.eu","Pranav Dinesh Kumar","Let’s not enable it yet for CS tickets. The CS team is sorting out a few things before enabling this. ","2026-01-23T09:45:48.828Z"],["3832839","DRX-28209","DRX","ajinkya.deshmukh@bolt.eu","Ajinkya Suhas Deshmukh","Thanks [~accountid:628dd714269a9a0068f2a783] for the detailed review!\n\nI have made the requested changes, could you please have a look -\n\n* [+DRIVERAPP-T4013 (1.0)+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/DRIVERAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/291515560] - Its mentioned in the preconditions to setup a sort or filter before hand.\n* [+DRIVERAPP-T4014 (1.0)+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/DRIVERAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/291515664] looks similar to [+DRIVERAPP-T4010 (1.0)+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/DRIVERAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/291513921] - Wanted to make a differentiation in terms of checking in [+DRIVERAPP-T4014 (1.0)+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/DRIVERAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/291515664] if the data is actually filtered and only the filtered orders are listed.\n* [+DRIVERAPP-T4027 (1.0)+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/DRIVERAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/292591736] , [+DRIVERAPP-T4028 (1.0)+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/DRIVERAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/292591790], [+DRIVERAPP-T4029 (1.0)+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/DRIVERAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/292592212] - updated the titles\n* [{color:#0747a6}+DRIVERAPP-T4041+{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/DRIVERAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/DRIVERAPP-T4041] - Added TC for moving filter to first position\n* [{color:#0747a6}+DRIVERAPP-T4042+{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/DRIVERAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/DRIVERAPP-T4042] - Added Reset All button should not be present if no filters are applied\n* [{color:#0747a6}+DRIVERAPP-T4043+{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/DRIVERAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/DRIVERAPP-T4043] - Added for checking persistent filters ","2026-01-23T09:47:54.096Z"],["3832841","PC-4955","PC","yauheni.zara@bolt.eu","Yauheni Zara","Reached out the PO support - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C010VCJ4T3Q/p1769068890054569|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C010VCJ4T3Q/p1769068890054569|smart-link] .\n\nFrom what we see short timeouts periodically happens during the applepay confirmation because of PO invoice creation timeouts.\n\n!image-20260123-094614.png|width=860,alt=\"image-20260123-094614.png\"!\n\n[https://nodemonitor.boltint.net/graph/goto/uBZ79sSDR?orgId=1|https://nodemonitor.boltint.net/graph/goto/uBZ79sSDR?orgId=1]","2026-01-23T09:48:08.265Z"],["3832844","PFI-837626","PFI","lukas.bocevicius@bolt-outsource.eu","Lukas Bocevičius","!Screenshot_20260116-173807_Artea.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T09:48:33.956Z"],["3832847","BEE-3668","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","I have analysed reported schemas and services for compatibility with TiDB based on the resources linked in the first point of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/3788374637/TiDB+Migration+Checklist|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/3788374637/TiDB+Migration+Checklist|smart-link]. I manually checked and allowed the Cursor to analyse the compatibility documentation and services one by one.\n\nThe services are ready for TiDB migration; however, one method in the beehive-task service concerns me: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/ec32ddcb34f1eb19e19d72f6220bfe23b294a52f/src/platform/beehive/beehive_task/main/repository/DbTaskRepository.ts#L153-L189|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/ec32ddcb34f1eb19e19d72f6220bfe23b294a52f/src/platform/beehive/beehive_task/main/repository/DbTaskRepository.ts#L153-L189]. It uses ID-based sorting, and we know that in TiDB, auto-increment IDs are not sequential. This method is only used in the backfill cron of the beehive-assembled service, which is currently disabled. Therefore, I do not see this as a problem.\n\nI used a script to migrate the beehive-task schema to TiDB locally and ran tests; everything seems to work fine. [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/3787425533/Migrating+to+TiDB+locally|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/3787425533/Migrating+to+TiDB+locally|smart-link] \n\ncc [~accountid:604aad65ceccdd006a3af17d], let me know if anything else needs to be done. I will mark the task as resolved for now.","2026-01-23T09:49:35.215Z"],["3832849","PFI-837629","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-23T09:50:19.623Z"],["3832850","PFI-835302","PFI","wiktoria.wawryszuk@bolt.eu","Wiktoria Wawryszuk","Hey Artem, it was the last ivnoice (PDF below) it looks like its been already corrected (screenshot) so you can close this request.\n\n[^PL5526-2.pdf]\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 10.49.45.png|width=627,height=333,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 10.49.45.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-23T09:50:33.873Z"],["3832851","SUPX-2313","SUPX","pranav.dineshkumar@bolt.eu","Pranav Dinesh Kumar","No need to change the design for this reminder. We just use the standard notification template. Copy can be specific.","2026-01-23T09:51:05.516Z"],["3832852","DSR-3985","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T09:51:07.092Z"],["3832854","HS-29309","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Hi Anastasiya,\n\nThank you for reaching out to us.\nA stamped and signed confirmation letter is waiting for you in the HQ reception.\nHave a great weekend!\n\nKind regards,\nAike-Maris","2026-01-23T09:52:04.195Z"],["3832855","LSS-59015","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac], hi Team - thanks for looping Privacy in! I’m taking a look at this to gather the full context on this case - bear with me :loading: ","2026-01-23T09:52:14.602Z"],["3832857","BDB-1548","BDB","tiffany.irianto@bolt.eu","Tiffany Ainnurrahmi Irianto","Hi, for the deisgn, I need to get the detail for promo offering first before proceeding with localization, so let’s put this on hold and I will update once the localization is in progress and/or done. [~accountid:5d289a7c3e09b40c262cfaa9] [~accountid:60a8d3053fae6f00681b708e] Thanks!","2026-01-23T09:52:37.352Z"],["3832858","PFI-837630","PFI","anna.zaritska@bolt.eu","Anna Zaritska","[^UA_Manual payout template - 23.01.csv]","2026-01-23T09:52:40.704Z"],["3832860","PFI-837631","PFI","edvin.hansson@bolt-outsource.eu","Edvin Hans Wilhelm Hansson","[^Bolt Dec 17 Receipt (1).pdf]\n\n[^Bolt Dec 17 Ride Details (1).pdf]","2026-01-23T09:52:52.504Z"],["3832861","PFI-837631","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-23T09:52:54.734Z"],["3832862","FRAUD-5602","FRAUD","aleksei.loos@bolt.eu","Aleksei Loos","Second round of grooming:\n\n* New tag\n* Adjusting the decision tree based on the diagram\n* Two checkpoints, same thing\n* Testing\n\nShould be doable in 2-3 days.\n\n[~accountid:712020:0ef4b6b0-5fb9-4a66-a66b-0a7c707a4f8f] this ticket is ready for prioritization (note: this is an overdue task, should be higher)","2026-01-23T09:53:12.508Z"],["3832865","LSS-62020","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Thanks [~accountid:712020:f50af85a-3d8b-4b5c-b19d-ad552b86d158] , I added one sentence regarding when the notice shall be deemed received. From this date we should start counting 90 Business day notice period. Other than this - all good. ","2026-01-23T09:53:44.143Z"],["3832868","DML-5457","DML","giacomo.giorgianni@bolt.eu","Giacomo Giorgianni","Rejecting for now as it doesn’t seem to be an extremely trivial change and we can work on other topics instead. \nShall we collect evidences in the future that this is heavily affecting our Customer Experience, we’ll create it again. ","2026-01-23T09:54:02.644Z"],["3832871","WFM-10100","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","SP granted. Please give it ~10 mins for the market access to kick in.","2026-01-23T09:54:33.479Z"],["3832872","AD-4","AD","eirini.zafeiratou@bolt.eu","Eirini Zafeiratou","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4126fc0-85ff-45d4-af88-bc851d5b32bc] can you please assign to Aurelien Pozzana instead of myself? he can’t view this ticket right now","2026-01-23T09:54:52.259Z"],["3832873","PFI-835970","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","გამარჯობა \n\n  \n\nგთხოვთ, დაგვიბრუნდეთ პასუხით \n\nსაკითხი კრიტიკულია \n\n   \n\n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n *{color:#0093D3} *პატივისცემით*{color}* \n\n *{color:#0093D3} *Sincerely*{color}* \n{color:#0093D3}{color}\n----\n{color:#0093D3}{color}  \n\n *{color:#0093D3} *ნათია ბატიაშვილი*{color}**{color:#0093D3} */*{color}*  *{color:#0093D3} *Natia Batiashvili*{color}* \n\n{color:#1F497D}ბარათების{color}{color:#1F497D}{color} {color:#1F497D}მენეჯერი{color}{color:#1F497D} /{color} {color:#1F497D}Card Manager{color} \n\n{color:#1F497D}მომხმარებელთა{color}{color:#1F497D}{color} {color:#1F497D}მხარდაჭერის{color}{color:#1F497D}{color} {color:#1F497D}განყოფილება{color}{color:#1F497D} /{color} {color:#1F497D}Customer Support Department{color}{color:#595959}{color}{color:#2F5496}{color} \n\n  \n\n  \n\n *{color:#333399} *Tel:*{color}* {color:#333399}+(995 32) 2 27 27 37 (*4){color} \n\n *{color:#333399} *Fax:*{color}* {color:#333399}+(995 32) 2 77 27 74{color} \n\n[{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}|https://urldefense.com/v3/__http:/www.tbcbank.ge/__;!\\!P1qVsL2A!JjZp3RvKmPyFPpMib2WSUCp6PkWNjFswW63tExjK8iJPWNwDfHIlD8kZT1rjOdXXWJZHtiNk2GquYRKhfMLnN1yk4Lcm6hI$] \n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T09:55:15.661Z"],["3832876","HS-29312","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Sent back.","2026-01-23T09:55:32.202Z"],["3832880","DSR-3987","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T09:56:05.560Z"],["3832885","HS-29309","HS","anastasiya.ivanova@bolt.eu","Anastasiya Ivanova","Can you please also send a scan to my email? ","2026-01-23T09:58:33.521Z"],["3832886","LSS-62027","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] Under Lithuanian law, the State Language Inspectorate has statutory powers to request information necessary for carrying out its supervisory tasks. This type of administrative legal obligation is, in principle, capable of constituting a valid legal basis. It’s a request based on administrative law.\n\n* Law on the State Language Inspectorate, Article 5(1)(2), grants the Inspectorate the right to obtain data and documents necessary to perform its functions","2026-01-23T09:58:40.743Z"],["3832887","PFI-837632","PFI","kosisochukwu.ochuaka@bolt-outsource.eu","Kosisochukwu Ochuaka","!image-20260123-095657.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T09:58:59.736Z"],["3832889","WD-22653","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:712020:2ac6873d-e350-474f-b592-55236553c3eb] please try to assign these roles. From Worker page->Actions->Add/remove roles. If any questions let me know","2026-01-23T09:59:48.681Z"],["3832897","WD-22674","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Bug fixed, should work from now on.","2026-01-23T10:00:47.139Z"],["3832898","SREDESK-7457","SREDESK","marcin.kogut@bolt.eu","Marcin Kogut","Hello,\nPlease make it UNSHARDED.\nWe changed the design. ","2026-01-23T10:01:06.427Z"],["3832902","GS-71","GS","radu.vasiliu@bolt.eu","Radu Vasiliu","ETA: 2026-01-30\nStatus: Implementation\n\nSummary: \nFinished integration with Admin-panel. Working on removing limitations:\n• specific polyline per category_group\n• enable/disable individual category_group directions\n\nBlockers: \n\n\nDetails:\n- :done: done implementation \"Alternative #2: Pickup directions per search_category_group\" . Released.\n- :done: done: integration with admin-panel: new UI fields to support editing of directions with search_category_group  => Example https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/pickup-dropoff-areas/areas/64/location/90?tab=directions (Tallinn Airport)\n- :loading: limitation: the walking polyline & the state are stored per area_location. This means that all categories will share the same polyline & state. Working on decoupling.","2026-01-23T10:02:38.976Z"],["3832904","LSS-61595","LSS","teresa.yeh@bolt.eu","Teresa Yeh","Hi [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] - Thanks for your response and professional advice. \n\nI will get back to DBS with the addition of clause 3.2.3 regarding the change of controlling interest.\n\nRegarding 11.11, noted. Since we are signing in Chinese, I will leave this clause as is (removed).\n\nI’ll keep you posted once DBS confirms and is ready to sign the finalized contract. Thanks!","2026-01-23T10:02:43.196Z"],["3832906","PFI-837635","PFI","paratthakon.ainchat@bolt-outsource.eu","Paratthakon Ainchat","!image_480.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image_720.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T10:03:04.154Z"],["3832908","LSS-61994","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/346139|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/346139|smart-link]  ","2026-01-23T10:04:04.402Z"],["3832909","RIDE-516","RIDE","katarina.saage@bolt.eu","Katarina Elisabeth Saage","{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n*Launch target for Marrakesh, Morocco, has been updated to* {{2026-03-03}}\n{panel}","2026-01-23T10:04:13.227Z"],["3832910","CSXRD-232","CSXRD","david.tomes@bolt.eu","David Tomeš","Launch postponed to {{2026-03-03}}","2026-01-23T10:04:14.682Z"],["3832911","WD-22669","WD","aire.vaigu@bolt.eu","Aire Vaigu","Hi,  [~accountid:712020:ad0f28bc-2e04-43b5-8352-a3a48fd3f720] - Box access was already granted to you on {{2026-01-06}}. If you are missing the Box application in your Okta profile, please create a ticket for Internal IT \n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/group/1/create/932|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/group/1/create/932|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T10:04:16.940Z"],["3832912","RISK2-3239","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","*22.01. Update -* Inheriting the Risk Description: We are not able to copy the Risk Description from Operational Risks to Operational Risk Instances. Currently, only text fields can be inherited; text area fields are not supported. This limitation also applies to Jobs, as there is no available option to handle this through Jobs.","2026-01-23T10:04:17.659Z"],["3832915","GC-3171","GC","radu.vasiliu@bolt.eu","Radu Vasiliu","ETA: 2026-01-30\nStatus: Implementation\n\nSummary: \nNo progress this week, due to working with priority on \"Bolt Chauffeur - Lux Category - Pickup Directions\":\n- :loading: Analysing BUG: TollRoad detection at large distance (few km away): causes EdgeDetection to estimate too many tolls. Analysis & testing in progress\n- Next week (starting on Monday, Jan 26) I will be team-duty . Team-duty is priority #1 , I will try to squeeze some effort on this task too.\n\nBlockers: \n\n\nDetails:\n- :done: implementation complete, last PR was merged this week.\n- :done: Run silent-live test for comparing EdgeDetection vs TollGuru,  in Thailand.\n- :done: Extract silent-live results\n- :done: Map OPs team found some bugs while analysing the last silent-live test: EdgeDetection vs TollGuru in  Thailand).\n- :loading: BUG: TollRoad detection at large distance (few km away): causes EdgeDetection to estimate too many tolls. Analysis & testing in progress\n- :done: Tooling: working on Admin-panel page for testing our internal solution: Route-Tolls","2026-01-23T10:05:41.685Z"],["3832916","WFM-10109","WFM","nikita.bogomazovs@bolt-outsource.eu","Nikita Bogomazovs","!Screenshot 2026-01-23 120524.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T10:05:45.155Z"],["3832917","PFI-835611","PFI","iryna.tkach@bolt-outsource.eu","Iryna Tkach","[~accountid:712020:1a99e337-a650-4a85-a8ed-f0825a04e850] please, help us","2026-01-23T10:06:00.907Z"],["3832919","MM-969","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description or requirements are provided. Developers lack information to start work.|\n|Clarity|🔴|The summary is vague and lacks detail. No sections or clear instructions.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting information are present.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate or original estimate is provided.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\n* Clarify the scope and expected outcome.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-23T10:06:17.466Z"],["3832920","PFI-835611","PFI","iryna.tkach@bolt-outsource.eu","Iryna Tkach","All details is correct in our system","2026-01-23T10:06:20.647Z"],["3832924","LSS-62059","LSS","tomasz.symonowicz@bolt.eu","Tomasz Symonowicz","[^Grupa CCC & Bolt Business_Szczególne Warunki_22.12.2025-podpisany.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-23T10:06:33.499Z"],["3832925","LSS-61185","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Under Article 19.1 of the Law of Azerbaijan \"On the State Register of Real Estate\", leases of immovable property must be notarized and registered. For compliance, it is recommended that the agreement term not exceed eleven (11) months; otherwise, notarization and registration provisions should be included.","2026-01-23T10:06:36.153Z"],["3832926","EBIKE1-87","EBIKE1","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","[~accountid:712020:82bad36a-3f0b-4609-8bbe-b4ba65e1094e] please inform YCX about or final decision to move on with the latest design (I will also add the STEP file link below here). YCX can open the mould asap now to be ready for the next order. \n\nWe also made a decision not to add the logo onto the handle.\n\n\n\n* It also means that we have to update the 3D model in assembly and update the revision number of the part and subassembly\n* I will ask supplier to update also the 2D drawing\n\n\n\nSTEP file:  [https://drive.google.com/open?id=1qiBDZUpond5RlkU3VoOlr0b5HgKMmzjX&usp=drive_fs|https://drive.google.com/open?id=1qiBDZUpond5RlkU3VoOlr0b5HgKMmzjX&usp=drive_fs|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T10:06:57.468Z"],["3832928","PFI-837641","PFI","robert.buzukasvili@bolt.eu","Robert Buzukašvili","[^SK1526-299 (3).pdf]","2026-01-23T10:07:36.799Z"],["3832929","PFI-837641","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-23T10:07:39.087Z"],["3832930","PFI-837117","PFI","iryna.tkach@bolt-outsource.eu","Iryna Tkach","[~accountid:712020:1a99e337-a650-4a85-a8ed-f0825a04e850], problem is that in account all details are correct, but when payout is processing there are incorrect bank code from our side and payout is failed all time\n\n","2026-01-23T10:07:45.744Z"],["3832931","LSS-62060","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","[^Bolt - Notice of Extension - January 2026.pdf] _(229 kB)_","2026-01-23T10:07:53.485Z"],["3832934","PFI-837101","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey, we’re not blocking this. This is a response by the payment processor.\nIf they’re still having issues with this, they should contact their bank or card issuer.\nThanks!","2026-01-23T10:08:39.212Z"],["3832935","DSR-3577","DSR","juan.sanchez@bolt.eu","Juan Martin Sanchez","Hi [~accountid:712020:714baa0e-ddd0-4776-8064-c5a5d3ae37aa] 🙂 \n\n(in which system(s)) the data WD needs access to and which team is the owner of it?","2026-01-23T10:09:09.582Z"],["3832943","LSS-62061","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nAghja Davudzade has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-23T10:11:23.243Z"],["3832948","LSS-62061","LSS","aghja.davudzade@bolt.eu","Aghja Davudzade","Hey \nCould you please assist with the following contract\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1b6I8BpS5ThGOJqPPHPrGtXF6YxafPf-2/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1b6I8BpS5ThGOJqPPHPrGtXF6YxafPf-2/edit]","2026-01-23T10:12:16.689Z"],["3832950","DRX-28088","DRX","radu.vasiliu@bolt.eu","Radu Vasiliu","ETA: 2026-03-30\nStatus: Technical Design doc\n\nSummary: \n• Design doc is nearing completion\n• We need the physical taximeter to close open questions and finalize the design doc\n• We can proceed with building out some smaller abstractions that will support this integration\n\nBlockers: \nWe need to verify some taximeter behavior which is ambiguous from documentation. This will only be possible once we get the physical device.\n\nDetails:\nWe have invested time into creating and doing some early reviews and discussions around the technical design. Overall design doc is mostly in place, but there are still some open questions.\n\nWe can also proceed with extracting some common logic shared with other taximeters. This is the 4th taximeter integration our team owns, so some patterns are beginning to emerge, and we can consolidate some logic to reduce future work and maintenance.","2026-01-23T10:13:11.139Z"],["3832951","PFI-836115","PFI","jakub.pekar@bolt-outsource.eu","Jakub Pekar","Please, could you check this case manually? ","2026-01-23T10:13:18.489Z"],["3832953","PFI-837649","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-23T10:13:41.115Z"],["3832955","PFI-837117","PFI","iryna.tkach@bolt-outsource.eu","Iryna Tkach","I will provide you her detail from bank and that IBAN and Code is correct, but payout was failed.\n\n!image.png|width=1750,height=264,alt=\"image.png\"!\n\n!image (1).png|width=1564,height=714,alt=\"image (1).png\"!\n\n!IMG_7803.jpeg|width=390,height=157,alt=\"IMG_7803.jpeg\"!\n\n!IMG_7804.jpeg|width=390,height=174,alt=\"IMG_7804.jpeg\"!\n\n","2026-01-23T10:14:03.749Z"],["3832958","PFI-835611","PFI","iryna.tkach@bolt-outsource.eu","Iryna Tkach","I will provide you her detail from bank and that IBAN and Code is correct, but payout was failed.\n\nWait for your answer \n\n!image.png|width=1750,height=264,alt=\"image.png\"!\n\n!IMG_7804.jpeg|width=390,height=174,alt=\"IMG_7804.jpeg\"!\n\n!image (1).png|width=1564,height=714,alt=\"image (1).png\"!\n\n!IMG_7803.jpeg|width=390,height=157,alt=\"IMG_7803.jpeg\"!\n\n","2026-01-23T10:15:09.234Z"],["3832960","DSR-3989","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T10:16:09.348Z"],["3832961","LSS-62061","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-23T10:16:09.951Z"],["3832962","MLC-3605","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","*Dubai* \n\n*Status:*\n\n* BA: Acquisition - needs translation and proofreading - due date was 21.01. No updates. \n\n*Moldova*\n\n*Status:*\n\n* BA: Onboarding, Product Education, 0 Orders, Awareness, HVO, Promo Codes, Churn - CLONED\n\n*Taiwan*\n\n* *WP:* Translations DONE, sent to proofreading!","2026-01-23T10:16:12.207Z"],["3832963","LSS-58645","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","One of the MOUs has three entities. I am currently getting the details of the signatory as well. I will share it as soon as I have them. \n\nThanks. ","2026-01-23T10:16:12.439Z"],["3832964","PFI-837657","PFI","endurance.lucky@bolt-outsource.eu","Endurance Lucky","!Screenshot_20260119-113853.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T10:17:00.153Z"],["3832965","VULN-681","VULN","radu.neacsu@bolt.eu","Radu-Ștefan Neacșu","The attacker would have to guess both auth_username (user_id) and phone_uuid (random string, uuid v4), making it improbable to happen.\n\nOn top of this, the team is already working on a new auth system. Existing rider / eater auth will start migration to the new system in the 2nd half of 2026. So we won’t invest time into fixing this issue, rather prioritize migration which will solve this indirectly.","2026-01-23T10:17:02.701Z"],["3832967","BLTF-128","BLTF","vladyslav.bohaichuk@bolt.eu","Vladyslav Bohaichuk","[https://nodemonitor.boltint.net/graph/d/ffb0yqk2j7r40c/business-metrics?orgId=1|https://nodemonitor.boltint.net/graph/d/ffb0yqk2j7r40c/business-metrics?orgId=1]","2026-01-23T10:17:18.919Z"],["3832969","LSS-62062","LSS","tom.evans@bolt.eu","Tom Evans","[^NDA LITE Mutual Form - Donut Lab OU (EST)- 2025-06-17.docx] _(32 kB)_","2026-01-23T10:17:44.870Z"],["3832970","WFM-10097","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Asked TLs to approve the request [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0969DN7RL1/p1769162643847919]","2026-01-23T10:17:49.867Z"],["3832974","PFI-837660","PFI","evelyn.obi@bolt-outsource.eu","Evelyn Obi","[^PaymentNotification.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-23T10:18:20.743Z"],["3832976","LSS-60674","LSS","rayko.chakarov@bolt.eu","Rayko Chakarov","\n\n[^Bolt_Partner_General_Terms_BG_ENG_BG_09_2025 (2).docx]\n\nHello after couple  of emails and calls this is the latest update.\n\nHello,We have reviewed the texts you suggested and have reduced our comments to just a few.We have highlighted in yellow in the text of the GTC the clauses on which we have comments or are not acceptable to us. In our opinion, these should be amended with corresponding texts in the special conditions.We consider the remaining clauses to be clarified.","2026-01-23T10:18:34.155Z"],["3832985","PFI-831009","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Hi [~accountid:712020:98578d7d-a19d-4341-a97c-e8099ba8d683], sorry for the delay in getting back to you. If you look further back in the balance entries, you can see that in the beginning of the month there had been a refund of 23796.68 HUF back to the balance. all the following claims have been deducted from this amount and the ride you have highlighted was covered by the balance only partially, the 2963,32 HUF is covering the leftover part for the ride.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 12.16.41.png|width=1101,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 12.16.41.png\"!","2026-01-23T10:19:49.886Z"],["3832986","PC-4951","PC","roman.zavodskikh@bolt.eu","Roman Zavodskikh","Andrei and I discussed this issue.\n\nAll orders are legitimate cancels → no GMV loss\n\nTo-do action item from my side is *not to print those logs (*or print them with info log level) for legitimate cancels.","2026-01-23T10:20:10.104Z"],["3832987","HS-29169","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:b2c09d5d-f839-4294-b3c4-98447cbfb8cb],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-23T10:20:31.836Z"],["3832989","LSS-60535","LSS","ksenia.korolkova@bolt.eu","Ksenia Korolkova","[~accountid:712020:11b028d0-a65b-4db4-93f7-938b14e353e9] update regarding this - we are currently waiting for final confirmations of the amounts for collaterals report, so we expect to have the letter ready in the beginning of the next week.","2026-01-23T10:20:44.955Z"],["3832990","DSR-3991","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T10:21:07.833Z"],["3832993","DSR-2883","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","[~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] , sorry! I misunderstood the exact location of the drivers folder. It should be in the right location now, the letter has been adjusted with the now correct link and I will send it out once access and reminder are set.","2026-01-23T10:21:43.686Z"],["3832995","DSR-2883","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","[~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] , sorry! I misunderstood the exact location of the drivers folder. It should be in the right location now, the letter has been adjusted with the now correct link and I will send it out once access and reminder are set.","2026-01-23T10:21:48.328Z"],["3832996","WD-22672","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:712020:979961a6-5216-4ee0-aa85-a7302993f5e6] we would need to get temporary access to you so that you can submit expense report for multiple entities. Could you please follow instruction [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/WDFTECH/pages/7196180597/How-to+Enable+users+to+submit+expense+reports+across+multiple+entities|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/WDFTECH/pages/7196180597/How-to+Enable+users+to+submit+expense+reports+across+multiple+entities|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T10:22:11.383Z"],["3832999","PFI-834137","PFI","clara.machado@bolt.eu","Clara Oliveira Machado","Hi [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f], \n\nInfo updated. \n\nThanks.","2026-01-23T10:22:21.005Z"],["3833003","RDS-1164","RDS","nami.salimi@bolt.eu","Nami Salimi","[~accountid:627b6b8f19b1290068296d3b] I believe we do, but we think it could be good to have some basic information cached (like license plate number, etc) to help riders in cases they loose connection getting out of a building (happens to be every time)","2026-01-23T10:23:19.133Z"],["3833009","BEE-3668","BEE","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","[~accountid:5d807af94f9cf00d60213212] weren’t there some sorting by id still in email-processing service? TBH I expected some there.","2026-01-23T10:23:51.219Z"],["3833010","RDS-1103","RDS","taras.sgibnev@bolt.eu","Taras Sgibnev","[~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] As we discussed yesterday, the actual solution should avoid such errors for the majority of riders.\n\nIf the user hasn’t set up a business payment → Do not display any entry points to Scheduled rides (neither SR button, nor custom ride category). Because the majority of riders have no idea what is business payment and how to get one.\n\nWe might still support this error message as an edge case: if a business payment is available to the user, but they are trying to schedule a ride while another payment is selected.","2026-01-23T10:24:07.175Z"],["3833011","CAMLE-9900","CAMLE","uladzislau.tolkach@bolt.eu","Uladzislau Tolkach","{quote}*= 40*{quote}\n\n:redalert: *ERROR :: driver-conditional-campaign-admin :: [Logs] errors last 2 min* Triggered with value *57.14* ","2026-01-23T10:24:08.127Z"],["3833012","CAMLE-9900","CAMLE",null,"Slack","[Uladzislau Tolkach|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6305dd67cf3340e8737f8f66] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C062K4EU0R4/p1769100391844389|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C062K4EU0R4/p1769100391844389|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-23T10:24:09.343Z"],["3833016","WFM-10103","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Hello [~accountid:712020:202fa69e-560f-4d95-9010-528fd370280e] you need to raise an Onboarding ticket to IT for the creation of Bolt emails.\nOnce Bolt emails are created, you’ll need to raise a separate Jira ticket to WFM to add the roles/permissions, in the same ticket, you can indicate to:\n- Switch off Play Mode\n- Assign them a role OS Restricted Sites Manager in Admin (which will give the same role in Assembled)\n- Any other requests please indicate it.\nClosing this ticket for now.","2026-01-23T10:25:00.866Z"],["3833019","DSR-2883","DSR","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","Hey [~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] \n\nYes, the letter has the correct link now and you can proceed with remaining steps. I’ve granted view access to [drahman1961@gmail.com|mailto:drahman1961@gmail.com] and will revoke in 7 days. ","2026-01-23T10:25:40.884Z"],["3833020","PFI-837666","PFI","success.igbinosa@bolt-outsource.eu","Success Igbinosa","!4K 19TH.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T10:26:03.800Z"],["3833022","MARTECH3-1562","MARTECH3","taqi.naqvi@bolt.eu","Taqi Naqvi","h2. *1. Content Block Versioning*\n\n*Current Issue:*\n\nContent blocks are effectively \"locked\" once they are set to *Active/Live*. Users cannot update a block (e.g., fixing a typo or updating a legal footer) without risking immediate impact on live campaigns or having to create a duplicate block, which fragments the library.\n\n*Proposed Approach:*\n\n* *Versioning System:* Implement a \"Draft/Publish\" workflow for existing blocks.\n* *Edit Flow:* Allow users to \"Create New Draft\" from a Live block. The Live version remains active in production until the new Draft is explicitly published.\n* *Rollback:* (Optional) Ability to revert to the previous version if an issue is detected.\n\n----\n\nh2. *2. Translation String Parsing (*{{<p>}} *Tag Segmentation)*\n\n*Current Issue:*\n\nThe HTML parser currently treats an entire {{<p>}} block (including all inline HTML and styles) as a *single Crowdin string*. This causes issues when styles change or when text needs to be segmented for different grammar structures in target languages.\n\n*Proposed Approach:*\n\n* *Granular Extraction:* Update the parser to treat text nodes as independent strings, separating them from the container styling.\n* *Structure:* Maintain the HTML structure as a skeleton but send only the text contents (and necessary inline tags like {{<a>}} or {{<b>}}) to Crowdin.\n\n----\n\nh2. *3. Personalization UI & Error Prevention*\n\n*Current Issue:*\n\n* *Insertion:* Users must manually type Liquid syntax (e.g., {{{{user_profile.first_name}}}}), leading to frequent typos (e.g., {{user_profle}}) and rendering errors.\n* *Testing:* The \"Preview\" pane relies on manual JSON input for user data, which is technical and error-prone.\n\n*Proposed Approach:*\n\n* *Variable Picker:* Introduce a \"Personalization\" dropdown menu in the editor toolbar. This should list all available user attributes (User ID, Name, City, etc.) and insert the correct Liquid tag upon click.\n* *Auto-Generated Testing Form:* The Preview panel should parse the HTML, detect all Liquid variables used, and automatically generate a *Form UI* (Input fields) for testing, replacing the raw JSON \"Override\" box.\n\n----\n\nh2. *4. Error Handling & Diagnostics*\n\n*Current Issue:*\n\n* Errors such as {{<— content block test_taqi not resolved -->}} are vague. Users cannot distinguish if the block is missing, unauthorized, or simply in \"Draft\" mode.\n* Liquid syntax errors often lack context.\n\n*Proposed Approach:*\n\n* *Granular Error States:* Update error messages to be specific:\n** _“Block exists but is in Draft state (Activate to view).”_\n** _“Block ID not found.”_\n** _“Circular dependency detected.”_\n* *Validation:* Implementation of \"Line & Column\" indicators for syntax errors to speed up debugging.\n\n----\n\nh2. *5. Documentation & Resources*\n\n*Current Issue:*\n\nUsers frequently ask for Liquid documentation, unaware of which standard tags (Shopify/Braze) are supported or what custom Bolt tags exist.\n\n*Proposed Approach:*\n\n* *Embedded Documentation:* Add a \"Reference\" or \"Help\" sidebar tab within the Editor UI.\n* *Content:* Include a \"Cheat Sheet\" of standard Liquid filters ({{date}}, {{default}}, {{capitalize}}) and a list of internal Bolt-specific variables/blocks.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 11.20.32 AM.png|width=766,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 11.20.32 AM.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 11.18.23 AM.png|width=766,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 11.18.23 AM.png\"!","2026-01-23T10:26:54.031Z"],["3833024","HS-29236","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-23T10:27:53.133Z"],["3833026","FRAUD-5726","FRAUD","martin.lovisuda@bolt.eu","Martin Lõvisüda","All of the old unused or legacy secrets have been deleted. All of the secrets that we actively use have been rotated. ","2026-01-23T10:28:20.324Z"],["3833027","PFI-836638","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Based on invoices. They have the order invoices and bolt invoice, so this is what they use to report their earnings. Earnings should always only be reported based on invoices - monthly or yearly summaries are not valid tax documents. ","2026-01-23T10:28:35.741Z"],["3833030","INT-668","INT","daniel.kamkha@bolt.eu","Daniel Kamkha","26W04: Finalized the design doc. Started working on the development tasks. Estimated rollout 26W07, with availability of new data fields in the Provider Profile as a potential blocker.","2026-01-23T10:28:46.407Z"],["3833031","PFI-837669","PFI","catarina.silva@bolt.eu","Catarina Caneira da Silva","[^Portugália - PT Split Payments template - Template (17).csv]","2026-01-23T10:28:49.423Z"],["3833035","LSS-57933","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Hey, [~accountid:61fbb921845d670071f3c1df]! Thank you for looking into this. I still have two issues not clarified though:\n\n* clause 2.2 - please provide me information about what Pickitoo means by “actions are performed according to the pre-agreed longlist which could be reviewed once per quarter“. This does not make sense legally without context and may be misinterpreted.\n* clause 3.8 - I understand that Bolt will not be responsible for all audit costs, but we need to say who will be covering costs. Would it be both parties equally?","2026-01-23T10:29:52.843Z"],["3833036","BEE-3668","BEE","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","As for sorting by id for backfilling purposes, I think it should still be fine even if ids aren’t monotonic.\n\nBefore any backfilling, a proper change to all new instances of entities should already be implemented.\n\nSo there may be 2 corner cases happening in the middle of the process of backfilling:\n\n* either a new instance id appeared behind the backfill window - we will never go back to it, but it’s expected and fine, since it should either way be correct\n* or a new instance id appeared in front of the backfill window - then we will process it as part of the backfill, potentially prolonging the backfill, but data-wise this should be no-op\n\nWe could theoretically migrate to ordering by some timestamps, but there is always an issue with timestamps that there can be multiple records with the same value, so backfill ranges would need to be overlapping. If there were N tasks with the same timestamp equal to CRON’s limit, it would mean that the CRON could not progress further.\n\nId based sorting does not have this problem, so I think it’s ok for it to stay.","2026-01-23T10:30:06.220Z"],["3833037","BEE-3668","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","[~accountid:604aad65ceccdd006a3af17d] Indeed, I forgot to mention these two methods [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/4b82edbf03a53286537f336509e4060349cd30b1/src/platform/cs/email_support_processing/main/table/EmailEventLogTable.ts#L55-L93|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/4b82edbf03a53286537f336509e4060349cd30b1/src/platform/cs/email_support_processing/main/table/EmailEventLogTable.ts#L55-L93] \n\nI believe it can be resolved by simply replacing ID column with created column, adding correct index is recommended ","2026-01-23T10:30:23.883Z"],["3833038","LSS-61707","LSS","bruno.pereira@bolt.eu","Bruno dos Reis Pereira","Hello Catarina,\n\n_“On_ *_October 28, 2025, at around 9:00 p.m., I placed an order_* _through the Bolt Food platform at the McDonald’s restaurant, with an_ *_estimated delivery time of approximately 9:30 p.m._*_”_ - Can we see if this is true? \n\nThe user probably made a typo with the date, the order took place on 26/10, exactly at 21:09:25, the estimate delivery time in the system was between 15 - 30 minutes\n\n_At_ *_around 9:15 p.m., the order was marked as “ready,” awaiting pickup by the courier._* _“_ - Can we see if this is true?\n\nThe order was marker as ready to be picked up at 26/10, 21:14:43, so the user is correct\n\n“_After_ *_contacting the courier via message_*_,_ *_he informed me that the motorcycle was broken down_*_, that he had accepted the order by mistake, and_ *_that he was unable to cancel the order_*_, also_ *_stating that the consumer did not have that option available in the application either_*_.”_\n\nWe can’t see the comms between courier and eater, if they happened more than 30 days ago.\n\n_At around_ *_10:25 p.m. a new courier was assigned to the first order_*_, which_ *_ended up being delivered only at 10:35 p.m_*_. - Do we have a ay to know if this is true?_\n\nA new courier was indeed assigned to the order, at 26/10, 22:23:22, the order was delivered in our system at 26/10, 22:33:50\n\n\n_Did we reach out to the courier for him to give is version of the facts? What did he say?_\n\nWe did not, there was no report from the courier regarding any issue when delivering, couriers are advised to contact us if there are any issues, take a picture of the food next to the delivery address/door, and this was not the case\n\nI must mention also, that the user made a second order 26/10, 21:38:06, as he thought he would not get his first order, which he did.\n\n\n\nApologies for the delay in replying","2026-01-23T10:30:27.478Z"],["3833040","RDS-1022","RDS","taras.sgibnev@bolt.eu","Taras Sgibnev","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] AFAIK, the snapping area is still defined by the Geo BE and measured in meters. While the expected behaviour is the opposite: it should be measured in px/pt (like a UI tool) and stay fixed regardless of the current map zoom level.\n\nUnfortunately, this is not a bug. It was originally designed by the Geo team this way.","2026-01-23T10:30:47.104Z"],["3833043","PFI-837675","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-23T10:32:18.137Z"],["3833044","PFI-837675","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:5d8df399c7d4e30dc2836580] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-23T10:32:19.758Z"],["3833045","PFI-837300","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Will look into this. ","2026-01-23T10:32:28.043Z"],["3833048","RDS-1212","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] Thx a lot for the context, now it is clearer.\n\nMy perspective on that: for things that are broken due to layout flaws, I believe it should definitely be a part of the debt. I would probably leave the ticket here, but rename it to something like: “Fixing layout for non-Latin languages”. \n\nThe next steps would probably be:\n- Take a closer look (ideally, by native speakers) to identify where the specific issues are to create relevant tickets (like: “Fixing Active Order View layout for Thai language on iOS”).\n- Design and Tech aligns about ways to prevent it (probably some rules about UI elements behaviour, plus QA) so we won’t introduce new Debt for future features.\n\n[~accountid:712020:28ec7636-10da-43ee-a95c-be32cdfb7744] [~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] FYI, please let us know if you see it differently. ","2026-01-23T10:33:32.823Z"],["3833049","DRX-27635","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","(/) {{Earnings Island Balance Tile Tapped}} event is created when the driver clicks on the Balance tile when the Earnings Island is expanded\n(/) {{Earnings Island Weekly Tile Tapped}} event is created when the driver clicks on the Weekly tile when the Earnings Island is expanded\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 12.33.23.png|width=1068,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 12.33.23.png\"!\n\n\n","2026-01-23T10:35:08.776Z"],["3833051","PFI-837567","PFI","elijah.ojeamien@bolt-outsource.eu","Elijah Ojeamien","Hi team, the payment has not been allocated.","2026-01-23T10:36:28.534Z"],["3833053","MM-970","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description or requirements are provided; only a summary exists.|\n|Clarity|🔴|The summary is vague and lacks detail, making the issue unclear.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting information are present.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate or original estimate is provided.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\n* Clarify the summary and scope.\n* Link to any relevant documentation.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-23T10:36:47.777Z"],["3833054","DAEN-1406","DAEN","amruth.anand@bolt.eu","Amruth Anand","Hey [~accountid:6424154157f0c028e2f7632d] , I will take a deeper look and get back to you asap. ","2026-01-23T10:38:05.730Z"],["3833055","PFI-837608","PFI","daniel.tirca@bolt.eu","Daniel-Cosmin Tîrcă","To be uploaded in SPV - E factura.\nThank you","2026-01-23T10:38:25.176Z"],["3833058","DML-5354","DML","tiberiu-mihai.iordache@bolt.eu","Tiberiu-Mihai Iordache","Billing profile events have been enabled in live via the config: \r\ncron/handler_node_config/cron/billing_profile_event_sending_cron/limit\r\n\r\nWe have the current setup in live: send at most 5 events every 30sec. This is because for each billing profile event we send a full provider update (big payload with all the details) and we don't want to overload the Salesforce servers. \r\n\r\nServices have been monitored for a few details and any issues that arise have been fixed. ","2026-01-23T10:39:37.241Z"],["3833061","RDS-1022","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:5e0f0e7f0242870e996ebba8] thx! So if I understand correctly, this debt item is rather on the Geo Team side, right? [~accountid:5f770d66021acf0076bbaef1] do you agree?","2026-01-23T10:41:07.453Z"],["3833064","PFI-837683","PFI","mercynorah.nyiti@bolt.eu","Mercynorah Nyiti","[^DL2512080072074-000000498260-SWIFT-ADVISE.pdf]","2026-01-23T10:41:45.858Z"],["3833065","PAW-15107","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @not-much-io\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161142\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-23 10:41:56 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-23T10:41:57.292Z"],["3833067","WD-22672","WD","dieulinh.tran@bolt.eu","Diệu Linh Tran","Sure, could you please grant me access to that Confluence page, if you have the ability to do so?","2026-01-23T10:42:14.344Z"],["3833069","WFM-10106","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Hey, Carolyne, could you please explain why you need this permission and provide a KB link stating that you’re supposed to monitor the queue? From what I can tell, these permissions are related to the TL role, not the specialist role and we need a reason to assign the correct role to you.","2026-01-23T10:42:35.664Z"],["3833072","DELIVERY-1154","DELIVERY","andrei.pit-rada@bolt.eu","Ioan-Andrei Piț-Rada","26W04: UI and backend integrated; minor touch-ups remain.","2026-01-23T10:43:02.382Z"],["3833079","WD-22656","WD","sittinam.phodee@bolt.eu","Sittinam Phodee","Hi [~accountid:712020:6850b463-f3bb-4458-b00b-b094810b5bcd] can a non-manager employee create the job requisition? Can i get the request for creating it?","2026-01-23T10:44:13.725Z"],["3833080","BEE-3668","BEE","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","[~accountid:5d807af94f9cf00d60213212] Can you form the plan for the changes and map out implementation tickets under “Tech Debt” please?\n\nAlso, if it’s AI who “forgot” can you tell it to check the services a couple of more times? 😄 Maybe it will find something more.","2026-01-23T10:44:21.686Z"],["3833081","PFI-837208","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Demetre, in addition to many device UID resets, I’m also seeing an unusual amount of cards associated with the account (though with minimal card-adding errors). We’re not seeing any significant uncovered payments or chargebacks, so in terms of actual fraud signals I don’t think we need to act on it.\nThanks for reporting still.","2026-01-23T10:44:29.572Z"],["3833082","LSS-54833","LSS","roisin.kirk@bolt.eu","Roisin Kirk","Thanks [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] I have replied on both points.  Let me know when it’s ok to share back and I will also argue the point with them about the exclusivity.  ","2026-01-23T10:44:53.708Z"],["3833091","CCM-22303","CCM","peace.anumia@bolt-outsource.eu","Peace Anumia","Awesome!\n\nShe can access it. Thank you very much.\nPlease help assign Ride Hailing Onboarding course to her.\n\n[^New Training Request form _ Teleperformance (23rd of January 26).xlsx]\n\n\n","2026-01-23T10:47:14.255Z"],["3833093","WFM-10106","WFM","eva.guantai@bolt.eu","Eva Guantai","Hey Kyrylo, \n\nThanks for getting back to us. \n\nI’d kindly request this permission on a succession-planning basis for Kenya market. Happy to sync with you further on DM. ","2026-01-23T10:47:25.276Z"],["3833094","DPO-159","DPO","mengel.paula@bolt.eu","Paula Maria Mengel","Employee test launched, A/B test launching on Monday","2026-01-23T10:47:41.525Z"],["3833095","WEBSD-1499","WEBSD","roisin.kirk@bolt.eu","Roisin Kirk","[~accountid:712020:9e668ce4-0877-43c6-bae9-52f1ecbc753f] Apologies I don’t know.  It is a comparable page to this one: [https://bolt.eu/en/legal/tnc-business/|https://bolt.eu/en/legal/tnc-business/|smart-link]  which is for the businesses (the new one is for individuals) so could it have the same mapping?","2026-01-23T10:47:48.664Z"],["3833096","DRAG101-405","DRAG101","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:5e4658b55a495e0c91a7a011] All info taken from [~accountid:5e4658b55a495e0c91a7a011] which needs to be updated in the BB datasheet and sent to TWS.\n\nTWS promised to release new document on {{2026-01-27}} ","2026-01-23T10:48:14.440Z"],["3833099","BEE-3668","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","[~accountid:604aad65ceccdd006a3af17d] No, it was me who forgot to mention it here. AI does not consider ordering by ID to be an issue because it states “TiDB's non-sequential IDs are still *monotonically increasing* - they skip numbers (2, 5, 8, 11...) but don't go out of order (not 8, 2, 11, 5). So {{ORDER BY id}} will return a valid result.”","2026-01-23T10:49:14.740Z"],["3833100","PFI-837212","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey, the issue was resolved for 265334666. It was rejected due to some missing verification datapoints, and due to the fact that the card was relatively new.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 12.47.22.png|width=1021,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 12.47.22.png\"!\n\nFor 132273983, it’s roughly the same case. To add and use a new card on a Family account, the payment method needs to be verified via 3DS. We recommend the user configure their card with their bank to always “require confirmation” or “always enforce SCA”, and then complete a transaction in-app or attempt to add the card again. This allows us to confirm a legitimate card addition and/or payment attempt.\n\nIf the card cannot be verified via 3DS, the user will need to wait for another 5 days before the card can be added successfully. \nThank you!","2026-01-23T10:49:33.685Z"],["3833105","DSR-3993","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T10:51:08.151Z"],["3833106","DSR-2883","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Outgoing case to driver [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/728487602] (/) \nResponse to WIE provided in the main ticket (/) ","2026-01-23T10:51:09.167Z"],["3833108","LSS-59448","LSS","emmanuel.lewis@bolt.eu","Emmanuel Lewis","Hi [~accountid:712020:1f24ce2a-c2f5-4736-ace6-da143abb0cc0], Peter said that he completed everything on his end. I am not sure what's going on, can you please double-check on your end?","2026-01-23T10:51:28.058Z"],["3833109","LSS-61616","LSS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] ,\n\nThank you for providing the letter! Just confirming that I am aligned with the drafted response","2026-01-23T10:51:36.754Z"],["3833112","LSS-61589","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Bolt_MWIIH_response_letter_23012026.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-23T10:52:06.797Z"],["3833113","BEE-3668","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","[~accountid:604aad65ceccdd006a3af17d] Ticket created [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BEE-3669|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BEE-3669|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T10:52:12.245Z"],["3833115","PFI-837242","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Tomas, this is not a Fraud block. Please reach out to the Identity team regarding this.","2026-01-23T10:52:48.080Z"],["3833116","PFI-836387","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi team,\n\nThe refund has failed. Our partner does not store refund details. We can ask our partner to issue the refund again, however we need the customers refund details. \nCould you please ask the customer to provide the following.\n\n*Bank name:* \n*Account name:* \n*Account number:*\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-23T10:53:01.672Z"],["3833120","PAW-15107","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @not-much-io\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161142\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-23 10:53:39 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-23T10:53:39.243Z"],["3833123","LSS-60908","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","*Update:*\n\nThe answer from #*dev-user-auth-support* identified that Thailand orders were created from an iPhone device (ID: 90B00A74-1315-407B-B9FD-8FB20E1168EE). \n_Further investigation is ongoing to confirm whether all affected orders originated from the same device and to terminate any remaining active sessions._\n\nFor next steps, CS may confirm with the user which devices they recognise as their own and whether they previously owned an iPhone that may no longer be in their possession.\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] ","2026-01-23T10:54:33.679Z"],["3833126","RS-1972","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hi [~accountid:5dbb027ba766000da47cf09d] ,\n\nThe legal basis is approved. Please update the sheet and proceed to the next steps. Thanks!","2026-01-23T10:54:58.594Z"],["3833130","PFI-837297","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Valeriia, the triggered fraud rules were specifically created to prevent promo abuse by users with multiple existing accounts, where the same promo code could otherwise be reused by simply creating new accounts. In this case, the user has multiple accounts linked, which is why the rule is triggering and the promo will not be applied.\n\nSince this is a fairly basic but important prevention rule aimed at limiting campaign abuse, we won’t be making changes or exceptions here.\nThank you!","2026-01-23T10:55:19.148Z"],["3833132","INT-854","INT","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","26W04 Update:\n\n* Done\n** Kickoff for dynamic holdout labels and scope breakdown in jira\n* Next\n** working on label backfills and migration ","2026-01-23T10:55:43.595Z"],["3833133","WD-22676","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:712020:07f1e332-abd8-45eb-a3b9-0dd3708ef2d7] !\n\nYes, there was request to introduce thsi validation - > [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22567|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22567|smart-link] \n\nI updated validation, so it is not applier to customer “ DE Bolt Drive customer / DE Bolt Drive Kunde” . Could you please try again upload invoices. \n\n!image-20260123-105550.png|width=1054,alt=\"image-20260123-105550.png\"!","2026-01-23T10:55:54.223Z"],["3833134","LSS-62050","LSS","kaija.riismaa@bolt.eu","Kaija Riismaa","[~accountid:712020:82bad36a-3f0b-4609-8bbe-b4ba65e1094e] Before this document can be sent to signing, we need to validate if the numbers reflected in it are accurate. Please invite to this ticket the person from finance team and Local Ops, who can confirm the numbers are correct. ","2026-01-23T10:55:58.551Z"],["3833135","RDS-1190","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] IMO, this specific suggestion is rather a pricing improvement idea, not Quality Debt.\n\nThat said, clear communication when recalculation happens is a better debt candidate, as it was likely overlooked when recalculation was introduced. Wdyt?","2026-01-23T10:56:54.215Z"],["3833136","PFI-837363","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Aida, this was applied by the locals, not the Fraud team. Please reach out to the local OPS team regarding this.\nThanks!","2026-01-23T10:57:04.132Z"],["3833137","INT-553","INT","hans.tulmin@bolt.eu","Hans-Peeter Tulmin","Just checking about prioritisation. P0 means that this is a company-wide priority(there’s a total of 10-15 of these). Is this really the case?\n\nGenerally:\n\nP0 = VPs and above care on a weekly basis\n\nP1 = your stakeholders care on a weekly basis\nP2 = you care on a weekly basis\nP3 = nice to have\n\nAlso, we now have 6 ideas for 1.5 eng in progress, is this really realistic? What’s the top priority?\n\nSorry for using this comments section but it seems to be the most generic. ","2026-01-23T10:57:30.126Z"],["3833138","DPX-3275","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","FE PR released\n\nOne extra BE PR is waiting for a review – [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161489|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161489]","2026-01-23T10:57:43.322Z"],["3833139","PC-4955","PC","yauheni.zara@bolt.eu","Yauheni Zara","From ProcessOut:\n\n{quote}Hey [@yauheni.zara|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/UQAR03LGY], I confirm we observe some spikes in ApplePay latency. See screenshot of the P98 latency by gateway for the last two days.ProcessOut service makes up a very small part of the overall transaction processing latency. P95 for past 2 days: PO 219ms, vs 2.14s for PSPsI spot checked one of the Adyen examples you shared from today, I see the PSP latency was 20.8sThere is little we can do where the PSP latency spikes, although you might want to escalate it with the PSP directly.On ProcessOut, our default  HTTP timeout is 30 seconds (although this can be configured upto 60 seconds).It has been a long running business decision by Bolt to maintain a 10sec max on the auth request. Of ProcessOut merchants, I believe Bolt is an outlier in having such a low threshold, but it's not for us to tell you how to set this 🙂 \n\n(Side Note: PO has a \"latency switch\" feature where we disable routing to your primary PSP if latency spikes above 10s as measured over 30s window.){quote}\n\n!image (16).png|width=845,alt=\"image (16).png\"!","2026-01-23T10:58:06.323Z"],["3833140","INT-553","INT","david.schryer@bolt.eu","David Schryer","We only do P2s on our team. ","2026-01-23T10:58:28.304Z"],["3833141","LSS-59460","LSS","ann.koljalg@bolt.eu","Ann Kõljalg","[~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] and [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] \nHey! I’m reopening the ticket for the Italy office lease agreement.\n\nOur termination notice period is coming up, and I’ve received a new proposal from Regus. The key commercial changes are:\n\n* Updated rent price\n* Contract term changed to month-to-month, giving us more flexibility and allowing termination with one month’s notice instead of fixed terms\n\nThe Regus team has confirmed that these are the only changes and that all other T&Cs remain the same, as outlined here: [https://serviceagreement.regus.com/TermsPDF/Office/Global20250301.pdf|https://serviceagreement.regus.com/TermsPDF/Office/Global20250301.pdf]\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions or need additional details or can go ahead and accept the extension.\nThanks! \nAnn","2026-01-23T10:58:40.058Z"],["3833142","DPX-3536","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","Requested [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101755?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101755?created=true|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T10:58:40.782Z"],["3833144","INT-553","INT","david.schryer@bolt.eu","David Schryer","Fixed","2026-01-23T10:59:01.642Z"],["3833145","BIZ-271","BIZ","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:614ad8f941af83007135337d] and [~accountid:712020:702efec4-7015-4024-99f6-32a1aaf764a1] - quick question after going through the document: is my understanding correct that we want to include the service fee paid by delivery customers in the scope? We chatted only about 1) courier fees and 2) payments for food to merchants on our kick-off call. Thanks for the response!","2026-01-23T10:59:28.741Z"],["3833148","DPX-3543","DPX","song.luo@bolt.eu","Song Luo","I suggest using the pagination component here, so users can switch manually. Since we don’t yet know if additional sections will be added to this performance/sales page in the future, manual pagination would make the layout more scalable.","2026-01-23T10:59:53.475Z"],["3833149","PAW-15114","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-23T10:59:54.020Z"],["3833150","PFI-836386","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-23T11:00:06.624Z"],["3833151","WD-22673","WD","vlad.badea@bolt.eu","Vlad-Dumitru Badea","I attached here the reply from the last opened IT ticket.\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 12.58.45.png|width=699,height=101,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 12.58.45.png\"!\n\nIs this something that can be done from your end?","2026-01-23T11:00:08.579Z"],["3833152","LSS-59597","LSS","ann.koljalg@bolt.eu","Ann Kõljalg","[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] thank you, will do!","2026-01-23T11:00:31.292Z"],["3833156","LSS-61589","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","thank you, [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] !!\n\n[~accountid:712020:38ef5817-1c12-4bf5-b0d1-116b99b69ddf] please find here two files to be attached to the e-mail you are supposed to send to the Authority:\n\n# the letter: [^Bolt_MWIIH_response_letter_23012026.docx (1) (bc1d33aa-beb3-415c-ba09-5e6c1a72ce97).pdf] \n# the attachment to the letter (KRS copy) [^Odpis_Aktualny_KRS_0000980293 (7) (054448fa-878a-4561-86cb-4ca80f37e19b).pdf] \n\n📧  The e-mail address: *ih_warszawa@wiih.org.pl* (Mazowiecki Wojewódzki Inspektor Inspekcji Handlowej)\n\nThe e-mail content: \n\n_Szanowni Państwo,_\n\n_w związku z nadesłaniem pisma od tut. Organu z dnia 5 stycznia 2026 r. (doręczone spółce 13 stycznia 2026 r.) w załączeniu przesyłam stanowisko spółki Bolt Poland sp. z o.o. z siedzibą w Warszawie w sprawie w sporze konsumenckim z wniosku o sygn. SK.837.952.2025._\n\n_Pozdrawiam_\n\n_Klaudia Bochenko_\n\n_Zespół Bolt_\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you all! ❤️ ","2026-01-23T11:01:05.219Z"],["3833157","LSS-60908","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:712020:3b4c18b5-d699-45e9-b875-1c6e35fcf7f1] \n\nPlease proceed as follows when contacting the customer:\n\n* Inform the customer that we identified *activity from a device that requires verification* and that we are securing the account.\n* Ask the customer to *confirm which devices they recognise as their own*.\n* Ask the customer whether they *previously owned an iPhone* that may have been lost, sold, or no longer in their possession.\n* Explain that these questions are asked *solely to secure the account and terminate any unauthorised access*.\n\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] ","2026-01-23T11:01:05.972Z"],["3833158","DSR-3995","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T11:01:09.474Z"],["3833159","PFI-836385","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi team,\n\nThe refund has failed. Our partner does not store refund details. We can ask our partner to issue the refund again, however we need the customers refund details. \nCould you please ask the customer to provide the following.\n\n*Bank name:* \n*Account name:* \n*Account number:*\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-23T11:01:17.087Z"],["3833162","INT-484","INT","sandeep.jaiswal@bolt.eu","Sandeep Prasad Jaiswal","\n\n26W04: Working on design doc right now for the first milestone i.e popular item campaign outside of smart promotion. we also had a meeting this week to discuss some of the other deliverables. ","2026-01-23T11:01:40.846Z"],["3833163","PFI-836384","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","\n\n\n\nHello Team!\n\nI completely understand why this might look like a double charge, but I can assure you that the user was only charged once. This is a common part of how card payments are processed. Here's what happens:\n\n# When the user first makes a payment, the bank temporarily ‘reserves' the funds and this is just the bank setting aside the amount for the transaction. The user’s account balance might show less amount but the payment hasn’t actually been taken out by the bank yet.\n# Later, when the payment is fully processed, that reserved amount is now “officially” debited from the user’s account. At that point, some banks send a second notification, which can make it seem like a second charge.\n\n\nI would advise the user to check their final account balance or statement, where they can confirm that only one payment was actually withdrawn. The earlier “pending” amount will either drop off or convert into the final charge.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-23T11:02:04.452Z"],["3833164","BIZ-271","BIZ","teresa.rodrigues@bolt.eu","Teresa Cipriano Rodrigues","[~accountid:5f23e228bedd1000153843ae]  can you tell us what have we done in Lithuania please?","2026-01-23T11:02:08.736Z"],["3833165","WD-22679","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Use “*Supplier Group EIB*” to move it. \nGenerate EIB with data - select the BG001 Supplier Group.\n\nBefore that create a new Supplier Group via Maintain Supplier Groups task, don’t forget to change the ref ID.","2026-01-23T11:02:19.214Z"],["3833170","RDXENG-4729","RDXENG","vsevolod.korol@bolt.eu","Vsevolod Korol","BTW, our idea is to add a deadline/timeout for matching (i think you already have some deadlines from your side, we just want to pass our deadline), and if matching is interrupted by the deadline/timeout:\n• Stop matching (only stop creating new matches; no need to reject existing offers).\n• For background matching, call {{internal/order/client/stopBackgroundMatching}}.","2026-01-23T11:03:06.028Z"],["3833171","RNTL-30626","RNTL","jan.tumanov@bolt.eu","Jan Tumanov","OPS should remove duplicated city to avoid such conflicts","2026-01-23T11:03:11.822Z"],["3833172","LSS-59460","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] fyi","2026-01-23T11:03:14.490Z"],["3833174","RDXENG-4729","RDXENG","vsevolod.korol@bolt.eu","Vsevolod Korol","WDYT, it is possible to implement?","2026-01-23T11:03:27.656Z"],["3833176","WFM-10111","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Hey, WFM team, please assign T1 and Safety Kenya queues for these TLs","2026-01-23T11:04:02.540Z"],["3833177","INT-799","INT","oleksii.kulbako@bolt.eu","Oleksii Kulbako","26W04 Update: Started discussing next steps for redesign. The meeting is planned for next Wednesday","2026-01-23T11:04:10.289Z"],["3833180","LSS-61908","LSS","britta.haal@bolt.eu","Britta Hääl","Correct, and we reported the matter and shared the driver’s details with the Metropolitan Police as per procedure, and we have not received any further data requests from the police.","2026-01-23T11:04:23.653Z"],["3833181","PFI-827841","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-23T11:04:32.901Z"],["3833183","PFI-828885","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-23T11:05:13.906Z"],["3833185","DSR-3995","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","DM sent to -Stephanie Carvalho Fioravanti-  *Jelena Šeller*","2026-01-23T11:05:22.192Z"],["3833190","HS-29247","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","Dear [~accountid:712020:b3680618-b73e-4f5c-b8d7-9b8c6b1b6eca] , kindly search for “My Payslips” in Workday. See the manual [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BILP/pages/1615462955/Portugal#Payroll-%F0%9F%92%B8]. Closing this ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-23T11:05:51.359Z"],["3833191","PFI-835239","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-23T11:05:57.777Z"],["3833192","CNT-432","CNT","aleksandra.onutsina@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Onutšina","[~accountid:637f67fb2acfad92d7b14abc] , hey! I see that Karl in on a long-term leave. Do you want me to proceed with this ticket or is it on hold currently? ","2026-01-23T11:06:37.557Z"],["3833195","PFI-835282","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-23T11:06:57.200Z"],["3833196","L10N-29785","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29783](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29783)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T11:07:07.143Z"],["3833197","L10N-29788","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29783](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29783)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T11:07:10.429Z"],["3833198","L10N-29792","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29783](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29783)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T11:07:11.035Z"],["3833199","L10N-29790","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29783](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29783)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T11:07:12.167Z"],["3833200","L10N-29796","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29783](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29783)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T11:07:13.182Z"],["3833201","L10N-29797","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29783](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29783)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T11:07:14.381Z"],["3833202","L10N-29799","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place