","Darja Netjaga","Hi [~accountid:712020:8a3969ff-a877-45c5-82e8-74d7260b03cb] \n\n\nI confirm that You have a full access now \n\nKind regards,\n\nDarja Netjaga","2026-01-23T11:08:40.348Z"],["3833208","PFI-836816","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","I know we just had a similar issue with another big provider where if the invoice wasn’t attached as a pdf, it wouldn’t go through on the provider’s side, even though from our side it’s ok. \n\nI’ll change the settings and then we can see if they received the invoices successfully next week.","2026-01-23T11:09:43.206Z"],["3833210","WD-22680","WD","cetlyn.ojamaa@bolt.eu","Cetlyn Ojamaa","!Screenshot 2026-01-22 at 15.44.07.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T11:10:01.189Z"],["3833211","LSS-62041","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","Hi [~accountid:614c2821a6f69e006d6166a0] , I sent to our external counsel the request to update the Trade Registry accordingly. In case any further documents are needed from your side, I will revert accordingly, or, in case not, I will revert to you with proof attesting update.\nBest,\n\nAlex","2026-01-23T11:10:05.397Z"],["3833212","RCE-373","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769166603028459]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@maksim.shashkov>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-373] `Investigate car suspension and block removal issue` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-23T11:10:16.439Z"],["3833213","PAW-15067","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-admin-panel, pint-product-admin-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-23T11:10:35.586Z"],["3833214","WD-22672","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/FIN/pages/5220860448/Creating+Expense+Reports+in+Multiple+Countries|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/FIN/pages/5220860448/Creating+Expense+Reports+in+Multiple+Countries|smart-link] sorry here is the correct link","2026-01-23T11:10:37.004Z"],["3833215","PFI-835494","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay/Cellulant transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-23T11:10:47.684Z"],["3833216","FPD-1533","FPD","anastasia.serebryannikova@bolt.eu","Nastya Serebryannikova","Status update:\n\nthe PR is in code review: [https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/809|https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/809|smart-link] \n\nNext steps:\n\n* enable the ingestion for the rest of the tables \n* delete unused code\n* write confluence page with the documentation","2026-01-23T11:10:56.659Z"],["3833217","LSS-59742","LSS","r.lonander@bolt.eu","Robin Lönander","Hi [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] \n\nI got the following comment from the partner: \n\nI have read through the contract and here are some minor clarifications and proposed amendments to improve balance and reduce ambiguity, while fully preserving Bolt’s commercial and IP protections.\n\n# *Material breach & right to remedy (Services)*\n\nIssue: Any deviation may be deemed a material breach “not capable of remedy”, at Bolt’s sole discretion. Especially the sentence _”Precise conformity… any deviation may be deemed a material breach not capable of remedy”_ is not fitting into a creative and linguistic type of work where I often have to find alternative translations to achieve a well localised text. \n\n*Proposed amendment* (that still preserves Bolt’s quality control but introduces proportionality and dialogue):\n\nReplace Clause 2.3 with:\n\n“Precise conformity of the Services as set out in the applicable Statement of Work is an important term of this Agreement.\n\nAny deviation from the Statement of Work shall be discussed in good faith between the Parties. Where such deviation does not materially affect the overall quality or purpose of the Services, the Consultant shall be given a reasonable opportunity to remedy such deviation before it may be deemed a material breach.”\n\n\n\n# *Confidentiality penalty – cap & intent*\n\nIssue: €5,000 per breach regardless of severity or intent.\n\nProposed amendment (Clause 9.5)\n\nReplace with:\n\n“In the event of a material and wilful breach of the Confidentiality Obligation, Bolt may claim a contractual penalty of EUR 5,000 per breach.\n\nThe Parties agree that this penalty shall be proportionate to the nature and impact of the breach and shall not apply to minor or inadvertent breaches that are promptly remedied.”\n\n# *Liability & indemnity – alignment with liability cap*\n\nIssue: Indemnities risk sitting outside the liability cap.\n\nProposed amendment (Clause 11)\n\nAdd:\n\n“Except in cases of wilful misconduct or gross negligence, the Consultant’s total aggregate liability, including under any indemnity, shall be subject to the limitation of liability set out in Clause 11.4.”\n\n# *Set-off right – notice requirement*\n\nIssue: Bolt may set off without notice.\n\nProposed amendment (Clause 7.4)\n\nReplace with:\n\n“Bolt may, upon prior written notice to the Consultant, set off any undisputed and due liability of the Consultant against any amounts payable to the Consultant under this Agreement.”\n\n# *Working hours & availability – flexibility safeguard*\n\nIssue: Fixed hours resemble employment-like control and is neither feasible nor fair for a consultant. We can agree that my general availability on slack will be weekdays 10:00 - 14:00, but these times may vary depending on my schedule. I can let you know in the beginning of each week what my weekly availability will be on slack so you can plan accordingly. If I will be unavailable due to holidays or other private matters I will communicate this to you as far in advance as possible.\n\nProposed amendment (SOW, Item 3)\n\nWith the above in mind, alter the final sentence:\n\n“The agreed working hours (Monday - Friday 10:00-14:00) reflect general availability expectations and shall not be interpreted as fixed working hours or as creating an employment relationship. The Consultant retains discretion over the manner and sequencing of work, provided the Services are delivered in accordance with the Agreement.”\n\n# *Jurisdiction clause – mutuality*\n\nIssue: Bolt unilaterally decides jurisdiction.\n\nProposed amendment (Governing Law and Jurisdiction)\n\nReplace final sentence with:\n\n“Each Party irrevocably agrees that the courts of Sweden shall have exclusive jurisdiction to settle any dispute or claim arising out of or in connection with this Agreement.”\n\n---\n\nThank you for reconsidering updating these parts of the contract and I'm happy to sign.","2026-01-23T11:11:13.355Z"],["3833218","RCE-373","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Max Shashkov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769166670286529]*{color}:\ncc <@UMJCP0AV9>\n{quote}","2026-01-23T11:11:21.183Z"],["3833219","CNT-479","CNT","aleksandra.onutsina@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Onutšina","[~accountid:624c636af40798007059caa8] , hey! I’ve added most of the content in the production file, but I need to ask some questions before I can proceed with the rest. I’ve left some comments in the doc and marked the fields with blockers with red. ","2026-01-23T11:13:03.559Z"],["3833220","WD-22616","WD","nataliia.pachkovska@bolt.eu","Nataliia Pachkovska","Hi. Confirming I agree to grant the security.\n[~accountid:712020:c24abb54-ee7f-43ba-bb8e-3ad5ff67df41] [~accountid:60b2030e25a51300698c52c6] Could you please confirm you will deal with spend categories only, not with expense items.","2026-01-23T11:13:04.616Z"],["3833221","PFI-836816","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Made the changes. Let me know if the providers receive the next week’s invoices successfully. ","2026-01-23T11:13:14.793Z"],["3833222","LSS-62032","LSS","paolo.catani@bolt.eu","Paolo Catani","Hello! Could this be done by today?\nThank you I understand you’re very busy!","2026-01-23T11:13:50.205Z"],["3833223","WD-22678","WD","arina.vorozhtsova@bolt.eu","Arina Vorozhtsova","Hi Noa, \n\nI see that in your tasks in WD, you still have the task related to the remote work submission. Please complete it first. \n\nRegards, Arina","2026-01-23T11:14:34.628Z"],["3833224","FPD-1505","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","Tested if adjustments to partner metrics are working as expected: [https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/1718226282087974?o=2472566184436351|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/1718226282087974?o=2472566184436351]\nAll looks good, so I’ll proceed with bumping the library version in the PR and merging it into {{master}} branch. ","2026-01-23T11:14:43.001Z"],["3833225","FPD-1532","FPD","anastasia.serebryannikova@bolt.eu","Nastya Serebryannikova","Status updates:\n\n* the configs for the spark tables into which the data will be ingested are stored here: [https://github.com/bolteu/change-data-capture/blob/master/src/ingestion_config/ng/s3/financial_planning_input_based_model.json|https://github.com/bolteu/change-data-capture/blob/master/src/ingestion_config/ng/s3/financial_planning_input_based_model.json|smart-link]\n** ingestion is configured to happen every 2 hours\n* the data that needs to be ingested will be placed into the {{presto-ingestion}} folder in our s3 bucket:\n** {{s3://bolt-datascience-financial-modeling/LIVE/presto-ingestion/fp-ibm-rh-cycle-metadata/}}\n** {{s3://bolt-datascience-financial-modeling/LIVE/presto-ingestion/fp-ibm-rh-city-dataset-metadata/}}\n** {{s3://bolt-datascience-financial-modeling/LIVE/presto-ingestion/fp-ibm-rh-scenario-metrics-forecast/}}\n* {{presto-ingestion}} folder has been chosen (despite its confusing name) because it already had all the necessary configurations for the ingestion\n* the PR with the code changes that enable the ingestion for 3 types of tables (cycle metadata, city dataset metadata, scenario metrics forecast) is in code review\n\nNext steps:\n\n* enable the ingestion for the other tables (adjustments, selected scenarios, comments, model metadata) \n** ingestion schemas\n** code changes\n* remove unused code\n* write confluence page with the documentation","2026-01-23T11:14:54.348Z"],["3833226","PTWS-2124","PTWS","alexandru.cerveanu@bolt.eu","Alex Cerveanu","One proposal will be to change the Job Profile name to include 3PL in the name e.g: _100072 - 3PL Mechanic_\n\nThen we can explore the possibility to change the name of the contingent worker type from 3PL to Agency from Maintain Contingent Worker Types Task - we need to check with IT the downstream impacts.\n\n!image-20260123-111444.png|width=962,alt=\"image-20260123-111444.png\"!","2026-01-23T11:15:26.776Z"],["3833236","ML-3716","ML","vivekkumar.singh@bolt.eu","Vivek Kumar Singh","[~accountid:6102799e8ad5b60070a153d1] [~accountid:5cefc04f0927e30f265e0d1f] can we kindly mark this done","2026-01-23T11:18:29.787Z"],["3833237","PFI-835217","PFI","mercynorah.nyiti@bolt.eu","Mercynorah Nyiti","Hi [~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e]  please assist with this ticket urgently\nClient did confirm with their bank and the payment has been successful sent to Citibank, kindly recheck. ","2026-01-23T11:19:18.633Z"],["3833239","SCM-1074","SCM","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","{color:#36B37E}*[ DECISION ]*{color} \n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/EBIKE1-87|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/EBIKE1-87|smart-link]  \n\n\n\nI have informed supplier that they have to update the 2D drawings\n\n\n\nTopic closed","2026-01-23T11:19:27.226Z"],["3833244","PRIV-518","PRIV","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (23.01)*+\n\n* Still no word from the business re what safety features will be rolled out :loading: \n* General things to note in the meantime:\n** Given the [safety prioritisation framework|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1JZFhbbnGtmo6q-GtB8xnflw33hLhDIWGlcIT969B8y0/edit?gid=1032762880#gid=1032762880], our inout would likely only be needed on the following (if rolled out):\n*** *Trusted Contact*:\n**** Usual advice applies - Rely on legitimate interest for processing TC details, but make sure that they are informed (i.e., user should notify them).\n*** *Mandatory User Verification*:\n**** Re ID verification, there are no obvious specific prohibitions on processing ID docs - we just need a legal basis. As such, we should be able to do this as per usual processes.\n***** We should ensure we are obtaining consent to any biometric processes, where applicable (and offer a manual option).\n***** User flow should be clear on exactly why the data is being requested.\n***** We should be retaining full copies for no longer than strictly necessary (e.g., verification and then perhaps not full-copy retention).\n***** ADM - We would aim to argue that a manual option is available (i.e., non-biometric option is available).\n***** Ensure that LIAs/DPIAs are in place for internal purposes.\n***** If we are involving a third party in the verification process, we will need to make sure that a proper agreement is in place.\n**** However, we may want to do a quick look into local laws on ID docs, just in case.\n*** *Women For Women*:\n**** Generally this feature would be ok (due to GDPR alignment), but we would need to be careful around: (i) local gender laws; and (ii) local ID verification requirements.\n**** We would need to work with Regional Legal to consider whether any gender discrimination / trans laws would be triggered here.\n**** Re ID verification, there are no specific prohibitions on processing ID docs - we just need a legal basis. As such, we should be able to do this as per usual processes (see above).\n*** *Audio Trip Recording*:\n**** Per usual processes, this would require local counsel input.\n**** We would aim to rely on LI, unless specific local laws require consent (which they could). Otherwise, usual advice applies re transparency and retention (see [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/7103938731/Audio+Trip+Recording]).\n** Other features (usually mandatory) do not explicitly pose obvious issues. We can revisit when the time comes.","2026-01-23T11:20:36.868Z"],["3833245","PFI-837698","PFI","jasmina.vaclavkova@bolt.eu","Jasmina Vaclavkova","!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 12.20.26.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T11:20:50.545Z"],["3833246","PFI-822817","PFI","kotryna.savukynaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Kotryna Savukynaitė","Are there any updates? ","2026-01-23T11:21:09.656Z"],["3833248","LSS-61589","LSS","klaudia.bochenko@bolt.eu","Klaudia Bochenko","Hello, I’ve sent the email. I’ll keep you informed if any update will come. \nThanks [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] for smooth cooperation. ","2026-01-23T11:22:05.810Z"],["3833251","PFI-837381","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Vidyur, my best guess is that the driver was unfamiliar with how the Chauffeur category works, or decided to take an alternative route with an extremely long detour. This seems more like a driver behaviour issue rather than financial fraud. Unfortunately we don’t deal with Driver Quality or matching issues.\nBest,\nKarl","2026-01-23T11:22:37.205Z"],["3833252","LSS-60921","LSS","andy.effiong@bolt.eu","Andy Effiong","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] ,\n\nThe original NDA still states the previous signatory name. Do we need a change made to the NDA to be reflected to the new singatory (Priit) before sending off for signature?","2026-01-23T11:22:51.879Z"],["3833253","CSDA-296","CSDA","roman.trohhalev@bolt.eu","Roman Trohhalev","Hi [~accountid:557058:67e15ba9-0972-4bf7-9e81-826e62fc001b],\n\nYes, that’s correct — *Delivery Type* (e.g. {{dine_out}}) is populated only when a case is linked to a completed order.\n\nIf there is no related order, Dine Out–related cases can still be identified via *Case Issue Keys*, for example {{question_about_dineout_eater}}.\nIn those cases, please make sure the *Delivery Type* filter is left *empty*, and when using the *Case Issue Keys* filter, select *“contains”* instead of the default *“is”* option.\n\nRegarding ticket eligibility for unsuccessful payments:\nBased on the limited number of Dine Out examples, it’s not fully conclusive yet whether users who were denied payment always generate cases without an associated order.\n\nFor other delivery types, we do observe that:\n\n* cases can exist without a completed order\n* and delivery-related attributes may still be populated\n\nFor Dine Out specifically, this behavior may differ, so for now such cases are most reliably identified via issue keys and case-level attributes, rather than order-based dimensions.\n\nWe can revalidate this once we have a larger sample of denied-payment Dine Out cases or if you provide some examples from dine_out with failed order.\n\nI’ve also added “*Is Failed Order*” filter for the convenience.","2026-01-23T11:23:16.224Z"],["3833254","WFM-10108","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Access provided [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/new|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/new]","2026-01-23T11:23:26.010Z"],["3833256","LSS-61359","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] I think these are already approved novation agreements (or potentially unchanged). If that is correct, could you send them for signatures? Thanks!","2026-01-23T11:23:29.847Z"],["3833257","WFM-10108","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Hey, WFM team, please assign the business queues for these agents","2026-01-23T11:23:32.132Z"],["3833259","HS-29316","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-23T11:23:57.325Z"],["3833260","BR-4075","BR","svetlova.katerina@bolt.eu","Katsiaryna Kasakouskaya","Query used \n\n{noformat}SELECT CONCAT(\n               QUOTE(d.public_id),\n               ', ',\n               CAST(CASE WHEN d.is_active THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS INT),\n               ', ',\n               QUOTE('to_execute')\n       ) AS values_row\nFROM ng_public_spark.billing_ride_hailing_task t\n         JOIN ng_public_spark.billing_document_invoice_document d\n              ON t.reference_id = d.id\n                  AND d.external_id NOT LIKE '%-r' AND d.external_id NOT LIKE '%-R'\n                  AND d.external_id NOT LIKE '%-C'\n                  AND d.external_id NOT LIKE '%-reissue'\n         JOIN ng_public_spark.billing_document_invoice_document od\n              ON od.id = d.parent_invoice_id\nWHERE t.entity_type = 'partner_invoice_status_changed'\n  AND t.reference_data = 'invoice_id'\n  AND get_json_object(t.payload_json, '$.change_type') = 're_issue'\n  AND t.created_date >= DATE('2024-01-01')\n  AND t.created_date < DATE('2025-01-01')\n  AND d.created_date >= DATE('2024-01-01')\n  AND d.created_date < DATE('2025-01-01')\n  AND d.public_id != 'TW5125-5'\norder by d.created desc;{noformat}\n\nNote that for period since Oct 2025 to 2026 only {{AND d.external_id NOT LIKE '%-r' AND d.external_id NOT LIKE '%-reissue'}} were used since other cases where identified later\n\nall affected invoices can be found in {{record_invoice_fix_log}} table","2026-01-23T11:24:01.672Z"],["3833261","WFM-10108","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Hey, the access provided, WFM team will assign the queues to them. Have a nice day!","2026-01-23T11:24:06.865Z"],["3833264","PFI-834897","PFI","adepeju.akinribide@bolt-outsource.eu","Adepeju Akinribide","Hi Team,\n\nPlease assist with an update on driver’s payment that is yet to reflect on his balance","2026-01-23T11:25:01.916Z"],["3833266","PFI-837702","PFI","shahnaz.huseynova@bolt-outsource.eu","Shahnaz Huseynova","[^Payment oktyabr.pdf (1).pdf]","2026-01-23T11:25:27.531Z"],["3833267","WD-22546","WD","aleksandra.kuzmina@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Kuzmina","[~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] which code should be used to add it to Telema?","2026-01-23T11:25:49.101Z"],["3833268","WD-22482","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","BNB issue [0051428|https://mantis.bnetbuilders.com/view.php?id=51428] created","2026-01-23T11:25:59.397Z"],["3833269","PFI-837703","PFI","lukas.dusek@bolt-outsource.eu","Lukas Dusek","!Screenshot_20260120_110741_cz_csas_georgego_TransactionDetailActivity.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T11:26:00.172Z"],["3833274","BP-13448","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Test cases:\n\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T243|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T243]\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T244|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T244]\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T245|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T245]\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T246|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T246]\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T247|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T247]\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T248|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T248]","2026-01-23T11:27:30.303Z"],["3833281","GEORM-481","GEORM","brindusa.niculae@bolt.eu","Brîndușa Niculae","Context: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ytLbX0PQpM3WEv-5PjSUxBxegHQZamd8a2MZJlcmJtE/edit?disco=AAABycY2MvY|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ytLbX0PQpM3WEv-5PjSUxBxegHQZamd8a2MZJlcmJtE/edit?disco=AAABycY2MvY|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T11:28:00.310Z"],["3833283","WD-22676","WD","karmen.aherma@bolt.eu","Karmen Aherma","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec], I’m now able to submit the invoices. Thank you for quick help.","2026-01-23T11:28:40.573Z"],["3833285","WDFT-3494","WDFT","dominika.bednarczyk@bolt.eu","Dominika Bednarczyk","any questions, let me know","2026-01-23T11:29:41.530Z"],["3833286","PFI-835503","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Thanks [~accountid:5f0c30effe23000022252e68] ☺️ \n\n[~accountid:712020:d77c5e6c-f92f-4d79-955d-9f88e6d0a883] or [~accountid:5b7bea09d08e47445d6fd01e], do you have examples of different series the FO is referring to? The only time I’m aware we’ve switched the series was end of last year due to the changes we had to do according to the TA request. I’ll also already raise it with Fonoa as they are the ones who automatically generate the series.","2026-01-23T11:29:48.610Z"],["3833287","WD-22673","WD","steve.white@bolt.eu","Steve White","hmmmm, i will deactivate and reactive.  See what we get","2026-01-23T11:29:57.738Z"],["3833289","PAW-15116","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-23T11:30:16.383Z"],["3833290","WD-22546","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:624b0ac7fd5e45007046b61a] the code was created to Telema by [~accountid:712020:42c95fcc-665c-491a-9341-767b89230c32] ","2026-01-23T11:30:20.750Z"],["3833293","WD-22667","WD","dominika.bednarczyk@bolt.eu","Dominika Bednarczyk","Tere [~accountid:712020:b91275f1-415a-4b3c-8490-974f09f14a0d] \n\nplease help 🙂 ","2026-01-23T11:30:30.193Z"],["3833294","VULN-1127","VULN","allar.lauk@bolt.eu","Allar Lauk","Testing was done with CA.150, but it’s been solved from CA.157 onwards with [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CLIENTAPP-36106|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CLIENTAPP-36106|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T11:30:47.062Z"],["3833301","PFI-837704","PFI","favour.isaac@bolt-outsource.eu","Favour Isaac","[^Receipt-11796066918145140553.pdf]","2026-01-23T11:31:51.905Z"],["3833303","LSS-62065","LSS","catalin.jitariu@bolt.eu","Cătălin-Ioan Jitariu","[^Kookoo act aditional 4.pdf] _(980 kB)_\n\n[^Annex 4 to lease agreement - Contract extension_Bolt Services RO S.R.L._KERMANY GRUP S.R.L._10.10.25.pdf] _(217 kB)_\n\n[^Kookoo contract.pdf] _(1.04 MB)_","2026-01-23T11:32:39.168Z"],["3833304","LSS-62065","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nCătălin-Ioan Jitariu has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-23T11:32:39.843Z"],["3833306","LSS-61082","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* email instructing OC and requesting fee quote.\n\n[^Bolt Mail - Request for help - Liverpool Warehouse Lease.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-23T11:33:26.386Z"],["3833307","DPX-3275","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","Second BE pr released as well","2026-01-23T11:33:36.140Z"],["3833308","LSS-61920","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* email instructing OC and requesting fee quote.\n\n[^Bolt Mail - Request for help - Liverpool Warehouse Lease.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-23T11:33:46.431Z"],["3833309","LSS-61807","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:712020:1d5390cd-af56-43c8-9d12-f431b20183ba] could you please confirm that we a) are able to comply with all requirements b) will indeed comply with not showing 3 party ads? If you confirm I can send them for signatures.","2026-01-23T11:34:07.744Z"],["3833310","LSS-52224","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","This ticket is being archived since the T&Cs have been published and are scheduled to enter into force on 16 February 2026:\n\n[https://bolt.eu/en-cy/legal/tnc-ride-hailing/?category=rides|https://bolt.eu/en-cy/legal/tnc-ride-hailing/?category=rides|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T11:34:10.686Z"],["3833311","FX-3689","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dmitrii Bokovikov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769168059810989]*{color}:\nHi <@UUASM18AC> Redirected this request to <#C0576CT9MQD> [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0576CT9MQD/p1769162332462439]\n\nLinked messages:\n[January 23rd, 2026 1:58 AM] dmitrii.bokovikov: Hi! Can you help with this request please [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769072433793069]?\n{quote}","2026-01-23T11:34:33.604Z"],["3833312","DPX-3194","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","[~accountid:60f2a71a2f97d5006920d5de] This is not valid anymore","2026-01-23T11:34:45.620Z"],["3833313","WD-22678","WD","noa.aharon@bolt.eu","Noa Aharon","Sorry, didn’t notice that\nI have completed the task now","2026-01-23T11:34:48.243Z"],["3833314","DPX-3194","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","Currently blocked by [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPX-3297|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPX-3297|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T11:35:05.311Z"],["3833315","LSS-61082","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:628b3e951a437e0070414307], quick update - I have had a call with OC and they have agreed to review the relevant lease documents once provided by Brabners. OC have said they will aim to get us a fee quote by today and once we agree, they can reach out to Brabners directly to get the ball rolling quicker.","2026-01-23T11:35:13.341Z"],["3833316","LSS-52245","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","This ticket is being archived since the T&Cs have been published and are scheduled to enter into force on 16 February 2026:\n\n[https://bolt.eu/es-py/legal/tnc-ride-hailing/?category=rides|https://bolt.eu/es-py/legal/tnc-ride-hailing/?category=rides|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T11:35:13.563Z"],["3833317","LSS-59260","LSS","indrek.eelmets@bolt.eu","Indrek Eelmets","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] Reopening this ticket as we need this document [^Bolt Support Services TH LMT Cert of Inc.pdf] signed by Nathadon Suksiritarnan. \n\nWe just need his name, date and signature added on the document (Thai version). Please let me know via slack if you have any questions. \n\nThanks. ","2026-01-23T11:35:17.666Z"],["3833318","LSS-61784","LSS","anna.hultengard@bolt.eu","Anna Hultengård","Request from [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] to have the POA in Swedish and to extend the period of validity: \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 12.30.46.png|width=958,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 12.30.46.png\"!\n\n*Anna Hultengård*  [10:06 AM|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0AAMCT6SG4/p1769159189405979]\n\nHi [@elisabeth.gunnarsson|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U07MTRKCYGZ] Please see the translated POA for your review. [Draft- Sw. Upplands-Bro - PoA - Bolt Support Sweden AB (Elisabeth Gunnarsson)|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yuAnq-GIbDa14hANfdFe9fpEDwSYaU8XtOZn6Libn_I/edit?tab=t.0].I am keen to get your eyes on this to ensure we use the proper tender-language here.  If you don't have any comments, I can send it for signature to Lars.\n\n*Elisabeth Gunnarsson*  [10:46 AM|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0AAMCT6SG4/p1769161581137559]\n\nI only have 1 comment, realizing the time limit set to the doc (and probably all the previous POA's) - as there can be requests to hand in complements to the tender, perhaps add  a week or two, so we don't get ourselves to the situation where I'm no longer authorized to hand in documents for Bolt Support in the process the tender?\n\n*Approval from Lars:* \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 12.32.53.png|width=1018,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 12.32.53.png\"!\n\nApproval from [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] on draft (machine translation): \n\n*Anna Hultengård*\n41 minutes ago\nHere is the translation of the PoA for Region Dalarna. Please review it @elisabeth.gunnarsson. I have extended the power of attorney until the end of February.\n[+Draft- SW Region Dalarna - PoA - Bolt Support Sweden AB (Elisabeth Gunnarsson)+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1E515qMmowAma66-uWxu5FCORm8WFyNsextO-h9bSUgk/edit?tab=t.0]\nIf everything looks OK, I’ll send it for signing and message Alexandra.\n@emelie.dufva should this be a regular signing or with an advanced signature? (edited)\n\n*Elisabeth Gunnarsson*\n29 minutes ago\nLooks good from my perspective 🙌 ","2026-01-23T11:35:22.853Z"],["3833322","DSR-3997","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T11:36:06.454Z"],["3833324","LSS-61920","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi all ([~accountid:712020:7bfaad56-f8bf-45b0-b951-dfd37b5ed5c2], [~accountid:712020:1d4eb168-65d8-4fe2-9240-3537fd827409] and [~accountid:628b3e951a437e0070414307]),\n\nJust a quick update - I have had a call with OC and shared my draft agreement. They have agreed to review this and will aim for next Tuesday. OC have said that they will aim to get us a fee quote by the end of today and once we agree, they can get started.\n\nWill keep you all updated 🙂 ","2026-01-23T11:36:34.746Z"],["3833325","LSS-52252","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","This ticket is being archived since the T&Cs have been published and are scheduled to enter into force on 16 February 2026:\n\n[https://bolt.eu/es-es/legal/tnc-ride-hailing/?category=rides|https://bolt.eu/es-es/legal/tnc-ride-hailing/?category=rides|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T11:36:36.208Z"],["3833327","WDFT-3558","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/WDFTECH/pages/edit-v2/7441154301?draftShareId=caff5a0e-40a5-4dce-81ae-f92d323c96a7|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/WDFTECH/pages/edit-v2/7441154301?draftShareId=caff5a0e-40a5-4dce-81ae-f92d323c96a7|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T11:36:44.839Z"],["3833328","DRX-27736","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DA.127.0 (1513) Firebase build on Google Pixel 8 Pro, OS:16\n\n||*TTD + Working time block*\n*prod_is_new_online_button_enabled: true*||*TTD + Working time block*\n*prod_is_new_online_button_enabled: false*||*Earnings FAB + TTD + Working time block*\n*prod_is_new_online_button_enabled: true*||\n|!Screenshot_20260123-133031.png|width=340,alt=\"Screenshot_20260123-133031.png\"!|!Screenshot_20260123-133137.png|width=340,alt=\"Screenshot_20260123-133137.png\"!|!Screenshot_20260123-132432 (1).png|width=340,alt=\"Screenshot_20260123-132432 (1).png\"!|","2026-01-23T11:37:00.612Z"],["3833331","SRED-396","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done, both live and prelive has now v2 dashboards for master/replica and cluster dashboard.","2026-01-23T11:38:24.888Z"],["3833334","RDS-1022","RDS","taras.sgibnev@bolt.eu","Taras Sgibnev","The Geo team should definitely control the position of suggested locations.\n\nBut the snapping behaviour should probably be considered as a UI tool and designed by the product design team.","2026-01-23T11:38:58.544Z"],["3833335","FX-3698","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769168335616209]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@alexandr.kuldin>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3698] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-23T11:39:07.813Z"],["3833336","RDXENG-4785","RDXENG","daniel.tjulinov@bolt.eu","Daniel Tjulinov","was fixed in this pr [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161716|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161716]","2026-01-23T11:39:39.679Z"],["3833337","LSS-61616","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","thank you [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] and [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] for your feedback! \n\nLet’s just wait for PP and Alexis feedback then.\n\nBest,\n\nElisabetta","2026-01-23T11:39:54.269Z"],["3833339","DO-5824","DO","mikhail.kliasheu@bolt.eu","Mikhail Kliasheu","Hi! There are 2 different reasons: \n\n# While using the notebooks and personal clusters, you need to properly set up your cluster - we do have it documented here [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/6021087382/Data+Platform+Authorisation#Databricks|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/6021087382/Data+Platform+Authorisation#Databricks|smart-link]. Tl;dr: you need to set a personal or group instance profile on your cluster config.\n# While using sql editor with sql warehouse, you have everything setted up correctly, but we found a bug that prevented policies being properly configured up for this schema. I’ve fixed these policies now and you should be able to use it now.\n\nPls let me know if you have any other issues","2026-01-23T11:40:12.669Z"],["3833341","FX-3698","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Alexandr Kuldin [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769168408895759]*{color}:\nO. As far as I can see the most loaded endpoint there is (1500 RPS).\n{quote}","2026-01-23T11:40:22.905Z"],["3833344","FX-3698","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769168454215079]*{color}:\nSeems to be owned by <#C02H52XUKPG> not by us. Generally the packages is owned by them!\n{quote}","2026-01-23T11:41:08.498Z"],["3833345","PFI-814406","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hey [~accountid:60c8641cb1f93b0069f576ef] \n\n21% chisinau will look like this\n\nYou will see in dropdown this name:\n\n!CleanShot 2026-01-23 at 13.39.45@2x-20260123-113947.png|width=401,alt=\"CleanShot 2026-01-23 at 13.39.45@2x-20260123-113947.png\"!\n\nUnder the hood the config is like this:\n\n!CleanShot 2026-01-23 at 13.39.33@2x-20260123-113937.png|width=401,alt=\"CleanShot 2026-01-23 at 13.39.33@2x-20260123-113937.png\"!\n\n\n\nplease confirm if that’s working","2026-01-23T11:41:11.178Z"],["3833346","PAW-15118","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-23T11:41:21.361Z"],["3833347","DSR-3999","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T11:41:23.158Z"],["3833351","FX-3698","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Alexandr Kuldin [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769168516924669]*{color}:\nOk. Thanks.\n{quote}","2026-01-23T11:42:09.638Z"],["3833352","LSS-41231","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Archiving this ticket, as a new Fleet Agreement will be put in place and rolled out for signature, replacing the current Special Conditions.","2026-01-23T11:42:12.233Z"],["3833355","PFI-835566","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Thanks! If it’s not, please create a new ticket so we could better track and this ticket doesn’t get lost in our queue. Thanks! ","2026-01-23T11:42:36.908Z"],["3833356","LSS-61811","LSS","nils.kacars@bolt.eu","Nils Kacars","Thank you [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] ,\n\nAll changes have been accepted and document updated with Accountings just created clawback request Invoice number.\n\n[^MU04 Taksi SIA C-EE003-26-000079.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-23T11:42:44.018Z"],["3833357","DO-5826","DO","mikhail.kliasheu@bolt.eu","Mikhail Kliasheu","Hi! To get access to databricks, you need to submit a request here first [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/group/1/create/932|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/group/1/create/932|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T11:42:54.426Z"],["3833358","PFI-835713","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-23T11:42:55.652Z"],["3833359","FX-3698","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769168567769239]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3698 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-23T11:42:59.968Z"],["3833361","RDS-1189","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] Very valid points, but it feels more like new functionality (ETA for multi stops), not debt. \n\n[~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c] , out of curiosity, do you know why we do not show it? ","2026-01-23T11:43:39.747Z"],["3833363","WDFT-3562","WDFT","dominika.bednarczyk@bolt.eu","Dominika Bednarczyk","Linton will share new list once he will confirm it with Zycus. \n\nAgreed that Reference ID should be also updated. ","2026-01-23T11:44:25.088Z"],["3833366","DO-5824","DO","kristo.sarnets@bolt.eu","Kristo Sarnets","1. Tried it with SQL editor, but still got the unauthorised access error.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 13.45.04.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T11:45:55.106Z"],["3833367","PFI-836085","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-23T11:45:56.202Z"],["3833368","LSS-58783","LSS","afonso.azevedo@bolt.eu","Afonso Varão de Azevedo","Hey [~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] \n\nHere is an example of a Comodato signed by a minor:\n\n[^Contrato de Aluguer ()_181320419.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-23T11:46:01.097Z"],["3833371","LSS-62065","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-23T11:47:20.976Z"],["3833373","PFI-836364","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-23T11:47:33.062Z"],["3833374","PFI-837129","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hi,\n\nI see that majority of the cities already have 25 and 13% Base Fee Calculators.\n\nonly Bottrop did not have.\n\ncould you confirm if you see the changes from your end?","2026-01-23T11:47:35.535Z"],["3833377","PFI-837182","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-23T11:48:32.161Z"],["3833378","WD-22676","WD","maile.nittim@bolt.eu","Maile Nittim","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] !\nPlease also remove this validation from customer “LV Bolt Drive customer”","2026-01-23T11:48:39.849Z"],["3833383","MKP-9832","MKP","alexandr.kuldin@bolt.eu","Alexandr Kuldin","Average request processing time for {{/internal/checkMatchingCompatibility}} increased from 1ms to 8-10ms:\n\n!image-20260123-113335.png|width=645,alt=\"image-20260123-113335.png\"!\n\nIt doesn’t affect such public endpoints as {{/driver/acceptScheduledRide}} and {{/orderDriver/v1/getScheduledRideRequests}} much, because they are already >250ms.","2026-01-23T11:49:11.061Z"],["3833384","PFI-837327","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-23T11:49:18.341Z"],["3833385","PFI-837718","PFI","mariam.pharsadanishvili@bolt.eu","Mariam Pharsadanishvili","!JPEG_1769165069051_7294192046092075593.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T11:49:22.423Z"],["3833386","PFI-837020","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Old commission:\n\n!CleanShot 2026-01-23 at 13.48.22@2x-20260123-114824.png|width=401,alt=\"CleanShot 2026-01-23 at 13.48.22@2x-20260123-114824.png\"!\n\nNew commission:\n\n!CleanShot 2026-01-23 at 13.48.48@2x-20260123-114850.png|width=401,alt=\"CleanShot 2026-01-23 at 13.48.48@2x-20260123-114850.png\"!\n\nfor this company: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/190095?tab=profile|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/190095?tab=profile]\n\nwill apply tomorrow","2026-01-23T11:49:33.914Z"],["3833388","PFI-837387","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-23T11:49:54.049Z"],["3833389","DO-5824","DO","kristo.sarnets@bolt.eu","Kristo Sarnets","And when setting up a compute with my instance profile, it also failed.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 13.49.44.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T11:50:05.612Z"],["3833390","PAR-1409","PAR","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","As this problem was reported over 2 years ago and we have improved our system that double payouts/cashouts would not be possible, no need to work on it anymore","2026-01-23T11:50:12.426Z"],["3833391","LSS-61929","LSS","ksenia.korolkova@bolt.eu","Ksenia Korolkova","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] , I have just received the comment from legal advisor that they require these forms of signature - Sigillum Sign, Szafir 2.0, proCertum SmartSign, PEM-HEART 3.9, and SecureDoc 2 from EuroCert. Would it be possible to re-sign the documents using one of the mentioned signatures? In addition please feel free to remove yellow markup of the date.\n\nOr as a reference the form of signature as on attached document also works. Thank you!\n\n[^Nicchiano nowy adres.docx.pdf] ","2026-01-23T11:50:21.241Z"],["3833395","DSR-4001","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T11:51:08.083Z"],["3833396","WD-22643","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello [~accountid:639703ee61aba8a6a32c5a30] should we also assign account certification preparer role access to both?","2026-01-23T11:51:12.119Z"],["3833397","PFI-837413","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-23T11:51:23.811Z"],["3833398","WFM-10094","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Hello [~accountid:712020:3a3742eb-3298-4df7-a8af-c0fd7279bf95] these segments have just been added\n\n!image-20260123-115134.png|width=1115,alt=\"image-20260123-115134.png\"!","2026-01-23T11:51:37.786Z"],["3833400","LSS-61979","LSS","joao.ramos@bolt.eu","João Nuno Ferreira Ramos","Hey!\n\nHe had this ride at the time.\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1459445587/386?orderTryId=2648789329|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1459445587/386?orderTryId=2648789329]\n\nI can’t understand if it went trough that area of the map though. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 11.51.35.png|width=813,height=457,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 11.51.35.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-23T11:52:28.476Z"],["3833404","HS-29030","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Contract went out to candidate. ","2026-01-23T11:53:09.101Z"],["3833406","HS-29322","HS","manish.kishorbhaipatel@bolt.eu","Manish Kishorbhai Patel","[^visa.pdf]\n\n[^zusatzblatt.pdf]","2026-01-23T11:53:52.688Z"],["3833407","PFI-837423","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-23T11:53:56.423Z"],["3833410","WD-22676","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:712020:ff293eea-e5af-4325-9057-8f1a09bd3aa3] !\n\nThe validation is updated. \n\n!image-20260123-115456.png|width=898,alt=\"image-20260123-115456.png\"!","2026-01-23T11:55:00.750Z"],["3833412","PFI-837508","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-23T11:55:13.107Z"],["3833413","PFI-837603","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-23T11:55:35.604Z"],["3833414","WD-22520","WD","andrea.figueroa@bolt.eu","Andrea Figueroa","Hi [~accountid:712020:a5535fc2-4c96-407b-864b-f673b781e58e] \nWe need to make an additional request regarding this ticket. \n\nCould you please add one day to employee E007499 - *Pedro Pietra Cabral*: Current beginning balance year: 5 days. *1 day to be added.* +*Total increase: 6 days for 2026*+\n\nThank you!","2026-01-23T11:56:32.309Z"],["3833417","LSS-62045","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] you may delete this ticket - a duplicate has been created for Legal Rentals. After the necessary confirmations, we will transition it to Legal Ops for signature support. Thank you for your help! ","2026-01-23T11:56:54.322Z"],["3833418","WD-22587","WD","steve.white@bolt.eu","Steve White","This was undone so should be good now?\n\nPlan is to round all from April (after aCR)","2026-01-23T11:56:56.061Z"],["3833419","LSS-57632","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Version for signature: [^2026.01 Bolt Rewards NG_Partnership Agreement - Bastion Health (final draft) (clean).docx.pdf] \n\nBolt signatory: Ahto Kink \n\nPartner: *Naomi Aduku (email:* [*wecare@bastionhmo.com*|mailto:wecare@bastionhmo.com]*)*\n\ncc. [~accountid:5e4cfe3b393ea90c94b40eb0] ","2026-01-23T11:56:59.697Z"],["3833421","WEBSD-1507","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:6332c7ab409249995ee9c5e8] 👋 \n\nI hope you are doing great! \n\nFrom my side there is nothing I can do because what you are suggesting is to change the main structure of our city pages. The city page structure is part of a *global template* established by our designers to maintain a unified experience.\n\nI recommend maintaining the current page structure. I don't see a clear *strategic advantage* or significant *functional gain* in merging them. Keeping them separate preserves the current clarity for the user and avoids unnecessary complexity.\n\nIf you want to move forward please create a ticket over [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1079/group/1329/create/13805] where engineering team can answer your request.\n\nI hope this helps!","2026-01-23T11:57:06.045Z"],["3833422","PIF-3302","PIF",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thanks for the bug!\nNo action needed from you right now.\nWe’ll move it to Clarification and review it then.\nIf we need anything, we’ll reach out.","2026-01-23T11:57:12.949Z"],["3833425","LSS-61811","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Thank you [~accountid:5bc4571d505b7a135722281f] ! \nLegal Ops, please set Ahto’s signature on this letter: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OA-eTi8uD7MWGXU1EdnIp7_P4nKSlRPkUdX7Z59Npbo/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OA-eTi8uD7MWGXU1EdnIp7_P4nKSlRPkUdX7Z59Npbo/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link]  ","2026-01-23T11:57:49.785Z"],["3833428","PRF-1860","PRF","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","@Karina Kochanovskaya MT🇲🇹 updated, minor feedback added. Thanks!","2026-01-23T11:58:03.648Z"],["3833429","PAR-366","PAR","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","This issue has been fixed (/) ","2026-01-23T11:58:07.644Z"],["3833430","PFI-835785","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-23T11:58:16.662Z"],["3833432","WD-22673","WD","vlad.badea@bolt.eu","Vlad-Dumitru Badea","Thanks. Once the account is deactivated and reactivated, how can we confirm whether everything is working correctly?\nShould the user try logging into Okta directly, or is there anything specific we should check on our side?","2026-01-23T11:58:49.006Z"],["3833433","LSS-46087","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/346221|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/346221|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T11:58:58.090Z"],["3833436","PFI-837451","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\r\n\r\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\r\n\r\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within 10 business days or more, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within 48 hours.\r\n\r\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the 