the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nAfiba","2026-01-23T11:59:40.009Z"],["3833440","PFI-836070","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\r\n\r\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\r\n\r\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within 10 business days or more, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within 48 hours.\r\n\r\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nAfiba","2026-01-23T11:59:41.833Z"],["3833441","LSS-61943","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/346113|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/346113|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T11:59:42.259Z"],["3833443","PFI-814406","PFI","sorin.chiriac@bolt.eu","Sorin Chiriac","that is working. ","2026-01-23T12:00:08.362Z"],["3833444","LSS-61807","LSS","giulio.delbalzo@bolt.eu","Giulio del Balzo di Caprigliano","yes - I confirm we will be compliant \n\ncc [~accountid:6038bb05f0327400688a35b0] \n\n","2026-01-23T12:00:10.082Z"],["3833445","LSS-61831","LSS","wojciech.wawro@bolt.eu","Wojciech Wawro","Hi [~accountid:5d833d1d8db4330c3b129500] do we have update in this case?","2026-01-23T12:00:10.922Z"],["3833446","PFI-837586","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-23T12:00:15.320Z"],["3833449","LSS-61943","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:712020:602d7a68-8a81-4bea-98bf-acb7026b1a56] sent out for signatures.","2026-01-23T12:00:46.696Z"],["3833451","CSP-290","CSP","michal.bielecki@bolt.eu","Michał Bielecki","26W04: Implementation is in progress. Designs are complete for alerting rules management. Plan is to finalize rules management for queues till end of 26W06. Future iterations will focus on usage of alerting rules to evaluate alerts and inform about them via visualization on queue overview page or via different means (like Slack notifications - yet to be decided if we’ll include it in the scope).","2026-01-23T12:01:13.910Z"],["3833452","WD-22676","WD","maile.nittim@bolt.eu","Maile Nittim","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] ! I was now able to submit the invoices. Thank you!","2026-01-23T12:01:27.313Z"],["3833453","RDS-1084","RDS","taras.sgibnev@bolt.eu","Taras Sgibnev","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] Yes, sounds like a new flow that should be properly designed.\n\nThe custom [*pickup directions*|https://www.figma.com/design/2NcBATQxS2oFhws1Vljamo/Pre-order?node-id=71563-312796&p=f&t=LPKnNUyddPl3p5Pu-11] (already implemented and available at all major airports where Bolt operates), is currently not used as effectively as it could be.\n\n*The problem* is that users can access pickup directions only after they start ordering. However, when people arrive at an unfamiliar airport, they are often hesitant to place an order before they understand where exactly they need to go. As a result, they usually try to find a pickup spot on their own first and only then initiate the order. This makes the idea of pickup directions much less useful.\n\nA possible improvement would be to make pickup directions more prominent directly on the home screen (+maybe a proactive push notification). The pickup code could be easily integrated into this flow as well.\n\nThis feels like a separate feature for the Pre-Order team. And it could significantly improve the rider experience and positively impact metrics not only in Warsaw, but across all airports. cc: [~accountid:712020:13244152-55c1-46c5-a6f1-86ca2de2c01c] \n\n\n\nBTW, at Warsaw Airport we have another related issue:\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDXENG-4736|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDXENG-4736|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T12:01:38.392Z"],["3833455","PFI-837726","PFI","elgun.javad@bolt-outsource.eu","Elgun Javad","!IMG-20260123-WA0028.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T12:01:51.760Z"],["3833457","ROPSC-518","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","Results analysed together with the local team.\n\n[HR audit results|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1l0jBNb5gZ6MUdnVZeB2hdCj0SYeKiOdZl_WtX8TcQsw/edit?gid=0#gid=0]","2026-01-23T12:02:03.353Z"],["3833458","WFM-10109","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Hello [~accountid:712020:a5d31f60-e8a7-4ce6-9f91-7af48161add4] , for DE PQs, do you mean?\n\nPQ_DE_Latvia - -100- Open cases > 5 cases (Danger)\nPQ_DE_Lithuania - -100- Open cases > 5 cases (Danger)\nPQ_DE_Estonia - -100- Open cases > 5 cases (Danger)","2026-01-23T12:02:17.918Z"],["3833460","LSS-61093","LSS","loredana.panait@bolt.eu","Loredana Panait","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ,\n\nAny update? Do we have and ETA on this?\n\nThank you, \n\nLore\n\n","2026-01-23T12:02:46.225Z"],["3833461","LSS-62045","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:62a88aabd0132d0068800eba] ! Thank you for letting me know!","2026-01-23T12:02:59.874Z"],["3833462","WD-22680","WD","steve.white@bolt.eu","Steve White","done 🙂 ","2026-01-23T12:03:16.367Z"],["3833463","LSS-61620","LSS","loredana.panait@bolt.eu","Loredana Panait","Hi [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] ,\n\nAny update? Do we have an ETA?\n\nThank you, \nLore","2026-01-23T12:03:23.794Z"],["3833464","ROPSC-517","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","[Working sheet|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1pwCulXIz-GCnTQmFWo_htwQT8ZDoNAguzrN_Ez6HclM/edit?gid=1600319568#gid=1600319568] for manual review created. ","2026-01-23T12:03:54.803Z"],["3833468","LSS-59767","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","@ Legal Ops, please collect signature by [~accountid:5b18f5574bec0e53fdb555d5] [^Non-Disclosure Agreement with Bolt (692d78e053) (version 4) (c93864be-3fdb-4c44-b2cb-cc7f3e3b9163).pdf] , thanks a lot!","2026-01-23T12:04:39.133Z"],["3833469","WD-22660","WD","maryia.batalava@bolt.eu","Maryia Batalava","hey [~accountid:712020:6850b463-f3bb-4458-b00b-b094810b5bcd], please reopen the ticket, it remains unfix. the problem is that Ingestion & Insights position should be removed!","2026-01-23T12:04:50.608Z"],["3833470","LSS-54833","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Thank you for your comments [~accountid:712020:2f68ebec-bff7-4acf-a855-0eeaf1c88737]! To be honest, I would push back on both points, and say that  100k EUR liability cap is non-negotiable under such an agreement.","2026-01-23T12:04:52.181Z"],["3833474","MLC-4058","MLC","sergio.ramirez@bolt.eu","Sergio Ramírez","* *W4:* No updates from the CP team. Awaiting confirmation of their availability to share required instructions. It’s on Deepak.  ","2026-01-23T12:05:54.022Z"],["3833475","LSS-62064","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/346227|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/346227|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T12:05:54.447Z"],["3833477","DSR-4003","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T12:06:07.081Z"],["3833479","CEBF-1703","CEBF","serhii.kostyhin@bolt.eu","Serhii Kostyhin","[~accountid:712020:7621878e-e68d-4cea-9df5-171c95c4c62d] \nAC2: Should the account plan be activated when it is sent for approval?\n\nAC6: to do read-only on UI, I have to change the standard layout on dynamic forms. Right?","2026-01-23T12:06:08.897Z"],["3833480","LSS-62070","LSS","fareed.mahaini@bolt.eu","Fareed Mahaini","[^Annex 2 to DE20250623-001 KTGermany - Bolt Drive DE.docx.pdf] _(156 kB)_","2026-01-23T12:06:10.902Z"],["3833481","CSP-451","CSP","quentin.legrand@bolt.eu","Quentin Émile N. Legrand","26W4\n\nI continued to explore data and started exploring prediction performance using a LightGBM regressor. Performance is ok-ish (wMAPE == 91%; MAE == 31.7 min) but needs to be analysed deeper and on a per-queue basis. \n\nThis doesn’t really leverage queuing theory (which might be ok), but it is a good basis as a baseline. _Remark_: I need to shakedown BH team a bit WRT to [this|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C030ME1919R/p1768992182706619] ([https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C030ME1919R/p1768992182706619|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C030ME1919R/p1768992182706619|smart-link]).\n\nI didn’t write anything in Confluence yet, I’ll share something next week","2026-01-23T12:07:01.613Z"],["3833484","ROPSC-512","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","All 11 363 drivers have been processed through the automated audit tool, and I’ve completed a preliminary review of the results. Overall, 53.9% of drivers were flagged.\n\nAfter a sync with the team, it turns out Veritas only has 1 version of contracts and as a result a lot of contracts were flagged as failed. After removing this issue, only 17% if drivers stayed flagged. ","2026-01-23T12:07:44.002Z"],["3833487","PAW-14598","PAW","viktor.pavlov@bolt.eu","Viktor Pavlov","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7421297465/2026-01-19+Redis+HashiCorp+Vault+PoC|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7421297465/2026-01-19+Redis+HashiCorp+Vault+PoC|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T12:08:41.586Z"],["3833489","ROPSC-512","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","Improvements to auto-acceptance that need to be done:\n\n* Expiry date of criminal record checks - we add 6 months to the issue date. The local team and auto-acceptance populates the expiry date field slightly differently:\n** For example, if the issue date is 3rd of January, the local team adds 3rd of June as the expiry date, but auto-acceptance adds 2nd of June. Could we add 6 months + 1 day to the tool to start populating the field the same way as the local team?\n* type_of_contractual_relationship - there have been new versions added and auto-acceptance if failing due to not having the versions in Veritas. Could you provide us with screenshots of which versions are in Veritas at the moment so we could compare what is still missing and add them?\n* Lets please start extracting Driving License number and populating it under Driving Licence number field.","2026-01-23T12:09:01.076Z"],["3833495","WFM-10101","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:712020:86fe5543-2da3-4e6f-a318-f35fcc13371b]!\r\n\r\nI confirm that you request is in progress.\r\n\r\n[~accountid:712020:86fe5543-2da3-4e6f-a318-f35fcc13371b], please clarify if you want me to assign the queues, too? If yes, do you want me to assign them as a Primary or Secondary?\r\n\r\nHave a great day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-23T12:09:56.098Z"],["3833497","CEBF-1703","CEBF","pradeep.yadav@bolt.eu","Pradeep Kumar Yadav","[~accountid:712020:c573470a-712d-474e-a9e6-b0635a9decb9]  No, only Approved ones can be activated.","2026-01-23T12:10:15.908Z"],["3833498","FPD-1567","FPD","ali.shojaee@bolt.eu","Ali Shojaee","I prepared a notebook that can help us pull data across different backtest labels and make it easier to compare, highlight, and interpret results. This is still in progress, as I’m working on adding more stats and metrics.\n\nI’d like to set up a session to discuss how we should assess whether an improvement is statistically and practically significant enough to incorporate into our forecasting approach.","2026-01-23T12:10:19.454Z"],["3833499","MLC-2542","MLC","daria.trokhina@bolt.eu","Daria Trokhina","*Week 4*:\n\n* Sabrina is calculated the minimum sample size for countries and figured out that we won’t reach it in PL. Thus it was decided to run the experiment in RO instead of PL. I’ve made sure that the abort content block was implemented in RO. \n* The experiment is going to be launched from Jan 26.","2026-01-23T12:10:35.980Z"],["3833500","PFI-835729","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\r\nThe payment state has now been adjusted to the order state and any Bolt balance debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-23T12:10:42.349Z"],["3833501","PFI-837077","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\r\nThe payment state has now been adjusted to the order state and any Bolt balance debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-23T12:10:44.842Z"],["3833502","PFI-837000","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\r\nThe payment state has now been adjusted to the order state and any Bolt balance debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-23T12:10:47.157Z"],["3833503","PFI-837196","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\r\nThe payment state has now been adjusted to the order state and any Bolt balance debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next o