65576393]{{) 🔐 Set permissions on job 50588265576393 to: aditi.sharma@bolt.eu, ali.shojaee@bolt.eu, anastasia.serebryannikova@bolt.eu, andrea.rabinelli@bolt.eu, andrei.kuchev@bolt.eu, kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu, matteo.casolari@bolt.eu, mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu, rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu, yuliia.puzanova@bolt.eu ✅ Set permissions for 10 users 🚀 Launched job run (run_id=331980459882795) with 120 tasks (url: }}[https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/#job/50588265576393/runs/331980459882795|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/#job/50588265576393/runs/331980459882795]{{) ✅ Job created: ID=50588265576393, Run ID=331980459882795  📊 Fold 12/12: Train 2023-01-01 → 2024-11-30, Forecast from 2024-12-01 Resolved policy_id: 0016DAB8EC37D5E8 ✅ Created job with ID: 684801617226607 (url: }}[https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/#job/684801617226607|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/#job/684801617226607]{{) 🔐 Set permissions on job 684801617226607 to: aditi.sharma@bolt.eu, ali.shojaee@bolt.eu, anastasia.serebryannikova@bolt.eu, andrea.rabinelli@bolt.eu, andrei.kuchev@bolt.eu, kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu, matteo.casolari@bolt.eu, mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu, rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu, yuliia.puzanova@bolt.eu ✅ Set permissions for 10 users 🚀 Launched job run (run_id=478303605845955) with 120 tasks (url: }}[https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/#job/684801617226607/runs/478303605845955|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/#job/684801617226607/runs/478303605845955]{{) ✅ Job created: ID=684801617226607, Run ID=478303605845955}}","2026-01-23T12:14:29.816Z"],["3833526","EBIKE1-405","EBIKE1","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","|!image-20260123-112445.png|width=460,alt=\"image-20260123-112445.png\"!\n\\\\\nAngle difference when the top end is closed and lower end is opened is only {color:#ff991f}*1.3 degrees*{color}\nHeight difference is {color:#ff991f}*8.3 mm*{color}|!image-20260123-112746.png|width=459,alt=\"image-20260123-112746.png\"!\n\\\\\nBecause of the length of the hatch the dimension changes are really small on the upper end of the hatch and that is also a reason why we can close the lock even the lower end is not in a correct position\nAngle change on the hook is same {color:#ff991f}*1.3 degrees*{color}\nDistance change on the hook:{color:#ff991f} *0.65 mm*{color}|Space between the battery and the hook of the hatch is max. ~6mm.\n!image-20260123-120514.png|width=459,alt=\"image-20260123-120514.png\"!\n\\\\\n!image-20260123-115704.png|width=459,alt=\"image-20260123-115704.png\"!\n\\\\\nThis extra 6mm will change the angle and distance\n\\\\\n!image-20260123-120051.png|width=459,alt=\"image-20260123-120051.png\"!\n!image-20260123-120653.png|width=460,alt=\"image-20260123-120653.png\"!\n\\\\\nAngle change on the hook is same {color:#ff991f}*2.1 degrees*{color}\nDistance change on the hook:{color:#ff991f} *1.06 mm*{color}|\n\n\n\nEven if we make the lower hook thicker, the change in angle and distance at the upper hook is not large enough to prevent the lock from being pressed closed.\n\n\n\n* One option to improve it could be to use a hinge that fixes the lower end of the hatch permanently\n* Second option could be an extra switch on the fixation bracket of the controller that gives open/close signal to the IoT or controller. This switch should be pressed then by the hatch but it is definitely way more complex solution and needs probably also IoT or controller changes.","2026-01-23T12:14:58.717Z"],["3833529","L10N-29802","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29800](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29800)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T12:15:48.452Z"],["3833530","L10N-29804","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29800](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29800)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T12:15:49.503Z"],["3833531","L10N-29807","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29800](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29800)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T12:15:51.550Z"],["3833532","L10N-29812","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all c