-23T12:16:37.003Z"],["3833543","LSS-58645","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Thank you. Please coordinate with [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] and Legal Ops team re/ signature.","2026-01-23T12:16:38.965Z"],["3833544","MLC-4069","MLC","daria.trokhina@bolt.eu","Daria Trokhina","*Week 4:*\n\n* Had a kick off meeting with Anette, where we discussed what exactly should be launched for BM Cashback comms (comms will be launched in EE, LV, RO, PL, PT)\n* Raised [a ticket for content localisation|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101679].\n* Canvases will be launched next week, once the content will be localised.","2026-01-23T12:16:50.185Z"],["3833546","PFI-835097","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-23T12:17:16.740Z"],["3833547","PIF-3302","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-alerting, pint-product-observability-and-incident-response-platform, pint-capability-observability\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-23T12:17:26.059Z"],["3833548","LSS-58899","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n# Confirmed with the stakeholder - the partner accepted the SCCs & updated wording in the privacy clause.\n# Business will coordinate with Legal Ops on signature.\n\nClosing as there are further questions from the business & [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] is coordinating on signature.","2026-01-23T12:18:21.442Z"],["3833550","DSR-3995","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Driver is suspended due to this [oder|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2325866389/574?orderTryId=2985182751]. \n It was a major collision with car damage, which is highest severity level and if confirmed (and this one was confirmed by both D and R) termination is applied from 1st report. Additionally Riders report contained other allegation - speeding and off-platform journey .Checking the D profile I see that he previously had reporting in less severe safety levels and quite a lot bad comments from R. His average rating is also 4.6 - which is quite bad to our standards\n\nTermination will not be lifted","2026-01-23T12:19:21.050Z"],["3833552","FPD-1553","FPD","ali.shojaee@bolt.eu","Ali Shojaee","Using blocked CV (train_size=0.2, test_size=0.1; ~3 folds on average), the challenger improves city-level performance in roughly *40–48%* of cases (depending on metric/horizon). However, at the *portfolio level* results are slightly worse overall: *finished_orders* is essentially flat at 1-month (0.0791 vs 0.0788) but better at 3-month (0.0752 vs 0.0850), while *gmv_local* is worse at both 1- and 3-month horizons (0.0996 vs 0.0950; 0.1032 vs 0.1011).\n\nThe main pattern is higher dispersion: the challenger makes some cities much better and some much worse. Clear “good” examples include *Baku* (large gains at 3-month), and also *Polokwane, Emalahleni, Dnipro, Split,* and *Milton Keynes*; “bad” examples include *Accra*, *Zurich, Nice, Algarve, Constanta, Galati,* and *Abuja*.\n\n\nhere is the link to the results of the backtesting for blocked time series split cross validation. \n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1yQPDaMSSN8ldlZjNEa2r_l3Ewkg8g_YvbLHItct6Ih0/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1yQPDaMSSN8ldlZjNEa2r_l3Ewkg8g_YvbLHItct6Ih0/edit?usp=sharing|smart-card]","2026-01-23T12:19:37.926Z"],["3833556","RDS-904","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c] Can’t see Slack description.","2026-01-23T12:20:09.166Z"],["3833561","PFI-837134","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. There was no charges for these payments on the customer’s card.\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* regarding these charges. \n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-23T12:21:16.676Z"],["3833563","DSR-4005","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T12:21:23.526Z"],["3833565","HS-29290","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Sent for signing.","2026-01-23T12:21:59.841Z"],["3833566","PFI-837745","PFI","agne.majauskaiteshah@bolt-outsource.eu","Agnė Majauskaiteshah","!IMG_0772.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T12:22:00.749Z"],["3833569","PFI-837437","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-23T12:22:11.603Z"],["3833571","DPX-3591","DPX","song.luo@bolt.eu","Song Luo","Hi [~accountid:712020:3408d64a-d0d3-407f-aa6a-b3114d0b6178]I quickly demoed the error notification — let’s review this design together:\n[https://www.figma.com/design/sE71acN6oCO1fq13Fw4oBG/Merchant-App?node-id=30496-6155&t=1kqvR1Da56jNdVSw-4|https://www.figma.com/design/sE71acN6oCO1fq13Fw4oBG/Merchant-App?node-id=30496-6155&t=1kqvR1Da56jNdVSw-4|smart-link] \n\nIf it works, we can move on and fix this bug\n","2026-01-23T12:22:31.710Z"],["3833577","SCM-815","SCM","zuzanna.antoniewska@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Izabela Antoniewska","[~accountid:627aae199311100068a00836] any update?","2026-01-23T12:23:17.011Z"],["3833578","PFI-837746","PFI","jane.dike@bolt-outsource.eu","Jane Dike","[^transfer_confirmation (64).pdf]","2026-01-23T12:23:25.309Z"],["3833583","HS-29311","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Wrong type in WD, waiting manager’s confirmation.","2026-01-23T12:24:19.975Z"],["3833585","PFI-832407","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, apologies for delay.\n\nSo, there weren’t any errors with adjustments, they just didn’t get approved. For each of the adjustments there needs to be two approvals given. The process has been decentralized to the Local Teams, my understanding it should be the following:\n\n# Somebody from your (Local) team submits an adjustment file and gives a first approval.\n# Person from the Controlling Team approves the adjustment.\n\nonly one approval was given and seems adjustment can’t be approved now already. Please, resubmit those as per the process above 🙏 \n\n# [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-adjustment/adjustments/19152331|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-adjustment/adjustments/19152331]\n# [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-adjustment/adjustments/19152330|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-adjustment/adjustments/19152330]\n# [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-adjustment/adjustments/19158683|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-adjustment/adjustments/19158683]","2026-01-23T12:24:30.366Z"],["3833591","LSS-61827","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:985a985c-b403-41bd-b116-abbf44b22175] [~accountid:712020:4afbd60d-276d-4d8c-8d4c-5669fd772468] please request the stated below from Open AI already, so we save time when we get new order ","2026-01-23T12:25:09.507Z"],["3833592","HS-29314","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Cancelled.","2026-01-23T12:25:13.777Z"],["3833594","DELIVERY-1639","DELIVERY","oleksandr.stelmakh@bolt.eu","Oleksandr Stelmakh","26W4: Rolled out ML based [+pricing+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/J4CerQE] in *Valetta (+4.38%Absolute contribution profit (+547K EUR))* and *Timisoara(+1.79% Absolute contribution profit* *(+26K EUR))*","2026-01-23T12:25:40.188Z"],["3833595","RDS-1184","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:73f630c1-899f-4b5d-ac71-8a7e5c89eb30] Can we separate the provided examples into separate tickets? \n\nFor the last point (web view), this is the same as this ticket, right? [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/RDS/ideas/view/6301152?selectedIssue=RDS-1025|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/RDS/ideas/view/6301152?selectedIssue=RDS-1025|smart-link] ","2026-01-23T12:25:40.969Z"],["3833596","PFI-837748","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-23T12:25:50.856Z"],["3833597","HS-29323","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Hi [~accountid:63b55e18fa5fbde2ba462120]! Assigning this ticket to you 🙏 ","2026-01-23T12:25:57.055Z"],["3833598","MICRO-343","MICRO","hannalore.taal@bolt.eu","Hannalore Taal","* What is the volume of cases in which micromobility users should be blocked?\n** 1,645 events required blocking during 2025, investigative blocks, final outcome breakdown:\n*** No Further Action - 1,313\n*** Termination - 146\n*** Warning - 138\n*** Hard-Block - 18 (from all verticals)\n*** - 12\n*** Leave the original Investigative Suspension on the user’s account (e.g., if no response) - 11\n*** Education - 3\n*** 7-Day Suspension - 2\n*** 1-Day Suspension - 1\n\nSo mainly, the \"hard block\" cases would mean the necessity for termination from all verticals, e.g., maliciously damaging our property, threats, underage user, etc.\n\n* What are the main reasons for blocking micromobility users?\n** Rental Used for Criminal Activity (should be blocked from all verticals)\n** [Micromobility (Safety): I want to report a personal accident|https://app.slack.com/beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/45764?country=global&language=en] (investigative block)\n** [Safety - I want to report an accident with a cyclist|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/63858?country=global&language=en] (investigative block)\n** [Safety - I want to report an accident with a pedestrian|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/89511?country=global&language=en] (investigative block)\n** [Safety - I want to report an accident due to unsafe parking|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/61713?country=global&language=en] (investigative block)\n** [Safety - I want to report an accident with another vehicle|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/14618?country=global&language=en] (investigative block)\n** [Safety - I want to report an accident with a property|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/25736?country=global&language=en] (investigative block)\n*** Behavioural root cause (user intoxicated, underage user, too many occupants, reckless riding):\n**** Follow the suspension matrix if the root cause is any of the following:\n***** Intoxicated User\n***** Underage User\n***** Too Many Occupants\n***** Reckless Driving User\n***** Unsafely carried goods/cargo\n***** Used for commercial purposes\n***** Unsafe Parking\n***** Unknown\n\n* In what cases are we blocking users from all Bolt vs only from a certain vertical?\n** For MM blocks, we're currently forced to block the users from all verticals; in reality, it would probably only be in certain cases, such as threats, malicious activity/damaging our property, or other criminal activity\n** For Drive, if the Vehicle Was Maliciously Damaged or Vandalised, Vehicle Used For Criminal Activity, Unlicensed Driver (depending on the case)","2026-01-23T12:26:05.415Z"],["3833603","PFI-830897","PFI","arnoldas.laurynas@bolt-outsource.eu","Arnoldas Laurynas","Waiting for an update.","2026-01-23T12:26:17.168Z"],["3833605","PFI-818403","PFI","clara.machado@bolt.eu","Clara Oliveira Machado","Hi Team, \n\nHope everything is great. This ticket is closed as “Done”. However, when i search for the accounts on Admin, the payments are not reflected in the admin page. \n\nCan you advise?\n\nThanks","2026-01-23T12:26:31.648Z"],["3833609","DPM-2360","DPM","pawel.dabrowski@bolt.eu","Paweł Dąbrowski","[~accountid:62b2cf2c99eafa602d88ec9e] from my perspective this should be highest priority? This is as relates to sensitive pricing which we need to have accurate when menu draft created in case agents would miss corrections during review\nfyi: [~accountid:712020:a8e993c7-e089-4c7f-96d3-8d2e1ee4caa6] ","2026-01-23T12:27:56.856Z"],["3833610","DRX-25039","DRX","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","RCE-343","2026-01-23T12:27:57.234Z"],["3833612","FPD-1503","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","*Additional insights*\n\nWhen the optimization recommends increasing *demand spend*, we observe higher incremental S2O, a larger number of active riders, and more search sessions, which collectively translate into higher finished orders. These gains come at the cost of lower online hours, organic S2O conversion, and overall O2F conversion rates.\n\nConversely, in cities where the optimal solution favors higher *supply spend*, the model increases online hours while reducing search sessions. This reduction is driven by lower incremental rider activations, fewer sessions per active rider, and higher rider churn. As a result, the OH / SS ratio improves, leading to higher overall O2F and organic S2O conversion rates. While incremental S2O conversion declines under this scenario, the drop is offset by a stronger organic component, resulting in a net improvement in total conversion efficiency.\n\nOverall, GMV uplift is larger in markets where the optimization recommends increasing demand spend compared to those where supply spend is increased. However, this comparison should be interpreted cautiously, as the number of cases with increased supply spend is significantly smaller than those with increased demand spend.\n\nAn increase in supply spend tends to be optimal in markets characterized by strong supply incrementality (primarily affecting online hours) and/or weak demand incrementality (which directly impacts active riders, sessions per rider, and S2O conversion). This asymmetry is also reflected in the higher number of markets where demand spend increases are recommended: supply-side campaigns typically exhibit weaker and lower-quality incremental effects than demand campaigns, resulting in lower overall supply incrementality.\n\nThe optimization outcome, in the end, seems to be driven more by the *strength and quality of incremental effects* than by a strict balancing of supply and demand. Demand spend primarily boosts search sessions and incremental S2O, while supply spend reduces search intensity and incremental S2O but improves organic conversion rates. The optimal allocation therefore depends on which set of effects dominates in a given market - those driven by demand investments or those driven by supply investments.\n\nThe figure below illustrates the distribution of relative differences across multiple forecasted metrics between the optimized and executed scenarios, comparing markets where demand spend is increased versus those where supply spend is increased.\n\n!image-20260123-121450.png|width=767,alt=\"image-20260123-121450.png\"!","2026-01-23T12:28:05.355Z"],["3833614","PFI-830581","PFI","konstantin.otsalu@bolt-outsource.eu","Konstantin Otsalu","Hi! Any update?","2026-01-23T12:28:29.936Z"],["3833615","LSS-62036","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:61f26e891bda70006e1597b7] - please kindly re-submit this request to Legal; this is not a privacy inquiry.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-23T12:28:37.372Z"],["3833616","TS-4656","TS","aleksandr.bregin@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Bregin","Creating slides :loading: ","2026-01-23T12:28:38.923Z"],["3833617","LSS-60396","LSS","hala.abdulhaq@bolt.eu","Hala Abdulhaq","Hello Team, \n\nThere was a typo in the previous engagement letter. Could we please resign this version? The Engagement Letter and the Addendum require signing. If we can have them all included in one PDF, in the following order, it would be much appreciated:\n\n# Engagement letter\n# Terms of Business\n# Addendum to Terms of Business.\n[^Addendum to Terms of Business - EAT 273252 (1).pdf] [^Engagement letter - EAT 273252 (3).pdf] [^Terms of Business - EAT 273252 (1) (1).pdf] \n","2026-01-23T12:28:43.897Z"],["3833618","PFI-837129","PFI","mba-okorie.chinyere@bolt.eu","Chinyere Mba-okorie","Hey [~accountid:712020:fc661671-1d51-4372-9578-b46465bd51ac] \nYes, I see now that all the cities have 25 and 13% Base Fee Calculators linked *except Bottrop* 🙏 \n\nAlso wanted to bring to your attention, these 3 cities ([Braunschweig|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/baseFeeCalculators?tz=Africa%2FLagos&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22city_id%22%3A1233%2C%22is_active%22%3A1%7D%7D], [Bielefeld|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/baseFeeCalculators?tz=Africa%2FLagos&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22city_id%22%3A1274%2C%22is_active%22%3A1%7D%7D] and [Aachen|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/baseFeeCalculators?tz=Africa%2FLagos&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22city_id%22%3A739%2C%22is_active%22%3A1%7D%7D] have [+Germany Taxis - Company based 13%+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/feeCalculators/543718] linked twice (image attached below). Is this something that can be correct? \n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 13.27.46.png|width=1145,height=359,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 13.27.46.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-23T12:29:12.966Z"],["3833619","AD-9","AD","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:5dce558363a2770df86e61ab] there is no file and name of the partner in the ticket, please add it here ","2026-01-23T12:29:38.272Z"],["3833621","LSS-61831","LSS","paula.pihelgas@bolt.eu","Paula Joanna Pihelgas","Hey, sent it out 21.01.26. \n\nSigned by us, waiting for counterparty. Sent out a reminder for them, \n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 14.28.12.png|width=549,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-23 at 14.28.12.png\"!","2026-01-23T12:29:43.919Z"],["3833623","HS-29254","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hello!\n\nThis has been signed and sent to your personal email.\n\n\n\nRegards,\nKadri","2026-01-23T12:30:01.544Z"],["3833624","LSS-60621","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:70d80a66-553d-4db2-b50f-6bdb7d3bd7a1] - considering no further updates, I am intending to close the privacy sub-ticket. Please reach out in Slack if you need further input on this from me!","2026-01-23T12:30:22.041Z"],["3833626","BR-3848","BR","triinu.tasa@bolt.eu","Triinu Tasa","This is caused by a bug in the code. Currently when rescheduling a partner_invoice task due to negative amount we also generate a vat_correction task if necessary, but with the time interval of the old task. This causes the new partner_invoice task to fail in case there are records with incorrect vat also from the new period, as vat correction was only performed for the previous period. \n\nThe solution is not to generate vat_correction task when partner_invoice task is postponed as during new task execution we check whether vat corrections are necessary. Then a vat_correction task is created, with the correct time interval.","2026-01-23T12:30:39.881Z"],["3833627","LSS-61078","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Update - closing as no further questions to privacy were raised.","2026-01-23T12:30:42.641Z"],["3833629","HS-29325","HS","promise.tshabalala@bolt.eu","Promise Nomaswazi Tshabalala","!image-20260123-123044.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-23T12:30:55.523Z"],["3833630","MLC-2553","MLC","sergio.ramirez@bolt.eu","Sergio Ramírez","*W4:* Roadmap and task ownership within the LCM Eater team defined. One additional session with Anette scheduled for Monday to align on workflow and next steps. Another one with Daria on catalogs and personalization. ","2026-01-23T12:30:57.557Z"],["3833632","L10N-29839","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working o