ssions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29837](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29837)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T12:31:15.265Z"],["3833639","L10N-29852","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29837](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29837)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T12:31:16.381Z"],["3833640","DRX-26220","DRX","radu.vasiliu@bolt.eu","Radu Vasiliu","ETA: 2026-01-30\nStatus: Implementation\n\nSummary: \n• Integration is ready and tested in prelive\n• There is one remaining task to block drivers/cars if discovered ineligible during trip reporting (currently such driver/cars are simply ignored and trips not reported)\n• Waiting for live URLs/credentials from ITC\n\nBlockers: \n• @artur Before live launch, all existing data for Abu Dhabi drivers/cars should match what the integration expects:\n    ◦ Drivers should have emirates ID number in their personal code fields, ideally without any dashes\n    ◦ Car plates must have the format {Plate code}/{Plate number}, e.g. 11/12345\n\nDetails:\n• Integration is ready and tested in prelive\n• There is one remaining task to block drivers/cars if discovered ineligible during trip reporting (currently such driver/cars are simply ignored and trips not reported)\n• Waiting for live URLs/credentials from ITC","2026-01-23T12:31:17.036Z"],["3833641","L10N-29857","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29837](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29837)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T12:31:18.538Z"],["3833642","LSS-59448","LSS","christiana.akinlade@bolt.eu","Christiana Modupe Akinlade","Hi [~accountid:5b7d5435b57ed25933f64464] can you please let him know that the important information on UBOs and Board of Director was not filled ? \nThanks \n","2026-01-23T12:31:18.586Z"],["3833643","DSR-4007","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-23T12:31:20.099Z"],["3833644","L10N-29855","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29837](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29837)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T12:31:20.595Z"],["3833645","L10N-29863","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-29837](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-29837)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-23T12:31:21.066Z"],["3833646","L10N-29865","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note 